AQET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/t-magazine/07holiday-arena-primac-slide-AQET/07holiday-arena-primac-slide-AQET-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guatemalan Modern', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guatemalan Modern', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weissenberg, Rudy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Primack, Rodman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guatemala City (Guatemala)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-01T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Delavan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Delavan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94d9bb4f-a71f-59b3-a1c9-5c9aadd41d42', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94d9bb4f-a71f-59b3-a1c9-5c9aadd41d42'}, {'abstract': 'Tam Mutu will get a second chance to make his Broadway debut in a leading role, this time as the title character in the musical “Doctor Zhivago.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/01/arts/zhivago-musical-casting-announced.html', 'snippet': 'Tam Mutu will get a second chance to make his Broadway debut in a leading role, this time as the title character in the musical “Doctor Zhivago.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tam Mutu will get a second chance to make his Broadway debut in a leading role, this time as the title character in the musical “Doctor Zhivago,” the show’s producers planned to announce on Monday. Kelli Barrett (“Baby It’s You,” “Wicked”), is to star opposite Mr. Mutu as Zhivago’s paramour, Lara Guishar, in the production based on Boris Pasternak’s 1957 novel about romance and revolution in Russia during World War I. While Mr. Mutu is a familiar presence in the West End of London, including a recent role as Javert in “Les Misérables” at Queen’s Theater and a coming starring role as Stone in the Donmar Warehouse production of “City of Angels,” his original Broadway debut was to have been “Rebecca,” which was undermined by financial shortcomings and scandal. Other key players in “Doctor Zhivago” will include the Tony-nominated Tom Hewitt (“The Rocky Horror Picture Show,” “Jesus Christ Superstar”) as the aristocrat Viktor Komarovsky, and Paul Nolan, (who is currently playing Guy in “Once”) as the revolutionary Pasha Antipov. Full casting is to be announced later. The musical version of “Doctor Zhivago” (with book by Michael Weller, music by Lucy Simon, and lyrics by Michael Korie and Amy Powers) had its world debut in 2006 at La Jolla Playhouse in California. In 2011, it was revised at the Lyric Theater in Sydney. Des McAnuff (“Jersey Boys,” “The Who’s Tommy”) will direct. Preview performances are set to begin March 27 at the Broadway Theater, with an official opening planned for April 21.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Zhivago’ Musical Casting Announced', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Zhivago’ Musical Casting Announced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mutu, Tam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrett, Kelli (1984- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hewitt, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nolan, Paul Alexander (Actor)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-01T05:01:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bf88786-ec29-5580-abd8-ac74fdc03752', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bf88786-ec29-5580-abd8-ac74fdc03752'}, {'abstract': 'The Girl Scouts of the U.S.A. has approved “Digital Cookie,” a platform for scouts to sell and ship Thin Mints, Samoas and others to friends and relatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/01/technology/online-sales-for-girl-scout-cookies-are-approved.html', 'snippet': 'The Girl Scouts of the U.S.A. has approved “Digital Cookie,” a platform for scouts to sell and ship Thin Mints, Samoas and others to friends and relatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Girl Scouts are adding digital marketing to their formidable arsenal of charm, cuteness and perseverance to sell millions of boxes of Thin Mints, Samoas and other longtime cookie favorites.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/01/business/scouts/scouts-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/01/business/scouts/scouts-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 798}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/01/business/scouts/scouts-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 770, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ