: 'images/2014/12/01/nyregion/01SHOOTING/01SHOOTING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/01/nyregion/01SHOOTING/01SHOOTING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/01/nyregion/01SHOOTING/01SHOOTING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '4 Wounded in Shooting at a Baby Shower in Brooklyn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '4 Wounded in Shooting at a Shower in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flatbush (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-01T05:06:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5503a9ae-72ca-5559-8ffb-c7ba1deaf039', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5503a9ae-72ca-5559-8ffb-c7ba1deaf039'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/01/arts/whats-on-tv-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) THE NORMAL HEART (2014) Larry Kramer adapted his 1985 play about the early years of the AIDS crisis for this film, directed by Ryan Murphy. Mark Ruffalo stars as Ned, a stand-in for Mr. Kramer, who notices that a mysterious disease is starting to claim lives in New York and pleads for his fellow gay men to change their sexual behavior — and for the political establishment to heed the crisis. Matt Bomer (above left, with Mr. Ruffalo) plays Felix, Ned’s lover, a reporter at The New York Times. And Julia Roberts is Dr. Emma Brookner, who takes notice of the terror and tries to fight on behalf of her patients. The play was first staged at the Public Theater and given its Broadway debut in 2011, where it won a Tony for best revival. This film “simultaneously exposes some of the play’s flaws and finds alternate sources of power in the story,” Neil Genzlinger wrote in The Times.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s on TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-01T05:16:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5b8deb8-be61-56b3-aec2-79cfb9858685', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5b8deb8-be61-56b3-aec2-79cfb9858685'}, {'abstract': 'A semblance of calm returned to the city’s streets on Monday after a tense and at times frightening night, with numerous pro-democracy protesters and police officers injured as both sides vied for control of a road along the main government offices.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/01/the-scene-as-police-sent-protesters-fleeing-in-hong-kong/', 'snippet': 'A semblance of calm returned to the city’s streets on Monday after a tense and at times frightening night, with numerous pro-democracy protesters and police officers injured as both sides vied for control of a road along the main government office...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The protesters and the police greeted each other with a quick good morning shortly after the sun rose over the Hong Kong skyscrapers on Monday. It was a brief moment of civility in what had otherwise been a tense and at times frightening night, with numerous injured as both sides vied for control of a road along the main government offices in the semiautonomous Chinese city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Scene as Police Sent Protesters Fleeing in Hong Kong', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-01T06:21:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65e902d8-ce8b-5e49-97fb-59df103efbe4', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65e902d8-ce8b-5e49-97fb-59df103efbe4'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Monday, December 1, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/01/pageoneplus/corrections-december-1-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Monday, December 1, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: December 1, 2014', 'kicker': None