king on was to drop in at the New York City Opera’s annual Vox Contemporary Opera Lab programs, which offered first glimpses of works in progress. But the City Opera is no more, and other companies have taken up the challenge, including the Fort Worth Opera, which announced the program for its Frontiers series on Monday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fort Worth Opera to Showcase Works in Progress', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Texas Showcase for Operas in Progress', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fort Worth Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-01T16:33:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b524666a-c36d-593c-b6c3-4c192efcb82c', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b524666a-c36d-593c-b6c3-4c192efcb82c'}, {'abstract': 'Elizabeth Lauten, the congressional staffer who posted critical comments of Sasha and Malia Obama on her Facebook page over the weekend, has resigned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/12/01/g-o-p-aide-quits-over-remarks-critical-of-obama-daughters/', 'snippet': 'Elizabeth Lauten, the congressional staffer who posted critical comments of Sasha and Malia Obama on her Facebook page over the weekend, has resigned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elizabeth Lauten, the congressional staff member who posted critical comments of Sasha and Malia Obama on her Facebook page late last week, has resigned. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank':