, 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c2bc9da-aa05-52ce-80dc-780edc23151e'}, {'abstract': 'Russia and Sweden have the buzziest entries — “Leviathan” and “Force Majeure” — but don’t count out France, Germany, Turkey, Argentina and, in a first, Mauritania.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/01/what-to-watch-for-in-the-foreign-language-race/', 'snippet': 'Russia and Sweden have the buzziest entries — “Leviathan” and “Force Majeure” — but don’t count out France, Germany, Turkey, Argentina and, in a first, Mauritania.', 'lead_paragraph': ' At first glance, the field for the Academy Award for best foreign-language film looks inscrutable: a record 83 countries and territories submitted entries, including four that are competing for the first time. But the number of real contenders for the Oscar to be awarded on Feb. 22 is actually much smaller, two dozen at most, and therefore somewhat easier to parse.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/28/arts/cotillard/cotillard-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/28/arts/cotillard/cotillard-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/28/arts/cotillard/cotillard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/28/arts/cotillard/cotillard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/28/arts/cotillard/cotillard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height':