rstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de2cadba-a598-534b-b7b8-60245e749410', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de2cadba-a598-534b-b7b8-60245e749410'}, {'abstract': 'Frosting three dozen cupcakes for school while helping with a science project and answering your email? Welcome to the modern parent’s alphabet.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/01/the-modern-parents-abc-h-is-for-harried/', 'snippet': 'Frosting three dozen cupcakes for school while helping with a science project and answering your email? Welcome to the modern parent’s alphabet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Spencer Wilson, illustrator of “Q is for Quinoa, A Modern Parent’s ABC” joined Motherlode as our latest artist-in-residence, we asked you to nominate your favorite letters of the modern parent’s alphabet. From hundreds of possibilities, it was hard to pick a favorite, but Spencer and Q is for Quinoa author Joel Rickett chose H is for Harried:“Someone who is harried,” Spencer wrote to me, “is feeling the stress of being rushed, overworked or harassed. A harried parent might be exhausted but still have to make three dozen cupcakes for school and help with a science project whilst answering their email on their phone…”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/01/us/motherlode-harried/motherlode-harried-articleLarge.png', 'height': 776, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/01/us/motherlode-harried/motherlode-harried-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 776}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/01/us/motherlode-harried/motherlode-harried-