ocused on infectious and tropical diseases, but the list has been refined to include access to drugs to mental illnesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the fourth time, GlaxoSmithKline has led all other pharmaceutical companies on an influential list ranking companies by how effectively they help the world’s poor get needed medicines. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'GlaxoSmithKline Leads In Getting Drugs to Poor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'GlaxoSmithKline Leads in Getting Drugs to Poor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GlaxoSmithKline PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-01T21:56:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74688b26-d365-5235-8541-bfe904182922', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74688b26-d365-5235-8541-bfe904182922'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Leibold’s research focuses on the Chinese government’s policies toward ethnic minorities and their effects on people’s daily lives. He recently returned from a trip to the western region of Xinjiang,', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/01/q-and-a-james-leibold-on-ethnic-policies-in-china/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Leibold’s research focuses on the Chinese government’s policies toward ethnic minorities and their effects on people’s daily lives. He recently returned from a trip to the western region of Xinjiang,', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Leibold is a senior lecturer in politics and Asian studies at La Trobe University in Australia, and is currently based in Beijing. His research has focused on the Chinese government’s policies toward ethnic minorities and their effects on people’s daily lives. He recently returned from a trip to the western region of Xinjiang, the nominally autonomous homeland of China’s ethnic Uighurs, a mostly Sunni Muslim, Turkic-speaking people. In recent years, government restraints on cultural and religious expression have bred resentment in Xinjiang that has sometimes erupted in deadly violence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/26/world/26sino-LEIBOLD2/26sino-LEIBOLD2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 541, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/26/world/26sino-LEIBOLD2/26sino-LEIBOLD2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 541, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/26/world/26sino-LEIBOLD2/26sino-LEIBOLD2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/26/world/26sino-LEIBOLD2/26sino-LEIBOLD2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/26/world/26sino-LEIBOLD2/26sino-LEIBOLD2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: James Leibold on Ethnic Policies in China', 'kicker':