ac8-2aac4dcf8f17'}, {'abstract': 'Readers have to take their time with James Hill’s new book, where he presents moments that have stayed with him, even if their meanings are sometimes ambiguous.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/02/photographing-the-moments-between-war-and-peace/', 'snippet': 'Readers have to take their time with James Hill’s new book, where he presents moments that have stayed with him, even if their meanings are sometimes ambiguous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can’t just flip through James Hill’s new book, “Somewhere Between War and Peace,” for a quick survey of his 20-years-and-counting career. Not only because the images are stark and demanding — but you’re also physically prevented. The pages are cut to different lengths, and the shorter pages carry Mr. Hill’s stories behind the photos. Thumb through, and you’ll land solely on those pictureless, text-only pages.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photographing the Moments Between War and Peace', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Azerbaijan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia (Georgian Republic)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nagorno-Karabakh', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T10:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 