ec. 6.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Louisiana Runoff', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cassidy, Bill (1957- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landrieu, Mary L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T11:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Axel Gerdau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Axel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gerdau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c354378b-7ff7-50f6-bc5f-7727a9df7514', 'word_count': 32, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c354378b-7ff7-50f6-bc5f-7727a9df7514'}, {'abstract': 'In hindsight the practice of orphans being forced into contract labor seems to have been cruel. But in the 19th century this system was deemed a type of “social welfare.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/03/opinion/the-swiss-and-needy-children.html', 'snippet': 'In hindsight the practice of orphans being forced into contract labor seems to have been cruel. But in the 19th century this system was deemed a type of “social welfare.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Re “Slavery’s shadow on Switzerland” (Opinion, Nov. 11): Tony Wild’s personal experience of finding out that his grandmother had been a verdingkind in Switzerland at the turn of the century offers an interesting perspective. But there are some inaccuracies in Mr. Wild’s account which, I feel, come from his strong emotional reaction based on his family relationship, rather than from the facts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Swiss and Needy Children', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T11:02:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ac1a572-0112-5c17-afd1-b310acc4b730', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ac1a572-0112-5c17-afd1-b310acc4b730'}, {'abstract': 'If the purpose of Thomas L. Friedman’s article was to commend the ultramodern wonders of Dubai, then it did a great job.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/03/opinion/roots-of-the-arab-awakening.html', 'snippet': 'If the purpose of Thomas L. Friedman’s article was to commend the ultramodern wonders of Dubai, then it did a great job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Re “Did Dubai do it?” (Nov. 20): If the purpose of Thomas L. Friedman’s article was to commend the ultramodern wonders of Dubai, then it did a great job. If it was to offer an underlying motive for the Arab Spring, then it failed. To say that the Arab awakening began because young Arab people were jealous of Dubai is fallacious. It is the equivalent of saying that sexual repression inspired the European Enlightenment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roots of the Arab Awakening', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dubai (United Arab Emirates)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T11:03:30+0000', 'document_ty