 a bitter war with Islamic extremists.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraqi Government and Kurds Reach Deal to Share Oil Revenues', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq Government Reaches Accord With the Kurds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arango, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pesh Merga', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abadi, Haider al-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Erbil (Iraq)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T13:26:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e01d438-a1bd-5231-805c-3b5d97b7148e', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e01d438-a1bd-5231-805c-3b5d97b7148e'}, {'abstract': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/12/02/daily-clip-report-73/', 'snippet': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Clip Report', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T13:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c892aeca-0ade-519a-abec-96a666742715', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c892aeca-0ade-519a-abec-96a666742715'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A poet sees a flock of blackbirds settling on wires and imagines judges in their robes or people watching a parade.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/02/a-change-of-seasons/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A poet sees a flock of blackbirds settling on wires and imagines judges in their robes or people watching a parade.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Change of Seasons', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-0