 repurposed as toppings for pizzas with very thin crusts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nobody goes to Rome for the pizza. Rectangles of pizza bianca cut with scissors on the Campo de’ Fiori from long planks shaped like diving boards, yes, but not for regular pizza. The standard circular pie is something travelers eat only after saltimbocca, puntarelle, spicy tripe, salt cod fritters, semolina gnocchi, porchetta, artichokes fried alla giudia and the holy pasta trinity of cacio e pepe, amatriciana and carbonara have all been checked off the list. It is food for the fifth night of vacation.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Review: Danny Meyer’s Marta in NoMad', 'kicker': 'Restaurants', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Those Roads to Rome, Lined With Pizza', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'NoMad (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Martha Washington Hotel (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marta (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T18:28:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/386238c6-7024-5a5b-972e-dae00d813f60', 'word_count': 1099, 'uri': 'nyt://article/386238c6-7024-5a5b-972e-dae00d813f60'}, {'abstract': 'The manufacturers estimated sales of 1.3 million vehicles in November, and were on pace to turn in their best annual performance since 2007.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/03/business/autom