by Patricia Barbizet, the chief executive of the Artémis Group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/03/business/steven-murphy-christies-chief-to-step-down.html', 'snippet': 'Steven P. Murphy, who has run the auction house since 2010, will be succeeded by Patricia Barbizet, the chief executive of the Artémis Group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly three weeks ago, Steven P. Murphy, Christie’s chief executive, played host to some of the world’s biggest art collectors at Christie’s important auction of postwar and contemporary art in New York. As he watched prices rise to dizzying heights, Mr. Murphy seemed at home in the company he has led since 2010.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/business/03christies-pic1/03christies-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 991, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/03/business/03christies-pic1/03christies-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 991}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/business/03christies-pic1/03christies-pic1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 621, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/business/03christies-pic1/03christies-pic1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1407, 'width': 852, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/business/03christies-pic1/03christies-pic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/03/business/03christies-pic1/03christies-pic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/business/03christies-pic1/03christies-pic1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Steven Murphy, Christie’s Chief, to Step Down', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weeks After Art Auction That Dazzled, Christie’s Chief Stuns With His Resignation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vogel, Carol', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Christie's", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowley, Graham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Steven P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barbizet, Patricia (1955- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T18:42:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel and Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71d4f8ef-fa96-58d9-9546-9cc695417d30', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71d4f8ef-fa96-58d9-9546-9cc695417d30'}, {'abstract': 'China’s leaders have self-interested reasons to combat pollution, as their recent pledge suggests. India’s leaders may have the same reasons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/03/upshot/the-next-big-climate-question-will-india-follow-china.html', 'snippet': 'China’s leaders have self-interested reasons to combat pollution, as their recent pledge suggests. India’s leaders may have the same reasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than 20 years, international climate talks have been dominated by a schism between those who created the problem of climate change (largely the United States and nations of the European Union) and those who would greatly contribute to it moving forward (largely China and India). But as climate negotiators meet in Lima, Peru, this week and next, and news reports are full of gloomy predictions that the negotiations will produce little, there are increasing signs that this stalemate may have been broken. This emerging shift is due in large part to China and its decision to break ranks and join the United States in making commitments to reduce greenhouse gas emissions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/upshot/03up-climate/03up-climate-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/03/upshot/03up-climate/03up-climate-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/upshot/03up-climate/03up-climate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/upshot/03up-climate/03up-climate-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1277, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/upshot/03up-climate/03up-climate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/03/upshot/03up-climate/03up-climate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/upshot/03up-climate/03up-climate-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Next Big Climate Question: Will India Follow China?', 'kicker': 'Tipping Point', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Treaties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T18:44:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Greenstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ff01e9f-b2c5-5ae0-832d-788724b49434', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ff01e9f-b2c5-5ae0-832d-788724b49434'}, {'abstract': 'When do legitimate policy grievances justify a “print the legend” attitude?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/02/my-ferguson-problem/', 'snippet': 'When do legitimate policy grievances justify a “print the legend” attitude?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes you write a column and decide, after the fact, that it should have come to a sharper point, or ended with a clearer question. And with my Sunday column about Ferguson, race and politics, which circled around a lot of different issues, a little such point-sharpening might be in order. So I’m going to try to do that here, in four paragraphs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Ferguson Problem', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Looting (Crime)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McWhorter, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T18:45:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61db5d94-217b-5b24-b8b6-6cb1272622eb', 'word_count': 948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61db5d94-217b-5b24-b8b6-6cb1272622eb'}, {'abstract': 'A trip to the source, in northwest Italy, can turn the pricey specialties into affordable treats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/02/travel/truffles-and-barolo-in-piedmont-the-frugal-way.html', 'snippet': 'A trip to the source, in northwest Italy, can turn the pricey specialties into affordable treats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'White truffles from Alba and red wine from Barolo are not usually part of the frugal traveler’s diet. After all, shavings of the former or a bottle of the latter can each easily cost over $100 in a New York restaurant. But what if you go straight to the source, the heart of the Piedmont region in northwestern Italy, for these indulgent luxuries? As I discovered during a recent weekend in the area, it’s possible to sample these superlative specialties — as well as excellent art, food and other charms — on a frugal budget.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/02/travel/02-frugal-luigi/02-frugal-luigi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/02/travel/02-frugal-luigi/02-frugal-luigi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/02/travel/02-frugal-luigi/02-frugal-luigi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/02/travel/02-frugal-luigi/02-frugal-luigi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1224, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/02/travel/02-frugal-luigi/02-frugal-luigi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/02/travel/02-frugal-luigi/02-frugal-luigi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/02/travel/02-frugal-luigi/02-frugal-luigi-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Truffles and Barolo in Piedmont, the Frugal Way', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Truffles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Piedmont (Italy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T18:47:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ingrid K. Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ingrid', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5daaba75-8ab0-5c34-9540-7228a747efb2', 'word_count': 1575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5daaba75-8ab0-5c34-9540-7228a747efb2'}, {'abstract': 'The chief executive of the Japanese auto supplier stopped short of saying the company would comply with the demand of United States regulators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/03/business/takata-resists-midnight-deadline-to-expand-airbag-recall.html', 'snippet': 'The chief executive of the Japanese auto supplier stopped short of saying the company would comply with the demand of United States regulators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facing a midnight deadline to expand a recall of defective airbags, Takata, the Japanese auto supplier, had not taken any action Tuesday night on the demand by United States regulators.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Takata Takes No Action on Demand to Expand Recall of Faulty Airbags', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Takata Takes No Action on U.S. Recall Demand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Takata Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T18:49:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Ivory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c551084-29a6-590f-9d3d-c426cf0b3020', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c551084-29a6-590f-9d3d-c426cf0b3020'}, {'abstract': 'I believe in voluntourism — that is to say, I believe we need to leave our islands of privilege and go see firsthand the inequality plaguing our world.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/02/voluntourists-needed-apply-within/', 'snippet': 'I believe in voluntourism — that is to say, I believe we need to leave our islands of privilege and go see firsthand the inequality plaguing our world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite what I like to think, the charity I run is pretty small.\xa0If we ever have more than five people in our office, it’s because my mom is there, helping us connect the wireless printer. So when a producer from NPR called last year and asked to speak with “the woman from our organization who had written the blog about voluntoursim,” I had to fight the urge to pretend to be my own assistant. It’s part of our nonprofit DNA — the tendency to stand on our tiptoes. We want people to take us seriously; we want to be the exact opposite of volunteers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/02/opinion/2kristof_kenya/2kristof_kenya-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 490, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/02/opinion/2kristof_kenya/2kristof_kenya-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 490}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/02/opinion/2kristof_kenya/2kristof_kenya-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 836, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/02/opinion/2kristof_kenya/2kristof_kenya-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1411, 'width': 1729, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/02/opinion/2kristof_kenya/2kristof_kenya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/02/opinion/2kristof_kenya/2kristof_kenya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/02/opinion/2kristof_kenya/2kristof_kenya-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Voluntourists Needed: Apply Within', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 