l Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cc233fb-77f2-562f-b22d-3dade98d7670', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cc233fb-77f2-562f-b22d-3dade98d7670'}, {'abstract': 'Just in time for Art Basel, the ICA Miami is opening in the city’s Design District with a dynamic young curator at the helm.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/02/institute-of-contemporary-art-miami-preview/', 'snippet': 'Just in time for Art Basel, the ICA Miami is opening in the city’s Design District with a dynamic young curator at the helm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As one of the world’s preeminent real estate playgrounds, where silhouetted cranes and I-beams figure prominently into the coral sunsets, Miami is a place where newness matters. And each time Art Basel Miami Beach rolls around in early December, fairgoers pay close attention to whichever oceanfront high-rise splashes onto the scene as the hotel of the season. Fortunately for art lovers, Miami’s grandest opening this year might be the rare debut of a newborn museum. This week, the Institute of Contemporary Art, Miami\xa0opens its doors due west of Miami Beach, occupying space in the historic Moore Building at the heart of the city in Miami’s Design District.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/02/t-magazine/02ica-mcgarry/02ica-mcgarry-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/02/t-magazine/02ica-mcgarry/02ica-mcgarry-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':