ami Design District (Miami, Fla)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-02T22:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1410e59c-7d70-555a-bda3-90803f87b30d', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1410e59c-7d70-555a-bda3-90803f87b30d'}, {'abstract': 'The food sparkles at this Gold Coast project by Paul Kahan, one of Chicago’s most versatile restaurateurs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/travel/restaurant-report-nico-osteria-in-chicago.html', 'snippet': 'The food sparkles at this Gold Coast project by Paul Kahan, one of Chicago’s most versatile restaurateurs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The success of a new project by Paul Kahan, one of Chicago’s most versatile restaurateurs and last year one of two James Beard “Outstanding Chef” winners, in the lobby of the trendy Thompson Chicago hotel, might seem effortless. Yet in a few significant ways, Nico is a departure for Mr. Kahan. Unlike his previous restaurants, which helped redefine neighborhoods in transition — the Publican, Avec and Blackbird in the Randolph Street corridor and Big Star in Wicker Park — Nico is in the well-established Gold Coast neighborhood, which Mr. Kahan pointedly described as “not my kind of neighborhood.”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/travel/07BITES/07BITES-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 544, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/07/travel/07BITES/07BITES-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 544}