ar” each have nabbed top honors, and the awards season is less than a week old. It could be proof that, as some are saying, it’s a wide-open year, or just a reflection of these particular organizations and nothing more. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Your Pick for Best Picture?', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T14:58:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7f55fba-37dd-578c-9174-1d471051deb6', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7f55fba-37dd-578c-9174-1d471051deb6'}, {'abstract': 'The strikes against the Islamic State represent an unusual confluence of interests in Iraq and Syria, where Tehran and Washington find themselves fighting the same enemy in an increasingly public fashion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/world/middleeast/iran-airstrikes-hit-islamic-state-in-iraq.html', 'snippet': 'The strikes against the Islamic State represent an unusual confluence of interests in Iraq and Syria, where Tehran and Washington find themselves fighting the same enemy in an increasingly public fashion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Iranian fighter jets struck extremist targets in Iraq recently, Iranian and American officials have confirmed, in the latest display of Tehran’s new willingness to conduct military operations openly on foreign battlefields rather than covertly and through proxies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. and Iran Both Attack ISIS, but Try Not to Look Like Allies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. and Iran Both Attack ISIS, but Try Not to Look Like Allies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arango, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic Revolutionary Guards Corps', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suleimani, Qassim', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T14:59:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango and Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c35ba5d-7a82-5a2b-a25f-d26ebbec6a13', 'word_count': 1254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c35ba5d-7a82-5a2b-a25f-d26ebbec6a13'}, {'abstract': 'The International Campaign to Ban Landmines attributed the drop to increased compliance with the Mine Ban Treaty, which was first signed 17 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/world/americas/land-mine-casualties-hit-a-low-and-production-seems-to-halt-group-says.html', 'snippet': 'The International Campaign to Ban Landmines attributed the drop to increased compliance with the Mine Ban Treaty, which was first signed 17 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deaths and injuries from land mines and other explosive remnants of war fell to the lowest level ever recorded last year, and production of the weapons appeared to have practically ceased, a leading disarmament group reported on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Land Mines Are Taking Smaller Toll, Group Says ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Land Mines Are Taking Smaller Toll, Group Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines, Explosive', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Campaign to Ban Landmines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMS CONTROL AND LIMITATION AND DISARMAMENT', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T15:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76219934-e8bb-56bf-a1cb-f5b49203b5a1', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76219934-e8bb-56bf-a1cb-f5b49203b5a1'}, {'abstract': 'A paper released by the Center for a New American Security in Washington concludes that China’s cybersecurity strategy, like its foreign policy, is driven mainly by the domestic political imperative to “protect the longevity of the Chinese Communist Party.”', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/03/for-china-cybersecurity-is-part-of-strategy-for-protecting-the-communist-party/', 'snippet': 'A paper released by the Center for a New American Security in Washington concludes that China’s cybersecurity strategy, like its foreign policy, is driven mainly by the domestic political imperative to “protect the longevity of the Chinese Communi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'For nearly two years, cyberespionage has been a tense focal point of relations between the United States and China. On Wednesday, the Center for a New American Security, a research group in Washington, released a paper written with the aim of understanding the motivations behind China’s cybersecurity strategy. Its conclusion: that the strategy, like China’s foreign policy, is driven mainly by the domestic political imperative of needing to “protect the longevity of the Chinese Communist Party.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/world/03sino-CYBER2/03sino-CYBER2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/world/03sino-CYBER2/03sino-CYBER2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/world/03sino-CYBER2/03sino-CYBER2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/03/world/03sino-CYBER2/03sino-CYBER2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/world/03sino-CYBER2/03sino-CYBER2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For China, Cybersecurity Is Part of Strategy for Protecting the Communist Party', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chang, Amy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for a New American Security', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Liberation Army (China)", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T15:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a05beb9b-f472-5070-b7fc-29c17044263a', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a05beb9b-f472-5070-b7fc-29c17044263a'}, {'abstract': 'In a reminder of hip-hop’s politically potent past, two performers strike a chord by sharing their emotions on a shooting in Ferguson, Mo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/arts/killer-mike-and-j-cole-bare-their-emotions-at-a-pivotal-time.html', 'snippet': 'In a reminder of hip-hop’s politically potent past, two performers strike a chord by sharing their emotions on a shooting in Ferguson, Mo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are few arguments more tiresome than the one over hip-hop’s political potential. It begins something like this: Hip-hop’s turn away from the socially conscious dates back to the early to mid-1990s, right around the time when Soundscan showed that hip-hop was truly integral to this country’s pop music. Over time, as hip-hop became flush with success, the agitating in the form of sloganeering and the implicit politics of gangster rap that were once the norm became scarcer and scarcer.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07KILLER1/07KILLER1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07KILLER1/07KILLER1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07KILLER1/07KILLER1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07KILLER1/07KILLER1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1306, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07KILLER1/07KILLER1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07KILLER1/07KILLER1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07KILLER1/07KILLER1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Viscerally Facing Up to Ferguson ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Viscerally Facing Up to Ferguson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 's