ltimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Songs Sung From a Prison in Malawi', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malawi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T15:54:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/235a99a1-da7f-54db-92fd-3adfd0a0c4ad', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/235a99a1-da7f-54db-92fd-3adfd0a0c4ad'}, {'abstract': 'Under the revised bid, GFI shareholders would receive $5.25 a share in cash and shares, bolstered by a higher cash bid by a group led by GFI’s management for the company’s wholesale brokerage business.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/03/cme-raises-bid-for-gfi-group-as-hostile-counteroffer-looms/', 'snippet': 'Under the revised bid, GFI shareholders would receive $5.25 a share in cash and shares, bolstered by a higher cash bid by a group led by GFI’s management for the company’s wholesale brokerage business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The CME Group said late Tuesday that it had increased its offer to acquire the GFI Group, a New York brokerage and clearing house, after BGC Partners started a competing, hostile bid for the company in October.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/business/dbpix-cme/dbpix-cme-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name