Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c74d869-72c9-5b5f-ab94-3dba415a313c', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c74d869-72c9-5b5f-ab94-3dba415a313c'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: 1914: The Rebel Leader, General De Wet, is Captured.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/03/1914-general-de-wet-is-captured/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: 1914: The Rebel Leader, General De Wet, is Captured.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Official news from Pretoria announces the taking of the rebel leader De Wet. The capture was effected by Commandant Brits on Tuesday in a farm a hundred miles east of Mafeking, where De Wet had taken refuge with fifty-two of his men. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1914: General De Wet Is Captured', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War and Revolution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T15:56:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c573a607-ec61-5a5a-8d02-3c5e25927a63', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c573a607-ec61-5a5a-8d02-3c5e25927a63'}, {'abstract': 'SugarString ran afoul of the public when The DailyDot reported in October that an editor recruiting journalists was warning them that the site would forbid reporting on “spying and net neutrality.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/business/media/verizon-shuts-down-sugarstring-technology-site.html', 'snippet': 'SugarString ran afoul of the public when The DailyDot reported in October that an editor recruiting journalists was warning them that the site would forbid reporting on “spying and net neutrality.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As journalism and corporate promotion merge, there have been many interesting experiments. Some work and some do not. This week one of the more controversial efforts, a site called SugarString which was backed by Verizon, was shut down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Verizon Shuts Down SugarString, Site That Had Drawn Journalistic Criticism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Net Neutrality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SugarString', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T15:57:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e877163a-06ee-50e9-9af3-4df8c67848c6', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e877163a-06ee-50e9-9af3-4df8c67848c6'}, {'abstract': 'The housing stock in Hartsdale, N.Y., about 20 miles north of Manhattan, runs the gamut from one-bedroom apartments to five-bedroom houses on nearly an acre.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/realestate/in-hartsdale-ny-everything-from-small-apartments-to-large-houses.html', 'snippet': 'The housing stock in Hartsdale, N.Y., about 20 miles north of Manhattan, runs the gamut from one-bedroom apartments to five-bedroom houses on nearly an acre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Jasleen Monga, a manager for a Chase bank branch in the village of Ardsley in lower Westchester, was searching for a home for herself “in a quiet and private neighborhood,” she said she never expected to find anything affordable within easy reach of her job.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/realestate/07LIVING/07LIVING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/07/realestate/07LIVING/07LIVING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/realestate/07LIVING/07LIVING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/realestate/07LIVING/07LIVING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/realestate/07LIVING/07LIVING-thumb