ppet': 'Nneka Okafor, starring in Katori Hall’s “Our Lady of Kibeho,” talks about her star turn, religious experiences and Texas cuisine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nneka Okafor kneels onstage at the Signature Theater, arms outstretched, mouth agape, entranced by a vision of the Virgin Mary. In Katori Hall’s “Our Lady of Kibeho,” Ms. Okafor’s professional stage debut, she plays Alphonsine Mumureke, one of three Rwandan schoolgirls who report Marian apparitions and dark prophecies a decade before the Rwandan genocide. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07SNAPSHOT/07SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1656, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07SNAPSHOT/07SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1656}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07SNAPSHOT/07SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 372, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07SNAPSHOT/07SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 743, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07SNAPSHOT/07SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07SNAPSHOT/07SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07SNAPSHOT/07SNAPSHOT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'hei