'A panel including Jules Feiffer and Art Spiegelman talks about art and aging.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Older can be better, and even a lot more fun, when it comes to the arts. This was the theme of “Old Masters,” a panel discussion presented by the Heyman Center for the Humanities at Columbia University on Tuesday night. The panelists were eminent: Art Spiegelman, the comic artist best known for the graphic novel “Maus”; Jules Feiffer, the cartoonist long associated with The Village Voice; and Alexander Melamid, the Russian conceptual artist, now involved in a project called the Art Healing Ministry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art From the Old School', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Booth, George', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feiffer, Jules', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jaffee, Al', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melamid, Alexander', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spiegelman, Art', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T21:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32265b7d-3ca6-57b2-9a45-3304807cbf11', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32265b7d-3ca6-57b2-9a45-3304807cbf11'}, {'abstract': 'The Toronto native with an eponymous cult jewelry line takes inspira