rnes and Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb6560a6-5c4b-55c9-91bc-d120b0f93876', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb6560a6-5c4b-55c9-91bc-d120b0f93876'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of companies, public interest groups and labor unions said the deal with Comcast would harm both consumers and competition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/business/media/coalition-formed-to-oppose-comcast-time-warner-cable-merger.html', 'snippet': 'A collection of companies, public interest groups and labor unions said the deal with Comcast would harm both consumers and competition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group of companies, public interest groups and labor unions have joined forces to urge regulators to reject Comcast’s proposed $45 billion merger with Time Warner Cable.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coalition Opposes Comcast-Time Warner Cable Merger', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coalition Opposes Comcast-Time Warner Cable Merger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Cable Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blaze, The', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DirecTV', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dish Network', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Writers Guild of America', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Glenn', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimmelman, Gene', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T21:29:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Steel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3885c6c6-1219-5b1d-8f19-f4b5e0da84ab', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3885c6c6-1219-5b1d-8f19-f4b5e0da84ab'}, {'abstract': 'The data on divorce aren’t perfect, but the three best sources all show that it has become less common.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/upshot/how-we-know-the-divorce-rate-is-falling.html', 'snippet': 'The data on divorce aren’t perfect, but the three best sources all show that it has become less common.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The divorce rate has been falling for more than three decades. That fact is not news, but it still surprises a lot of people. And so when Claire Cain Miller wrote about the trend for The Upshot this week, several readers asked for more detail, with some citing a Huffington Post article questioning the official Census Bureau data on the trends. As one of the researchers who has studied the issue, I thought it worth digging deeper into the data.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/upshot/04up-divorce/04up-divorce-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/04/upshot/04up-divorce/04up-divorce-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 443}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/upshot/04up-divorce/04up-divorce-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/upshot/04up-divorce/04up-divorce-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1513, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/upshot/04up-divorce/04up-divorce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/04/upshot/04up-divorce/04up-divorce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/upshot/04up-divorce/04up-divorce-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How We Know the Divorce Rate Is Falling', 'kicker': 'Happily Ever After', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statistics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T21:31:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'Justin Wolfers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolfers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2ca6edc-fe63-58db-8b5a-8e994aa1f6f5', 'word_count': 1653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2ca6edc-fe63-58db-8b5a-8e994aa1f6f5'}, {'abstract': 'Catherine McNeur’s “Taming Manhattan: Environmental Battles in the Antebellum City” recounts the battles over old New York’s barnyard conditions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/books/taming-manhattan-catherine-mcneurs-environmental-history.html', 'snippet': 'Catherine McNeur’s “Taming Manhattan: Environmental Battles in the Antebellum City” recounts the battles over old New York’s barnyard conditions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Travel with me all you Red Hook farmers and Inwood foragers, you artisanal visionaries of Quooklyn, to a time and place called antebellum Manhattan, a city that’s less an urban jungle than an urban barnyard, famous the world over for its filth. Hogs and dogs roam free, eating garbage that nobody bothers to collect; “hogtown” (today, roughly, the billionaires’ enclave of 57th Street) welcomes the intrepid visitor with the smell of boiling porcine remains. Distillery discharge is recycled as feed for cows, who produce a bluish “swill milk.” Human waste is claimed by companies that turn “night soil” into fertilizer. The city is green. But it is also brown.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 767}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1531, 'width': 1198, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Streets of Gold? Sure Smelled Like Something Else', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Streets of Gold? Sure Smelled Like Something Else', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nazaryan, Alexander', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeur, Catherine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Taming Manhattan: Environmental Battles in the Antebellum City (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T21:37:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Nazaryan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nazaryan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b6c2ce5-dfd5-5247-8892-0834297f9d59', 'word_count': 1111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b6c2ce5-dfd5-5247-8892-0834297f9d59'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers used highly sophisticated sensors to map Old Sarum, an 11th-century town near Stonehenge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/world/europe/without-lifting-a-shovel-archaeologists-survey-a-medieval-town-in-britain.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers used highly sophisticated sensors to map Old Sarum, an 11th-century town near Stonehenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Without any digging and using highly sophisticated sensors, British researchers have produced a detailed plan of an 11th-century town near Stonehenge that shows the locations of individual residential and industrial buildings, like kilns and furnaces.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shovels Untouched, Archaeologists Survey a Medieval Town in Britain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shovels Untouched, Archaeologists Survey a Medieval Town in Britain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle Ages (Historical Period)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Southampton', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T21:47:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d306e2f8-dd04-5893-95b3-03f7b30b89e8', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d306e2f8-dd04-5893-95b3-03f7b30b89e8'}, {'abstract': 'Falls Park became a spark for a pedestrian-friendly city center when it opened in 2004.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/travel/opening-the-gate-to-a-vibrant-main-street-in-greenville-sc.html', 'snippet': 'Falls Park became a spark for a pedestrian-friendly city center when it opened in 2004.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in 1998, few could have imagined Greenville’s transformation when Mayor Knox White began selling the idea of a park on Main Street incorporating the Reedy River’s 40-foot waterfall. Falls Park became a spark for a pedestrian-friendly city center when it opened in 2004. Last year, the newly \xaderected One building — located at 1 Main Street — provided yet another stamp of validation and a new home for high-end retailers to complement an already dense selection of restaurants, cafes and shops. “Main Street was not an attractive destination,” the mayor said. “Today, it’s the most vibrant place in the region.”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/travel/07-surfacing-sub-park/07-surfacing-sub-park-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/07/travel/07-surfacing-sub-park/07-surfacing-sub-park-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/travel/07-surfacing-sub-park/07-surfacing-sub-park-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/travel/07-surfacing-sub-park/07-surfacing-sub-park-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/travel/07-surfacing-sub-park/07-surfacing-sub-park-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/07/travel/07-surfacing-sub-park/07-surfacing-sub-park-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/travel/07-surfacing-sub-park/07-surfacing-sub-park-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Opening the Gate to a Vibrant Main Street in Greenville, S.C.', 'kicker': '5 Places', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Opening the Gate to a Vibrant Main Street', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crevar, Alex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenville (SC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T21:48:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Crevar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crevar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71c5b7f6-7cf9-5002-aa7e-5ea438367cf6', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71c5b7f6-7cf9-5002-aa7e-5ea438367cf6'}, {'abstract': 'Annaleigh Ashford juggles a cabaret act at 54 Below with her Broadway role in “You Can’t Take It With You” and her TV role as Betty in “Masters of Sex.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/arts/music/annaleigh-ashford-at-54-below.html', 'snippet': 'Annaleigh Ashford juggles a cabaret act at 54 Below with her Broadway role in “You Can’t Take It With You” and her TV role as Betty in “Masters of Sex.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Annaleigh Ashford is in a lineage of fearlessly saucy entertainers who seem born to conquer. The persona she inhabits in her show, “Lost in the Stars.” which opened at 54 Below on Monday evening, is a classic archetype: a glittery comedic showgirl who is nobody’s fool. The tradition embraces Jean Harlow, Judy Holliday, Cyndi Lauper and countless other wised-up kooks whose antics camouflage hearts of tarnished gold. Her tough-cookie voice perfectly matches her image as a mouthy, outspoken disco doll at the center of the party. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/ASHFORD/ASHFORD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/ASHFORD/ASHFORD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/ASHFORD/ASHFORD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/ASHFORD/ASHFORD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/ASHFORD/ASHFORD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/ASHFORD/ASHFORD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/ASHFORD/ASHFORD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Saucy Persona, Peppered With Wisdom ', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Saucy Persona, Peppered With Wisdom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashford, Annaleigh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '54 Below (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T21:48:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ffb93df-ca16-5c55-a9c0-97d673380e02', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ffb93df-ca16-5c55-a9c0-97d673380e02'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities charged the politician, María Corina Machado, with taking part in a plot to assassinate President Nicolás Maduro, but they did not make evidence public.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/world/americas/venezuela-assassination-plot-maduro-machado.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities charged the politician, María Corina Machado, with taking part in a plot to assassinate President Nicolás Maduro, but they did not make evidence public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela — The authorities in Venezuela charged a leading opposition politician on Wednesday with taking part in a plot to assassinate President Nicolás Maduro. The politician, María Corina Machado, was informed of the charge in a meeting with prosecutors but was not detained. The national prosecutor’s office said in a statement on its website that Ms. Machado was charged with conspiracy and that, if found guilty, she could be sentenced to eight to 16 years in prison.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuelan Opposition Politician Charged in Plot to Kill President', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Opposition Politician Is Charged in Assassination Plot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Machado, Maria Corina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maduro, Nicolas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T21:50:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f48a0940-b471-5895-9d40-ea1dafa442ce', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f48a0940-b471-5895-9d40-ea1dafa442ce'}, {'abstract': 'Doug Varone and Dancers bring a world and a New York premiere to the Joyce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/arts/doug-varone-and-company-with-eddie-taketa-at-the-joyce.html', 'snippet': 'Doug Varone and Dancers bring a world and a New York premiere to the Joyce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Doug Varone’s ornate movement tends to crackle like electricity: Churning this way and that, it appears to be propelled less by muscles and bones than by centrifugal force. Dancers run backward in semicircles, pause as if in mid-thought and, led by a swinging arm, carry on in the opposite direction. Mr. Varone’s dances, in other words, can be seriously windswept. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/VARONE2/VARONE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 953, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/VARONE2/VARONE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 953}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/VARONE2/VARONE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 645, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/VARONE2/VARONE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1290, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/VARONE2/VARONE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/04/arts/VARONE2/VARONE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': N