hat the balance of loans delinquent 60 days increased 27 percent, to roughly $4 billion, in the third quarter from the same period a year ago.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/03/more-borrowers-fall-behind-on-car-payments-report-shows/', 'snippet': 'The credit and research firm Experian said that the balance of loans delinquent 60 days increased 27 percent, to roughly $4 billion, in the third quarter from the same period a year ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An increasing number of borrowers are falling behind on their car payments, even as the total amount of outstanding debt reaches new heights, according to the latest report by Experian, the credit and research firm.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/business/dbpix-autos/dbpix-autos-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/04/business/dbpix-autos/dbpix-autos-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 342}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/business/dbpix-autos/dbpix-autos-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/business/dbpix-autos/dbpix-autos-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1168, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/business/dbpix-autos/dbpix-autos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/04/business/dbpix-autos/dbpix-autos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/business/dbpix-autos/dbpix-autos-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Borrowers Fall Behind on Car Payments, Report Shows', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Auto Delinquents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Experian Group Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T22:27:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Corkery and Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corkery', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7d46a3e-1bd5-558b-ba69-88a6fde355d7', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7d46a3e-1bd5-558b-ba69-88a6fde355d7'}, {'abstract': 'Plans for a mission in the island nation of São Tomé and Príncipe aim to foster defense cooperation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/world/americas/brazil-plans-naval-mission-in-africa.html', 'snippet': 'Plans for a mission in the island nation of São Tomé and Príncipe aim to foster defense cooperation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO DE JANEIRO — The Brazilian Navy has said that it will establish a naval mission in São Tomé and Príncipe, the small African island nation in the Gulf of Guinea. The mission, created in November and announced on Wednesday on Twitter by Brazil’s government, will involve a survey of the needs of São Tomé and Príncipe’s coast guard with the aim of fostering defense cooperation between the two countries, said Júlio Soares de Moura Neto, the commander of the Brazilian Navy. The move in São Tomé and Príncipe, a former Portuguese colony, reflects Brazil’s ambitions of increasing its influence in Africa by building on linguistic and cultural ties. Brazil has been training a small number of military personnel from São Tomé and Príncipe, and donating boats to its coast guard.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil Plans Naval Mission in Africa', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazil: New Naval Mission in Africa Aims to Foster Ties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Guinea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T22:27:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8916307a-9690-52e5-a1c6-81003457211f', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8916307a-9690-52e5-a1c6-81003457211f'}, {'abstract': 'The White House says President Obama met with Hillary Rodham Clinton in the Oval Office for about an hour this afternoon for a “general check-in.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/12/03/an-unscheduled-obama-clinton-meeting/', 'snippet': 'The White House says President Obama met with Hillary Rodham Clinton in the Oval Office for about an hour this afternoon for a “general check-in.”', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Unscheduled Obama-Clinton Meeting', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T22:29:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03099840-fa65-5ba6-a743-9b82dabf95f2', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03099840-fa65-5ba6-a743-9b82dabf95f2'}, {'abstract': 'After 46 years, Michael P. Price is stepping down as executive director of Goodspeed Musicals in Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/theater/michael-price-prepares-to-leave-goodspeed-musicals.html', 'snippet': 'After 46 years, Michael P. Price is stepping down as executive director of Goodspeed Musicals in Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST HADDAM, Conn. — The first time Michael P. Price went to work at Goodspeed Opera House, during its inaugural season in 1963, things didn’t go so well. Fresh out of the Yale School of Drama, he was a young, brash production manager, and he lasted all of four months before he was fired.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bowing Out? Bet Your Bottom Dollar ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bowing Out? Bet Your Bottom Dollar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Price, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goodspeed Musicals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goodspeed Opera House', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'ANNIE (PLAY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T22:31:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Collins-Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins-Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03c3a210-23cf-5042-82ad-2f1ee9f69055', 'word_count': 1703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03c3a210-23cf-5042-82ad-2f1ee9f69055'}, {'abstract': 'Two Israeli men were wounded in an attack in a West Bank supermarket, and the suspect was shot and wounded by an off-duty guard who was shopping there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/world/middleeast/palestinian-teenager-accused-of-stabbing-2-israelis.html', 'snippet': 'Two Israeli men were wounded in an attack in a West Bank supermarket, and the suspect was shot and wounded by an off-duty guard who was shopping there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — A Palestinian teenager stabbed two middle-age Israeli men at a supermarket in the occupied West Bank on Wednesday afternoon, the Israeli police said, wounding them moderately before being shot by an off-duty security guard who was shopping there.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinian Teenager Accused of Stabbing 2 Israelis', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Israelis Stabbed in West Bank', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T22:34:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20265ffa-2625-5c62-bab2-94d07a6775e3', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20265ffa-2625-5c62-bab2-94d07a6775e3'}, {'abstract': 'An urbane take on the holiday sweater cliché; a style tip from a “Hunger Games” actor; Shinola makes a sweatshirt; and the newest face to embrace Helvetica.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/fashion/shinolas-first-clothing-line-not-so-ugly-christmas-sweaters-and-more-mens-holiday-shopping.html', 'snippet': 'An urbane take on the holiday sweater cliché; a style tip from a “Hunger Games” actor; Shinola makes a sweatshirt; and the newest face to embrace Helvetica.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ugly Christmas sweater, with its cast of reindeer, snowmen and elves, is so much a part of the visual language of the season that puckish hosts even specify it as mandatory for their parties. The British designer Margaret Howell, whose men’s collections are sophisticated studies in restraint, isn’t the sort to send effusively decorated red-and-green knits down the runway, but in her fall show, there was what could be considered an antler-free take on the cliché sweater. Minimal and monochromatic, the urbane pullover, and the others here, are appropriate for a holiday party and any other day of winter.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/fashion/04BROWSE_COMBO/04BROWSE_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/04/fashion/04BROWSE_COMBO/04BROWSE_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 638}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/fashion/04BROWSE_COMBO/04BROWSE_COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 963, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/fashion/04BROWSE_COMBO/04BROWSE_COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1926, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/fashion/04BROWSE_COMBO/04BROWSE_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/04/fashion/04BROWSE_COMBO/04BROWSE_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':