 {'abstract': 'Louis Segna, who was convicted in August of falsely reporting emergencies, like explosions and death threats, received six months in jail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/nyregion/brooklyn-man-sentenced-for-making-false-reports-to-911.html', 'snippet': 'Louis Segna, who was convicted in August of falsely reporting emergencies, like explosions and death threats, received six months in jail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man who was a familiar presence at the 94th Precinct Community Council was sentenced Wednesday to six months in jail for making a number of 911 calls reporting fake emergencies in Williamsburg, Brooklyn.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brooklyn Man Sentenced for Making False Reports to 911', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Gets 6 Months for False 911 Reports', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clifford, Stephanie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Segna, Louis (1961- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nine-One-One (911) (Emergency Phone Number)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-03T22:43:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8771516b-2631-5a3c-8fbf-f5425d2781a1', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8771516b-2631-5a3c-8fbf-f5425d2781a1'}, {'abstract': 'Frank and Ross debate Christopher Nolan’s politics and swap some favorite performances (Rene Russo and Benedict Cumberbatch). And one columnist wants Nolan to stop letting his pretensions get in the way of his adventures.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/03/are-the-oscars-going-to-heaven-interstellar-or-to-earth-birdman/', 'snippet': 'Frank and Ross debate Christopher Nolan’s politics and swap some favorite performances (Rene Russo and Benedict Cumberbatch). And one columnist wants Nolan to stop letting his pretensions get in the way of his adventures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Douthat: It’s a pleasure to be back with you, here in the fall movie season’s eye-of-the-storm moment, when we get a chance to take a breath and catch up on all the prestige movies released before Thanksgiving — or, you know, take the kids to “Penguins of Madagascar,” depending — before the Christmas hurricane arrives. And I’m going to start us off by talking about the biggest, most ambitious and in certain ways the most political of the fall releases that made landfall last month: Christopher Nolan’s “Interstellar.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/opinion/nyto-movie1/nyto-movie1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/03/opinion/nyto-movie1/nyto-movie1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/opinion/nyto-movie1/nyto-movie1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/opinion/nyto-movie1/nyto-movie1-superJumbo.jpg', 'heigh