by Vettery, a start-up recruiting firm. That level exceeded the 27.5 percent of junior bankers who stayed in the same group at their bank, Vettery said. The data, which covers about 1,400 analysts, sheds more light on a recruiting race that begins for so-called analysts soon after they start work at investment banks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Young Bankers Flock to Private Equity', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T12:48:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e769fb6a-821f-54a9-9109-b028b2a1d0c4', 'word_count': 2036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e769fb6a-821f-54a9-9109-b028b2a1d0c4'}, {'abstract': 'The questions are growing more urgent over how much longer the European Central Bank can merely hint at actions to come before markets lose faith in it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/business/international/ecb-rate-announcement-draghi.html', 'snippet': 'The questions are growing more urgent over how much longer the European Central Bank can merely hint at actions to come before markets lose faith in it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — Mario Draghi wanted everyone to understand on Thursday that the European Central Bank was determined to honor its prime directive: keeping inflation, now dangerously low, in check.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/business/05eurates-pic2/05eurates-pic2-articleLar