nergies instead to the fraternal assistance of the developing countries.”\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Dec. 5, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Pope Asks  to End Arms Race', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMS CONTROL AND LIMITATION AND DISARMAMENT', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Popes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T12:55:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2afa8c94-bb60-5d89-8e9f-796a0d16b217', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2afa8c94-bb60-5d89-8e9f-796a0d16b217'}, {'abstract': 'The Chinese system has become the third, after GPS and Russia’s Global Navigation Satellite System, recognized by the United Nations body that sets standards for international shipping.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/a-step-forward-for-beidou-chinas-satellite-navigation-system/', 'snippet': 'The Chinese system has become the third, after GPS and Russia’s Global Navigation Satellite System, recognized by the United Nations body that sets standards for international shipping.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China’s own satellite navigation system has won a stamp of approval from an international maritime body, an important step toward its goal of global acceptance for its answer to the United States’ Global Positioning System (GPS).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype':