 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2048e989-2cce-513d-9b24-a46fc320b5dc', 'word_count': 1006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2048e989-2cce-513d-9b24-a46fc320b5dc'}, {'abstract': 'In the U.S., paid parental leave is more of a perk than a guarantee.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/facts-s-unique-take-on-maternity-leave/', 'snippet': 'In the U.S., paid parental leave is more of a perk than a guarantee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday the Supreme Court heard a pregnancy discrimination case. As The Guardian points out, the U.S. is an outlier when it comes to paid parental leave.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facts & Figures: America’s Unique Take on Maternity Leave', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T16:45:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c10f064-679a-5b5c-acbb-1e901b6d7a94', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c10f064-679a-5b5c-acbb-1e901b6d7a94'}, {'abstract': 'Despite fierce competition, Ben Okri wins the award, issued by The Literary Review, with a passage from “The Age of Magic.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/a-booker-prize-winners-latest-laurel-bad-sex-in-fiction-award/', 'snippet': 'Despite fierce competition, Ben Okri wins the award, issued by The Literary Review, with a passage from “The Age of Magic.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Richard Flanagan, this year’s Man Booker Prize winner, was a finalist. So were Michael Cunningham, Haruki Murakami and Wilbur Smith. But they were beaten out by Ben Okri for The Literary Review’s Bad Sex in Fiction award, presented on Wednesday evening at the In & Out (Naval and Military Club)  here.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Booker Prize Winner’s Latest Laurel: Bad Sex in Fiction Award', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Earth Doesn’t Quite Move', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Man Booker Prize', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flanagan, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murakami, Haruki', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Okri, Ben', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Literary Review, The', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T16:49:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a7c9a76-d0af-5361-abdc-ed773c4503a1', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a7c9a76-d0af-5361-abdc-ed773c4503a1'}, {'abstract': 'Judith Scott, who was born with Down syndrome, created sculptures from objects swathed in cloth and twine, the subject of a show at the Brooklyn Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/arts/design/judith-scotts-enigmatic-sculptures-at-the-brooklyn-museum.html', 'snippet': 'Judith Scott, who was born with Down syndrome, created sculptures from objects swathed in cloth and twine, the subject of a show at the Brooklyn Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judith Scott’s sculptures sit like large, unopened, possibly unopenable bundles, contents unknown, in the Elizabeth A. Sackler Center for Feminist Art at the Brooklyn Museum. In a few, objects can be made out under layers of tightly bound string, rope and fabric strips: a child’s chair, wire hangers, and in one ambitious instance a not-at-all disguised shopping cart. Some pieces suggest the contours of musical instruments, or weapons, or tools. Most are irregularly rounded and sheathed in bright-color yarn. All untitled, they look like gift-wrapped boulders, though it’s hard to gauge their weight or what they might feel like to the touch. Heavy or light? Soft or hard? ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Silence Wrapped in Eloquent Cocoons ', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Silence Wrapped in Eloquent Cocoons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Judith (1943-2005)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Down Syndrome', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Higgs, Matthew', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Catherine J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T16:53:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/41b34f2d-6ff8-5f37-87c3-9750256eeb4f', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41b34f2d-6ff8-5f37-87c3-9750256eeb4f'}, {'abstract': 'Seahawks quarterback Russell Wilson was inconsistent earlier this season, but he has averaged 21 fantasy points per game over the last four weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/sports/football/100000003269454/fantasy-football-picks-for-week-14.html', 'snippet': 'Seahawks quarterback Russell Wilson was inconsistent earlier this season, but he has averaged 21 fantasy points per game over the last four weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seahawks quarterback Russell Wilson was inconsistent earlier this season, but he has averaged 21 fantasy points per game over the last four weeks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/multimedia/fantasy-week14/fantasy-week14-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/03/multimedia/fantasy-week14/fantasy-week14-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/multimedia/fantasy-week14/fantasy-week14-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/multimedia/fantasy-week14/fantasy-week14-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1432, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 