 'nyt://video/50f7ddd0-63cb-5841-aa4c-6ff5f859c534'}, {'abstract': 'Not quite as simple as it seems.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/a-note-on-oil-prices-and-the-economy/', 'snippet': 'Not quite as simple as it seems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I may be doing some media where people will ask me about what the oil plunge means for the US economy, so I thought I’d spend a bit of time figuring out what if anything I might say that’s interesting. And it does seem to me that there’s a bit more to the story than a casual pass might suggest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Note on Oil Prices and the Economy', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T17:28:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86a79d39-d984-53d3-81ce-d3aa4155157b', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86a79d39-d984-53d3-81ce-d3aa4155157b'}, {'abstract': 'Gardiner Harris, a Times correspondent in India, writes about visiting a neonatal intensive care unit in Gurgaon and covering the health of children in the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/12/04/the-perils-of-being-born-infant-deaths-in-india/', 'snippet': 'Gardiner Harris, a Times correspondent in India, writes about visiting a neonatal intensive care unit in Gurgaon and covering the health of children in the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Thursday’s Times, Gardiner Harris reports on a deadly epidemic that is quietly sweeping India; among its victims are tens of thousands of newborns who are dying because once-miraculous cures no longer work. Here, Mr. Harris describes his jarring visit to an undersupplied hospital in India.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/blogs/india/india-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/04/blogs/india/india-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/blogs/india/india-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/blogs/india/india-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/blogs/india/india-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/04/blogs/india/india-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/blogs/india/india-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Perils of Being Born: Infant Deaths in India', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Gardiner', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T17:31:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44c2b383-ce47-5890-ac3c-5d45b3f24242', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44c2b383-ce47-5890-ac3c-5d45b3f24242'}, {'abstract': 'Lisa Bielawa’s latest work, “Vireo: The Spiritual Biography of a Witch’s Accuser,” will be recorded before live audiences and delivered in a series of episodes over two years.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/an-opera-offered-on-the-installment-plan/', 'snippet': 'Lisa Bielawa’s latest work, “Vireo: The Spiritual Biography of a Witch’s Accuser,” will be recorded before live audiences and delivered in a series of episodes over two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For opera critics pondering the future of the form, the composer Lisa Bielawa’s latest work, “Vireo: The Spiritual Biography of a Witch’s Accuser,” offers a new twist. The work is a serial opera – serial in the television sense, not in the 12-tone sense – and although it will be filmed before live audiences, it is meant to be seen on television or online, in short installments that will be released over two years. The production will also include online extras, including video clips that look at the process of composing and staging the piece.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Opera Offered on the Installment Plan', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Opera Offered on the Installment Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bielawa, Lisa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T17:32:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e24780c-2ceb-53eb-b9f4-25221fde6891', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e24780c-2ceb-53eb-b9f4-25221fde6891'}, {'abstract': 'Janet Yellen as Little Miss Muffet? Mario Draghi and Angela Merkel acting as Punch and Judy? No one is off limits for Bill Gross.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/bill-gross-muses-on-nursery-rhymes-and-domestic-abuse-in-latest-investment-letter/', 'snippet': 'Janet Yellen as Little Miss Muffet? Mario Draghi and Angela Merkel acting as Punch and Judy? No one is off limits for Bill Gross.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Gross, during his reign as chief investment officer of the mutual fund giant Pimco, was known as much for his zany market commentary as for his bond investing abilities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/business/dbpix-bill-gross/dbpix-bill-gross-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/05/business/dbpix-bill-gross/dbpix-bill-gross-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/business/dbpix-bill-gross/dbpix-bill-gross-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJ