alifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71f7d92a-7fb0-5a6a-87e1-9ac8f07cdb92', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71f7d92a-7fb0-5a6a-87e1-9ac8f07cdb92'}, {'abstract': 'Officials, using data from birth certificates, said there were 3.93 million births in 2013, down slightly from 3.95 million in 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/us/us-sees-decline-in-births-for-sixth-year.html', 'snippet': 'Officials, using data from birth certificates, said there were 3.93 million births in 2013, down slightly from 3.95 million in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The number of women in the United States who gave birth dropped last year, according to federal statistics released Thursday, extending the decline for a sixth year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Birthrate Declines for Sixth Consecutive Year; Economy Could Be Factor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Birthrate Declines for Sixth Consecutive Year; Economy Could Be Factor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Rates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Center for Health Statistics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T18:46:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7a179f2-9708-5650-be4c-5851a10f7aea', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7a179f2-9708-5650-be4c-5851a10f7aea'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Garner’s death and the balance between liberty and order.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/our-police-problem/', 'snippet': 'Eric Garner’s death and the balance between liberty and order.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, I wrote about my worry that the way the Ferguson story had turned out, with a widening gap between the activist narrative and the seeming facts, might end up setting back the possibilities for right-left\xa0consensus on criminal justice reform. Yesterday, as if in some malign answer\xa0to that concern, a Staten Island grand jury declined to indict, on any charge, the policeman whose chokehold — caught on video —\xa0on an unarmed man\xa0being detained on suspicion of selling loose cigarettes led to his asphyxiation, cardiac arrest\xa0and death. And in this case, unlike the non-indictment of the Ferguson cop, the shocked/troubled response to the non-indictment has spanned the partisan divide. (For a range of views from people in various ways on the “right,” I recommend reading\xa0Sean Davis, Russell Moore, Pete Wehner, John Podhoretz, Rod Dreher, Glenn Beck, Peter Suderman,\xa0and even the not-exactly-a-civil-libertarian\xa0Andrew McCarthy.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Police Problem', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T18:53:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e30c3093-4fbe-5cb5-bca2-f0c9992f5b4d', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e30c3093-4fbe-5cb5-bca2-f0c9992f5b4d'}, {'abstract': 'Skier Nick McNutt burst onto the scene this year because of his progressive skiing, including his prowess at landing “switch,” or backwards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/sports/video-rookie-skier-impresses-sports-best.html', 'snippet': 'Skier Nick McNutt burst onto the scene this year because of his progressive skiing, including his prowess at landing “switch,” or backwards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What does it take to impress some of the best skiers in the world? Ask British Columbia native Nick McNutt, whose abilities are taking the skiing world by storm. McNutt, who was previously named rookie of the year, is a nominee for male performance of the year at this year’s Powder Awards, one of skiing’s highest accolades.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Rookie Skier Impresses Sport’s Best', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Teton Gravity Research', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Whistler (British Columbia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNutt, Nick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T18:54:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39ac8a25-bf3d-5161-b38e-1591f6ed586e', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39ac8a25-bf3d-5161-b38e-1591f6ed586e'}, {'abstract': 'Environmental concerns have led San Jose to clear a vast homeless camp, but in one of the nation’s priciest housing markets, not everyone has a place to go.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/us/driven-from-silicon-valleys-jungle-homeless-face-limited-options.html', 'snippet': 'Environmental concerns have led San Jose to clear a vast homeless camp, but in one of the nation’s priciest housing markets, not everyone has a place to go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN JOSE, Calif. — The makeshift tents and debris stretching for nearly a mile along a creek in San Jose are partly obscured from the view of drivers on a nearby road. But this homeless camp in the heart of Silicon Valley — a full 68 acres of mismatched belongings, shopping carts, clotheslines and wooden shanties — is widely seen as the nation’s largest.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Few Options for Homeless as San Jose Clears Camp', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Few Options for Homeless as San Jose Clears Camp', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Jose (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 