d by Jules Verne’s “Around the World in 80 Days,” will open next fall, with previews in the spring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lincoln Center’s educational department has commissioned an original theater work specifically for children on the autism spectrum, Russell Granet, the executive director of Lincoln Center Education said on Thursday. The work, “Up and Away,” was conceived and created by the Trusty Sidekick Theater Company, a troupe known for its family productions, and is inspired by Jules Verne’s “Around the World in 80 Days.” The production is scheduled to open in the fall of 2015. Lincoln Center will present preview performances April 29 to May 3 at the Clark Studio Theater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln Center Plans a Theater Work for Children With Autism', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trusty Sidekick Theater Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T19:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19ed0502-e4ce-5654-83ed-727bd3ddf5ad', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19ed0502-e4ce-5654-83ed-727bd3ddf5ad'}, {'abstract': '“Biograph, Last Year…” by the performance artists Iver Findlay and Marit Sandsmark explores the meaning of memory in the age of the selfie.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/04/biograph-last-year-findlay-sandsmark/', 'snippet': '“Biograph, Last Year…” by the performance artists Iver Findlay and Marit Sandsmark explores the meaning of memory in the age of the selfie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our sped-up Internet culture, in which today’s viral memes quickly become tomorrow’s misty watercolor memories, “nostalgia is on fast-forward,” according to the American theater artist Iver Findlay, a Wooster Group alum who helms the Norway-based performance company Findlay//Sandsmark with his Norwegian wife, Marit Sandsmark. Today through Sunday, the pair joins a few friends at Abrons Arts Center to perform in the show named, in part, “Biograph, Last Year” (the rest of the title is unpublishable), a collage of contemporary dance and both live and recorded audio and video that aims to explore how we experience nostalgia — that most unreliable of emotions — in an era in which events take on a those-were-the-days patina after a mere few years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Multimedia Show Explores Nostalgia, Moment by Moment', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABRONS ARTS CENTER', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T19:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb34348e-be9e-5778-9932-1e500424e433', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb34348e-be9e-5778-9932-1e500424e433'}, {'abstract': 'Samanthan Power, the United States general ambassador to the United Nations, is also a Red Sox fan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/12/04/verbatim-pressing-issues/', 'snippet': 'Samanthan Power, the United States general ambassador to the United Nations, is also a Red Sox fan.', 'lead_paragraph': '— Samantha Power, the American ambassador to the United Nations, referring to one of the most sought-after free agents of the baseball off-season, former Red Sox pitcher Jon Lester. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Verbatim: Pressing Issues', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T19:02:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55392878-e86b-5272-bdda-cabd87507a6b', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55392878-e86b-5272-bdda-cabd87507a6b'}, {'abstract': 'The nonprofit organization links students with drivers who have a thorough knowledge of the American landscape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/automobiles/trucker-buddy-international-makes-pen-pals-of-students-and-truckers.html', 'snippet': 'The nonprofit organization links students with drivers who have a thorough knowledge of the American landscape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not uncommon for adults to criticize school-age children over their lack of geographical knowledge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/automobiles/05TRUCKER-image2/05TRUCKER-image2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 581, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/