 Valerie Van Cleve, “Poverty Inc.” finds modern-day slavery and indentured servitude spawned by corporate practices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/movies/poverty-inc-paints-a-bleak-picture-of-life-after-2008.html', 'snippet': 'A documentary by Gary Null and Valerie Van Cleve, “Poverty Inc.” finds modern-day slavery and indentured servitude spawned by corporate practices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world map in “Poverty Inc.” stands out. Corporation names — Monsanto, Merck, Halliburton, Coca-Cola and Koch — are in giant letters where country names would normally be.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Corporate Creation of a New Class Structure', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Corporate Creation of a New Class Structure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Anita', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Null, Gary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Van Cleve, Valerie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Poverty, Inc. (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T22:46:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4421c068-a8dc-5db6-b134-3965ccddcb29', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4421c068-a8dc-5db6-b134-3965ccddcb29'}, {'abstract': '“Selected Stories,” at the Kitchen in Chelsea, includes homemade films, in which Lutz makes cameos as a tiny figure dressed in white.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/arts/design/klaus-lutz-selected-stories.html', 'snippet': '“Selected Stories,” at the Kitchen in Chelsea, includes homemade films, in which Lutz makes cameos as a tiny figure dressed in white.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Swiss-born artist Klaus Lutz (1940-2009) moved to New York in 1993 and stayed to the end of his life.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05LUTZ-GALLERY3/LUTZ-GALLERY3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 483, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05LUTZ-GALLERY3/LUTZ-GALLERY3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 483}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05LUTZ-GALLERY3/LUTZ-GALLERY3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 825, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05LUTZ-GALLERY3/LUTZ-GALLERY3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1650, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05LUTZ-GALLERY3/LUTZ-GALLERY3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05LUTZ-GALLERY3/LUTZ-GALLERY3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05LUTZ-GALLERY3/LUTZ-GALLERY3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbL