g head-to-head with Picasso shows: “Picasso and Jacqueline: The Evolution of Style,” at the Pace Gallery, and “Picasso and the Camera,” at Gagosian. But this occasion isn’t exactly the anticipated lively duel. Both exhibitions suffer from a kind of muse fatigue: The Pace show explores the impact of Picasso’s last companion and second wife, Jacqueline Roque, and the Gagosian show often relies on Picasso’s wives and girlfriends to give shape to its overly broad, amorphous theme.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05PICASSO1/PICASSO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05PICASSO1/PICASSO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 819}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05PICASSO1/PICASSO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 751, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05PICASSO1/PICASSO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1501, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05PICASSO1/PICASSO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05PICASSO1/PICASSO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05PICASSO1/PICASSO1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', '