 christened his new work just that? In “This,” an austere yet airy dance performed Wednesday at New York Live Arts, there is not just one object, but many. They come in forms of movement, courtesy of four dancers. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05NEIL/NEIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05NEIL/NEIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05NEIL/NEIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05NEIL/NEIL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05NEIL/NEIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05NEIL/NEIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05NEIL/NEIL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Defying Obvious Meanings ', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defying Obvious Meanings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenberg, Neil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Live Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T23:46:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/44faaee4-db55-5c9a-a90a-9af6fec6e80c', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44faaee4-db55-5c9a-a90a-9af6fec6e80c'}, {'abstract': 'A lesbian prostitute and her heterosexual mentor in sex work experience comic adventures around New York in “The Foxy Merkins,” which has the tone of an absurdist buddy comedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/movies/the-foxy-merkins-a-satirical-buddy-comedy.html', 'snippet': 'A lesbian prostitute and her heterosexual mentor in sex work experience comic adventures around New York in “The Foxy Merkins,” which has the tone of an absurdist buddy comedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Margaret (Lisa Haas), the heroine of Madeleine Olnek’s sly, loose-jointed satire “The Foxy Merkins,” is probably no one’s idea of a lesbian prostitute, or a midnight cowgirl. Brand-new to New York, the stocky, bespectacled Margaret camps out in a restroom in the Port Authority Bus Terminal, where she sleeps, wrapped in clear plastic. But as she wanders the city, she is avidly cruised by closeted suburban women who ogle from their car windows and do double takes when they pass her on the sidewalk.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05FOXY/FOXY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'article