stated the criminal indictments of two men who were caught in a drug-and-gun sting operation. The panel, of the Ninth Circuit Court of Appeals, also granted the government’s request to reassign the case to a different trial judge.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federal Appeals Court Reinstates Indictments in a Drug-and-Gun Sting ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Federal Appeals Court Reinstates Indictments in a Drug-and-Gun Sting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Otis D II', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T23:56:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fde5ff6e-46ff-5af6-9620-0acb3245df0d', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fde5ff6e-46ff-5af6-9620-0acb3245df0d'}, {'abstract': 'In “Concerning Violence,” Goran Hugo Olsson uses archival clips, texts by the scholar Frantz Fanon and voice-overs by musicians to revisit anticolonialist struggles of the 20th century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/movies/concerning-violence-a-postcolonialist-montage.html', 'snippet': 'In “Concerning Violence,” Goran Hugo Olsson uses archival clips, texts by the scholar Frantz Fanon and voice-overs by musicians to revisit anticolonialist struggles of the 20th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can’t say that “Concerning Violence,” Goran Hugo Olsson’s found-footage essay, doesn’t warn you. Its affirming prologue, starring the critical theorist Gayatri Chakravorty Spivak, refers to the writings of the psychiatrist and philosopher Frantz Fanon as a “teaching text,” and what follows is a clip of soldiers in helicopters, gunning down cattle. True to form, this documentary is a didactic illustration of Fanon’s 1961 anticolonialist broadside, “The Wretched of the Earth,” abridged and sharpened to its ferocious point.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reverberations of a Subjugated Past ', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reverberations of a Subjugated Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olsson, Goran Hugo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fanon, Frantz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Concerning Violence (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T23:56:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicolas Rapold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicolas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rapold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/76856bb9-5023-57fe-a957-3a210f3b9cba', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76856bb9-5023-57fe-a957-3a210f3b9cba'}, {'abstract': 'A video for her song, written in response to the death of Eric Garner during an encounter with the police on Staten Island, combines photos of civil rights demonstrations from the past and present.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/nyregion/alicia-keys-with-garner-anthem-we-gotta-pray-pleads-for-peaceful-protests.html', 'snippet': 'A video for her song, written in response to the death of Eric Garner during an encounter with the police on Staten Island, combines photos of civil rights demonstrations from the past and present.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While Alicia Keys is known for her unabashed celebration of New York on Jay Z’s “Empire State of Mind,” she released another kind of anthem on Wednesday night: “We Gotta Pray,” which protests a Staten Island grand jury’s decision not to indict a New York police officer in the death of Eric Garner.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alicia Keys, With Garner Anthem ‘We Gotta Pray,’ Pleads for Peaceful Protests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Anthem, Singer Pleads for Strength', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keys, Alicia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-04T23:59:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew R. Chow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Chow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c678e0cc-57c2-5bc7-96f3-82e90d2292f2', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c678e0cc-57c2-5bc7-96f3-82e90d2292f2'}, {'abstract': '“A Spell to Ward Off the Darkness” harnesses the formal properties of film to ponder ways of engaging with the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/movies/metaphysical-moments-in-a-spell-to-ward-off-the-darkness.html', 'snippet': '“A Spell to Ward Off the Darkness” harnesses the formal properties of film to ponder ways of engaging with the world.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A Spell to Ward Off the Darkness” is a collaboration between two stalwarts of the experimental-film scene: the British director Ben Rivers (“Two Years at Sea”) and the American Ben Russell (“Let Each One Go Where He May”).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05ASPELL/ASPELL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05ASPELL/ASPELL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05ASPELL/ASPELL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05ASPELL/ASPELL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/05/arts/05ASPELL/ASPELL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': '