IN, Tex. — The elections are over. Campaign fund-raising is not. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Texas, a New Shopping Season: For Donors, Not Votes', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Shopping Season: For Donors, Not Votes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Straus, Joseph R III', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-05T01:20:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecce4c09-70ed-5581-96c2-d80093f50b4f', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecce4c09-70ed-5581-96c2-d80093f50b4f'}, {'abstract': 'New books about “The Great Gatsby” and Vanity Fair offer a chance for renewed consideration of the Jazz Age.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/books/review/so-we-read-on-and-bohemians-bootleggers-flappers-and-swells.html', 'snippet': 'New books about “The Great Gatsby” and Vanity Fair offer a chance for renewed consideration of the Jazz Age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Did the Jazz Age ever exist — apart from being a cultural construct, that is, a coinage credited to F. Scott Fitzgerald, and one that he had a singular role in characterizing (raccoon coats, bootleggers, bobs, cool cars, flappers in short skirts) by virtue of his novels, “This Side of Paradise” and “The Great Gatsby” in particular? Did the Lost Generation know it was lost any more than the Me Decade recognized its own solipsism or those who lived in the fin de siècle 1890s realized they were at the end of something? Decadology is an intriguing if somewhat arbitrary device, allowing us to view the preceding, largely amorphous segments of history as slim and discrete crosscuttings of time. Then again, not every cluster of 10 years lends itself to being named in an equivalently catchy way; the 1940s, although known as the War Years and the Duration, seemed to recede between the more emphatically summed-up “radical” ’30s and “quietist” ’50s.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/books/review/07MERKIN1/07MERKIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/07/books/review/07MERKIN1/07MERKIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 700}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/books/review/07MERKIN1/07MERKIN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 879, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/books/review/07MERKIN1/07MERKIN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1757, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/books/review/07MERKIN1/07MERKIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/