e where voters seem to be favoring Republicans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HAMMOND, La. — She has been rebuffed by her liberal colleagues in Washington and pilloried at home for voting with the president, and has watched helplessly while her Democratic base has eroded like a cheap levee.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Louisiana Runoff Election, Senator Landrieu Tries to Revive Her Base', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Louisiana, Dynasty Faces a Fateful Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landrieu, Mary L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cassidy, Bill (1957- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-05T01:38:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Fausset', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fausset', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32ed73e8-8ccd-5335-994f-740fcd991b79', 'word_count': 1323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32ed73e8-8ccd-5335-994f-740fcd991b79'}, {'abstract': 'Grand juries, like the one that declined to indict a police officer in the killing of Eric Garner on Staten Island, rarely indict in cases involving police officers who have killed civilians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/nyregion/police-violence-seems-to-result-in-no-punishment.html', 'snippet': 'Grand juries, like the one that declined to indict a police officer in the killing of Eric Garner on Staten Island, rarely indict in cases involving police officers who have killed civilians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a grand jury on Staten Island declined, on Wednesday, to indict Officer Daniel Pantaleo in the killing of Eric Garner, some critics blamed Staten Island itself, easily equating it with a culture of police coddling and conservatism. But grand juries, so willing to issue indictments in so many instances, rarely do so in cases involving police officers who have killed civilians. And they have failed to do so in far more liberal environments — in Manhattan, Brooklyn and the Bronx.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/nyregion/07BIG/07BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 329, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/07/nyregion/07BIG/07BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 329}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/nyregion/07BIG/07BIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 561, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/nyregion/07BIG/07BIG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1122, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/nyregion/07BIG/07BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75