ation of Anita Diamant’s novel about a biblical story, is being broadcast on Sunday and Monday on Lifetime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/06/arts/television/the-red-tent-imagines-the-life-of-dinah.html', 'snippet': '“The Red Tent,” a two-part adaptation of Anita Diamant’s novel about a biblical story, is being broadcast on Sunday and Monday on Lifetime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sunday and Monday would be good nights for the men of the world to go out somewhere. Anyplace that doesn’t have television. That way they won’t accidentally channel-surf their way into “The Red Tent,” a two-part adaptation of Anita Diamant’s novel being broadcast on Lifetime on those nights.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Biblical Girls’ Club ', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Biblical Girls’ Club', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lifetime Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferguson, Rebecca (1983- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diamant, Anita', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Red Tent (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Red Tent (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-05T21:37:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/82b30170-746f-55c9-8ded-3ba1e331b0a5', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82b30170-746f-55c9-8ded-3ba1e331b0a5'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Librarians,” a new TNT series, an underground trove of powerful artifacts is protected by a special team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/06/arts/television/the-librarians-on-tnt-charged-with-a-special-collection.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Librarians,” a new TNT series, an underground trove of powerful artifacts is protected by a special team.', 'lead_paragraph': '“So he got stabbed,” Jenkins says, shrugging off an injury to a librarian named Flynn Carsen. “Librarians get stabbed and shot and bitten and cursed all the time.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paper Cuts Don’t Faze Them', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paper Cuts Don’t Faze Them', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Turner Network Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Librarians (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-05T21:38:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4b5c4a6-a212-566e-8502-c82b1aed84aa', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4b5c4a6-a212-566e-8502-c82b1aed84aa'}, {'abstract': 'A duplex penthouse on the Upper East Side, with five bedrooms and views of Central Park, was the sale of the week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/realestate/upper-east-side-penthouse-for-227-million.html', 'snippet': 'A duplex penthouse on the Upper East Side, with five bedrooms and views of Central Park, was the sale of the week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sun-drenched duplex penthouse at the pinnacle of 135 East 79th Street, the stylish limestone-and-brick condominium developed by the Brodsky Organization and designed by William Sofield, sold for $22,705,312.50 and was the most expensive sale of the week, according to city records. The monthly carrying costs for the 5,429-square-foot residence, PH19W, originally listed at $26.5 million, are $16,562.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/realestate/07SUBTICKET/07TICKETSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/07/realestate/07SUBTICKET/07TICKETSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/realestate/07SUBTICKET/07TICKETSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/realestate/07SUBTICKET/07TICKETSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/realestate/07SUBTICKET/07TICKETSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/07/realestate/07SUBTICKET/07TICKETSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/realestate/07SUBTICKET/07TICK