/12/05/can-sarkozy-give-france-a-new-start/', 'snippet': 'Will Nicolas Sarkozy make a successful comeback in France? Observers have their doubts about him —\xa0and about the country’s leaders in general.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Sarko is back!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Sarkozy Give France a ‘New Start’?', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-05T22:23:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Guida', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Guida', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dddc1f0f-936b-50cd-b1f8-65d6957e3cf8', 'word_count': 1104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dddc1f0f-936b-50cd-b1f8-65d6957e3cf8'}, {'abstract': 'A win would be a huge boost for the Bengals because every team below them in the A.F.C. North has a winning record, leaving the Bengals little wiggle room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/sports/football/pittsburgh-steelers-at-cincinnati-bengals-matchup.html', 'snippet': 'A win would be a huge boost for the Bengals because every team below them in the A.F.C. North has a winning record, leaving the Bengals little wiggle room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steelers (7-5) at Bengals (8-3-1)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pittsburgh Steelers at Cincinnati Bengals Preview', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Bengals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-05T22:29:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d733a6aa-95ca-5dc5-9672-b079dff7e572', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d733a6aa-95ca-5dc5-9672-b079dff7e572'}, {'abstract': 'At this year’s stateside outpost of the Art Basel fair, several galleries are showing works that explore and parody the visual language of fashion magazines and catalogs.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/art-basel-miami-where-art-imitates-fashion/', 'snippet': 'At this year’s stateside outpost of the Art Basel fair, several galleries are showing works that explore and parody the visual language of fashion magazines and catalogs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art Basel in Miami Beach’s rap for being a decadent, image-obsessed orgy would be tough to disprove. However, there are a number of works on view in the week’s namesake fair — which is open until Sunday at the Miami Beach Convention Center — that simultaneously reify the glamour industry and parody it, co-opting the language of glossy magazines to present fashion portraits as art. At Berlin’s Société gallery in Art Basel’s Nova section (dedicated to “new” galleries), Timur Si-Qin’s light box of three sinewy youths in a bright, bucolic setting catches the lens in precisely the style of an Abercrombie & Fitch ad. The shot is blown up from Si-Qin’s artist book, which resembles a complete A&F catalog, replacing the iconic initials with his own yin-yang “peace” logo. Reena Spaulings Fine Art from New York has a number of works on view by the feminist provocateur K8 Hardy, including a large-scale reproduction of her underground zine from the early aughts, “Fashion Fashion,” inflecting the language of the women’s magazine with a post-riot-grrrl conceptual wit. Another Berlin gallery, Contemporary Fine Arts, is showing the largest cover among the three as a central feature of its booth. Not even for sale (or so the gallery says), Juergen Teller’s shot of Stella Tennant in men’s briefs, a hooded robe and trainers is intended to draw attention to the booth as much as to contribute to its context — a harmony heard loud and clear all around town.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/t-magazine/04trend-mcgarry/04trend-mcgarry-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/04/t-magazine/04trend-mcgarry/04trend-mcgarry-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/t-magazine/04trend-mcgarry/04trend-mcgarry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/t-magazine/04trend-mcgarry/04trend-mcgarry-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/t-magazine/04trend-mcgarry/04trend-mcgarry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/04/t-magazine/04trend-mcgarry/04trend-mcgarry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/04/t-magazine/04trend-m