', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shimmies and Shouts for a Genre’s Revival', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shimmies and Shouts for a Genre’s Revival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APOLLO THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Daptone Records', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dap-Kings (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Sharon Lafaye (1956- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-05T23:10:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/578e6c70-715c-5dc0-bd45-0084b190420d', 'word_count': 658, 'uri': 'nyt://article/578e6c70-715c-5dc0-bd45-0084b190420d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Oh, who was involved in some of the private equity firm’s most prominent energy investments, is said to be considering either starting his own firm or joining a smaller firm in a more senior role.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/05/apollo-global-partner-sam-oh-is-said-to-be-leaving/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Oh, who was involved in some of the private equity firm’s most prominent energy investments, is said to be considering either starting his own firm or joining a smaller firm in a more senior role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sam Oh, a partner at Apollo Global Management who worked on deals in the energy sector, is leaving the private equity firm, two people briefed on the matter said on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multime