which were initially touched off by the disappearance of 43 students in southern Mexico, have developed into a broader movement for an end to government corruption. During a large protest on Nov. 20, the police arrested 11 people; they were sent to maximum security jails, only to be released by a judge for lack of evidence.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Police Chief Says He Is Stepping Down', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Police Chief in Capital Is Stepping Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Almeida, Jesus Rodriguez (1971- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico City (Mexico)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-06T00:41:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/31f6852b-c901-59df-8bbf-6d309313b39a', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31f6852b-c901-59df-8bbf-6d309313b39a'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense has identified 2,340 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/06/us/us-military-deaths-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense has identified 2,340 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department 