any technicians in the Bronx to improperly sway them to vote against unionizing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Calls Cablevision’s Raises an Anti-Union Act', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Calls Cablevision’s Raises an Anti-Union Act', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenhouse, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cablevision Systems Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolan, James L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Labor Relations Board', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communications Workers of America', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fish, Steven', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-06T03:23:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86ba3de4-ad3d-57f7-83aa-72d56121948f', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86ba3de4-ad3d-57f7-83aa-72d56121948f'}, {'abstract': 'Allah Justice McQueen was arrested in connection with a scheme that the authorities said defrauded elderly victims in California, Colorado, Illinois, New York, Texas and Washington of more than $170,000.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/06/nyregion/brooklyn-man-charged-in-phone-fraud-that-targeted-elderly-people.html', 'snippet': 'Allah Justice McQueen was arrested in connection with a scheme that the authorities said defrauded elderly victims in California, Colorado, Illinois, New York, Texas and Washington of more than $170,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The calls to the grandparents last year usually began the same way. First, someone identifying himself as a state trooper, a sergeant or a lawyer, would get on the line suggesting that a child or grandchild had been arrested and jailed on a drug offense. The grandparent would then be asked to send bail money immediately so that the grandchild could be released. Sometimes, the grandparent would hear another voice — the purported grandchild on the line, crying and pleading with the grandparent to send money and not tell other relatives, federal prosecutors said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brooklyn Man Charged in Phone Fraud That Targeted Elderly People', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Charges in Telephone Fraud That Targeted Elderly People', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQueen, Allah Justice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-06T03:29:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5838e8b5-7982-534b-a000-109f9ef13c2f', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5838e8b5-7982-534b-a000-109f9ef13c2f'}, {'abstract': 'In October 2012, Hurricane Sandy dumped four feet of water into David Lonergan’s bungalow in the Rockaways in Queens. Over two years later, after fixing his house himself, he moved back in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/06/nyregion/after-a-storm-celebrating-a-hard-earned-homecoming.html', 'snippet': 'In October 2012, Hurricane Sandy dumped four feet of water into David Lonergan’s bungalow in the Rockaways in Queens. Over two years later, after fixing his house himself, he moved back in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was down to the finishing touches: the window blinds, the curtain rods, the new washer-dryer, the closet shelves. After two years of wandering, David Lonergan was home.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/06/nyregion/06NEEDIEST/06NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/06/nyregion/06NEEDIEST/06NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/06/nyregion/06NEEDIEST/06NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit'