cument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8926dff8-b4b1-53f3-8aa6-567956f6bea4', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8926dff8-b4b1-53f3-8aa6-567956f6bea4'}, {'abstract': 'Obama > Bush, for what it’s worth.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/06/comparing-postmodern-recoveries/', 'snippet': 'Obama > Bush, for what it’s worth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Very early on — in fact, long before the 2007 recession was either declared officially, or admitted as reality by those still touting a Bush Boom — some of us warned that recovery would be slow, and initially jobless. Why? Because this was a postmodern business cycle, brought on not by monetary tightening but by private-sector overreach, and hence harder to turn around than, say, the 1979-82 slump. Nonetheless, as Menzie Chinn notes, a constant talking point on the right has been that slow growth showed the damage done by Obama policies. And not just at Heritage or whatever; people like Ed Lazear or John Taylor demonstrated the reality of the hack gap by asserting that the private sector wasn’t creating jobs because Obama was looking at them funny; also Obamacare.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comparing Postmodern Recoveries', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-06T13:11:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40c73f99-a083-5b4a-9a86-033e745c3d63', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40c73f99-a083-5b4a-9a86-033e745c3d63'}, {'abstract': 'The international multimedia company celebrates with a beyond-eclectic bill of musicians and actors playing musicians deep in the bowels of the Brooklyn Navy Yard.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/06/happy-20th-birthday-vice-media/', 'snippet': 'The international multimedia company celebrates with a beyond-eclectic bill of musicians and actors playing musicians deep in the bowels of the Brooklyn Navy Yard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To celebrate its 20th birthday, Vice Media threw itself a makeshift music festival, food trucks and Porta-Potties included.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy 20th Birthday, Vice Media', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cocker, Jarvis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graves, Meredith', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Jonah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johansson, Scarlett', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jonze, Spike', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Killah, Ghostface', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lil Wayne', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malkmus, Stephen', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vice (Magazine)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vice Media Inc', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Navy Yard (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-06T13:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'ar