n on the Sunday shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Another week of nationwide protests followed a Staten Island grand jury’s decision to not criminally charge a white police offer whose chokehold on an unarmed black man resulted in Eric Garner’s death. These protests come on the heels of a St. Louis County grand jury that also chose, earlier this month, not to indict a white police officer who shot and killed an unarmed black teenager.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Watching: Sunday Shows', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Cornell William', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Joaquin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Julian', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lankford, James', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-06T22:05:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elena Schneider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f936f260-4d25-5b8a-b12b-cbbdfab03dff', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f936f260-4d25-5b8a-b12b-cbbdfab03dff'}, {'abstract': 'Hoarding gold is the economy’s comfort food.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/sunday-review/the-golden-age.html', 'snippet': 'Hoarding gold is the economy’s comfort food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOU would have thought by now — 43 years after President Richard M. Nixon scrapped the gold standard — that gold’s role as an economic instrument was over. After all, the mighty metal that once held sway over the global monetary system was supposed to have, by this point, finally been reduced to just another asset peddled on the Internet.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Golden Age', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Golden Age', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feuer, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold Standard (Monetary)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-06T22:06:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/441abe1e-126e-50db-94c8-3b46490a0c82', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/441abe1e-126e-50db-94c8-3b46490a0c82'}, {'abstract': 'There are no facts, only interpretations, Nietzsche said, and there was good evidence of that this past week, from Staten Island to Russia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/opinion/sunday/a-week-of-facts-vs-interpretation.html', 'snippet': 'There are no facts, only interpretations, Nietzsche said, and there was good evidence of that this past week, from Staten Island to Russia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are no facts, only interpretations, Nietzsche said, and there was good evidence of that this past week in the decision of a grand jury on Staten Island, and in President Vladimir V. Putin’s take on Russia’s economic plight. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sunday-review/07SERGE/07SERGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/07/sunday-review/07SERGE/07SERGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sunday-review/07SERGE/07SERGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sunday-review/07SERGE/07SERGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sunday-review/07SERGE/07SERGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/07/sunday-review/07SERGE/07SERGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sunday-review/07SERGE/07SERGE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Week of Facts vs. Interpretation ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Week of Facts vs. Interpretation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pantaleo, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-06T22:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Serge Schmemann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmemann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ef62cd5-4490-5ed7-b7b7-6a3b5fdc8801', 'word_count': 1132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ef62cd5-4490-5ed7-b7b7-6a3b5fdc8801'}, {'abstract': 'The Park Avenue Armory has played host to many ambitious installations in recent years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/arts/design/at-the-armory-a-great-flood.html', 'snippet': 'The Park Avenue Armory has played host to many ambitious installations in recent years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Park Avenue Armory has played host to many ambitious installations in recent years, accommodating motorcycle gangs, massive video screens, multiple orchestras and Hollywood-style soundstages. Now, the artist Douglas Gordon and the musician Hélène Grimaud are flooding the armory’s 55,000-square-foot Drill Hall with water for their project “Tears Become ... Streams Become ...,” which opens Tuesday. It’s an unusual collaboration between a multimedia artist (Mr. Gordon) and a classical pianist (Ms. Grimaud), one that promises to build on Mr. Gordon’s previous music-inspired projects, like his film installation “K.364,” based on Mozart’s “Sinfonio Concertante” in E flat, K.364.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Armory, a Great Flood', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art: At the Armory, a Great Flood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-06T22:31:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c31f041-c0b2-50fe-84f2-171b098c8b4e', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c31f041-c0b2-50fe-84f2-171b098c8b4e'}, {'abstract': 'Daniil Trifonov and Yuja Wang are still in their 20s, but both pianists have developed outsize reputations for the power and poetry of their playing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/arts/music/wunderkinds-at-work.html', 'snippet': 'Daniil Trifonov and Yuja Wang are still in their 20s, but both pianists have developed outsize reputations for the power and poetry of their playing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniil Trifonov and Yuja Wang are still in their 20s, but both pianists have developed outsize reputations for the power and poetry of their playing. This week, you can catch them both at Carnegie Hall — Mr. Trifonov on Tuesday, Ms. Wang on Thursday — in programs that pay homage to the process of transcription and transmission.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07GUIDE2/07GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07GUIDE2/07GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07GUIDE2/07GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07GUIDE2/07GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07GUIDE2/07SILOGUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07GUIDE2/07SILOGUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/arts/07GUIDE2/07SILOGUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wunderkinds at Work', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker'