 to lead the Buckeyes in a drubbing of Wisconsin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/sports/ncaafootball/buckeyes-capture-big-ten-bolstering-playoff-hopes-.html', 'snippet': 'Cardale Jones, in his first career start as Ohio State’s quarterback, threw three touchdown passes to lead the Buckeyes in a drubbing of Wisconsin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS — Cardale Jones paced the Ohio State sideline, smiling and slapping hands with his teammates. Moments earlier, a defender had been barreling down on him as he delivered an arcing pass that his receiver caught in stride for a 44-yard touchdown.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/big-10/big-10-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/big-10/big-10-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 865}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/big-10/big-10-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 711, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/big-10/big-10-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1421, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/big-10/big-10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/big-10/big-10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/big-10/big-10-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Buckeyes Capture Big Ten, Bolstering Playoff Hopes ', 'kicker': 'Ohio State 59, Wisconsin 0', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Buckeyes Capture Big Ten, Bolstering Playoff Hopes ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big Ten Conference', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Wisconsin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-07T05:20:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9df9fbe-a18b-5f6a-a554-f60f745e55f1', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9df9fbe-a18b-5f6a-a554-f60f745e55f1'}, {'abstract': 'Florida State held on to beat Georgia Tech for the Atlantic Coast Conference title and was left waiting to see if the College Football Playoff’s selection committee would dare leave it out of the top four.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/sports/ncaafootball/fsu-grinds-out-another-acc-title-with-a-win-over-gerorgia-tech.html', 'snippet': 'Florida State held on to beat Georgia Tech for the Atlantic Coast Conference title and was left waiting to see if the College Football Playoff’s selection committee would dare leave it out of the top four.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — Florida State’s modus operandi this season has been to play down to the competition and do just enough to come away with the win. As it traded touchdowns with Georgia Tech on Saturday during the first half of the Atlantic Coast Conference championship game — the teams combined for seven touchdowns on the first nine possessions — it seemed as if the Seminoles were headed for another nail-biter.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/acc-1/acc-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 468, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/acc-1/acc-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 468}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/acc-1/acc-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 799, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/acc-1/acc-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1598, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/acc-1/acc-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/acc-1/acc-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/07/sports/acc-1/acc-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspense Never Ends for Seminoles', 'kicker': 'Florida State 37, Georgia Tech 35', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suspense Never Ends for Seminoles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tracy, Marc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlantic Coast Conference', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winston, Jameis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Georgia Institute of Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida State University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-07T05:24:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Tracy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tracy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/173ce995-923e-58ae-90bd-2cbbefa2ba63', 'word_count': 1036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/173ce995-923e-58ae-90bd-2cbbefa2ba63'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (Lifetime) THE RED TENT Rebecca Ferguson, above center, stars as Dinah, the biblical figure, and Minnie Driver and Iain Glen are her parents, Leah and Jacob, in this two-part adaptation of Anita Diamant’s best seller about Jacob and his four wives. Morena Baccarin plays Rachel, Jacob’s favorite; Debra Winger is Rebecca, his mother; and Will Tudor is Joseph, Dinah’s brother. “Fans of the novel will no doubt watch and revel in this relatively big-budget treatment,” Neil Genzlinger wrote in The New York Times. “Others might find its pseudo-biblical, pseudo-feminist mix hard to take. Yes, women tend to get short shrift in the Bible once Eve disappears, but this is a decidedly Lifetime version of their unknown story — episodes of love at first sight followed by sexual ecstasy; lots of child-birthing; a tent where the sisterhood keeps the flame while stupid, callous men rage outside.” “The Women of the Bible,” in which religious scholars share stories of Eve, Sarah, Rahab, Mary Magdalene and Mary, leads in at 7. Part 2 of “The Red Tent” will be broadcast Monday.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-07T06:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6d4d10f-56cd-5fa6-9924-1566d1a528c2', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6d4d10f-56cd-5fa6-9924-1566d1a528c2'}, {'abstract': 'Jim Delany, the conference’s commissioner, said of moving the event to the Garden, “We wanted to get out there as soon as we could.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/sports/ncaabasketball/big-ten-to-hold-2018-mens-tournament-at-madison-square-garden.html', 'snippet': 'Jim Delany, the conference’s commissioner, said of moving the event to the Garden, “We wanted to get out there as soon as we could.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Big Ten Conference will hold its 2018 men’s basketball tournament at Madison Square Garden, Commissioner Jim Delany said Saturday night. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Ten to Hold 2018 Men’s Tournament at Madison Square Garden', 'kicker':