itters-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daily Gift: Bitters, for Sweeties', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-07T14:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a056e2ed-de42-506d-b473-c44397212f55', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a056e2ed-de42-506d-b473-c44397212f55'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The deposed Brazilian emperor arrived in his Lisbon exile in 1889.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/1889-dom-pedro-in-exile/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The deposed Brazilian emperor arrived in his Lisbon exile in 1889.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LISBON — Dom Pedro, the Democratic Emperor of Brazil, arrived here to-day [Dec. 7] an exile from his country after forty-nine years of spotless reign. “He will never go back,” said Vicomte de Nioac, who entered the Emperor’s service as a young man, to leave it when age and gray hair bade him rest from his faithful duty. The Vicomte, a former chamberlain and bosom friend to the Emperor, who, notwithstanding his age, made the severe journey from Paris, unmindful of the terrible cold of the passage through the mountains of Spain to be a t the side of his old and adored m aster in his hour of great trial, and place his remaining years and services at the disposal of Dom Pedro. He continued “No, sir, the Emperor would never return, even if they begged him. Never!” The Emperor, while conversing generally and freely, refused to touch upon any subject concerning the political situation. He said they had a very good voyage, with beautiful weather, but his lips were sealed upon political topics. Princess Isabella said: “I cannot understand this Revolution having taken place during my father’s lifetime after a reign of forty-nine years. Had it occurred after I had come to the throne I should not have been so surprised.” So closes a page of history which must touch the hearts of everybody with sadness and sympathy for an aged and enlightened Monarch upon whom so terrible a blow has fallen at the end of a long and useful life. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Dec. 8, 1889', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/blogs/08iht-olddec08-1889/08iht-olddec08-1889-jumbo.png', 'height': 565, 'width': 389, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/blogs/08iht-olddec08-1889/08iht-olddec08-1889-superJumbo.png', 'height': 565, 'width': 389, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/blogs/08iht-olddec08-1889/08iht-olddec08-1889-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/08/blogs/08iht-olddec08-1889/08iht-olddec08-1889-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/blogs/08iht-olddec08-1889/08iht-olddec08-1889-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1889: Dom Pedro in Exile', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War and Revolution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lisbon (Portugal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-07T16:11:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/516f3a88-e509-5d52-9e4e-3e530c8fce39', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/516f3a88-e509-5d52-9e4e-3e530c8fce39'}, {'abstract': 'A mother reflects on the lack of charges brought in the police killings in Ferguson, Mo., and on Staten Island, a subject that weighs on many black parents who fear for their children’s safety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/08/nyregion/for-black-parents-shielding-children-from-talk-of-ferguson-and-garner-cannot-protect-them.html', 'snippet': 'A mother reflects on the lack of charges brought in the police killings in Ferguson, Mo., and on Staten Island, a subject that weighs on many black parents who fear for their children’s safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We were driving to Whole Foods on a blustery evening last month when my 7-year-old son asked me the question: “Can a police officer be arrested?”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None