'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bc053a8-9356-564a-8ca8-a35da5e0c156', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bc053a8-9356-564a-8ca8-a35da5e0c156'}, {'abstract': 'The Giants scored on five of their first six possessions, opening up a 17-0 lead before the Titans picked up a first down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/08/sports/football/eli-manning-and-odell-beckham-help-giants-rout-titans-and-end-7-game-skid.html', 'snippet': 'The Giants scored on five of their first six possessions, opening up a 17-0 lead before the Titans picked up a first down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASHVILLE — The Giants arrived at LP Field mired in a losing streak that had stretched to an unsightly seven games. Winless since Oct. 5, when they rallied from a 10-point deficit to beat Atlanta and push their record to 3-2, the Giants had spent the last two months two ways: gawking at the athletic genius of wide receiver Odell Beckham Jr. and finding new methods of self-destruction. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/sports/GIANTS1/GIANTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/08/sports/GIANTS1/GIANTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/sports/GIANTS1/GIANTS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/sports/GIANTS1/GIANTS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/sports/GIANTS1/GIANTS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/08/sports/GIANTS1/GIANTS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/sports/GIANTS1/GIANTS1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Put End to Seven-Game Skid With a Rare All-Around Effort ', 'kicker': 'Giants 36, Titans 7', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giants Put End to Seven-Game Skid With a Rare All-Around Effort', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckham, Odell Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Andre', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tennessee Titans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-07T21:53:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/519e213d-4192-5d08-bbce-e72c20256f13', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/519e213d-4192-5d08-bbce-e72c20256f13'}, {'abstract': 'Yannick Nézet-Séguin, the Philadelphia Orchestra’s charismatic music director, offered a topsy-turvy program incorporating a Brahms symphony, a Haydn concerto and a Strauss suite.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/08/arts/yannick-nezet-seguin-leads-the-philadelphia-orchestra-at-carnegie.html', 'snippet': 'Yannick Nézet-Séguin, the Philadelphia Orchestra’s charismatic music director, offered a topsy-turvy program incorporating a Brahms symphony, a Haydn concerto and a Strauss suite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first glance, the program that the Philadelphia Orchestra presented at Carnegie Hall on Friday appeared perfectly conservative: a Brahms symphony, a Haydn concerto, the suite from “Der Rosenkavalier” by Richard Strauss. But on closer inspection, its presentation was highly unusual: topsy-turvy, even, by the rigid standards of concert etiquette. Instead of opening with the palate-tickling suite followed by the crowd-pleasing concerto with the meaty symphony served up last, Yannick Nézet-Séguin, the orchestra’s charismatic music director, reversed the order.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/arts/ORCHESTRA/ORCHESTRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/08/arts/ORCHESTRA/ORCHESTRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/arts/ORCHESTRA/ORCHESTRA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/arts/ORCHESTRA/ORCHESTRA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1306, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, '