lifier': 'Jr.', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6366b95b-a831-51b4-a81f-49bef5ed96a8', 'word_count': 1474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6366b95b-a831-51b4-a81f-49bef5ed96a8'}, {'abstract': 'For years, general managers at baseball’s winter meetings made trades in hushed hotel lobbies, but deals now usually take place away from frenzied gatherings of fans, scouts, reporters and agents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/08/sports/baseball/where-baseball-is-all-the-buzz-general-managers-just-want-peace-and-quiet.html', 'snippet': 'For years, general managers at baseball’s winter meetings made trades in hushed hotel lobbies, but deals now usually take place away from frenzied gatherings of fans, scouts, reporters and agents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early one morning, Brian Cashman was walking from his suite to another location in the hotel. Or maybe it was afternoon, or late at night. It hardly mattered. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/sports/08meeting1/08meeting1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/08/sports/08meeting1/08meeting1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/sports/08meeting1/08meeting1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/08/sports/08meeting1/08me