elin, Alain (1943-2014)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Balmain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-08T18:04:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/276d1087-d4a9-533e-85ad-6de25529a53b', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/276d1087-d4a9-533e-85ad-6de25529a53b'}, {'abstract': 'A Cleveland officer’s fatal shooting of 12-year-old Tamir Rice has highlighted differences in a neighborhood over the police’s role.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/us/family-of-boy-killed-by-cleveland-officer-to-pursue-criminal-case.html', 'snippet': 'A Cleveland officer’s fatal shooting of 12-year-old Tamir Rice has highlighted differences in a neighborhood over the police’s role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — It began as a fairly typical Saturday afternoon for Tamir Rice, playing at a park a block from his home. But when a friend lent him a black toy pistol used to fire plastic pellets, everything changed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Questions Over Police Hit Home in Cleveland ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'National Questions Over Police Hit Home in Cleveland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oppel, Richard A Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cleveland (Ohio)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Tamir E (2002-14)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'su