g by The Washington Post, among other news outlets, mean that the story was only superficially inaccurate or substantially false.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rolling Stone and Rape on Campus', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rolling Stone and Rape on Campus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolling Stone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Virginia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-08T21:55:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4d032ea-3d84-5cbd-92a5-c493bd169faa', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4d032ea-3d84-5cbd-92a5-c493bd169faa'}, {'abstract': 'Hotels are lending items like small appliances, bicycles, cars and running gear. Some let guests leave their own items behind, for return trips.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/business/hotels-let-guests-borrow-items-or-leave-them.html', 'snippet': 'Hotels are lending items like small appliances, bicycles, cars and running gear. Some let guests leave their own items behind, for return trips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until last year, when she became a planning consultant for a college in Florida, Alison Barlow traveled almost full time for an information technology company. She was away as long as three weeks a month, making it home on weekends about half the time.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'm