emblazoned with the phrase “I Can’t Breathe” during warm-ups before a game last Saturday in Chicago.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/sports/Y-BASKETS-1/Y-BASKETS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/09/sports/Y-BASKETS-1/Y-BASKETS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 834}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/sports/Y-BASKETS-1/Y-BASKETS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/sports/Y-BASKETS-1/Y-BASKETS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1474, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/sports/Y-BASKETS-1/Y-BASKETS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/09/sports/Y-BASKETS-1/Y-BASKETS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/sports/Y-BASKETS-1/Y-BASKETS-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For LeBron James and Other Stars, the Political Is Personal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For James and Other Stars, the Political Is Personal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jack, Jarrett', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Cavaliers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T04:28:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4049375-b5f6-56b5-9a7d-ef3b51f975c7', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4049375-b5f6-56b5-9a7d-ef3b51f975c7'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State John Kerry will attend climate talks in Lima, Peru, to encourage countries to strike an agreement on reducing carbon emissions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/us/politics/kerry-plans-to-attend-climate-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State John Kerry will attend climate talks in Lima, Peru, to encourage countries to strike an agreement on reducing carbon emissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIMA, Peru — In a sign of the importance that the Obama administration has placed on the outcome of United Nations climate change negotiations taking place here this week, Secretary of State John Kerry will arrive on Thursday to strongly urge negotiators to reach a deal, according to sources familiar with Mr. Kerry’s plans but unauthorized to speak to the media. Typically, the secretary of state would not join diplomatic negotiations at this level, but Mr. Kerry has made climate change a priority of his tenure. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kerry Plans to Attend Climate Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kerry Plans to Attend Climate Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T04:50:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Coral Davenport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Coral', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davenport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75ed7e17-5fe2-5de7-8e16-96865fed0090', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75ed7e17-5fe2-5de7-8e16-96865fed0090'}, {'abstract': 'The designer, who collects decorative and functional clay items, will sell a host of them in her Crosby Street store tomorrow, just in time for the holidays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/t-magazine/rachel-comey-curates-a-ceramics-pop-up.html', 'snippet': 'The designer, who collects decorative and functional clay items, will sell a host of them in her Crosby Street store tomorrow, just in time for the holidays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rachel Comey, like seemingly everyone else these days, is bullish on ceramics. “There just seem to be so many friends making clay art,” the designer says. “We wanted to take a moment to celebrate them.” And so was born the first-ever Rachel Comey Ceramics Bazaar, taking place tomorrow at the brand’s Crosby Street flagship. Decorative and functional pieces by a host of influential talents — including Rebekah Miles, Ben Medansky, Jessica Hans and Comey’s favorite of late, Jennie Jieun Lee, who recently created a textile print for the designer’s pre-fall 2015 collection — will share the shelves with the label’s clothing and accessories; cocktails served after 5 p.m. will encourage a spirit of merrymaking (and holiday shopping). As Comey puts it, “Who doesn’t want to gift something that gives the recipient the sense of the hand that made it?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09hartman-comey/09hartman-comey-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09hartman-comey/09hartman-comey-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09hartman-comey/09hartman-comey-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09hartman-comey/09hartman-comey-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09hartman-comey/09hartman-comey-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09hartman-comey/09hartman-comey-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09hartman-comey/09hartman-comey-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rachel Comey Curates a Ceramics Pop-Up', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74c9de49-817e-5691-ac3c-fa4712d408ae', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74c9de49-817e-5691-ac3c-fa4712d408ae'}, {'abstract': 'To celebrate the anniversaries of both its existence and the end of Prohibition — and the season to be merry — the West Village speakeasy shares the secret to its festive, flavorful punch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/t-magazine/absinthe-cocktail-recipe-employees-only.html', 'snippet': 'To celebrate the anniversaries of both its existence and the end of Prohibition — and the season to be merry — the West Village speakeasy shares the secret to its festive, flavorful punch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tucked away behind a psychic readings storefront, Employees Only, the West Village memorial to the speakeasy, celebrated last night not just the 81st anniversary of the end of Prohibition, but also its own 10th anniversary. Between the libations, the jazz band and the burlesque dancers, revelers might have forgotten what decade it was. And there was a distinct element of yuletide cheer about the night’s knockout drink, the absinthe punch. Somewhere between the Champagne, cucumber and nutmeg, an urge to sing “Auld Lang Syne” bubbled forth. “We don’t do any punches, usually,” the bar’s manager, Steve Schneider, said, “but every year we get the punch bowls out of storage and make it happen.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09absinthe-nichols/09absinthe-nichols-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09absinthe-nichols/09absinthe-nichols-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09absinthe-nichols/09absinthe-nichols-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09absinthe-nichols/09absinthe-nichols-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09absinthe-nichols/09absinthe-nichols-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09absinthe-nichols/09absinthe-nichols-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09absinthe-nichols/09absinthe-nichols-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Seasonal Absinthe Cocktail Recipe From Employees Only', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Nichols', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nichols', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81265170-636e-5c6d-a88d-d3f112b8450c', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81265170-636e-5c6d-a88d-d3f112b8450c'}, {'abstract': 'Express Scripts says that nearly half the people who took opioids for more than 30 days in the study’s first year were still using them three years later.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/business/patients-prescribed-narcotic-painkillers-use-more-of-them-for-longer-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'Express Scripts says that nearly half the people who took opioids for more than 30 days in the study’s first year were still using them three years later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While a major public health campaign has had some success in reducing the number of people who take potentially addictive narcotic painkillers, those patients who are prescribed the drugs are getting more of them for a longer time, according to a new study.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/business/Opiate/Opiate-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/09/business/Opiate/Opiate-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20