ame': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Pedulla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pedulla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7817b9d2-0fb6-5d74-9f82-de3d3bcae4a1', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7817b9d2-0fb6-5d74-9f82-de3d3bcae4a1'}, {'abstract': 'A debate over whether to reappoint the budget director raises a larger question about resistance to good news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/upshot/the-battle-over-douglas-elmendorf-and-the-inability-to-see-good-news.html', 'snippet': 'A debate over whether to reappoint the budget director raises a larger question about resistance to good news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many Senate hearings are mere theater, but one that took place on July 16, 2009, mattered. With Congress in the midst of writing the bill that became Obamacare, senators asked Douglas Elmendorf, the director of the Congressional Budget Office, to evaluate their efforts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/business/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/09/business/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/business/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/business/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1517, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/business/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/09/business/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/business/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB/09UP-Leonhardt-SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Battle Over Douglas Elmendorf — and the Inability to See Good News', 'kicker': 'Propensity for Pessimism', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Puzzling Resistance to Good Economic News', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Budget Office', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leonhardt, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elmendorf, Douglas W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T05:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e96c874-cfa7-53d8-be98-6f302c72e0df', 'word_count': 1188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e96c874-cfa7-53d8-be98-6f302c72e0df'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/arts/television/whats-on-tv-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (CBS) THE VICTORIA’S SECRET FASHION SHOW Beauties like Karlie Kloss, Doutzen Kroes, Candice Swanepoel, Lily Aldridge, Behati Prinsloo and Lindsay Ellingson don angel wings and skimpies — including two $2 million fantasy bras designed by Pascal Mouawad, encrusted with rubies, diamonds and sapphires and worn by Alessandra Ambrosio and Adriana Lima — to sashay down the runway at Earls Court in London in this extravaganza, recorded on Dec. 2. Taylor Swift, Ariana Grande, Ed Sheeran and Hozier provide background music in segments titled “Gilded Angels,” “Exotic Traveler,” “Dream Girl” and “Angel Ball.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T06:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/826f4170-6bfb-5313-9ee9-01d9c9989c25', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/826f4170-6bfb-5313-9ee9-01d9c9989c25'}, {'abstract': 'Robertson, who converted 39 of 44 save opportunities last season, agreed to a four-year, $46 million deal, according to an official with knowledge of the agreement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/sports/baseball/yankees-said-to-lose-david-robertson-to-white-sox.html', 'snippet': 'Robertson, who converted 39 of 44 save opportunities last season, agreed to a four-year, $46 million deal, according to an official with knowledge of the agreement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — The Yankees believe they will have a strong bullpen again next season. But the hopes of an overwhelming three-man group to close out games evaporated late Monday night when closer David Robertson agreed to a four-year, $46 million deal with the Chicago White Sox.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/sports/baseball/10yankees1/10yankees1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/10/sports/baseball/10yankees1/10yankees1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/sports/baseball/10yankees1/10yankees1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/sports/baseball/10yankees1/10yankees1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1393, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/sports/baseball/10yankees1/10yankees1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/10/sports/baseball/10yankees1/10yankees1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/sports/baseball/10yankees1/10yankees1-thumbLarg