s', 'value': 'Bray, Chad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tesco PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Dave', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T11:15:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/478f08e6-7ece-5d84-b826-116f4bc0be03', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/478f08e6-7ece-5d84-b826-116f4bc0be03'}, {'abstract': 'The goal is not to reach as many people as possible, but to influence smaller groups like journalists, who are themselves influencers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/upshot/campaign-tweets-aimed-at-a-select-audience.html', 'snippet': 'The goal is not to reach as many people as possible, but to influence smaller groups like journalists, who are themselves influencers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The quotation from Caitlin Checkett, a digital staffer for Mitt Romney’s 2012 presidential campaign, was too good to ignore: “So whether it was a tweet, Facebook post, blog post, photo — anything you could imagine — it had to be sent around to everyone for approval. Toward the end of the campaign that was 22 individuals who had to approve it.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/upshot/09UP-Twitter/09UP-Twitter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarg