 had the skills as a producer to start a business and create shows for profit. He is chronicling his progress in a podcast called “StartUp.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 15 years, Alex Blumberg worked as a producer and reporter at the public radio show “This American Life” and National Public Radio’s “Planet Money,” a podcast he helped start during the financial crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Documenting the Journey From Public Radio to Start-Up Owner', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdfunding (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kickstarter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Public Radio', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T12:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eilene Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eilene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5faeb849-733d-5b2f-9498-334a03c0ea32', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5faeb849-733d-5b2f-9498-334a03c0ea32'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A second day without meat is introduced in wartime France in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/1939-second-meatless-day-is-named/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A second day without meat is introduced in wartime France in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A second meatless day each week is instituted in France by a decree published in the ‘‘Journal Officiel’’ this morning. This new day of fasting will be Friday. Thus French housewives will henceforth have to limit their marketing on Mondays and Fridays to fish and vegetables, besides forgoing beef on Tuesdays. The sale of ‘‘charcuterie’’ is likewise forbidden on Fridays, but poultry and rabbits may be purchased. This measure is necessary because copious meat rations are essential for France’s soldiers and more cattle than usual have been slaughtered in consequence since mobilization of the country’s armed forces. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Dec. 10, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Second Meatless Day Is Named', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T12:04:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f26d1cd-2580-54af-b333-148f5d9373ec', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f26d1cd-2580-54af-b333-148f5d9373ec'}, {'abstract': 'Officials have sometimes referred to a 24-year-old clause that says countries should have “common but differentiated responsibilities,” meaning developed and developing nations have different standards to meet when it comes to taking action on climate change.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/at-climate-meeting-china-balks-at-verifying-cuts-in-carbon-emissions/', 'snippet': 'Officials have sometimes referred to a 24-year-old clause that says countries should have “common but differentiated responsibilities,” meaning developed and developing nations have different standards to meet when it comes to taking action on cli...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, climate change negotiators from around the world converged on Lima, Peru, with a new sense of momentum. One driver of that attitude was the fact that just last month, President Obama and President Xi Jinping of China made a joint announcement in Beijing in which each pledged to try to limit or reduce carbon dioxide emissions in the coming years. Mr. Xi promised that China would reach an emissions peak by “around 2030” and have 20 percent of its energy come from non-fossil fuels by that year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/world/09sino-CLIMATE/09sino-CLIMATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/09/world/09sino-CLIMATE/09sino-CLIMATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/world/09sino-CLIMATE/09sino-CLIMATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':