 {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghul, Hassan', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T16:11:39+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By MATT APUZZO, HAEYOUN PARK and LARRY BUCHANAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'APUZZO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Haeyoun', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'PARK', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BUCHANAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/d7fb6d52-b3f3-5587-a194-32a2f24654b0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/d7fb6d52-b3f3-5587-a194-32a2f24654b0'}, {'abstract': 'The report paints a devastating picture of an agency that was ill equipped to question terrorism suspects, bungled the job and misrepresented the results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/world/senate-torture-report-shows-cia-infighting-over-interrogation-program.html', 'snippet': 'The report paints a devastating picture of an agency that was ill equipped to question terrorism suspects, bungled the job and misrepresented the results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In January 2003, 10 months into the Central Intelligence Agency’s secret prison program, the agency’s chief of interrogations sent an email to colleagues saying that the relentlessly brutal treatment of prisoners was a train wreck “waiting to happen and I intend to get the hell off the train before it happens.” He said he had told his bosses he had “serious reservations” about the program and no longer wanted to be associated with it “in any way.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headli