tative Steve King of Iowa, the second time in just a few months that the governor will go to Iowa to attend an event with Mr. King.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie will attend a conference next month hosted by Representative Steve King of Iowa, the Republican whose outspoken and conservative views on immigration have made him a divisive figure. It will be the second time in just a few months that Mr. Christie will travel to Iowa to attend an event with Mr. King.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Christie Heading Back to Iowa Next Month', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Steven A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T16:16:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc29aa8e-a851-5780-b71a-29c7ab21bd6e', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc29aa8e-a851-5780-b71a-29c7ab21bd6e'}, {'abstract': 'An emergency appeal through social media brought an outpouring of donations for the World Food Program, which the agency’s director called unprecedented.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/world/middleeast/un-food-agency-to-resume-suspended-aid-to-syrian-refugees.html', 'snippet': 'An emergency appeal through social media brought an outpouring of donations for the World Food Program, which the agency’s director called unprecedented.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — The United Nations said Tuesday that it would soon resume food aid to Syrian refugees after a successful emergency appeal through social media, which brought an outpouring of financial support from thousands of people and a number of Middle Eastern and European governments.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Food Agency to Resume Aid to Syrians After Donors Step Up ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Food Agency to Resume Aid to Syrians After Donors Step Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming-Bruce, Nick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdfunding (Internet)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Food Program', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T16:25:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3339fa9-46ff-5730-97ef-96014272c5bb', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3339fa9-46ff-5730-97ef-96014272c5bb'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate Intelligence Committee has released its long-awaited review on the torture of prisoners held by the Central Intelligence Agency during the George W. Bush administration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/12/09/live-coverage-of-the-c-i-a-torture-report/', 'snippet': 'The Senate Intelligence Committee has released its long-awaited review on the torture of prisoners held by the Central Intelligence Agency during the George W. Bush administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate Intelligence Committee has released its long-awaited review on the torture of prisoners held by the Central Intelligence Agency during the George W. Bush administration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Coverage of the C.I.A. Torture Report', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T16:27:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c244c509-0966-50e6-ac29-6ead6538f69b', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c244c509-0966-50e6-ac29-6ead6538f69b'}, {'abstract': 'The report says the agency routinely misled the White House and Congress about the information it obtained from the detention and interrogation of terrorism suspects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/12/09/world/cia-torture-report-document.html', 'snippet': 'The report says the agency routinely misled the White House and Congress about the information it obtained from the detention and interrogation of terrorism suspects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The report says the agency routinely misled the White House and Congress a