restaurant-review-dirty-french-on-the-lower-east-side.html', 'snippet': 'Rich Torrisi and Mario Carbone treat the food of France with a hugely energizing lack of respect at Dirty French.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new restaurant from the chefs Rich Torrisi and Mario Carbone and their partner Jeff Zalaznick tiptoed onto the Lower East Side in September, demurely announcing its name with two eight-foot-high neon signs in peep-show pink. DIRTY, says one. FRENCH, reads the other.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Review: Dirty French on the Lower East Side', 'kicker': 'Restaurants', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France in a Parallel Universe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dirty French (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T17:51:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b377197f-2e96-5102-b7d2-94c6ef44b1d1', 'word_count': 1159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b377197f-2e96-5102-b7d2-94c6ef44b1d1'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s winners do not include any directors, conductors or composers.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/five-singers-win-opera-news-awards/', 'snippet': 'This year’s winners do not include any directors, conductors or composers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opera News will honor five singers with its 2015 Opera News Award, a prize given annually by the magazine to recognize contributions to the opera world. The winners, who will received their awards at a gala at the Plaza Hotel on April 19, are the tenor Piotr Beczala; the bass-baritone Samuel Ramey; the bass Ferruccio Furlanetto, and the sopranos Sondra Radvanovsky and Teresa Stratas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Five Singers Win Opera News Awards', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Opera News', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T17:53:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d5534f1-3e5f-5d0d-89b2-d28241163dde', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d5534f1-3e5f-5d0d-89b2-d28241163dde'}, {'abstract': 'Readers discuss whether and how those responsible for torture should be held accountable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/opinion/accountability-and-the-torture-report.html', 'snippet': 'Readers discuss whether and how those responsible for torture should be held accountable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accountability and the Torture Report', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Accountability and the Torture Report', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unit