nel’s report on the torture of prisoners by the Central Intelligence Agency. They condemned the report o...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several Republican members of the Senate Intelligence Committee on Tuesday pushed back against the release of the declassified executive summary of the panel’s report on the torture of prisoners by the Central Intelligence Agency. They condemned the report on techniques used during the George W. Bush administration as “partisan.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Panel’s Republicans Dismiss Torture Report as ‘Partisan’', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chambliss, Saxby', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coats, Dan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Susan M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Risch, James E', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Intelligence', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T19:19:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d3f613c-3585-5047-9722-94142aa8b0c5', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d3f613c-3585-5047-9722-94142aa8b0c5'}, {'abstract': 'Terrence Pendergrass, a former Rikers captain, is charged with violating the rights of a mentally ill inmate who died after swallowing a packet of toxic detergent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/nyregion/rikers-inmate-civil-rights-trial.html', 'snippet': 'Terrence Pendergrass, a former Rikers captain, is charged with violating the rights of a mentally ill inmate who died after swallowing a packet of toxic detergent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his final hours, Jason Echevarria, a 25-year-old inmate at Rikers Island, was hunched over in his cell, clutching his stomach, gasping for breath, vomiting and pleading for medical attention that did not come, a federal prosecutor told a jury in Manhattan on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Account of Death at Rikers Is Disputed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Account of Death at Rikers Is Disputed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rikers Island Prison Complex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Echevarria, Jason', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pendergrass, Terrence', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T19:23:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24b37305-d9ed-58a2-99a9-a414c2b86d0f', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24b37305-d9ed-58a2-99a9-a414c2b86d0f'}, {'abstract': 'Here is a record of calls made to über, inc. since August by customers trying to contact Uber.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/ber-vs-uber-the-phone-log/', 'snippet': 'Here is a record of calls made to über, inc. since August by customers trying to contact Uber.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Saturday, I wrote about a woman named Herta Kriegner, whose graphic design company, über inc., has become ground zero for phone calls intended for the tech-savvy car company, Uber. As I wrote in my column, Uber’s customer service representatives handle everything by email. The only telephone number provided by the company leads to an automated message asking you to email them instead. As a result, customers determined to speak to a human being often end up talking to the wrong uber. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'über vs. Uber – The Phone Log', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T19:24:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/186eaab0-7a0b-53eb-afb9-dbef6a753bfb', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/186eaab0-7a0b-53eb-afb9-dbef6a753bfb'}, {'abstract': 'The company said a fuel sensor was not properly installed; Hyundai, Jaguar and Porsche also issued recalls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/automobiles/nissan-recalls-470000-vehicles-over-fuel-leaks.html', 'snippet': 'The company said a fuel sensor was not properly installed; Hyundai, Jaguar and Porsche also issued recalls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nissan is recalling about 470,000 vehicles worldwide, including 133,000 in the United States, because of possible fuel leaks, the automaker said in a report posted Tuesday on the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration website.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/automobiles/10RECALLS-image/10RECALLS-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/10/automobiles/10RECALLS-image/10RECALLS-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/automobiles/10RECALLS-image/10RECALLS-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 607, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/automobiles/10RECALLS-image/10RECALLS-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 607, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/automobiles/10RECALLS-image/10RECALLS-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/10/automobiles/10RECALLS-image/10RECALLS-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/automobiles/10RECALLS-image/10RECALLS-image-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'th