 could do something that would be very damaging.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/us/politics/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/09/us/politics/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/us/politics/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/us/politics/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/us/politics/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/09/us/politics/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/us/politics/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2/09firstdraft-obama-nashville-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'First Draft Focus: Pass a Bill', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T22:21:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jabin Botsford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jabin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botsford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6a509d2-ea9a-5623-8a0c-968a1a8ad1e3', 'word_count': 55, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6a509d2-ea9a-5623-8a0c-968a1a8ad1e3'}, {'abstract': 'The singer-songwriter, harpist and newly minted actress shares a few of her cultural influences with T in advance of the release of her new film, “Inherent Vice.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/09/joanna-newsom-favorite-film-furniture-fashion/', 'snippet': 'The singer-songwriter, harpist and newly minted actress shares a few of her cultural influences with T in advance of the release of her new film, “Inherent Vice.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In both her songs and her personal style, the singer-songwriter and harpist Joanna Newsom hearkens back to the era that saw the ascent of women like Joan Baez and Karen Dalton. (For a short film collaboration with the fashion line Wren, Newsom covered Sandy Denny.) Now, Newsom’s distinctive voice is primed to become familiar to a new audience, thanks to her role in “Inherent Vice,” the director Paul Thomas Anderson’s highly anticipated adaptation of Thomas Pynchon’s hallucinatory noir detective novel. In addition to narrating\xa0the film, Newsom plays Sortilège, a useful confidante to Joaquin Phoenix’s detective Larry “Doc” Sportello. The character is possessed of quasi-mystical powers that would not feel out of place in Newsom’s own personal mythology.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/09/t-magazine/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ/09newsom-miller-slide-OBHZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Joanna Newsom on Her Favorites in Film, Furniture and Fashion', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Under the Influence: Strike a Cord', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newsom, Joanna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-09T22:35:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d00684c-c1c9-5ed8-b5e2-d4352b827cc0', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d00684c-c1c9-5ed8-b5e2-d4352b827cc0'}, {'abstract': 'In “Magician: The Astonishing Life and Work of Orson Welles,” the director Chuck Workman examines that ambitious filmmaker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/movies/magician-an-orson-welles-retrospective-by-chuck-workman.html', 'snippet': 'In “Magician: The Astonishing Life and Work of Orson Welles,” the director Chuck Workman examines that ambitious filmmaker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like one of those machines that can inhale a car and spit out a tidy cube of squashed components, “Magician: The Astonishing Life and Work of Orson Welles” is a near-indigestible lump of clips and quips and snipped opinions. Assembled chronologically and delivered at warp speed (there’s enough astonishment here for double the 94-minute running time), this potted history of one of our rarest moviemaking talents offers nothing new for fans and seems likely to overwhelm the uninitiated.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/arts/MAGICIAN/MAGICIAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/10/arts/MAGICIAN/MAGICIAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 832}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 