02d8bcf7-aa72-59b6-99b4-f9b8c2499975'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Rick Snyder on Tuesday agreed to end Detroit’s status as a city in financial emergency and to send home the emergency manager he appointed in March 2013 to oversee the city through its crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/us/michigan-detroit-manager-ends-work.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Rick Snyder on Tuesday agreed to end Detroit’s status as a city in financial emergency and to send home the emergency manager he appointed in March 2013 to oversee the city through its crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Rick Snyder on Tuesday agreed to end Detroit’s status as a city in financial emergency and to send home the emergency manager he appointed in March 2013 to oversee the city through its crisis. In a letter to Kevyn D. Orr, the emergency manager, Mr. Snyder said the city’s journey through bankruptcy court, with a new budget in place, had put Detroit “on a path to meet its obligations to its citizens.” Last month, a federal bankruptcy judge approved Detroit’s plan to shed about $7 billion of its debts and to reinvest about $1.7 billion in the city’s insufficient services. The exit plan was expected to take effect as early as Wednesday, state officials said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan: Detroit Manager Ends Work ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan: Detroit Manager Ends Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orr, Kevyn D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snyder, Richard Dale', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T01:06:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline'