', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/sports/NFLfloater/NFLfloater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/10/sports/NFLfloater/NFLfloater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/sports/NFLfloater/NFLfloater-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cam Newton, Panthers’ Quarterback, Sustains Back Injury in a Car Crash  ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panthers’ Newton Sustains Back Injury in a Car Crash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zinser, Lynn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newton, Cameron J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carolina Panthers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T01:09:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4822f785-b800-55de-950d-22b314d04060', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4822f785-b800-55de-950d-22b314d04060'}, {'abstract': 'The Massachusetts Institute of Technology said it has determined that a retired faculty member, Walter Lewin, a physicist with a distinguished teaching career, has “engaged in online sexual harassment.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/us/massachusetts-online-harassment-inquiry-at-mit.html', 'snippet': 'The Massachusetts Institute of Technology said it has determined that a retired faculty member, Walter Lewin, a physicist with a distinguished teaching career, has “engaged in online sexual harassment.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Massachusetts Institute of Technology said it had determined that a retired faculty member, Walter Lewin, a physicist with a distinguished teaching career, “engaged in online sexual harassment.” As a result, the university said, it has revoked his status as professor emeritus and removed his lecture videos and other course material from OpenCourseWare and edEx, the online learning platform started by Harvard and M.I.T. In a statement Monday, the university said it received a complaint in October from an online learner who provided information about Dr. Lewin’s interactions with her and other women online. After an investigation, the statement said, M.I.T. “determined that Lewin’s behavior toward the complainant violated the institute’s policy on sexual harassment.” Dr. Lewin, 78, retired from M.I.T. in July 2009, last taught a course on campus in spring 2008 and last taught an online course in fall 2013. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Online Harassment Inquiry at M.I.T. ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Online Harassment Inquiry at M.I.T.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberharassment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewin, Walter H G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T01:12:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebdbe087-a675-5a72-8795-2145f4895c91', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebdbe087-a675-5a72-8795-2145f4895c91'}, {'abstract': 'The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention reported Tuesday that airport workers in the United States screened 1,993 travelers arriving from the West African countries most affected by the Ebola virus in the month after enhanced screening first began.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/us/nearly-2000-travelers-screened-for-ebola-.html', 'snippet': 'The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention reported Tuesday that airport workers in the United States screened 1,993 travelers arriving from the West African countries most affected by the Ebola virus in the month after enhanced screening firs...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention reported Tuesday that airport workers in the United States screened 1,993 travelers arriving from the West African countries most affected by the Ebola virus in the month after enhanced screening began on Oct. 11. Just 4 percent of the total, or 86 people, were flagged for further evaluation. Seven had symptoms and received medical attention, but none were found to have Ebola. The United States has reported four Ebola cases, including those of a Liberian man who contracted the disease in his home country and died in a Dallas hospital in October, and an American doctor who became infected while working in Guinea. ', 'p