 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd8c54d8-f7b7-5076-8d72-42672f875846', 'word_count': 1099, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd8c54d8-f7b7-5076-8d72-42672f875846'}, {'abstract': 'The Pakistani youth and the Indian rights campaigner were named winners in October, a choice that seemed to speak to a desire to transcend differences in a common cause.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/world/europe/malala-yousafzai-kailash-satyarthi-nobel-peace-prize.html', 'snippet': 'The Pakistani youth and the Indian rights campaigner were named winners in October, a choice that seemed to speak to a desire to transcend differences in a common cause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — They came from lands that had fought wars against each other, and that still skirmish — an older man and a high school student divided by faith and generations; he a Hindu, she a Muslim; he age 60, she 17.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Malala Yousafzai and Kailash Satyarthi Collect Nobel Peace Prizes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Advocates for Children Receive Nobel Peace Prize', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nobel Prizes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Satyarthi, Kailash', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yousafzai, Malala', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T11:35:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8410ef0e-a4f3-5eaa-8a60-3e1e13d80cb8', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8410ef0e-a4f3-5eaa-8a60-3e1e13d80cb8'}, {'abstract': 'The ratio of job openings to hiring has been higher in the last few months than at any time since the data was first recorded in 2001.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/upshot/employers-will-have-to-raise-wages-they-just-dont-know-it-yet.html', 'snippet': 'The ratio of job openings to hiring has been higher in the last few months than at any time since the data was first recorded in 2001.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American employers are the equivalent of a shopkeeper who has a “Help Wanted” sign permanently on display in his window, but never actually hires anybody. None of the applicants who come in offer the perfect mix of skills, experience and willingness to accept low pay that the shopkeeper is looking for.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/upshot/10UP-JOBS/10UP-JOBS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/10/upshot/10UP-JOBS/10UP-JOBS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/upshot/10UP-JOBS/10UP-JOBS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/upshot/10UP-JOBS/10UP-JOBS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1520, 'width': 2048,