dings from a survey of 133 countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/world/europe/united-nations-domestic-violence-report.html', 'snippet': 'One in four children has been physically abused, and one in five girls have been sexually abused, according to findings from a survey of 133 countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — Homicide and acts of personal violence kill more people than wars and are the third-leading cause of death among men aged 15 to 44, the United Nations said Wednesday in a new report.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More People Die From Homicide Than in Wars, U.N. Says ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More People Die From Homicide Than in Wars, U.N. Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming-Bruce, Nick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Abuse', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T13:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0f90f51-ada3-5868-a666-5612ff4c3822', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0f90f51-ada3-5868-a666-5612ff4c3822'}, {'abstract': 'Just a single minute of high-intensity exercise in a 10-minute workout can improve your fitness level, research showed.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/one-minute-workout/', 'snippet': 'Just a single minute of high-intensity exercise in a 10-minute workout can improve your fitness level, research showed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, I’ve been writing about the benefits of short bursts of exercise. Studies and anecdotes suggest that 10 minutes, seven minutes, six minutes, or even four minutes of very hard exercise interspersed with periods of rest can lead to a robust improvement in fitness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/science/09PhysEd/09PhysEd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/science/09PhysEd/09PhysEd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/science/09PhysEd/09PhysEd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/science/09PhysEd/09PhysEd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/science/09PhysEd/09PhysEd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/science/09PhysEd/09PhysEd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/science/09PhysEd/09PhysEd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Got a Minute? Let’s Work Out', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibala, Martin J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McMaster University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T13:07:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c12456bf-bfb6-5d2a-8392-6fe3612b06b9', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c12456bf-bfb6-5d2a-8392-6fe3612b06b9'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: German cruisers were sunk in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/1914-sinking-of-the-nurnberg/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: German cruisers were sunk in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The Secretary of the Admiralty issues the following statement: ‘‘Another telegram from Vice-Admiral Sir Frederick Sturdee announces that the German cruiser Nürnberg was also sunk on Tuesday [Dec. 8]. The pursuit of the Dresden continues. The engagement lasted five hours. The Scharnhorst was sunk at the end of three hours, and t