, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T17:18:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vindu Goel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vindu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2206905c-ec3f-5d61-b2e7-5e1b4b96863f', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2206905c-ec3f-5d61-b2e7-5e1b4b96863f'}, {'abstract': 'With the opening of a new ice skating complex in Prospect Park in Brooklyn, curling, last popular in New York City in the 1800s, is being warmly welcomed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/nyregion/the-sport-of-curling-finds-a-new-popularity-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'With the opening of a new ice skating complex in Prospect Park in Brooklyn, curling, last popular in New York City in the 1800s, is being warmly welcomed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It might have been preordained. In the borough of knitting, flea markets and bocce, when gleaming new ice rinks opened last year, one knew that curling couldn’t be far behind. The sport, involving ice, brooms and rocks, was born in medieval Scotland and continues to enthrall Canada, and it is just the sort of retro pastime that booms in Brooklyn these days.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Borough of Beards, Lay Down Some Ice, and Out Come the Brooms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Arrival of New Ice, Borough of Enthusiasts Breaks Out the Brooms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Curling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LeFrak Center at Lakeside', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T17:19:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa W. Foderaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Foderaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee4ef4da-cc9d-5dee-a32c-32a7660a940d', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee4ef4da-cc9d-5dee-a32c-32a7660a940d'}, {'abstract': 'Panthers Coach Ron Rivera told reporters that Derek Anderson, Newton’s backup, would start Sunday against Tampa Bay and that Newton was unlikely to play after sustaining two fractures in his back in a car accident.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/sports/football/carolina-panthers-cam-newton-released-from-hospital.html', 'snippet': 'Panthers Coach Ron Rivera told reporters that Derek Anderson, Newton’s backup, would start Sunday against Tampa Bay and that Newton was unlikely to play after sustaining two fractures in his back in a car accident.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carolina Panthers quarterback Cam Newton was released from a Charlotte, N.C., hospital on Wednesday, the team said, a day after sustaining two fractures in his lower back in a car accident near the Panthers’ stadium.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/sports/11newton1/11newton1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/11/sports/11newton1