'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b8a62e3-9fb0-52a2-986b-48f38c2b7f99'}, {'abstract': 'On the importance of “reasoned courage” in the face of terrorist (and other) threats.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/why-we-tortured-why-we-shouldnt/', 'snippet': 'On the importance of “reasoned courage” in the face of terrorist (and other) threats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six years\xa0ago, when an earlier set of\xa0revelations about our interrogation procedures in the years immediately following 9/11 were in the news, I wrote a rambling piece for The Atlantic on torture, in\xa0which I tried to work through how my own mind had changed on the issue, to contextualize the torture debate in America’s long history of dubiously-moral wartime measures, and to think through how we should pass judgment on our leaders and their choices\xa0in this case.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why We Tortured, Why We Shouldn’t', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fort Hood Shooting (2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interrogations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waterboarding', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarke, Richard A', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manzi, Jim', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Woodrow', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Hood (Tex)', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T17:28:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f25f485-e5a8-54fd-8fcb-a30a2c551d9d', 'word_count': 1924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f25f485-e5a8-54fd-8fcb-a30a2c551d9d'}, {'abstract': 'A new picture book captures the powerful scene of a soldier’s arrival home from a child’s point of view.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/books/review/greg-ruths-coming-home.html', 'snippet': 'A new picture book captures the powerful scene of a soldier’s arrival home from a child’s point of view.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days, the image of a soldier reuniting with family at the airport has an outsize emotional impact. After years in which our country’s military personnel were given extended deployments to fight wars that have produced new possibilities of personal catastrophe, there’s been some powerful photojournalism documenting the early moments of those who make it home — scenes of incredible relief etched in faces and onto bodies. Old grief and immediate joy seem somehow to merge. There are no words, these images seem to say.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/books/review/10childrens/10childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/10/books/review/10childrens/10childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/books/review/10childrens/10childrens-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 571, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/books/review/10childrens/10childrens-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 1381, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/books/review/10childrens/10childrens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/10/books/review/10childrens/10childrens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/books/review/10childrens/10childrens-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Parent’s Return from War', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruth, Greg', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 's