d 100,000 tons of steel, not including barbed wire. The amount of barbed wire alone could form a bristling hedge four meters wide and 4,000 kilometers long — equivalent to half the distance between the North Pole and the equator.  — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Dec. 11, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/blogs/10iht-old11-2/10iht-old11-2-articleLarge-v3.png', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/10/blogs/10iht-old11-2/10iht-old11-2-articleLarge-v3.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/blogs/10iht-old11-2/10iht-old11-2-jumbo-v3.png', 'height': 570, 'width': 899, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/blogs/10iht-old11-2/10iht-old11-2-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 570, 'width': 899, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/blogs/10iht-old11-2/10iht-old11-2-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/10/blogs/10iht-old11-2/10iht-old11-2-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/blogs/10iht-old11-2/10iht-old11-2-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1939: France Extends Fortifications', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'prin