ter Gets Message From Dissident in Prison', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Xiaobo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liao Yiwu', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Xia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T18:38:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong and Ian Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/378e818e-fa92-5e48-ad72-4ecaeb6ad0c8', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/378e818e-fa92-5e48-ad72-4ecaeb6ad0c8'}, {'abstract': 'Fifty percent of the nation said torture could be justified against terrorism suspects, a new poll found. Partisanship played a role.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/upshot/americans-have-become-more-accepting-of-use-of-torture.html', 'snippet': 'Fifty percent of the nation said torture could be justified against terrorism suspects, a new poll found. Partisanship played a role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans, once largely opposed to the use of torture, have become more accepting of its use against terrorism suspects to obtain information. It remains to be seen whether the newly released Senate Intelligence Committee report on C.I.A. torture changes publi