ases, it’s an act of aggression, as A.O. Scott notes in his essay for this year’s Great Performers issue. ‘‘Think of Michael Corleone locking lips with his traitorous brother Fredo on New Year’s Eve in Havana, a fratricidal kiss of death.’’ Kisses can therefore be lethal — but not always right away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/magazine/14greatperformers-sidebar3/14greatperformers-sidebar3-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 375, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/magazine/14greatperformers-sidebar3/14greatperformers-sidebar3-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1314, 'width': 481, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/magazine/14greatperformers-sidebar3/14greatperformers-sidebar3-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/magazine/14greatperformers-sidebar3/14greatperformers-sidebar3-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/magazine/14greatperformers-sidebar3/14greatperformers-sidebar3-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Long Before a Kiss of Death Takes Hold in the Movies?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kissing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T19:20:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e2dec12-bfd6-5638-950a-43d2d8792527', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e2dec12-bfd6-5638-950a-43d2d8792527'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes a kiss in cinema signals stormy weather; sometimes it signals clear skies.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/10/classic-cinema-kisses-in-the-rain-or-shine/', 'snippet': 'Sometimes a kiss in cinema signals stormy weather; sometimes it signals clear skies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Using weather to heighten the emotions of a kiss scene may be clichéd, as A.O. Scott acknowledges in his brief history of kissing in movies for this year’s Great Performers issue. But such scenes, he writes, ‘‘still seduce.’’ Here, the quintessential film kisses under stormy or clear skies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/magazine/14greatperformers-sidebar2/14greatperformers-sidebar2-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 274, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/magazine/14greatperformers-sidebar2/14greatperformers-sidebar2-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1797, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/magazine/14greatperformers-sidebar2/14greatperformers-sidebar2-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/magazine/14greatperformers-sidebar2/14greatperformers-sidebar2-thumbSt