https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/12/10/josh-earnest-takes-questions-but-offers-few-answers-on-c-i-a-report/', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s press secretary, Josh Earnest, puts on a clinic for how to take questions from reporters without actually answering them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The job of a White House press secretary is to face reporters every day to take their questions. On Wednesday, the current press secretary, Josh Earnest, put on a clinic for how to take such questions without actually answering them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Josh Earnest Takes Questions, but Offers Few Answers, on C.I.A. Report', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Earnest, Josh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T21:24:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08b07058-a54c-5e4e-b683-f5b59b65340a', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08b07058-a54c-5e4e-b683-f5b59b65340a'}, {'abstract': 'This year, there’s more terrain to ski and more après-ski activities, including snowshoeing, tubing and night clubs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/travel/whats-new-in-ski-resorts.html', 'snippet': 'This year, there’s more terrain to ski and more après-ski activities, including snowshoeing, tubing and night clubs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The flurry of recent ski news in North America has drifted into several piles. To ensure their own longevity, resorts continue to court families and increasingly offer a variety of nonski activities — from the novelty of biking in the snow to pre-ski-run yoga classes — that keep casual skiers from straying. This year, there’s more terrain to ski, and sometimes more terrain per pass (Vail Resorts’ recent acquisition of Park City Mountain Resort in Utah means a lift ticket there is also good at nearby Canyons Resort, another Vail property). Among novelties, expect snowcat-based “food trucks,” ice glamping and a nightclub at a lightheaded 10,000 feet.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14ROUNDUP/14ROUNDUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14ROUNDUP/14ROUNDUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14ROUNDUP/14ROUNDUP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14ROUNDUP/14ROUNDUP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14ROUNDUP/14ROUNDUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14ROUNDUP/14ROUNDUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14ROUNDUP/14ROUNDUP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150,