': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florence (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T23:13:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stefania Rousselle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stefania', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rousselle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7742ee8f-c6ff-571d-ab8c-3ca9ef880ab5', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7742ee8f-c6ff-571d-ab8c-3ca9ef880ab5'}, {'abstract': 'The latest micro trend fueled by social media marries two subcultures that might otherwise never commingle — goths and gym rats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/fashion/health-goth-when-darkness-and-gym-rats-meet.html', 'snippet': 'The latest micro trend fueled by social media marries two subcultures that might otherwise never commingle — goths and gym rats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walk toward the graffiti wall, turn left at the 11-foot pentagram, pass the polished gimp suit (watch your head, there is a leather-harnessed bicycle suspended from the ceiling) and descend the steps into the basement.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11HEALTHGOTH1/11HEALTHGOTH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11HEALTHGOTH1/11HEALTHGOTH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11HEALTHGOTH1/11HEALTHGOTH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo',