’t.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/opinion/dont-homogenize-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'Guidelines presume we doctors always know the best treatment. We don’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN American medicine today, “variation” has become a dirty word. Variation in the treatment of a medical condition is associated with wastefulness, lack of evidence and even capricious care. To minimize variation, insurers and medical specialty societies have banded together to produce a dizzying array of treatment guidelines for everything from asthma to diabetes, from urinary incontinence to gout.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular/Jauhar-Sandeep-circular-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Homogenize Health Care', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Homogenize Health Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jauhar, Sandeep', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-10T23:23:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandeep Jauhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandeep', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jauhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cbdfc5a-5a82-572c-8811-73d9cf3cd82c', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cbdfc5a-5a82-572c-8811-73d9cf3cd82c'}, {'abstract': 'Scarlett Johansson, Jonah Hill, Spike Jonze and others join mayhem orchestrated by the hip media company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/style/vice-turns-20-with-a-big-brooklyn-party.html', 'snippet': 'Scarlett Johansson, Jonah Hill, Spike Jonze and others join mayhem orchestrated by the hip media company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To reach Vice’s 20th anniversary party at the Brooklyn Navy Yard last Friday, attendees braved heavy rain, waited in long lines and had to walk several blocks more to reach a hangar-like space. Oh, and the 