: 'CB2', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas Trees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kavanaugh, Gere', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T00:09:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8343e11f-c756-5852-bee9-84398055f5af', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8343e11f-c756-5852-bee9-84398055f5af'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Martin O’Malley of Maryland, a Democrat who is considering a run for president, condemned the C.I.A.’s use of torture as described in a Senate report, staking out a position to the left of the party’s favorite, Hillary Rodham Clinton.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/12/10/on-torture-omalley-stands-to-the-left-of-clinton/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Martin O’Malley of Maryland, a Democrat who is considering a run for president, condemned the C.I.A.’s use of torture as described in a Senate report, staking out a position to the left of the party’s favorite, Hillary Rodham Clinton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Staking out a position to the left of Hillary Rodham Clinton, Gov. Martin O’Malley of Maryland, a Democrat who is considering a 2016 presidential bid, called Wednesday for the Justice Department to reopen its investigation into the Central Intelligence Agency’s harsh interrogation tactics and to consider prosecuting those who engaged in them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Torture, O’Malley Stands to the Left of Clinton', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Malley, Martin J", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T00:10:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50c44955-1999-569e-9cfd-0d86c20aae63', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50c44955-1999-569e-9cfd-0d86c20aae63'}, {'abstract': 'The porcelain decorations are part of a larger creative effort to put smiles everywhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/garden/brought-to-you-by-friendswithyou-and-lladr-.html', 'snippet': 'The porcelain decorations are part of a larger creative effort to put smiles everywhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FriendsWithYou, a 12-year-old artists’ collaborative founded by Samuel Borkson and Arturo Sandoval III, which began by making plush toy sculptures and had the chutzpah to trademark the slogan “Magic, Luck and Friendship,” has partnered with the Spanish company Lladró on a collection of ornaments and tabletop totems. Magical and lucky, they may be; friendly they certainly are, with their globular shapes and smiley faces reminiscent of other playful objects created by the two men (their Little Cloud Lamp, for instance). The striped porcelain ornaments with pastel ribbons are $165 each, online or at the Lladró Boutique, 500 Madison Avenue (East 52nd Street). Information: 800-785-3490 or lladro.com.\xad', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR3combo/11CURR3combo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR3combo/11CURR3combo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR3combo/11CURR3combo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR3combo/11CURR3combo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1531, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR3combo/11CURR3combo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR3combo/11CURR3combo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR3combo/11CURR3combo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Have Yourself a Friendly Little Christmas', 'kicker': 'Cheery', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Playful Ornaments That Do the Smiling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lladro SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FriendsWithYou', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madison Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas Trees', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T00:10:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5389c701-fbdf-52da-bb5d-63078ee56316', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5389c701-fbdf-52da-bb5d-63078ee56316'}, {'abstract': 'Among the menu items, glass ornaments shaped like Camembert and prosciutto.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/garden/at-john-derian-charcuterie-for-your-christmas-tree.html', 'snippet': 'Among the menu items, glass ornaments shaped like Camembert and prosciutto.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Visitors to John Derian’s East Village shop will find the space decked out for the holidays. This year, the decorations include a gourmet store’s worth of food-themed ornaments from Inge-Glas, a German company dating from 1596, where artisans still blow and paint every piece by hand. Mr. Derian discovered the ornaments in January at Christmasworld, a trade show in Frankfurt, and ordered peas, carrots, jam, honey, ice cream sandwiches and much more. “You think you’ve seen it all, then there’s hand-painted glass charcuterie,” he said about the prosciutto, cheeses and baguette (those shown are $19 to $26). “It’s the perfect hostess gift” he added, “bringing the appetizer.” Information: 212-677-3917 or johnderian.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR8/11CURR8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR8/11CURR8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR8/11CURR8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR8/11CURR8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR8/11CURR8-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR8/11CURR8-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR8/11CURR8-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Nibble on the Branches', 'kicker': 'Appetizing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Nibble on the Branches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suqi, Rima', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Derian, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Inge's Christmas Decor GmbH", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas Trees', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T00:11:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2180b054-e5d9-57b0-ab8b-4db308ce41c9', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2180b054-e5d9-57b0-ab8b-4db308ce41c9'}, {'abstract': 'Dedicated fans of the designer braved the elements for discounted goods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/fashion/at-the-alexander-wang-sample-sale-a-predawn-wait-in-the-rain-and-cold.html', 'snippet': 'Dedicated fans of the designer braved the elements for discounted goods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a grim, rainy Tuesday morning, as New York’s commuting masses rushed from stoops to subway entrances, a group of shoppers more concerned with style than with comfort huddled for hours outside 151 Wooster Street in SoHo, waiting for the 9 a.m. opening of the highly anticipated Alexander Wang sample sale, with some showing up as early as 4:45 a.m. Arranged in a loose line over at least a half-block, they clutched unruly umbrellas, rapidly cooling coffee from Starbucks and damp cigarettes. Some clinged to friends, a few made use of plastic bags and one savvy consumer brought a car and a partner with whom she repeatedly traded places, grabbing a few minutes of warmth before running back out to her spot. These customers were the dedicated few, battling the elements in the hope of walking away with a coveted (and deeply discounted) item from the Alexander Wang collection.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11LIFE10/11LIFE10-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11LIFE10/11LIFE10-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11LIFE10/11LIFE10-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11LIFE10/11LIFE10-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1372, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11LIFE10/11LIFE10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11LIFE10/11LIFE10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11LIFE10/11LIFE10-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Alexander Wang Sample Sale, a Predawn Wait in the Rain and Cold', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s a Little Rain When Bargains Await?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Safronova, Valeriya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Alexander (1983- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handbags and Purses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T00:11:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valeriya Safronova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valeriya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Safronova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f51103f-e961-5b22-bcfc-cfa27ae0d95d', 'word_count': 1889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f51103f-e961-5b22-bcfc-cfa27ae0d95d'}, {'abstract': 'Bergdorf Goodman’s senior vice president, and her fabulous wardrobe, are shrunk down once again for the holidays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/garden/linda-fargo-is-that-really-you.html', 'snippet': 'Bergdorf Goodman’s senior vice president, and her fabulous wardrobe, are shrunk down once again for the holidays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the fourth year that Soffieria de Carlini , an Italian glass company, has produced a hand-painted ornament modeled on Linda Fargo, the Bergdorf Goodman vice president and fashion maven, in an outfit she’s actually worn. “My biggest fear was that I’d end up in the markdown bin,” Ms. Fargo said about her first Mini-Me, which was dressed in an Yves Saint Laurent leopard-print dress and Michael Kors fur-collared blanket coat. But that ornament sold out, and an edition was born. This year’s look, a Naeem Khan cape with glittering patterns inspired by the Fountain of Apollo at Versailles, paired with a shocking pink Naeem Khan gown, was sported by Ms. Fargo at the Met Costume Institute Gala two years ago. Sold in an edition of 200, the Linda Fargo 2014 ornament is $85. Information: 888-774-2424 or bergdorfgoodman.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR9/11CURR9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 908, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR9/11CURR9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 908}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR9/11CURR9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 677, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR9/11CURR9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1354, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR9/11CURR9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR9/11CURR9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/garden/11CURR9/11CURR9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Tree That’s Well Dressed', 'kicker': 'Stylish', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Tree That’s Well Dressed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 