days wandering the streets. “I get very depressed because it’s like I’m on the treadmill going 80 miles an hour with the brakes on,” he said.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11HAIRCUTTER2/11HAIRCUTTER2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11HAIRCUTTER2/11HAIRCUTTER2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11HAIRCUTTER2/11HAIRCUTTER2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11HAIRCUTTER2/11HAIRCUTTER2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11HAIRCUTTER2/11HAIRCUTTER2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11HAIRCUTTER2/11HAIRCUTTER2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/fashion/11HAIRCUTTER2/11HAIRCUTTER2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hairstylist Provides Free Cuts to the Homeless', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Kindest Cut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bustos, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krueger, Alyson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T00:51:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alyson Krueger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alyson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krueger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15a74d83-20c2-53ec-8559-0312142f8461', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15a74d83-20c2-53ec-8559-0312142f8461'}, {'abstract': 'The case of a pregnant UPS driver before the Supreme Court is a reminder that working while pregnant has confounded the justices for a long time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/opinion/the-supreme-court-and-rights-for-pregnant-workers.html', 'snippet': 'The case of a pregnant UPS driver before the Supreme Court is a reminder that working while pregnant has confounded the justices for a long time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of my sharpest memories of elementary school is the way that teachers – the young, pretty, married ones – would occasionally just disappear. One day they would be in the classroom, looking as they always did, and the next day they would be gone, replaced by a substitute – in reality, the new teacher. Over the summer or during the next school year, you might catch a glimpse of the mysteriously vanished teacher at the grocery store, pushing a baby carriage. Where had the baby come from? The pattern became clear: Once a teacher even began thinking about having a baby, the classroom was no place for her – or any like-minded woman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'r