, free domestic calling and a charging station for mobile devices, will cost more than $200 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/nyregion/plan-approved-for-wi-fi-at-new-york-citys-pay-phones.html', 'snippet': 'The project, which will provide free Internet access, free domestic calling and a charging station for mobile devices, will cost more than $200 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The de Blasio administration’s plan to convert aging pay phones to Wi-Fi hot spots won unanimous approval on Wednesday from a review committee, clearing the way for the installation of thousands of Wi-Fi sites across New York City over the next decade.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan Approved for Wi-Fi at New York City’s Pay Phones', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panel Approves Plan for Wi-Fi at Pay Phones', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CityBridge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T02:53:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddd8faa0-5139-51f4-bc48-ccd78228c999', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddd8faa0-5139-51f4-bc48-ccd78228c999'}, {'abstract': 'The agency envisioned a system in which detainees would be offered the same rights and protections as inmates held in federal or American military prisons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/us/politics/cia-first-planned-jails-abiding-by-us-standards-.html', 'snippet': 'The agency envisioned a system in which detainees would be offered the same rights and protections as inmates held in federal or American military prisons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Just six days after the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks, President Bush signed a secret order that gave the Central Intelligence Agency the power to capture and imprison terrorists with Al Qaeda. But the order said nothing about where they should be held or how the agency should go about the business of questioning them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/world/JP-PRISONS-2/JP-PRISONS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/11/world/JP-PRISONS-2/JP-PRISONS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/world/JP-PRISONS-2/JP-PRISONS-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/world/JP-PRISONS-2/JP-PRISONS-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1302, 'width': 1994, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/world/JP-PRISONS-2/JP-PRISONS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/11/world/JP-PRISONS-2/JP-PRISONS-2-