rent kind of corporate maneuver: the spinoff, seen at work at companies ranging from Hewlett-Packard to eBay to Symantec.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corporate Spinoffs Expected to Grow Next Year, Study Finds', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ConocoPhillips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'eBay Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T04:37:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab3e5668-ed02-5f89-b81c-2e0697de753e', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab3e5668-ed02-5f89-b81c-2e0697de753e'}, {'abstract': 'The official account of a mission to rescue an American hostage being held by the Qaeda affiliate in Yemen was impossible to reconcile with villagers’ accounts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/world/middleeast/conflicting-accounts-rise-in-failed-hostage-rescue.html', 'snippet': 'The official account of a mission to rescue an American hostage being held by the Qaeda affiliate in Yemen was impossible to reconcile with villagers’ accounts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AL MUKALLA, Yemen — As the raid got underway in his village, Mubarak al-Harad was woken first by barking dogs, then explosions. Instinctively, he grabbed his gun.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conflicting Accounts Rise in Failed Hostage Rescue in Yemen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Conflicting Accounts Rise in Failed Hostage Rescue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Somers, Luke (1981- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Korkie, Pierre', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping and Hostages', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T04:42:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Saeed Al-Batati and Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Saeed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Al-Batati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b40412f7-58b7-57a0-b228-5e3c30fbd042', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b40412f7-58b7-57a0-b228-5e3c30fbd042'}, {'abstract': 'Airport workers have been attending the authority’s monthly meetings to press for a minimum wage of $10.10 an hour at its three major airports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/nyregion/board-of-port-authority-proposes-a-wage-increase-for-airport-workers.html', 'snippet': 'Airport workers have been attending the authority’s monthly meetings to press for a minimum wage of $10.10 an hour at its three major airports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The board meeting held by the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey on Wednesday may turn out to be the last one held somewhere other than the World Trade Center and the last one atten