or': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T05:04:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1982f1ae-a1c8-5291-9835-68fcb837f1c4', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1982f1ae-a1c8-5291-9835-68fcb837f1c4'}, {'abstract': 'Judges at the International Criminal Court ruled Wednesday that Libya had failed to comply with court orders relating to Seif al-Islam el-Qaddafi, a son of the former Libyan dictator, and referred the matter to the United Nations Security Council.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/world/europe/the-hague-court-seeks-united-nations-help-in-qaddafi-case.html', 'snippet': 'Judges at the International Criminal Court ruled Wednesday that Libya had failed to comply with court orders relating to Seif al-Islam el-Qaddafi, a son of the former Libyan dictator, and referred the matter to the United Nations Security Council.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Judges at the International Criminal Court ruled\xa0Wednesday\xa0that\xa0Libya\xa0had failed to comply with court orders relating to Seif al-Islam el-Qaddafi, a son of the former Libyan dictator, and referred\xa0the matter to the United Nations Security Council. They said\xa0Libya\xa0must hand over Mr. Qaddafi for trial in\xa0The Hague, as ordered by the court. He is accused of murder and persecution of civilians during the uprising that toppled his father, Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi. It is unclear what the Council could do, given that\xa0Libya\xa0is mired in chaos and fighting. A rebel faction based in\xa0Zintan, which has held Mr. Qaddafi since his capture in 2011,\xa0has always refused to surrender him, even to the government. Libya\xa0has argued it has the right to try him at home. “Noncompliance by Libya effectively prevents the court from fulfilling its mandate,”\xa0the judges wrote. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hague: Court Seeks U.N. Help in Qaddafi Case', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hague: Court Seeks U.N. Help in Qaddafi Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simons, Marlise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Seif al-Islam el-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T05:20:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3da4f6f-7a9a-5d70-94b8-eed2bb3d3e98', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3da4f6f-7a9a-5d70-94b8-eed2bb3d3e98'}, {'abstract': 'States that have not established exchanges could face severe disruption, or the prospect of creating one from scratch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/upshot/many-states-will-be-unprepared-if-court-weakens-health-law.html', 'snippet': 'States that have not established exchanges could face severe disruption, or the prospect of creating one from scratch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Supreme Court ruling this spring could upend health insurance markets in at least 34 stat