': 'nyt://article/272ffd9d-c303-55c0-9bc4-64719178c79b'}, {'abstract': 'A new book looks at Group f.64, one of the most famous collectives in the history of photography, whose members battled the Depression while grappling with photography’s evolving role in society.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/an-in-depth-history-of-group-f-64/', 'snippet': 'A new book looks at Group f.64, one of the most famous collectives in the history of photography, whose members battled the Depression while grappling with photography’s evolving role in society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1967, a 20-year-old photography student named Mary Street Alinder went to the University of Oregon for a workshop featuring several of her idols, four of the original members of the famed Group f.64: Ansel Adams, Imogen Cunningham, Brett Weston and Willard Van Dyke. The experience changed her life, starting with her working for Adams for the last few years of his. She was a co-author of the best-selling “Ansel Adams: An Autobiography,” and later wrote a biography, which has just been re-released. In the process she got to know members of Group f.64 and entwined herself with photographic history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An In-Depth History of Group f.64', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ADAMS, ANSEL', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alinder, Mary Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Imogen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lange, Dorothea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lavenson, Alma', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weston, Edward', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oakland (Calif)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T10:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Blaustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blaustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90ad61ad-e36d-5f95-8fd6-3f8ea5c2a64b', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90ad61ad-e36d-5f95-8fd6-3f8ea5c2a64b'}, {'abstract': 'What were you protesting? What was the experience like?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/have-your-ever-taken-part-in-a-protest/', 'snippet': 'What were you protesting? What was the experience like?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In response to the recent grand jury decisions in the Michael Brown and Eric Garner cases, many students have organized protests around the country to voice their anger.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/nyregion/y-SCHOOLS-LN/y-SCHOOLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/10/nyregion/y-SCHOOLS-LN/y-SCHOOLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/nyregion/y-SCHOOLS-LN/y-SCHOOLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/nyregion/y-SCHOOLS-LN/y-SCHOOLS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1472, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/nyregion/y-SCHOOLS-LN/y-SCHOOLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/10/nyregion/y-SCHOOLS-LN/y-SCHOOLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/nyregion/y-SCHOOLS-LN/y-SCHOOLS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Have You Ever Taken Part in a Protest?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T10:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7e7b73a-3e9c-5ae4-9a79-7ce8e2ed6081', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7e7b73a-3e9c-5ae4-9a79-7ce8e2ed6081'}, {'abstract': 'Wind turbines are mechanical devices that require regular maintenance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/opinion/the-cost-of-renewable-power.html', 'snippet': 'Wind turbines are mechanical devices that require regular maintenance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Re “Denmark’s tricky transition from fossil fuel” (Science, Nov. 12): Justin Gillis argues that “renewable power sources like wind and solar cost nothing to run, once installed.” I appreciate the author’s desire to promote renewable power sources, but wind turbines in particular are mechanical devices that require regular maintenance, such as lubrication, depending on their usage. It would be far more accurate to say that they require relatively little to run compared with traditional power generation sources.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cost of Renewable Power', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T10:13:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f33adf5-86bf-58b4-873c-86e430fcfd2d', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f33adf5-86bf-58b4-873c-86e430fcfd2d'}, {'abstract': 'Only a dictator could impose the further austerity required by the lenders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/opinion/greece-cant-suffer-more-austerity.html', 'snippet': 'Only a dictator could impose the further austerity required by the lenders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Re “A sea change in Greece?” (Opinion, Nov. 28) by Nicholas Gage: There is no doubt that successive Greek governments overspent in order to fuel their clientelistic networks and turned a blind eye to tax evasion. But European governments and European Union institutions should bear part of the blame; it suited them nicely to tolerate Greek governments’ questionable economic data: partly because data from other Union members were by no means impeccable either; and partly because European companies were doing lucrative business in Greece, bribing corrupt politicians.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece Can’t Suffer More Austerity', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T10:16:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/73d34c5f-c50d-51bf-aa68-145e93824b1c', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73d34c5f-c50d-51bf-aa68-145e93824b1c'}, {'abstract': 'Often castigated by the United States over its record on rights, democracy and civil liberties, Russia seized on the report to turn the tables on Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/world/europe/russia-us-cia-torture-report.html', 'snippet': 'Often castigated by the United States over its record on rights, democracy and civil liberties, Russia seized on the report to turn the tables on Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Often castigated by the United States over its record on human rights, democracy and civil liberties, Russia on Thursday seized on the Senate Intelligence Committee report on the use of torture by the C.I.A. to turn the tables on Washington and demand that those responsible be brought to justice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Denounces U.S. Over C.I.A. Torture Report', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Denounces U.S. Over C.I.A. Torture Report', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central 