own as heavy rain and wind began lashing the area as a storm moved down the coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/us/california-storm-pineapple-express-san-francisco-braces.html', 'snippet': 'Schools were closed and residents were hunkering down as heavy rain and wind began lashing the area as a storm moved down the coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Bay Area residents, bedeviled by water restrictions and arid farmland after three years of drought, suddenly had to cope with too much water Thursday as the strongest storm in at least five years pushed across Northern California, flooding roads and towns, toppling trees and knocking out power to tens of thousands of homes and businesses.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rainstorm Turns the San Francisco Area From Arid to Soggy in Hours', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rainstorm Turns the San Francisco Area From Arid to Soggy in Hours', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pogash, Carol', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Weather Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T15:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Pogash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce39e0a4-5bd8-5a35-944b-73e2760abff1', 'word_count': 1265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce39e0a4-5bd8-5a35-944b-73e2760abff1'}, {'abstract': '“The Cuckoo’s Calling” and “The Silkworm,” written under the alias Robert Galbraith and featuring a one-legged former military police investigator, will form the basis of the TV adaptation.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/j-k-rowlings-detective-novels-set-for-bbc-series/', 'snippet': '“The Cuckoo’s Calling” and “The Silkworm,” written under the alias Robert Galbraith and featuring a one-legged former military police investigator, will form the basis of the TV adaptation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The detective novels written by J. K. Rowling under the pseudonym Robert Galbraith are to be the basis for a new television series, the BBC said on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'J. K. Rowling’s Detective Novels Set for BBC Series', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowling, J K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T15:10:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94a81c8c-ca2c-5cf2-ae74-57f5f4977718', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94a81c8c-ca2c-5cf2-ae74-57f5f4977718'}, {'abstract': 'Juan E. Méndez, the United Nations’ special rapporteur on torture, said those responsible for C.I.A. abuses need to be punished.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/world/juan-mendez-calls-for-cia-torture-prosecutions.html', 'snippet': 'Juan E. Méndez, the United Nations’ special rapporteur on torture, said those responsible for C.I.A. abuses need to be punished.', 'lead_paragraph': "GENEVA — The C.I.A.'s use of torture and the United States’ reluctance to punish those responsible have set back efforts to fight torture worldwide, the United Nations expert investigating such abuses said Thursday, reinforcing a United Nations human rights official’s call for those involved to be prosecuted.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Torture Fight Set Back by U.S. Failure to Prosecute, U.N. Official Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T15:13:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74cb12ad-c67a-506d-9db6-5464e07ae735', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74cb12ad-c67a-506d-9db6-5464e07ae735'}, {'abstract': 'While reporting on the first beer mile world championships, Lindsay Crouse found serious athletes gleefully recounting strategies that included stomach stretching and chugging time trials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/12/11/enthusiasm-on-tap-at-the-beer-mile/', 'snippet': 'While reporting on the first beer mile world championships, Lindsay Crouse found serious athletes gleefully recounting strategies that included stomach stretching and chugging time trials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, Lindsay Crouse reported on a sporting event that is unfamiliar to most: the “beer mile.” But even before the first world championship race was announced, Ms. Crouse had some expertise. Below, she tells of her experience with the down-then-dash event and what she learned while covering the competition. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Enthusiasm on Tap at the Beer Mile', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crouse, Lindsay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T15:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc4beb81-8c58-5448-8b2c-9589158a4080', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc4beb81-8c58-5448-8b2c-9589158a4080'}, {'abstract': 'Jacob J. Lew discussed the impact of oil prices and sanctions on Russia, saying there’s a “perfect storm” of pressures on the country’s economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000003298636/treasury-secretary