ine': {'main': 'A Gateway to North Sumatra ', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Gateway to North Sumatra', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mishan, Ligaya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sky Cafe (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Elmhurst (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T15:28:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5882ca7-db10-58a3-ba9e-a5a67d2d75e9', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5882ca7-db10-58a3-ba9e-a5a67d2d75e9'}, {'abstract': 'Phil Jackson’s first Knicks team stinks to the tune of 4-20. How much worse could it be without Carmelo Anthony, its $124 million centerpiece?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/sports/basketball/carmelo-anthony-knicks-rebuild-might-be-better-off-as-a-tear-down.html', 'snippet': 'Phil Jackson’s first Knicks team stinks to the tune of 4-20. How much worse could it be without Carmelo Anthony, its $124 million centerpiece?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometime very soon, Carmelo Anthony and his people will need to sit down with Phil Jackson and his people, including Coach Derek Fisher and especially the Knicks’ owner, James L. Dolan, to lay some cards on the table. They will need to acknowledge that jokers in Knicks uniforms are running wild and that the quick Jackson fix that Anthony believed he was signing up for last summer is not happening this season or quite possibly next season.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/sports/ARATON/ARATON-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 483, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/sports/ARATON/ARATON-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 483}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/sports/ARATON/ARATON-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 824, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/sports/ARATON/ARATON-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1649, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/sports/ARATON/ARATON-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/sports/ARATON/ARATON-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/sports/ARATON/ARATON-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Knicks Rebuild, a Bulldozer May Help', 'kicker': 'On Pro Basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Light at End of Tunnel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Phil (1945- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T15:34:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c39e7bca-78d7-5d0a-8a07-4bc73dd9e570', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c39e7bca-78d7-5d0a-8a07-4bc73dd9e570'}, {'abstract': 'To get truly great sinkers, you’re going to have to make them yourself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/07/magazine/time-to-make-the-doughnuts.html', 'snippet': 'To get truly great sinkers, you’re going to have to make them yourself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s something I’ve never quite understood. Places that serve fried food — French fries, fried chicken, tempura, you name it — either serve it straight from the fryer, at its peak, or they find some way, often a heat lamp, to keep it as crisp as possible. So why don’t doughnuts get the same love? Most are so far removed from that bubbling bath of oil by the time you eat them that they’ve almost entirely lost their fresh-fried luster.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/magazine/14eat1/14mag-14eat.t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 549, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/magazine/14eat1/14mag-14eat.t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 549}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/magazine/14eat1/14mag-14eat.t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 937, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'lega