: 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T16:04:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bf3a052-5699-5cf4-b0d3-16d41b91324a', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bf3a052-5699-5cf4-b0d3-16d41b91324a'}, {'abstract': 'Classical music is serious business, yet some of this year’s performances were playful and wickedly funny.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/arts/music/the-funniest-classical-music-performances-of-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Classical music is serious business, yet some of this year’s performances were playful and wickedly funny.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a funny thing about classical music. However much you love it, it’s hard to argue that it is just that: funny. So when I announced to my colleagues that my end-of-year list would highlight the performances of 2014 that made me laugh, one of them deadpanned, “You mean as in: laugh at them?”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14WOLLHEIM/14WOLLHEIM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14WOLLHEIM/14WOLLHEIM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14WOLLHEIM/14WOLLHEIM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14WOLLHEIM/14WOLLHEIM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14WOLLHEIM/14WOLLHEIM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14WOLLHEIM/14WOLLHEIM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14WOLLHEIM/14WOLLHEIM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Funniest Classical Music Performances of 2014', 'kicker': 'The Year in Culture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Welcome Hints of Mischief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T16:08:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22f25ab3-865f-53a8-8e3a-bc3a07c3386e', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22f25ab3-865f-53a8-8e3a-bc3a07c3386e'}, {'abstract': 'The art often thrives most vividly these days in the hands of a teeming worldwide pool of gifted young musicians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/arts/music/youthful-mastery-on-display-at-tanglewood-spoleto-and-lucerne-festivals.html', 'snippet': 'The art often thrives most vividly these days in the hands of a teeming worldwide pool of gifted young musicians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ah, youth! Young audience members, to hear classical music administrators tell it, are the holy grail, an elusive, endangered species that must assiduously be preserved and cultivated if the art is to survive. Yet — cruel or happy paradox — the art itself often thrives most vividly these days in the hands of its youth: a teeming worldwide pool of young musicians that has never been more gifted.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14OESTREICH/14OESTREICH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14OESTREICH/14OESTREICH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14OESTREICH/14OESTREICH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14OESTREICH/14OESTREICH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14OESTREICH/14OESTREICH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14OESTREICH/14OESTREICH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14OESTREICH/14OESTREICH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Youthful Mastery on Display at Tanglewood, Spoleto and Lucerne Festivals', 'kicker': 'The Year in Culture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classical Artistry in Young Hands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T16:10:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/108153d8-5553-5a92-867b-d2af5730c4a0', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/108153d8-5553-5a92-867b-d2af5730c4a0'}, {'abstract': 'The actress, who received two nominations, said she was stunned that a movie she shot in March was already up for awards.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/golden-globes-2015-julianne-moore-waited-and-cleaned/', 'snippet': 'The actress, who received two nominations, said she was stunned that a movie she shot in March was already up for awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The thing about living in New York and waiting for the big award nominations to be revealed is that they happen around 8:30 a.m. Eastern standard time, when most everyone in the city is already up. Which is what happened with Julianne Moore on Thursday. She was up, she had fed her kids and was trying to bide her time calmly until the Golden Globes nods came out. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/arts/juliannemoore/juliannemoore-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/11/arts/juliannemoore/juliannemoore-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/arts/juliannemoore/juliannemoore-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/arts/juliannemoore/juliannemoore-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/arts/juliannemoore/juliannemoore-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/11/arts/juliannemoore/juliannemoore-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/arts/juliannemoore/juliannemoore-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Golden Globes 2015: Julianne Moore Waited and Cleaned', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Julianne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T16:11:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcfe9af2-c278-59cc-8782-e14ba43ec313', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcfe9af2-c278-59cc-8782-e14ba43ec313'}, {'abstract': 'If the post-downturn classical music world sometimes seemed to have more slamming doors than a Feydeau farce this year, there was also glorious music and breakout performances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/arts/music/the-biggest-classical-music-stories-of-2014.html', 'snippet': 'If the post-downturn classical music world sometimes seemed to have more slamming doors than a Feydeau farce this year, there was also glorious music and breakout performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'he Minnesota Orchestra ended its 16-month lockout, the Atlanta Symphony Orchestra started and ended its second lockout in two years, and the Metropolitan Opera managed to avoid a lockout of its own after months of labor battles. But if the post-downturn classical music world sometimes seemed to have more slamming doors than a Feydeau farce this year, there was also glorious music, breakout performances and lots to chew over. Here, then, is the latest installment of the not-quite-annual, arbitrary, unsought and utterly undistinguished Special Awards for 2014, hereby rechristened the Ludwig Awards. (They are named for Ludwig Minkus, the ballet composer. Maybe you were thinking of someone else?)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14COPPER