ite children’s activity, and the Geneva-based MSC Cruises has teamed with the Lego Group\xa0 to bring the popular pastime to the seas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/topics/11lego/11lego-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/11/topics/11lego/11lego-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 651}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/topics/11lego/11lego-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 945, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/topics/11lego/11lego-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1889, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/topics/11lego/11lego-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/11/topics/11lego/11lego-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/topics/11lego/11lego-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Playing: Lego the Cruise', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lego Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T16:29:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5c4e841-be75-5a2c-9c10-08fc6fa20adf', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5c4e841-be75-5a2c-9c10-08fc6fa20adf'}, {'abstract': '“Inherent Vice,” Paul Thomas Anderson’s adaptation of the Thomas Pynchon novel, is a labyrinthine noir set in sunny Los Angeles, circa 1970.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/movies/inherent-vice-directed-by-paul-thomas-anderson.html', 'snippet': '“Inherent Vice,” Paul Thomas Anderson’s adaptation of the Thomas Pynchon novel, is a labyrinthine noir set in sunny Los Angeles, circa 1970.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Paul Thomas Anderson’s cinematic love-in “Inherent Vice,” Joaquin Phoenix plays Doc Sportello, a Los Angeles shamus in Jesus sandals trucking through the sunshine and noir like a stoner Philip Marlowe. Based on the 2009 Thomas Pynchon novel, the film is set in 1970, the year after Charles Manson freaked the city out and its good vibrations faded into an endless summer bummer. That’s the gospel according to Joan Didion, at any rate, who in “The White Album” writes that many people she knew believed the 1960s ended Aug. 9, 1969, the day the Manson Family began its Helter Skelter frenzy. Somehow Doc, a hippie crowned in a halo of pot smoke, never got the message. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/inherent1/inherent1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/inherent1/inherent1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/inherent1/inherent1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/inherent1/inherent1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1526, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/inherent1/inherent1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/inherent1/inherent1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/inherent1/inherent1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Noir Days of Sun, Los Angeles Smog and Marijuana Haze', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Noir Days of Sun, Los Angeles Smog and Marijuana Haze', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, PAUL THOMAS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pynchon, Thomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Inherent Vice (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T16:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e57fe85-f08b-5e6f-b5b4-040d8781a852', 'word_count': 1271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e57fe85-f08b-5e6f-b5b4-040d8781a852'}, {'abstract': 'Guerlain’s limited-edition top coat lends an artistic sensibility to seasonal manicures.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/gold-nail-polish-guerlain-for-the-holiday-season/', 'snippet': 'Guerlain’s limited-edition top coat lends an artistic sensibility to seasonal manicures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shimmery nail polishes are a dime a dozen this time of year: glitter-filled bottles, metallic versions of every color imaginable, paints that come with glitzy powder to dust on top. But for a more artistic take on festive lacquer, consider Guerlain’s L’Oiseau de Feu top coat. The limited-edition bottle, whose name is French for “firebird,” is essentially gold leaf for your fingertips. Spackling on layers creates all-over sparkle with texture, but it’s in exercising restraint that\xa0the magic happens. Strategically apply the asymmetrical little flecks of gold —\xa0a swipe across the tips, dabs to create circles —\xa0for a sophisticated manicure with a painterly touch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/t-magazine/11nails-beddie/11nails-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/11/t-magazine/11nails-beddie/11nails-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/11/t-magazine/11nails-beddie/11nails-beddie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, 