me': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilford, John Noble', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Science (Journal)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T18:09:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Corcoran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corcoran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a39cfbaf-181a-5ca3-ba80-7d55dd1d29e1', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a39cfbaf-181a-5ca3-ba80-7d55dd1d29e1'}, {'abstract': 'In this lesson, students will learn about the extent of cyberattacks just in the past year and the risks they pose for companies, governments and individuals.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/teaching-about-cybersecurity-taking-steps-to-improve-online-safety-and-prevent-data-breaches/', 'snippet': 'In this lesson, students will learn about the extent of cyberattacks just in the past year and the risks they pose for companies, governments and individuals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | From data breaches at Target, Home Depot, JPMorgan and even the White House to celebrities’ stolen photos, cybersecurity and online privacy have been making the headlines every week. But how do data breaches at companies and government institutions affect individuals? What can individuals do to enhance their digital security? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/technology/03HACK-LN/03HACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/03/technology/03HACK-LN/03HACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 696}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/technology/03HACK-LN/03HACK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 883, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/technology/03HACK-LN/03HACK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1766, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/technology/03HACK-LN/03HACK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/03/technology/03HACK-LN/03HACK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/03/technology/03HACK-LN/03HACK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Teaching About Cybersecurity: Taking Steps to Improve Online Safety and Prevent Data Breaches', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T18:12:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Cutraro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cutraro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c2e9331-6aae-5a1e-b371-38400b00b1c5', 'word_count': 1500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c2e9331-6aae-5a1e-b371-38400b00b1c5'}, {'abstract': 'Jorge Ramos insisted that the president could have stopped deportations long ago.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/finally-a-news-anchor-challenged-the-president-over-deportations/', 'snippet': 'Jorge Ramos insisted that the president could have stopped deportations long ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few editorial pages do it, immigrant-rights and Latino advocates certainly do it, but mainstream news outlets, not so much. That is, forcefully challenge President Obama on immigration – on the disconnect between his oratory about hopes and dreams and his actual deportation record; and on the dissonance behind his recently announced plan to use executive action to defer deportations for millions. He kept saying he couldn’t legally do such a thing – until he did it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finally, a News Anchor Challenged the President Over Deportations', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramos, Jorge (1958- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Univision', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T18:14:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c8c73fa-ecc8-512c-9393-5251f7e8958b', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c8c73fa-ecc8-512c-9393-5251f7e8958b'}, {'abstract': 'Federal prosecutors investigating the lane closings at the George Washington Bridge are considering using a provision to argue that the bridge was used for a purpose other than its intended one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/nyregion/in-george-washington-bridge-case-prosecutors-could-use-fraud-statute-to-charge-christie-associates.html', 'snippet': 'Federal prosecutors investigating the lane closings at the George Washington Bridge are considering using a provision to argue that the bridge was used for a purpose other than its intended one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal prosecutors investigating the lane closings at the George Washington Bridge last year are considering charges based on a rarely used provision of a fraud statute, under which they could argue that associates of Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey used the bridge for a purpose other than its intended one, according to people close to the case.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/nyregion/CHRISTIEweb1/CHRISTIEweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/nyregion/CHRISTIEweb1/CHRISTIEweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/nyregion/CHRISTIEweb1/CHRISTIEweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/nyregion/CHRISTIEweb1/CHRISTIEweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/nyregion/CHRISTIEweb1/CHRISTIEweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/nyregion/CHRISTIEweb1/CHRISTIEweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/nyregion/CHRISTIEweb1/CHRISTIEweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bridge Scandal Prosecutors May Use Obscure Fraud Law to Charge Christie Associates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. May Use Obscure Law to Prosecute Bridge Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zernike, Kate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'George Washington Bridge', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Lee (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fishman, Paul J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T18:14:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zernike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/148780c7-d0ad-557e-90f4-de37bc72684f', 'word_count': 1194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/148780c7-d0ad-557e-90f4-de37bc72684f'}, {'abstract': 'While the actual pieces could be impressive, the mounting of works in museums and galleries this year was noteworthy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/arts/design/roberta-smiths-top-art-shows-of-2014-gober-koons-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'While the actual pieces could be impressive, the mounting of works in museums and galleries this year was noteworthy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many ways to parse the highs and lows of the year just ending. Among the more uplifting events was, for example, the Detroit Institute of Arts’ being rescued from the city’s predatory creditors — and also from city ownership. Another was the large and fabulous assortment of Cubist works given by the collector Leonard A. Lauder to the Metropolitan Museum of Art, one of the most important gifts in the museum’s 144-year history. Among the lows was the Met’s clumsy redesign of its three-block-long plaza along Fifth Avenue. (Never mind who paid for it.) The deepest low: the needless destruction of the building formerly known as the American Folk Art Museum by the Museum of Modern Art.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14SMITH1/14SMITH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14SMITH1/14SMITH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14SMITH1/14SMITH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14SMITH1/14SMITH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14SMITH1/14SMITH1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14SMITH1/14SMITH1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14SMITH1/14SMITH1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Roberta Smith’s Top Art Shows of 2014: Gober, Koons and More', 'kicker': 'The Year in Culture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perfecting the How as Well as the What', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gober, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koons, Jeff', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T18:17:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45b3d0d7-3227-503e-976e-b03ef4486270', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45b3d0d7-3227-503e-976e-b03ef4486270'}, {'abstract': 'Holland Cotter lists notable art events of the year, from the Pompidou’s “Multiple Modernities” show to a collaborative exhibition in Berkeley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/arts/design/holland-cotters-notable-art-events-of-2014-black-radical-brooklyn-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Holland Cotter lists notable art events of the year, from the Pompidou’s “Multiple Modernities” show to a collaborative exhibition in Berkeley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This was a good year to stop taking notice of money. What’s the point? Auction prices and the plausible value are a joke. And annual “records” are guaranteed (an $853 million Christie’s night in November) because they’re good advertising. Buyers and sellers get to strut; the press gets to write. Total win. And it’s all happening on some odd little art-world planet populated by (mostly) boys playing “I’m bigger than you are.” But in the real art world, which is a spacious and complex place, more interesting things are going on. Here are a few I remember from this year:', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14COTTER1/14COTTER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14COTTER1/14COTTER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14COTTER1/14COTTER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/arts/14COTTER1/14COTTER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1273, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 