 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/b219fb10-3b43-5378-8fa8-6c74ffcba644', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/b219fb10-3b43-5378-8fa8-6c74ffcba644'}, {'abstract': 'In Ali Smith’s novel “How to Be Both,” a teenage girl and a Renaissance painter are linked across the centuries in a story exploring dualities in art, life and gender identity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/books/how-to-be-both-a-novel-by-ali-smith.html', 'snippet': 'In Ali Smith’s novel “How to Be Both,” a teenage girl and a Renaissance painter are linked across the centuries in a story exploring dualities in art, life and gender identity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As an introduction to the conundrums and complexities of Ali Smith’s bicameral novel “How to Be Both,” consider this conversation between a hairsplitting teenage girl named George and her more loosely cerebral mother. The mother is dead, and the conversation is taking place in George’s memory. But let’s not get too complicated — yet. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12BOOK/12BOOK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 917, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12BOOK/12BOOK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 917}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12BOOK/12BOOK-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 671, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12BOOK/12BOOK-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1341, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i