nce and deprivation.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Salt of the Earth,” Wim Wenders’s new documentary about the life and work of the Brazilian photographer Sebastião Salgado, elegantly inhabits a moral and aesthetic paradox. Mr. Salgado’s photographs illuminate some of the worst horrors of the modern world: starvation, war, poverty, displacement. They are also beautiful, dramatic visual artifacts, and their power has a double effect. We are drawn into the contemplation of terrible realities, but at the same time our attention turns to the person bearing witness.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/SALT1/SALT1-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/SALT1/SALT1-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/SALT1/SALT1-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/SALT1/SALT1-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/SALT1/SALT1-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/SALT1/SALT1-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/SALT1/SALT1-thumbLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Eyes of a Beholder of Hardship', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Eyes of a Beholder of Hardship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wenders, Wim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salgado, Juliano Ribeiro', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salgado, Sebastiao', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Salt of the Earth (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T20:28:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/771f33ad-fd38-5b6f-9bad-2e8d219b06dc', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/771f33ad-fd38-5b6f-9bad-2e8d219b06dc'}, {'abstract': 'Tabata workouts, a rigorous form of interval training developed in Japan, is offered at several locations in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/nyregion/tabata-workouts-offer-a-rigorous-intensity.html', 'snippet': 'Tabata workouts, a rigorous form of interval training developed in Japan, is offered at several locations in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERVAL training — alternating short bouts of intense exercise with periods of recovery — is considered part of any well-rounded fitness routine. Exercise physiologists and trainers say it helps speed weight loss and build endurance. But those seeking an especially rigorous form of interval training, without spending hours trying to do it, might consider Tabata workouts. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12URBANATHLETE/12URBANATHLETE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12URBANATHLETE/12URBANATHLETE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12URBANATHLETE/12URBANATHLETE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12URBANATHLETE/12URBANATHLETE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1273, 'width': 1999, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12URBANATHLETE/12URBANATHLETE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12URBANATHLETE/12URBANATHLETE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12URBANATHLETE/12URBANATHLETE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Raising the Bar for Interval Training ', 'kicker': 'Urban Athlete', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Raising the Bar for Interval Training', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tabata, Izumi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T20:31:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13569f48-bc24-5811-b598-9d04a53c756c', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13569f48-bc24-5811-b598-9d04a53c756c'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Dianne Feinstein, chairwoman of the committee that investigated the C.I.A.’s interrogation program, offered a live rebuttal as John O. Brennan, the agency’s director, responded to the committee’s findings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/12/11/feinstein-takes-to-twitter-to-rebut-brennan-on-c-i-a-interrogation/', 'snippet': 'Senator Dianne Feinstein, chairwoman of the committee that investigated the C.I.A.’s interrogation program, offered a live rebuttal as John O. Brennan, the agency’s director, responded to the committee’s findings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Dianne Feinstein was not in the audience when John O. Brennan, the director of the Central Intelligence Agency, addressed his rank and file and took questions Thursday in a news conference at the agency’s headquarters, but she was clearly watching.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feinstein Takes to Twitter to Rebut Brennan on C.I.A. Interrogation', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, John O', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinstein, Dianne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T20:31:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4773b9d2-8231-5a1c-a47c-2309c1fcb49d', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4773b9d2-8231-5a1c-a47c-2309c1fcb49d'}, {'abstract': 'These skis, boards, boots, gloves and goggles will ease your way on the mountain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/travel/gear-for-a-snowy-getaway.html', 'snippet': 'These skis, boards, boots, gloves and goggles will ease your way on the mountain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forget the GoPro and the Bluetooth gloves. This season’s best ski and snowboard gear takes full advantage of technology to simply help improve your experience on the slopes. Ski materials like lightweight carbon, gloves that warm your hands effectively and boards that help ease your ascent are a few examples of the items that take the essentialist approach to skiing and boarding. At right is a fuller look at these and more.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14GEAR_COMBO/14GEAR_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 307, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14GEAR_COMBO/14GEAR_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 307}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14GEAR_COMBO/14GEAR_COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 524, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14GEAR_COMBO/14GEAR_COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1047, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14GEAR_COMBO/14GEAR_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14GEAR_COMBO/14GEAR_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/travel/14GEAR_COMBO/14GEAR_COMBO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gear for a Snowy Getaway', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winter-Worthy Gear for a Snowy Getaway . . .', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snowboarding', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protective Clothing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T20:39:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cindy Hirschfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cindy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirschfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adba42a9-0e5c-5b6e-bc4a-6a4404d4e9d1', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adba42a9-0e5c-5b6e-bc4a-6a4404d4e9d1'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary “Maidan,” filmed during protests in Ukraine, focuses on the physical movement of crowds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/movies/maidan-filmed-during-protests-in-ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'The documentary “Maidan,” filmed during protests in Ukraine, focuses on the physical movement of crowds.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Maidan,” filmed in and around Independence Square in Kiev during the protests of late 2013 and early 2014, is interested in the physical movement of a movement. This documentary from Sergei Loznitsa, perhaps best known in the United States for the fiction feature “My Joy,” forgoes explanations. It unfolds almost exclusively in static tableau shots, as concerned with form and beauty as it is with advocacy.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12MAIDEN/12MAIDEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12MAIDEN/12MAIDEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12MAIDEN/12MAIDEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12MAIDEN/12MAIDEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12MAIDEN/12MAIDEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12MAIDEN/12MAIDEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12MAIDEN/12MAIDEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So Many Faces Make Up One Crowd', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Maidan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loznitsa, Sergei', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Maidan (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T20:40:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Kenigsberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6dd67ba-6fd8-57cf-bd14-5808a60652b6', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6dd67ba-6fd8-57cf-bd14-5808a60652b6'}, {'abstract': 'A teacher in North Korea witnesses the regime’s limited embrace of change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/books/review/suki-kims-without-you-there-is-no-us.html', 'snippet': 'A teacher in North Korea witnesses the regime’s limited embrace of change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suki Kim’s “Without You, There Is No Us,” a chilling memoir of this Korean-American author’s 2011 stint as a visiting English instructor at a North Korean \xaduniversity, takes its title from a patriotic song extolling the Great General Comrade Kim Jong-il, whose death was announced on what happened to be the day of the author’s final class in the Democratic People’s Republic. The book reminds us that evil is not only banal; it is also completely arbitrary. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/books/review/14HONG/14HONG-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 543, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/books/review/14HONG/14HONG-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 543}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/books/review/14HONG/14HONG-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 926, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/books/review/14HONG/14HONG-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1733, 'width': 1916, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/books/review/14HONG/14HONG-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/books/review/14HONG/14HONG-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/books/review/14HONG/14HONG-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Suki Kim’s ‘Without You, There Is No Us’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State of Isolation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim, Suki', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T20:44:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Euny Hong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Euny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c890cd52-fcad-5c68-b74f-0b0b4bcf7de9', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c890cd52-fcad-5c68-b74f-0b0b4bcf7de9'}, {'abstract': '“Yoko Ono: One Woman Show, 1960-1971,” including 125 of Ms. Ono’s early installations, audio recordings and works on paper, is to open in May.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/11/moma-plans-a-yoko-ono-show/', 'snippet': '“Yoko Ono: One Woman Show, 1960-1971,” including 125 of Ms. Ono’s early installations, audio recordings and works on paper, is to open in May.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In December 1971, Yoko Ono presented a conceptual work at the Museum of Modern Art – sort of. The typically prankish piece purported to be a solo exhibition by Ms. Ono at the museum. But though she advertised the show and printed a catalog for it, the show was unauthorized, and none of Ms. Ono’s work was on display, except for a sign she posted at the entrance telling visitors that she had released flies at the museum, and that everyone was invited to track them down throughout the city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MoMA Plans a Yoko Ono Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subj