couple comedy about a prim older woman and her dance teacher, a young gay man.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The credits of “Six Dance Lessons in Six Weeks” evoke a lost film from the 1970s, featuring both the John Cassavetes collaborator Gena Rowlands and the storied cinematographer Vilmos Zsigmond. The reality of this new film from Arthur Allan Seidelman is that it’s a cornball odd-couple comedy: Prim older woman meets a brassy young gay man. Still, it’s extraordinary just watching the peerless Ms. Rowlands wring the most out of the repartee in this adaptation of a play by Richard Alfieri.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SIXLESSON/12SIXLESSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SIXLESSON/12SIXLESSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 717}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SIXLESSON/12SIXLESSON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 857, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SIXLESSON/12SIXLESSON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1919, 'width': 1605, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SIXLESSON/12SIXLESSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SIXLESSON/12SIXLESSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 