d illustrations to a jukebox commemoration. The Odetta of the title is the great African-American singer whose full name was Odetta Holmes; her voice alone, so gravely lustrous, gives the piece drama. In her singing, we hear beauty, eloquence, suspense. Her words help us recognize that Odetta was an inspiring pioneer and symbol for civil rights; her folk-based music — one of the songs is by Bob Dylan — gives us the sense of a movement larger than any one person or even any one cause.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12JUMPODETTA/JUMPODETTA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 880, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12JUMPODETTA/JUMPODETTA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 880}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12JUMPODETTA/JUMPODETTA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 699, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12JUMPODETTA/JUMPODETTA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1397, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12JUMPODETTA/JUMPODETTA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12JUMPODETTA/JUMPODETTA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12JUMPODETTA/JUMPODETTA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'widt