_paragraph': 'In “Skating to New York,” four Canadian high school friends and a kid brother spend one of the coldest days of the year trying to skate roughly 25 miles across Lake Ontario, frozen over for the first time in decades. Hoping to become local legends, they meet ice fishermen and smugglers, battle the elements and hypothermia. But it’s what they’re leaving behind — and what they’ll return to — that’s the real story.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SKATINGTONEWYORK/SKATINGTONEWYORK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 257, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SKATINGTONEWYORK/SKATINGTONEWYORK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 257}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SKATINGTONEWYORK/SKATINGTONEWYORK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SKATINGTONEWYORK/SKATINGTONEWYORK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 878, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SKATINGTONEWYORK/SKATINGTONEWYORK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SKATINGTONEWYORK/SKATINGTONEWYORK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/12SKATINGTONEWYORK/SKATINGTONEWYORK-thumbLarge.jp