'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/cb5fe9f8-f252-5753-987e-da08120c276a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/cb5fe9f8-f252-5753-987e-da08120c276a'}, {'abstract': 'Young men work less. Older men work more. Here’s what happens at every age.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/upshot/the-rise-of-men-who-dont-work-and-what-they-do-instead.html', 'snippet': 'Young men work less. Older men work more. Here’s what happens at every age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At every age, the chances of not working have changed in the last 15 years. Teenagers are far more likely not to work. Older people are retiring later and working more. In the ages in between — the periods of life when most people work — the changes have been smaller, but they are still substantial.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rise of Men Who Don’t Work, and What They Do Instead', 'kicker': 'Nonemployed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Labor Statistics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T23:15:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fae80446-31d3-567f-9dd6-cd6616ca289e', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fae80