ndship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T23:30:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Strawser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strawser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/727f6ad3-ab66-5e8b-a5f4-2e84ea740afb', 'word_count': 1490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/727f6ad3-ab66-5e8b-a5f4-2e84ea740afb'}, {'abstract': 'A “Live From Lincoln Center” broadcast of “Curtain Up” documents a commemoration of the School of American Ballet’s 80th anniversary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/arts/dance/live-from-lincoln-center-to-air-curtain-up.html', 'snippet': 'A “Live From Lincoln Center” broadcast of “Curtain Up” documents a commemoration of the School of American Ballet’s 80th anniversary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'America has far too few broadcasts of performances by its own dancers on either television or the big screen. In cinemas, it’s become easier in recent years to see current performances by the Bolshoi and the Royal Ballet than by New York City Ballet and American Ballet Theater. This is bizarre; no city in the world has a better claim to be Dance City than New York, and yet there’s far too little evidence of this (or of dance across America) on our screens. Where is local pride?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Performance Onstage Returns Anew on the Screen', 'kicker': "Critic's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Performance Onstage Returns Anew on the Screen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Balanchine, George', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diamond, Matthew', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'School of American Ballet', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Curtain Up: The School of American Ballet Workshop Performance (TV Program)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-11T23:32:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98c22c36-44c9-5aa9-a729-76f38ebb6a33', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98c22c36-44c9-5aa9-a729-76f38ebb6a33'}, {'abstract': 'The share of men aged 25 to 54 who are not working has more than tripled since the late 1960s, with many having decided that low-wage jobs will not improve their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/upshot/unemployment-the-vanishing-male-worker-how-america-fell-behind.html', 'snippet': 'The share of men aged 25 to 54 who are not working has more than tripled since the late 1960s, with many having decided that low-wage jobs will not improve their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANNAPOLIS, Md. — Frank Walsh still pays dues to the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers, but more than four years have passed since his name was called at the union hall where the few available jobs are distri