rgency to the effort by Park Geun-hye, president of South Korea, to boost domestic support for unification and lay the practical groundwork to make it happen. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Peaceful Korean Unification Possible?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is Peaceful Korean Unification Possible?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park Geun-hye', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T02:12:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9424a651-467b-51c8-bfc0-df98f92979f4', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9424a651-467b-51c8-bfc0-df98f92979f4'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Marcus wrote many episodes of shows like “Peyton Place” as well as the soap-opera parody “Mary Hartman, Mary Hartman.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/arts/television/ann-marcus-writer-for-mary-hartman-dies-at-93.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Marcus wrote many episodes of shows like “Peyton Place” as well as the soap-opera parody “Mary Hartman, Mary Hartman.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ann Marcus, who wrote scripts for soap operas and won an Emmy for parodying them as a creator and head writer for the 1970s cult hit “Mary Hartman, Mary Hartman,” died on Dec. 3 in Los Angeles. She was 93. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The Ne