ed costumes, primitive cats, birds, dreamlike fish and grinning dogs are recurrent themes. Of course, Mr. Kuchera’s father never actually visited his ancestral home, nor did he have pets.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14REASONS1/14REASONS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14REASONS1/14REASONS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14REASONS1/14REASONS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14REASONS1/14REASONS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14REASONS1/14REASONS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14REASONS1/14REASONS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14REASONS1/14REASONS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Ramen Nearby, Kuchera Museum Houses a Father’s Art in Morningside Heights', 'kicker': 'Two Good Reasons', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Legacy of Art, With Ramen Nearby', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Besonen, Julie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kuchera Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Morningside Heights (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuchera, John C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jin Ramen (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T05:54:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Besonen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Besonen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d5b82b0-6d7e-5891-89b5-67106aa0e708', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d5b82b0-6d7e-5891-89b5-67106aa0e708'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/arts/television/whats-on-tv-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': "9 P.M. (Starz) TRUST ME (2014) Clark Gregg (“Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.”) wrote, directed and stars in this black comedy about Hollywood wheeling and dealing, centered on Howard Holloway, a floundering agent specializing in child actors. He should know: Howard used to be one himself, until his career sank 36 years earlier with a Jan-Michael Vincent surf movie that was never made. But a chance meeting with a wildly talented 13-year-old from Oklahoma (Saxon Sharbino) with a controlling, alcoholic father (Paul Sparks) might be his road to redemption. Felicity Huffman plays the producer of a new vampire franchise, and Allison Janney is her casting director, both of whom loathe Howard; Sam Rockwell is his client-poaching archrival. “The performances and some of the writing are the movie’s strongest elements,” Stephen Holden wrote in The New York Times. Ms. Sharbino “has the radiance and skills to be a teenage megastar in a ‘Twilight'-like series.” He said Mr. Gregg “succeeds in finding some humanity inside a dislikable creep.” But “as the movie picks up speed and undergoes sudden, confusing plot reversals, it loses its satirical edge,” he added. “You can’t help wondering if the production ran out of money while racing to meet a deadline.”", 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T06:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/31483c45-50c9-5ac9-965c-a09530a613f7', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31483c45-50c9-5ac9-965c-a09530a613f7'}, {'abstract': 'Fátima Ptacek, a 14-year-old actress, walks her dog before a Sunday filled with gymnastics, reading and time with her family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/nyregion/the-voice-of-dora-the-explorer-fatima-ptacek-is-a-busy-teenager.html', 'snippet': 'Fátima Ptacek, a 14-year-old actress, walks her dog before a Sunday filled with gymnastics, reading and time with her family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the voice of the cross-cultural cartoon icon Dora the Explorer, Fátima Ptacek, 14, spends her week racing from classes at Avenues: The World School, in Chelsea, to Hyperbolic Audio studios in Midtown, where she tapes Nickelodeon’s “Dora the Explorer” and a spinoff, “Dora and Friends: Into The City!” The actress, who recently appeared in the film “Before I Disappear,” lives in Jackson Heights, Queens, with her mother, Lucia, 37; her father, Jack, 47; her half sister, Lesley, 18; and her dog, Sasha. Her half brothers — Andrew, 21; Jonathan, 19; and Alex, 17 — visit on weekends.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE2/14ROUTINE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE2/14ROUTINE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE2/14ROUTINE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE2/14ROUTINE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE2/14ROUTINE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE2/14ROUTINE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE2/14ROUTINE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150