{'main': 'Morlot to Step Down as Conductor of Théâtre Royal de la Monnaie', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morlot, Ludovic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Theatre Royal de la Monnaie (Brussels, Belgium)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T16:58:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37f7709f-c6a4-59c2-b488-fb55e42e4694', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37f7709f-c6a4-59c2-b488-fb55e42e4694'}, {'abstract': '“Sinatra: An American Icon” will open in March at the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/sinatra-exhibition-set-for-performing-arts-library/', 'snippet': '“Sinatra: An American Icon” will open in March at the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a full year until Frank Sinatra’s centenary – Friday would have been his 99th birthday – but the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts is starting its celebration early. In a collaboration with the Grammy Museum of Los Angeles and the Sinatra family, the library will present “Sinatra: An American Icon,” an exhibition that will recognize Sinatra’s work as a singer and as an actor. The exhibition opens on March 4 at the library’s Donald and Mary Oenslager Gallery and will run through Sept. 4.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/arts/12artsbeat-sinatra2/12artsbeat-sinatra2-articleLarge.jp