-new-york-citys-buildings-lit-out-for-the-territories.html', 'snippet': 'The Eastern fascination for the American West was reflected in building names.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From P. T. Barnum’s exhibits of American Indians in the 1840s to dime cowboy novels after the Civil War, Easterners were increasingly tantalized by the mystique of the American West. Edward Clark brought some of the romance here when he built the Dakota apartment house, started in 1880 and completed in 1884. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/realestate/14SCAPES3/14SCAPES3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/realestate/14SCAPES3/14SCAPES3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/realestate/14SCAPES3/14SCAPES3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/realestate/14SCAPES3/14SCAPES3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/realestate/14SCAPES3/14SCAPES3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/realestate/14SCAPES3/14SCAPES3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/realestate/14SCAPES3/14SCAPES3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When New York City’s Buildings Lit Out for the Territories', 'kicker': 'Streetscapes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Buildings Lit Out for the Territories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Geographical', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buildings (Structures)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T19:22:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Gray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b03946d-65d9-52a0-b519-d03ba38f4d41', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b03946d-65d9-52a0-b519-d03ba38f4d41'}, {'abstract': 'Two new books provide insight into lesser-known stages of Charles M. Schulz and Jack Kirby’s careers.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/a-fresh-look-at-schulz-and-kirby/', 'snippet': 'Two new books provide insight into lesser-known stages of Charles M. Schulz and Jack Kirby’s careers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Their work couldn’t be more different, but Jack Kirby and Charles M. Schulz belong in the same breath as two of the most significant comics artists of the 20th century. Both were veterans of World War II and shared as heroes cartoonists like Milton Caniff (“Terry and the Pirates”), Alex Raymond (“Flash Gordon”) and Hal Foster (“Prince Valiant”). And upon their deaths, both left behind a trove of characters that continue to resonate and thrive. To name just a few: Captain America, the Mighty Thor, the Incredible Hulk (Kirby); Snoopy, Charlie Brown, Linus and Lucy (Schulz).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/books/12kirby/12kirby-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/books/12kirby/12kirby-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/books/12kirby/12kirby-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/books/12kirby/12kirby-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1469, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/books/12kirby/12kirby-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/books/12kirby/12kirby-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/books/12kirby/12kirby-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fresh Look at Schulz and Kirby', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, '