man', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1b69bf9-60f5-5f58-998b-ad4f1bef8cc3', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1b69bf9-60f5-5f58-998b-ad4f1bef8cc3'}, {'abstract': 'How the selfie transformed this year’s demonstrations, from Ferguson to New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/magazine/moving-pictures.html', 'snippet': 'How the selfie transformed this year’s demonstrations, from Ferguson to New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Wednesday night, four hours after a grand jury in Staten Island announced it would not indict the N.Y.P.D. officer Daniel Pantaleo for charges relating to the death of Eric Garner, the only evidence of the coming tumult in Times Square was a group of four protesters who stood in a nearly empty plaza. Dressed all in black, they held up signs for Eric Garner, Michael Brown and Ayotzinapa — the Mexican teachers’ college from which 43 students disappeared this summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/magazine/12mag-GarnerProtests/12mag-GarnerProtests-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/magazine/12mag-GarnerProtests/12mag-GarnerProtests-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/magazine/12mag-GarnerProtests/12mag-GarnerProtests-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/magazine/12mag-GarnerProtests/12mag-GarnerProtests-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/magazine/12mag-GarnerProtests/12mag-GarnerProtests-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/magazine/12mag-GarnerProtests/12mag-GarnerProtests-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/magazine/12mag-GarnerProtests/12mag-GarnerProtests-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Moving Pictures', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rattman, Jonno', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T21:15:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Caspian Kang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': 'Caspian', 'lastname': 'Kang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1527ea1-df88-5414-a6de-dadbf9ca69e6', 'word_count': 1149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1527ea1-df88-5414-a6de-dadbf9ca69e6'}, {'abstract': 'For a party tonight, the brand agency Chandelier Creative commissioned a video for a remix of “Jolene,” an exclusive preview of which appears here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/dolly-parton-exclusive-jolene-remix-video-todd-terje/', 'snippet': 'For a party tonight, the brand agency Chandelier Creative commissioned a video for a remix of “Jolene,” an exclusive preview of which appears here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the brand agency Chandelier Creative, eccentric and outsize parties are nothing new: last year’s holiday bash featured sexy angels, devils and nuns, plus a scantily clad Adam and Eve. Tonight, Chandelier throws a celebration dedicated to another object of worship (for a certain kind of die-hard fan, anyway): Dolly Parton, who will be honored in various ways throughout the evening, from tribute performances by artists including Rufus Wainwright and Jake Shears of Scissor Sisters, to an exhibition of the Iron Butterfly’s costumes. The agency also tapped the young director Nathaniel Brown to create a trippy datamoshed video, set to\xa0a remix of “Jolene” by the buzzy Norwegian producer Todd Terje. An exclusive preview — featuring kaleidoscopic visuals, a cameo by Paul Reubens and lots and lots of sequins — premieres here. A silent auction at Gavel & Grand, now live online, accompanies the exhibition; proceeds will benefit Dolly Parton’s Imagination Library.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Trippy Tribute to Dolly Parton, Soundtracked by Todd Terje', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parton, Dolly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T21:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandria Symonds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Symonds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07601b71-183b-567f-adb5-dcd83ceb60f0', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07601b71-183b-567f-adb5-dcd83ceb60f0'}, {'abstract': 'When buying holiday gifts for children, one seems to straddle the camps of “give them what they want” and “give them what they need.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/fashion/holiday-gifts-giving-children-books.html', 'snippet': 'When buying holiday gifts for children, one seems to straddle the camps of “give them what they want” and “give them what they need.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like everything else in contemporary families, holiday gift buying for children divides people into camps. The first camp can be categorized as “give them what they want” — the video game, the skateboard, the umpteenth Harry Potter or Elsa product extension. The second camp can be categorized as “give them what they need” or, alternately, “give them what you want them to like” — the mittens, the new sleeping bag, the penny collecting kit like the one your grandfather gave you that you just know they’re going to love someday.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/fashion/14THISLIFE/14THISLIFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 196, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/fashion/14THISLIFE/14THISLIFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 196}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/fashion/14THISLIFE/14THISLIFE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/fashion/14THISLIFE/14THISLIFE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/fashion/14THISLIFE/14THISLIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/fashion/14THISLIFE/14THISLIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/fashion/14THISLIFE/14THISLIFE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So, How Do You Wrap an E-Book?', 'kicker': 'This Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So, How Do You Wrap an E-Book?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feiler, Bruce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T21:16:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Feiler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feiler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/690fae6a-50e8-5a2b-ba81-f06186d349d6', 'word_count': 1280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/690fae6a-50e8-5a2b-ba81-f06186d349d6'}, {'abstract': 'Prefall is happening — though the when and the where are squishier than is the norm for full-fledged fashion weeks, which tend to have firm beginnings and ends.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/adding-fashion-weeks-to-a-packed-calendar/', 'snippet': 'Prefall is happening — though the when and the where are squishier than is the norm for full-fledged fashion weeks, which tend to have firm beginnings and ends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a saying popular among the partners, friends and family of those who cover fashion for a living: It’s always fashion week somewhere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adding Fashion Weeks to a Packed Calendar', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Altuzarra, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de la Renta, Oscar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herrera, Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posen, Zac', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Narciso', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chanel SA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chloe (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Esprit Holdings Ltd', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Neiman Marcus Group', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proenza Schouler', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T21:21:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], '