ray Hill, including matcha, which is gaining a wider following in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the foyer of a Japanese vegetarian restaurant on East 39th Street, around the corner from several nail salons and the House of Lasagna, a Japanese tea ceremony was unfolding. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Starbucks Meets Matcha: Ippodo Tea in Murray Hill', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Starbucks Meets Matcha', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ippodo Tea Co Ltd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Murray Hill (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T21:45:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Snow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Snow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c45b023-6958-51fc-881b-f1bf3d51e7e8', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c45b023-6958-51fc-881b-f1bf3d51e7e8'}, {'abstract': 'To toast her eight years at the house’s helm, T looks back at 10 of her best designs, both on the runway and on the red carpet.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/frida-giannini-top-gucci-moments/', 'snippet': 'To toast her eight years at the house’s helm, T looks back at 10 of her best designs, both on the runway and on the red carpet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today, it was announced that Gucci’s creative director, Frida Giannini, will leave the fashion house in February after her fall/winter 2015 collection is shown in Milan. Earlier in the month, she spoke at the at the 2014 New York Times International Luxury Conference on the intersection of fashion and the arts, elaborating on Gucci’s partnership with\xa0the Film Foundation, which has helped to restore significant cinematic titles since 2006. “A fashion designer can find inspiration anywhere, of course,” Giannini explained, “but a great piece of art or an extraordinary movie — it should be very inspiring. I think that the important thing is to have your mind open 360 degrees.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/t-magazine/12gucci-frida/12gucci-frida-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/t-magazine/12gucci-frida/12gucci-frida-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 707}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/t-magazine/12gucci-frida/12gucci-frida-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 870, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/t-magazine/12gucci-frida/12gucci-frida-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1739, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/t-magazine/12gucci-frida/12gucci-frida-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/t-magazine/12gucci-frida/12gucci-frida-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/t-magazine/12gucci-frida/12gucci-frida-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Frida Giannini’s Most Memorable Moments at Gucci', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giannini, Frida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gucci', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T21:45:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e79584d-5405-5577-b85f-5ece2124e17d', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e79584d-5405-5577-b85f-5ece2124e17d'}, {'abstract': 'Mark O’Rowe’s word-drunk and whiskey-soaked 1999 play, “Howie the Rookie,” returns, to the Fishman Space at BAM Fisher.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/13/theater/howie-the-rookie-in-bams-next-wave-festival.html', 'snippet': 'Mark O’Rowe’s word-drunk and whiskey-soaked 1999 play, “Howie the Rookie,” returns, to the Fishman Space at BAM Fisher.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of arms and the man, they sing. Well, men. And also scabies, microwave lasagna, Mayan legends, Siamese fighting fish and a flatulent hussy named Avalanche. In Mark O’Rowe’s word-drunk and whiskey-soaked 1999 play, “Howie the Rookie,” two young Dublin louts — one named “The Howie Lee,” one named “The Rookie Lee” — deliver rowdy monologues.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/arts/subhowie/subhowie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 850, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/13/arts/subhowie/subhowie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 850}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/arts/subhowie/subhowie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 724, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/arts/subhowie/subhowie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1447, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/arts/subhowie/subhowie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/13/arts/subhowie/subhowie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/arts/subhowie/subhowie-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Harsh Tongues, Marinated in Whiskey', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Harsh Tongues, Marinated in Whiskey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Rowe, Mark", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vaughan-Lawlor, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Howie the Rookie (Play)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T21:46:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Soloski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soloski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/199b0ad1-c4d3-5294-924f-01ec55bbac25', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/199b0ad1-c4d3-5294-924f-01ec55bbac25'}, {'abstract': 'Joe discusses Uber and Preet Bharara’s Terrible, Horrible, No Good, Very Bad week.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/joe-on-wnycs-money-talking-20/', 'snippet': 'Joe discusses Uber and Preet Bharara’s Terrible, Horrible, No Good, Very Bad week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do U.S. Attorney Preet Bharara and global ride-sharing company Uber have in common? Both powerhouses just had a Terrible, Horrible, No Good, Very Bad week. In New York, Attorney Bharara saw the insider trading convictions of two former hedge fund traders overturned in a case likely to spur challenges to guilty pleas his office has already obtained. Meanwhile Uber, no stranger to controversy, saw its services banned, curtailed, or challenged in at least half a dozen cities, while two of its drivers were placed under investigation for allegedly raping their passengers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe on WNYC’s Money Talking', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bharara, Preet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-12T21:46:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Dallett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dallett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab7b619e-b7e9-532f-84f5-abdce8c3c4a9', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab7b619e-b7e9-532f-84f5-abdce8c3c4a9'}, {'abstract': 'Motus, an Italian troupe, presents “The Tempest” as a full-throated cry to the young and disaffected to get off their collective duffs, shake off their shackles and do something.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/15/theater/motuss-nella-tempesta-evokes-shakespeares-stormy-play.html', 'snippet': 'Motus, an Italian troupe, presents “The Tempest” as a full-throated cry to the young and disaffected to get off their collective duffs, shake off their shackles and do something.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can talk all you like about ideals and class resentment and visions of the future. But the ingredient most essential to getting a revolution off the ground is energy, the kind that incinerates as it moves. And the place you’ll find the highest concentration of that precious entity is in the restless bodies of the young. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/arts/NELLA/NELLA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/13/arts/NELLA/NELLA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/arts/NELLA/NELLA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/arts/NELLA/NELLA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'leg