ank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Woodside (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T02:01:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cba909ca-c622-5966-876f-db2ae0474047', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cba909ca-c622-5966-876f-db2ae0474047'}, {'abstract': 'Newly declassified documents show disagreement among judges on the secret surveillance court, and the Bush administration pushing forward with “innovative” solutions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/13/us/politics/documents-shed-new-light-on-legal-wrangling-over-spying-in-us-.html', 'snippet': 'Newly declassified documents show disagreement among judges on the secret surveillance court, and the Bush administration pushing forward with “innovative” solutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In January 2007, Judge Malcolm Howard issued an extraordinary order on behalf of the nation’s secret surveillance court. He interpreted the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act, which requires individual warrants to wiretap on domestic soil, in a way that authorized the Bush administration’s warrantless wiretapping program, according to documents declassified on Friday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Documents Shed New Light on Legal Wrangling Over Spying in U.S. ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Documents Shed New Light on Legal Wrangling Over Spying in U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzales, Alberto R', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T02:03:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b0ad1ad-b3d6-51be-b431-c12eddbc184e', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b0ad1ad-b3d6-51be-b431-c12eddbc184e'}, {'abstract': 'Four people were injured in a shooting outside a Portland high school on Friday, throwing an area in the north end of the city into chaos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/13/us/oregon-4-hurt-in-shooting-near-portland-high-school.html', 'snippet': 'Four people were injured in a shooting outside a Portland high school on Friday, throwing an area in the north end of the city into chaos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four people were wounded in a shooting outside a Portland high school on Friday, throwing an area in the north end of the city into chaos as medical responders rushed to the scene and the police searched for someone believed to be involved with a local gang. A 16-year-old girl was hospitalized in critical condition and two young men, ages 17 and 20, were in serious condition. A 19-year-old woman was treated for a graze wound. The victims were able to run into the school after the attack, a police spokesman said. Their names were not available. Rosemary Anderson High School, with about 200 students, is an alternative public school for students who have either been expelled from or dropped out of regular high school. The shootings occurred just after noon on an unseasonably warm and dry day when many students were outside, but a spokesman for the Portland Police Bureau, Sgt. Pete Simpson, said it was not clear whether the victims were specifically targeted or just happened to be in the wrong place at the wrong time. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oregon: 4 Hurt in Shooting Near Portland High School', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oregon: 4 Hurt in Shooting Near School', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Kirk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings and Armed Attacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gangs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': '