bject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T02:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/120d2c3c-1d47-55c5-82a7-e6cac4d4fc79', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/120d2c3c-1d47-55c5-82a7-e6cac4d4fc79'}, {'abstract': 'The counteroffensive, which includes a new website, began even before the Senate committee issued its report on the agency’s harsh treatment of detainees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/13/us/politics/ex-chief-leads-vocal-defense-of-spy-agency.html', 'snippet': 'The counteroffensive, which includes a new website, began even before the Senate committee issued its report on the agency’s harsh treatment of detainees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The last time George Tenet was asked about torture on television, he sounded defiant and jabbed his finger in the air. The year was 2007, and Mr. Tenet, the former director of the Central Intelligence Agency, was promoting his memoir when a question about waterboarding came up while he was being interviewed on CBS’ “60 Minutes.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Chief Leads Vocal Defense of C.I.A.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Chief Leads Vocal Defense of Spy Agency', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interrogations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tenet, George J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hayden, Michael V', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goss, Porter J', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T02:27:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg and Eric Lichtblau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lichtblau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ae623ec-8519-55cc-a227-56c8facc2022', 'word_count': 1291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ae623ec-8519-55cc-a227-56c8facc2022'}, {'abstract': 'Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. spoke with the police and community members in Chicago on Friday about law enforcement practices, his latest stop in a nationwide tour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/13/us/illinois-holder-speaks-on-police-tactics.html', 'snippet': 'Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. spoke with the police and community members in Chicago on Friday about law enforcement practices, his latest stop in a nationwide tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. spoke with the police and community members in Chicago\xa0on Friday about law enforcement practices, his latest stop in a nationwide tour that coincides with heightened national discussion about how officers use force. Mr. Holder, who talked for about five minutes before the roundtable discussion was closed to reporters, said it was important for the police and residents to build mutual trust. “We have to ask ourselves some fundamental questions about the lack of trust” between the police and certain communities, Mr. Holder told the group, which included Mayor Rahm Emanuel, police officials and several young men. The visit followed similar forums in Cleveland, Atlanta and Memphis. Mr. Emanuel complimented the Chicagoans who have taken to the streets in recent weeks to protest police practices and grand jury decisions in Ferguson, Mo., and New York.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: Holder Speaks on Police Tactics', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: Holder Speaks on Police Tactics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T02:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitch Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f7f78b3-48b0-547c-a009-ceddc4390b3c', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f7f78b3-48b0-547c-a009-ceddc4390b3c'}, {'abstract': 'Recent overturned convictions have changed the rules.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/13/opinion/joe-nocera-prosecuting-insider-trading.html', 'snippet': 'Recent overturned convictions have changed the rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the summer of 1991, the