e'}, {'abstract': 'Whatever you do, don’t confuse the cromnibus with the cronut, the pastry that’s half-croissant and half-doughnut at your holiday party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/13/opinion/gail-collins-dinner-party-political-primer.html', 'snippet': 'Whatever you do, don’t confuse the cromnibus with the cronut, the pastry that’s half-croissant and half-doughnut at your holiday party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The burdens of being an Informed Citizen are many. This weekend, you’ll probably be going out to some holiday party or dinner where your friends will expect you to have an opinion about the monster spending bill that’s been staggering through Congress.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-jumbo-v7.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-superJumbo-v7.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1850, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-thumbStandard-v7.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-thumbStandard-v7.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/collins-circular/collins-circular-thumbLarge-v9.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dinner Party Political Primer', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dinner Party Political Primer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Gail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Susan M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trucks and Trucking', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Driver Distraction and Fatigue', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T02:53:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/692f0285-3922-576c-a080-08afdd4a12ac', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/692f0285-3922-576c-a080-08afdd4a12ac'}, {'abstract': 'A Saturday romp with James Mulhern and Ashton Anderson.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/12/caesars-predecessor/', 'snippet': 'A Saturday romp with James Mulhern and Ashton Anderson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY PUZZLE — What is there to say about a puzzle that opens with the entry BUTTOCKS, which is then clued as “Cheeky couple?” I realize that you’re bound to want to crack some jokes about that but, in the end, we are a sophisticated group. So let’s do ourselves a favor and leave that all behind us.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caesar’s Predecessor', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T03:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68b723a8-b66e-580a-9a21-ec794c2569a8', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68b723a8-b66e-580a-9a21-ec794c2569a8'}, {'abstract': 'A leader who was a political prisoner took a moral stand in accepting six detainees. If others also stepped forward, it could hasten the closing of the prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/13/opinion/uruguays-guantanamo-gesture.html', 'snippet': 'A leader who was a political prisoner took a moral stand in accepting six detainees. If others also stepped forward, it could hasten the closing of the prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last weekend, Uruguay made good on its offer to take six Guantánamo Bay detainees, a gesture that other countries in Latin America could be persuaded to emulate. The transfer of the prisoners, who had long been cleared for release, marked the largest reduction in the number of inmates at Guantánamo Bay since 2009. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uruguay’s Guantánamo Gesture', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uruguay’s Guantánamo Gesture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uruguay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mujica, Jose', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diyab, Jihad Ahmed Mujstafa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T03:02:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bffddecd-c4f3-5a98-a684-9e20ed4fa4bc', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bffddecd-c4f3-5a98-a684-9e20ed4fa4bc'}, {'abstract': 'Ron Burke inherited his father’s training business and became the first harness racing trainer to earn $100 million in purses won.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/13/sports/no-longer-fearful-a-trainer-presides-over-an-empire.html', 'snippet': 'Ron Burke inherited his father’s training business and became the first harness racing trainer to earn $100 million in purses won.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Ron Burke was young, he was afraid of horses. Now harness racing’s leading trainer, Burke has transformed himself into an intimidating force.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Longer Fearful, a Trainer Presides Over an Empire ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Longer Fearful, a Trainer Presides Over an Empire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Harness Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burke, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jockeys, Drivers and Trainers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yonkers Raceway', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T03:04:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Bossert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bossert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9153baf4-8dfe-5fa5-ab3b-57edb0a1ffb2', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9153baf4-8dfe-5fa5-ab3b-57edb0a1ffb2'}, {'abstract': 'Ashton B. Carter, President Obama’s nominee to become defense secretary, underwent what an administration official called “a long-planned surgical procedure on his back” on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/13/us/politics/defense-nominee-ashton-carter-has-back-surgery.html', 'snippet': 'Ashton B. Carter, President Obama’s nominee to become defense secretary, underwent what an administration official called “a long-planned surgical procedure on his back” on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ashton B. Carter, President Obama’s nominee to become defense secretary, underwent what an administration official called “a long-planned surgical procedure on his back”\xa0on Friday. Mr. Carter, 60, was resting comfortably with his family, according to Josh Earnest, the White House press secretary. Mr. Earnest and other White House officials did not elaborate on what was wrong with Mr. Carter’s back or why the procedure was necessary. “Mr. Carter decided to go ahead with the previously scheduled procedure so that he could complete it before beginning his confirmation process,” Mr. Earnest said. Mr. Obama nominated Mr. Carter on Dec. 5 to become the top civilian in charge of the Pentagon after Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel resigned under pressure. Mr. Carter is slated to begin his confirmation process next year, when Republicans take control of the Senate.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Defense Nominee Ashton Carter Has Back Surgery', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defense Nominee Has Back Surgery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Ashton B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T03:06:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/19121c52-22fb-5f75-8a82-fbb1e28e9284', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19121c52-22fb-5f75-8a82-fbb1e28e9284'}, {'abstract': 'Fantasy Cuisine in Hartsdale includes many specialties of China’s Sichuan region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/nyregion/a-review-of-fantasy-cuisine-in-hartsdale.html', 'snippet': 'Fantasy Cuisine in Hartsdale includes many specialties of China’s Sichuan region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years, Japanese and Asian fusion restaurants have largely supplanted the neighborhood Chinese restaurant as the informal go-to place for an inexpensive bite with family and friends. Bucking that trend is Fantasy Cuisine, a Chinese restaurant on Hartsdale’s Central Avenue that opened in the summer.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14DINEWE3/14DINEWE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14DINEWE3/14DINEWE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14DINEWE3/14DINEWE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14DINEWE3/14DINEWE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14DINEWE3/14DINEWE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14DINEWE3/14DINEWE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/nyregion/14DINEWE3/14DINEWE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Working With Varying Degrees of Heat', 'kicker': 'Dining Review | Westchester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Working With Varying Degrees of Heat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hartsdale (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fantasy Cuisine (Hartsdale, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T03:10:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By M. H. Reed', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5992d27-7878-5983-a3d7-fcc62b0f4f79', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5992d27-7878-5983-a3d7-fcc62b0f4f79'}, {'abstract': 'Mrs. Cochran, a former teacher, was in a nursing home when she became part of an unsuccessful attack ad against her husband, Senator Thad Cochran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/13/us/rose-cochran-a-figure-in-a-campaign-attack-video-dies-at-73.html', 'snippet': 'Mrs. Cochran, a former teacher, was in a nursing home when she became part of an unsuccessful attack ad against her husband, Senator Thad Cochran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rose Cochran, who was unwittingly thrust into the middle of a bitter primary campaign being waged by her husband, Senator Thad Cochran, in Mississippi this year, died on Friday at a hospice in Ridgeland, Miss. She was 73.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/us/COCHRAN-obit/COCHRAN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/13/us/COCHRAN-obit/COCHRAN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/us/COCHRAN-ob