lawed or sloppy manufacturing could account for some of the hazards seen in the devices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/business/international/chinas-e-cigarette-boom-lacks-oversight-for-safety-.html', 'snippet': 'Almost all of the world’s e-cigarettes are made without oversight, and experts say flawed or sloppy manufacturing could account for some of the hazards seen in the devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHENZHEN, China — In a grimy workshop, among boiling vats of chemicals, factory workers are busy turning stainless steel rods into slender tube casings, a crucial component of electronic cigarettes. Not long ago, Skorite Electronics was a tiny firm struggling to produce pen parts. Today, it is part of an enormous — and virtually unregulated — supply chain centered here that produces about 90 percent of the world’s e-cigarettes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s E-Cigarette Boom Lacks Oversight for Safety ', 'kicker': 'The New Smoke', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China’s E-Cigarette Boom Lacks Oversight for Safety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barboza, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Cigarettes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shenzhen (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T18:59:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/505c28db-4f2b-51a0-8d47-9a0ca196a742', 'word_count': 1798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/505c28db-4f2b-51a0-8d47-9a0ca196a742'}, {'abstract': 'Preservationists are working to salvage badly deteriorating buildings in Yangon’s historic downtown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/world/racing-to-save-a-colonial-past-in-decay.html', 'snippet': 'Preservationists are working to salvage badly deteriorating buildings in Yangon’s historic downtown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YANGON, Myanmar — The once-grand colonial building of marble floors and iron fretwork, an elegant outpost of Britain’s trading empire, is now a wreck. Moss encrusts the walls, rainwater drips down rusted steel beams, flimsy lights glow yellow in dark interiors. A century-old birdcage elevator lies idle, stuck on the first floor. It hasn’t moved in more than 60 years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Myanmar, Racing to Save a Colonial Past in Decay', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Racing to Save a Colonial Past in Decay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perlez, Jane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yangon (Myanmar)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buildings (Structures)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T19:01:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Perlez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44f5966a-84db-5d91-8b9c-af537fbe3d85', 'word_count': 1282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44f5966a-84db-5d91-8b9c-af537fbe3d85'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Morehouse is on a mission to introduce fencing, a historically aristocratic sport, to financially disadvantaged youths in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/sports/an-olympian-take-fencing-to-children-in-cities.html', 'snippet': 'Tim Morehouse is on a mission to introduce fencing, a historically aristocratic sport, to financially disadvantaged youths in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — The cold rain had been pouring for several hours by the time the Olympian Tim Morehouse exited a cab in front of North Star Academy’s Vailsburg elementary school location. Over his shoulder, he carried a large black duffel bag filled with plastic foils and fencing masks. Despite the gray skies, he seemed giddy.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/sports/fencing/fencing-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/13/sports/fencing/fencing-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/13/sports/fencing/fencing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank