ble plate instead. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/sunday-review/14GREENBERGsub/14GREENBERGsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 339, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/14/sunday-review/14GREENBERGsub/14GREENBERGsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 339}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/sunday-review/14GREENBERGsub/14GREENBERGsub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/sunday-review/14GREENBERGsub/14GREENBERGsub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1157, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/sunday-review/14GREENBERGsub/14GREENBERGsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/14/sunday-review/14GREENBERGsub/14GREENBERGsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/sunday-review/14GREENBERGsub/14GREENBERGsub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Seafood Be Kosher and Sustainable?', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can Seafood Be Kosher and Sustainable?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenberg, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kosher Foods and Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish Farming', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T19:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/981ff30b-f3f9-5f4c-9817-1349078d323f', 'word_count': 1133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/981ff30b-f3f9-5f4c-9817-1349078d323f'}, {'abstract': 'This could have been the year that tipped the scales toward action on climate change. Then the price of oil started falling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/opinion/sunday/thomas-l-friedman-why-2014-is-a-big-deal.html', 'snippet': 'This could have been the year that tipped the scales toward action on climate change. Then the price of oil started falling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I WAS just about to go with a column that started like this: When they write the history of the global response to climate change, 2014 could well be seen as the moment when the balance between action and denial tipped decisively toward action. That’s thanks to the convergence of four giant forces: São Paulo, Brazil, went dry; China and the United States together went green; solar panels went cheap; and Google and Apple went home.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why 2014 Is a Big Deal', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why 2014 Is a Big Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Thomas L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gasoline Tax (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Energy Agency', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T19:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4e64475-a4e1-5952-bff8-264a6745c7ed', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4e64475-a4e1-5952-bff8-264a6745c7ed'}, {'abstract': 'Curbing financial recklessness, predation and discrimination is the way to create conditions for sound homeownership.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/opinion/sunday/a-home-of-ones-own.html', 'snippet': 'Curbing financial recklessness, predation and discrimination is the way to create conditions for sound homeownership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Melvin Watt, the federal mortgage regulator, recently unveiled new government plans to encourage low-down-payment mortgages for cash-strapped buyers, the move was correctly understood as an effort to revive the still-ailing housing industry. But it is more than that. It is a challenge to the enduring misperception that most of the people who lost their homes in the housing bust should never have been homeowners in the first place. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Home of One’s Own ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Home of One’s Own', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watt, Melvin L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-13T19:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6e99907-5ba9-5429-be0b-1ae4ac90e847', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6e99907-5ba9-5429-be0b-1ae4ac90e847'}, {'abstract': 'Funding for the global campaign against malaria needs to be doubled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/14/opinion/sunday/fragile-gains-against-malaria.html', 'snippet': 'Funding for the global campaign against malaria needs to be doubled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The global battle against malaria, a mosquito-borne infectious disease, continues to yield impressive gains, but it is encountering new obstacles that threaten future progress. It is imperative that funding from all sources be doubled to solidify the achievements and move toward the elimination of malaria from as many countries as possible.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/14/opinion/14sun3/14sun3-articleLarge.j