le': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7012f05d-4e93-5521-9d91-e906b20bc802', 'word_count': 2033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7012f05d-4e93-5521-9d91-e906b20bc802'}, {'abstract': 'Admirers of Jane Freilicher, who died last Tuesday, attended “Presenting Jane,” a celebration of her life and career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/15/arts/jane-freilichers-friends-celebrate-her-life-and-art.html', 'snippet': 'Admirers of Jane Freilicher, who died last Tuesday, attended “Presenting Jane,” a celebration of her life and career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jane Freilicher, a painter of gauzy Long Island marshes and floral still lifes perched, like observing angels, in windows high above Manhattan, was a leading figure among the New York School artists of the 1950s who reinserted the real world into abstraction. She was also a muse to poets whose careers, like hers, were taking off at the time. And she was a terrific person; smart, funny, generous. In short, she spread good karma all around.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/JANE/JANE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 501, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/JANE/JANE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 501}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/JANE/JANE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 856, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/JANE/JANE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1286, 'width': 1539, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 