.html', 'snippet': 'Julia Kristeva, through an alter ego in “Teresa, My Love,” imagines the life of Teresa of Ávila.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is hard, even knowing just a few facts about Teresa of Ávila, not to fall in love with her. This 16th-century Spanish mystic, saint and doctor of the church could sigh over her own limitations with the precision, earthiness and wit of a born writer. “I could be bribed by a sardine,” she once wrote. Nor did she muffle her sighs over the sisters in her care. “Believe me,” she wrote, “I fear an unhappy nun more than many devils.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/SUB-BOOK/SUB-BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 507, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/SUB-BOOK/SUB-BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 507, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/SUB-BOOK/SUB-BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/SUB-BOOK/SUB-BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/SUB-BOOK/SUB-BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Imagining a Saintly Life, Some of It Not So Holy ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Imagining a Saintly Life, Some of It Not So Holy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'