Out After Tests Reveal Case of Mumps', 'kicker': 'N.H.L. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crosby Has Mumps; So Does Brassard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mumps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crosby, Sidney', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brassard, Derick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Penguins', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T02:59:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a29bdf3f-c12a-5ed0-a7c3-97f5895290a9', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a29bdf3f-c12a-5ed0-a7c3-97f5895290a9'}, {'abstract': 'Duncan Macmillan and Jonny Donahoe’s “Every Brilliant Thing” offers a long list of reasons not to commit suicide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/15/theater/jonny-donahoe-in-every-brilliant-thing-at-barrow-street.html', 'snippet': 'Duncan Macmillan and Jonny Donahoe’s “Every Brilliant Thing” offers a long list of reasons not to commit suicide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even the most dry-eyed among us get weepy in December. There’s something about short, dark days piling up toward another year’s end, while carolers trill about comfort and joy, that brings out the Niobe in men and women of stone. Put one of them in front of a television with James Stewart on the brink in “It’s a Wonderful Life,” and you’ll need mops to wipe up the tears.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raindrops on Roses, for the Potentially Suicidal', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Raindrops on Roses, for the Potentially Suicidal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macmillan, Duncan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donahoe, Jonny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perrin, George', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Every Brilliant Thing (Play)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T03:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/447f32b0-5bed-59ef-9194-39183fff7340', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/447f32b0-5bed-59ef-9194-39183fff7340'}, {'abstract': 'Aaron Sorkin’s HBO series “The Newsroom” ended after three seasons, and despite strong writing and a charming cast, the show was eclipsed by more knowing and acerbic dramas about journalism and society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/15/arts/the-newsroom-ends-its-final-season-on-hbo.html', 'snippet': 'Aaron Sorkin’s HBO series “The Newsroom” ended after three seasons, and despite strong writing and a charming cast, the show was eclipsed by more knowing and acerbic dramas about journalism and society.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Newsroom” came to a close Sunday on HBO, and even after three seasons, this Aaron Sorkin series is still puzzling. It was a paean to journalism that many journalists hated, an inside look at the immediacy of a 24-hour cable news division that was set two years in the past. Oddest of all, it was a 1940s-style screwball comedy about reporters filled with sanctimony, not cynicism: a “His Girl Friday” by Allen Drury.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/NEWSROOM-1418589286410/NEWSROOM-1418589286410-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/NEWSROOM-1418589286410/NEWSROOM-1418589286410-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/NEWSROOM-1418589286410/NEWSROOM-1418589286410-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/NEWSROOM-1418589286410/NEWSROOM-1418589286410-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/NEWSROOM-1418589286410/NEWSROOM-1418589286410-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/NEWSROOM-1418589286410/NEWSROOM-1418589286410-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/15/arts/NEWSROOM-1418589286410/NEWSROOM-1418589286410-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'hea