in a year that has been defined by huge mergers, most of which have been by corporate buyers rather than private equity firms. PetSmart has long been seen as a good target for private equity firms, given its relatively strong cash flow and low debt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: PetSmart’s Big Buyout Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T12:42:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f710a62f-c1d3-5d1f-8b43-def193562b64', 'word_count': 2384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f710a62f-c1d3-5d1f-8b43-def193562b64'}, {'abstract': 'Ni Fake, a former vice governor of Anhui Province in eastern China, enjoyed being a government official. But what he apparently loved most was jade.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/15/a-corruption-case-laden-with-jade/', 'snippet': 'Ni Fake, a former vice governor of Anhui Province in eastern China, enjoyed being a government official. But what he apparently loved most was jade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ni Fake, a former vice governor of Anhui Province in eastern China, enjoyed being a government official. But what he apparently loved most was jade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Corruption Case Laden With Jade', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'majo