cter and singing in front of Mr. Sondheim.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/15/into-the-woods-emily-blunt-stephen-sondheim/', 'snippet': 'The actress talks about naming her nameless character and singing in front of Mr. Sondheim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the big-budget adaptation of the musical “Into the Woods,” directed by Rob Marshall and set for a Dec. 25 release, Emily Blunt teams up again with Meryl Streep, her on-screen foil in “The Devil Wears Prada” and her off-screen friend. In the new film Ms. Blunt plays the Baker’s Wife, whose yearning for a child sets the intertwining fairy-tale plot in motion. Ms. Streep plays the Witch, who promises to have “the curse reversed” — as Stephen Sondheim’s lyrics go — so the Baker’s Wife will no longer be barren, as long as a few key demands are met. In New York for the film’s premiere this month, before she learned of her Golden Globe nomination for best actress in a musical or comedy, Ms. Blunt had a quick sit-down with the Bagger over English tea to talk about a role she assumed she’d never get; the names she and James Corden, who plays her husband, chose for their characters; and shots from the chest up. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/intothewoods/intothewoods-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/intothewoods/intothewoods-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/intothewoods/intothewoods-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/intothewoods/intothewoods-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/intothewoods/intothewoods-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/intothewoods/intothewoods-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/12/arts/intothewoods/intothewoods-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': "‘Into the Woods': Emily Blunt on Singing for Stephen Sondheim", 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Prada or Robes, a Familiar Foil Is on the Set', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blunt, Emily', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marshall, Rob (1960- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sondheim, Stephen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Meryl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T16:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54579cbf-b7c3-5f72-aaa4-47a8305654ef', 'word_count': 922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54579cbf-b7c3-5f72-aaa4-47a8305654ef'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A British mail steamer was attacked at the African port of Lindi in 1889.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/15/1889-natives-attack-mail-boat/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A British mail steamer was attacked at the African port of Lindi in 1889.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ZANZIBAR — While a boat from the British mail steamer was delivering the mails at the German port of Lindi, she was attacked by the natives. The boat eventually got off safely, but the natives kept up a fire upon the crew as they returned to the steamer. Mr. Mackenzie arrived here today [Dec. 15] and met with a cordial reception from the Sultan and the natives. He reports having visited all the British East African Company’s posts, and says that he found everywhere signs of greater tranquility and prosperity. —\xa0The New York Herald, European Edition, Dec. 16, 1889', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1889: Natives Attack Mail Boat', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zanzibar (Tanzania)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T16:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26163a67-34cc-5a8f-a8d1-034620fa7aac', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26163a67-34cc-5a8f-a8d1-034620fa7aac'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’s executive editor, Dean Baquet, reflects on Sony Pictures Entertainment’s request to avoid publication of material stolen from the studio’s computer system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/12/15/hacked-sony-documents-are-not-pentagon-papers-editors-view/', 'snippet': 'The Times’s executive editor, Dean Baquet, reflects on Sony Pictures Entertainment’s request to avoid publication of material stolen from the studio’s computer system.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Sony Pictures Entertainment warned media outlets on Sunday against using material obtained by hackers who raided the studio’s computer systems. In a sharply worded letter sent to news organizations, including The New York Times, David Boies, a lawyer hired by Sony, demanded that news outlets avoid or destroy hacked material. (In a Sunday Op-Ed column, the screenwriter and playwright Aaron Sorkin wrote that journalists shouldn’t help hackers.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hacked Sony Documents Are Not Pentagon Papers: Editor’s View', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T16:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Baquet, Executive Editor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baquet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Executive', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e319265f-2267-5d3d-b8d9-5428e955e643', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e319265f-2267-5d3d-b8d9-5428e955e643'}, {'abstract': 'Imaging technique captures the turbulence of hot gases when a match is lit.', 'we