'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanson, Ronald K', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tilghman, Matthew Seidel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T16:06:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec9210d2-77ee-5a40-87fc-85417a012c52', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec9210d2-77ee-5a40-87fc-85417a012c52'}, {'abstract': 'A study published online Monday in the journal Pediatrics seems to add to the evidence that e-cigarettes are doing more to promote nicotine use than to help people quit.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/15/e-cigarettes-may-serve-as-gateway-to-smoking-for-teens-study-suggests/', 'snippet': 'A study published online Monday in the journal Pediatrics seems to add to the evidence that e-cigarettes are doing more to promote nicotine use than to help people quit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was in middle school, I asked my mom if she would be mad if I tried smoking. I’ve never forgotten her answer: “Go ahead and try it,” she said. “You’ll hate it, and you’ll never want to do it again.” So about a year later, when the opportunity presented itself, I took a puff off an older kid’s cigarette in a public bathroom. I could barely inhale, and I’ve never had the desire to try one since. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/12/nyregion/12VAPORIUM_SPAN/12VAPORIUM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarg