ss Lwoff-Parlaghy, a Hungarian portrait painter who has made likenesses of crowned heads and many other notable persons, has left her apartment in the Plaza Hotel, owing a bill of $12,000. The management has retained the objects of art in the apartment. It has had them appraised, and is told they are worth more than $100,000. They include portraits of the Kaiser, Mr. August Belmont, Mr. Seth Low, the late Mr. Whitelaw Reid and the late General Daniel E. Sickles. King Edward VII visited her exhibition in Marienbad in 1904 and promised to give her some sittings for a portrait. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Dec. 16, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/blogs/16iht-olddec16/16iht-olddec16-jumbo.png', 'height': 553, 'width': 344, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/blogs/16iht-olddec16/16iht-olddec16-superJumbo.png', 'height': 553, 'width': 344, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/blogs/16iht-olddec16/16iht-olddec16-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/16/blogs/16iht-olddec16/16iht-olddec16-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/blogs/16iht-olddec16/16iht-olddec16-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1914: Hotel Seizes Princess’s Art', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Plaza Hotel (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hungary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T16:32:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aba2830-3d2a-52f1-a4c6-962960b81f56', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aba2830-3d2a-52f1-a4c6-962960b81f56'}, {'abstract': 'To achieve its independence from the the Frank Lloyd Wright Foundation, an architecture school says it needs to raise $2 million by the end of 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/15/wright-architecture-school-sets-fund-raising-goal-for-independence/', 'snippet': 'To achieve its independence from the the Frank Lloyd Wright Foundation, an architecture school says it needs to raise $2 million by the end of 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The architecture school run by the Frank Lloyd Wright Foundation will try to raise $2 million before the end of 2015 to ensure its future as an independent organization, the foundation announced on Monday, having approved a possible path toward the school’s incorporation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wright Architecture School Sets Fund-raising Goal for Independence', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCREDITATION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges