otographer whose images caught the horrors of war, the bittersweet joys of a doomed president’s inaugural ball and the intimate moments of jazz greats and Hollywood stars just being themselves, died on Saturday in Los Angeles. He was 95.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Phil Stern, 95, Dies; Photographed War, Movie Stars and a President', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Phil Stern, Photographer; Chronicler of Movie Stars And a President Was 95', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McFadden, Robert D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, Phil (1919-2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T19:25:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert D. McFadden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/af24397e-61a1-51e7-87c8-10f5f99231a8', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af24397e-61a1-51e7-87c8-10f5f99231a8'}, {'abstract': 'The ruble, down more than oil.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/15/putin-on-the-fritz/', 'snippet': 'The ruble, down more than oil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s impressive just how quickly and convincingly the wheels have been coming off the Russian economy. Obviously the plunge in oil prices is the big driver, but the ruble has actually fallen more than Brent — oil is down 40 percent since the start of the year, but the ruble is down by half.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putin on the Fritz', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T19:38:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7261585a-5ff9-57d3-b257-a96e9813b521', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7261585a-5ff9-57d3-b257-a96e9813b521'}, {'abstract': 'Diplomacy is never easy, especially in the dark.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/12/15/lights-out-at-the-state-department/', 'snippet': 'Diplomacy is never easy, especially in the dark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Diplomacy is never easy, especially in the dark.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lights Out at the State Department', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T20:07:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5aaef60-7f92-558b-94bb-aa4e2b89294f', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://ar