ph': 'Since 2010, when American Ballet Theater debuted its current production of “The Nutcracker” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, I have seen it a half-dozen times. Every time, I’ve noticed new felicities and connections. This is choreography, by Alexei Ratmansky, that rewards repeated viewings — though since the company will be taking it to Southern California next year, there aren’t many chances left for New Yorkers to see it again, or to catch it for the first time.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/arts/ABT/ABT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 826, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/16/arts/ABT/ABT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 826}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/arts/ABT/ABT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 745, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/arts/ABT/ABT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1489, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/arts/ABT/ABT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/16/arts/ABT/ABT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/arts/ABT/ABT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Christmas Standard, Still