ations, glaciers, forests, canyons, fossils, deserts, hot springs and volcanoes. Now, lawmakers have decided that the nation needs one for the atom bomb.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Preserving Manhattan Project Sites', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Preserving Manhattan Project Sites', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broad, William J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Manhattan Project', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oppenheimer, J Robert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Cynthia C', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T22:06:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By William J. Broad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Broad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f925e331-a0fc-54ee-9c74-5c3437146d94', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f925e331-a0fc-54ee-9c74-5c3437146d94'}, {'abstract': 'Cancer treatments can be particularly hard on children. But in the Infusionarium their minds are transported to mountain slopes where, depending on their tastes, they are surrounded by extreme skiers or Disney princesses.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/15/chemo-kids-infusionarium/', 'snippet': 'Cancer treatments can be particularly hard on children. But in the Infusionarium their minds are transported to mountain slopes where, depending on their tastes, they are surrounded by extreme skiers or Disney princesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Orange, Calif. — Nick Meza, 18, recently had another five-day round of chemotherapy at the outpatient clinic here at Children’s Hospital of Orange County. Usually those days drag for Nick, an Eagle Scout with a flashing grin, a hunger for conversation, and acute lymphoblastic leukemia.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16infuse/16infuse-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16infuse/16infuse-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16infuse/16infuse-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16infuse/16infuse-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1147, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16infuse/16infuse-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16infuse/16infuse-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16infuse/16infuse-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'th