ing older population. Ten thousand Americans now turn 65 every day, entering their golden years of disproportionate consumption of medical care.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16zuger/16zuger-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16zuger/16zuger-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16zuger/16zuger-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16zuger/16zuger-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1794, 'width': 1794, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16zuger/16zuger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16zuger/16zuger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/science/16zuger/16zuger-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shortage of Juggling Doctors', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Shortage of Juggling Doctors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shortages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Assn of American Medical Colleges', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T22:29:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abigail Zuger, M.d', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abigail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zuger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/216e415c-7ff1-5366-90d3-cfeeab538f05', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/216e415c-7ff1-5366-90d3-cfeeab538f05'}, {'abstract': '“The Pinkprint” is Ms. Minaj’s third studio album, and like the first two it’s full of compromises and half-successes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/16/arts/music/review-nicki-minajs-the-pinkprint.html', 'snippet': '“The Pinkprint” is Ms. Minaj’s third studio album, and like the first two it’s full of compromises and half-successes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Part of the magic of the modern record business is that the worth of the album has been diminished. Almost anything can be a great album now — a mixtape, a cluster of songs on Soundcloud, a dump of digital files. That to some the album still has a sort of aesthetic integrity, that it should mean something different from the rest of their creative output, is an increasingly old-fashioned idea.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/arts/jpnewmusic2/jpnewmusic2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge':