ure sign of an emerging-markets currency crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/16/upshot/vladimir-putin-vs-the-currency-markets-what-to-know-about-the-rubles-collapse.html', 'snippet': 'Raising interest rates by 6.5 percentage points in the middle of the night is a sure sign of an emerging-markets currency crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vladimir Putin’s biggest enemy right now may well be the currency markets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vladimir Putin vs. the Currency Markets: What to Know About the Ruble’s Collapse', 'kicker': 'Market Turmoil', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ruble (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Bank of Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-15T23:58:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Irwin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Irwin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bfe98cf-abab-5156-9a01-bfc37e362511', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bfe98cf-abab-5156-9a01-bfc37e362511'}, {'abstract': 'There was no suicide note. Maybe the doctor could explain.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/15/qusetions-for-my-grandfathers-psychiatrist/', 'snippet': 'There was no suicide note. Maybe the doctor could explain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My maternal grandfather killed himself inside his bedroom closet on the morning of March 22, 1966. I have a copy of his death certificate here beside me, stamped with the seal of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts. His basic biographical data is all there — name: Francis Michael Wiener; birthplace: Prague; age at time of death: 55 years and 19 days — and the cause of death still makes me flinch a little every time I see it: “Suicide — Shotgun wound, left side of face below ear.” He was an acoustic engineer, trained in the intricacies of sound design, so I imagine he chose his closet as the place to pull the trigger for its sound-dampening qualities. It worked; no one heard the gunshot that morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions for My Grandfather’s Psychiatrist', 'kicker': 'Couch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-16T00:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Anastas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anastas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/495997c2-ee9e-57a5-8ed3-879dfa448480', 'word_count': 1369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/495997c2-ee9e-57a5-8ed3-879dfa448480'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations Security Council agreed late Monday to consider the human rights situation in North Korea next week, paving the way for discussions on whether to refer the country to the International Criminal Court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/16/world/asia/united-nations-security-council-to-discuss-north-korea.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations Security Council agreed late Monday to consider the human rights situation in North Korea next week, paving the way for discussions on whether to refer the country to the International Criminal Court.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United Nations Security Council agreed late Monday to consider the human rights situation in North Korea next week, paving the way for discussions on whether to refer the country to the International Criminal Court. The move places China, North Korea’s principal ally on the Council, under a spotlight. Rebuffing Chinese concerns, the Council on Monday said that it would seek a briefing from senior United Nations officials next week. The Council is not expected to take any immediate action. The move follows a landmark decision by the human rights committee of the General Assembly to ask the Council to consider referring North Korea to the court. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Security Council to Discuss North Korea', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Security Council to Discuss North Korea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-16T00:16:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8244ed05-4304-5452-8c00-98ed832f998b', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8244