e Supreme Court sided with Mr. Phillips in a lawsuit tied to the episode.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jack Phillips explains his reasons for refusing to make a cake for a same-sex wedding. In June 2018, the Supreme Court sided with Mr. Phillips in a lawsuit tied to the episode.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/us/CAKE-alpha/CAKE-alpha-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/16/us/CAKE-alpha/CAKE-alpha-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/us/CAKE-alpha/CAKE-alpha-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/us/CAKE-alpha/CAKE-alpha-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/us/CAKE-alpha/CAKE-alpha-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/16/us/CAKE-alpha/CAKE-alpha-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/us/CAKE-alpha/CAKE-alpha-thumbLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Clash of Cake and Faith', 'kicker': 'U.S.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phillips, Jack (1956- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-16T03:47:54+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/5d23067f-ddad-5491-89f1-17fc47d35dda', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/5d23067f-ddad-5491-89f1-17fc47d35dda'}, {'abstract': 'The number of deaths linked to the problem is now more than triple the automaker’s original estimate of 13.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/16/business/lawyer-raises-death-toll-to-42-in-faulty-gm-vehicles.html', 'snippet': 'The number of deaths linked to the problem is now more than triple the automaker’s original estimate of 13.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lawyer overseeing the program to compensate victims of General Motors’ defective ignition switch has declared 42 death claims eligible for payment, bringing the number of deaths linked to the problem to more than triple the automaker’s original estimate of 13. The total was posted on Monday in a weekly update by the lawyer, Kenneth R. Feinberg. The report also said that Mr. Feinberg had accepted seven claims for catastrophic injuries — a category that includes permanent brain damage, quadriplegia and paraplegia — and 51 claims for other injuries that were serious enough to require hospitalization. G.M. has given Mr. Feinberg sole discretion to determine which claims are eligible for payment, so his determinations serve as the public record of the human toll from the defective switch, a flaw that the automaker has admitted was known in some parts of the company for more than a decade before it decided to recall 2.6 million cars for the problem this year. Monday’s update showed that a total of 2,326 claims had been filed so far, including 251 for deaths. Of those, 306 claims — including 46 death claims — were rejected. Most of the others are awaiting additional evidence. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawyer Raises Death Toll to 42 in Faulty G.M. Vehicles', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawyer Raises Death Toll to 42 in Faulty G.M. Vehicles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinberg, Kenneth R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-16T03:59:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Stout', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stout', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/aee56c5c-a1ba-5a47-a4f0-fffef59d310c', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aee56c5c-a1ba-5a47-a4f0-fffef59d310c'}, {'abstract': 'There is a way to “hide” items from your list so they aren’t visible on a shared computer. Also, how to enlarge the New Message window in Gmail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/technology/personaltech/how-to-hide-past-itunes-purchases.html', 'snippet': 'There is a way to “hide” items from your list so they aren’