e': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/dining/koreamap-1418760479438/koreamap-1418760479438-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pete Wells’s Choices for Korean Dishes in Queens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Korean Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flushing (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-16T18:27:37+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Food', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/8f71c879-63c4-5eef-9506-10b4acd510db', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/8f71c879-63c4-5eef-9506-10b4acd510db'}, {'abstract': 'The Queens kimchi belt has got to be the least explored, discussed and celebrated of the city’s great ethnic-food districts. In and near Flushing, hundreds of restaurants serve classic Korean dishes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/17/dining/critics-notebook-pete-wells-explores-korean-restaurants-in-queens.html', 'snippet': 'The Queens kimchi belt has got to be the least explored, discussed and celebrated of the city’s great ethnic-food districts. In and near Flushing, hundreds of restaurants serve classic Korean dishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We can blame the IRT. The No. 7 train was never meant to end at Main Street in Flushing. If the Interborough Rapid Transit Company had followed through on plans to extend it, then all the remarkable Korean food of Queens might be as famous as the dosas of Jackson Heights, the tamales of Corona, the som tums of Elmhurst.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Queens, Kimchi Is Just the Start', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Queens, Kimchi Is Just the Start', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Korean Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flushing (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bayside (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-16T18:29:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/498b1c5d-1790-50b0-a148-a42176e88726', 'word_count': 2767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/498b1c5d-1790-50b0-a148-a42176e88726'}, {'abstract': 'Faustine Steinmetz uses elaborate handiwork to create couture-grade versions of populist pieces.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/16/faustine-steinmetz-london-designer-opening-ceremony/', 'snippet': 'Faustine Steinmetz uses elaborate handiwork to create couture-grade versions of populist pieces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Buy a piece from the London-based, Paris-raised designer\xa0Faustine Steinmetz, and she will send you a password-protected link leading to almost uncomfortably intimate videos and photos documenting the garment’s creation, which can take more than a month. From dye bath to loom, each item from the year-old line is created at the hand of only one artisan in Steinmetz’s studio. “This is what luxury is to me, giving people a piece that took all your efforts. I love the feeling of almost being like a little hand,” says Steinmetz, who studied at Atelier Chardon Savard and Central Saint Martins before launching her label out of her kitchen. “I’ve always had a bit of a fascination with the backstage of the couture houses.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/t-magazine/16faustine-wu/16faustine-wu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/16/t-magazine/16faustine-wu/16faustine-wu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/t-magazine/16faustine-wu/16faustine-wu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/t-magazine/16faustine-wu/16faustine-wu-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/t-magazine/16faustine-wu/16faustine-wu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/16/t-magazine/16faustine-wu/16faustine-wu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/t-magazine/16faustine-wu/16faustine-wu-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A London Designer Reinvents the Basics, By Hand', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_he