es', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/business/dbpix-jefferies-1/dbpix-jefferies-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/09/09/business/dbpix-jefferies-1/dbpix-jefferies-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/business/dbpix-jefferies-1/dbpix-jefferies-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/business/dbpix-jefferies-1/dbpix-jefferies-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/business/dbpix-jefferies-1/dbpix-jefferies-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/09/09/business/dbpix-jefferies-1/dbpix-jefferies-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/09/09/business/dbpix-jefferies-1/dbpix-jefferies-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bad Quarter, and Bad Year, for Jefferies', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Sage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jefferies Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-16T19:16:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antony Currie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Currie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3ae0c44-5b06-5e71-b74e-81c9d5d2ae6a', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3ae0c44-5b06-5e71-b74e-81c9d5d2ae6a'}, {'abstract': 'In the course of a half century, Barton Silverman has gone from being a scrappy Brooklyn kid making his own breaks — and almost falling off a bridge — to taking classic pictures of athletes like Joe Namath and Derek Jeter. Now retiring from The New York Times, he recalls a memorable image.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/16/the-bat-broke-but-the-photographer-did-not/', 'snippet': 'In the course of a half century, Barton Silverman has gone from being a scrappy Brooklyn kid making his own breaks — and almost falling off a bridge — to taking classic pictures of athletes like Joe Namath and Derek Jeter. Now retiring from The Ne...', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was an incident during the 2000 Subway Series between the Yankees and Mets that a lot of New Yorkers think was one of my career moments. Roger Clemens had a dispute with Mike Piazza, since earlier in the year Clemens threw a ball that had knocked Piazza unconscious. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bat Broke, but the Photographer Did Not', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clemens, Roger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piazza, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-16T19:16:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barton Silverman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barton', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silverman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f798f417-7b4b-51d0-91a7-15d8b31b3aaa', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f798f417-7b4b-51d0-91a7-15d8b31b3aaa'}, {'abstract': 'To catch a glimpse of Ireland’s rugged beauty, you needn’t travel west. Just hop on Dublin’s rail network to the staggeringly scenic eastern coastline.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/16/travel/by-public-transit-from-dublin-hikes-vistas-and-seafood-all-for-a-song.html', 'snippet': 'To catch a glimpse of Ireland’s rugged beauty, you needn’t travel west. Just hop on Dublin’s rail network to the staggeringly scenic eastern coastline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For its vertical limestone cliffs and unspoiled sea views, Ireland’s dramatic western coastline may get top billing. But visitors to Dublin hoping to catch a glimpse of the rugged beauty of the Emerald Isle needn’t spend extra hours and expense traveling west. For little more than the cost of a pint, they can hop on Dublin Area Rapid Transit, or DART, the city’s electric rail network that winds roughly 30 miles along the eastern coastline, for convenient under-an-hour escapes. The following day trips — whose draws include staggeringly scenic sea cliffs that are destinations in their own right, a James Joyce museum and, no surprise, excellent seafood and beer — promise memorable, and frugal, additions to any Dublin vacation. (Factor in maximum prices for “the Dort,” the Dublin Bus, and the Luas light rail tram system — at 10 euros a day, $12.20 at $1.22 to the euro, or 40 euros a week — and travel costs become even cheaper.) And while wintertime daily highs average in the mid-40s, confining swimming to only the hardiest souls, with views like these, who needs a dip in the ocean?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/travel/Dublin-1/Dublin-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/16/travel/Dublin-1/Dublin-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/travel/Dublin-1/Dublin-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/travel/Dublin-1/Dublin-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1299, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/travel/Dublin-1/Dublin-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/16/travel/Dublin-1/Dublin-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/travel/Dublin-1/Dublin-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'By Public Transit From Dublin: Hikes, Vistas and Seafood, All for a Song', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'