: 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ac67cd9-7468-53eb-b81f-e6c04f654d99'}, {'abstract': 'A new book by John Osburg, “Anxious Wealth: Money and Morality Among China’s New Rich,” paints a rich picture of the complex ways in which men and women try to buy favors and get ahead in business ventures, often by courting government officials at night clubs and often over drinking and sex.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/16/q-and-a-john-osburg-on-the-angst-found-among-chinas-newly-rich/', 'snippet': 'A new book by John Osburg, “Anxious Wealth: Money and Morality Among China’s New Rich,” paints a rich picture of the complex ways in which men and women try to buy favors and get ahead in business ventures, often by courting government officials a...', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Osburg, 39, an assistant professor of anthropology at the University of Rochester, is the author of “Anxious Wealth: Money and Morality Among China’s New Rich,” based on research he conducted in the southwestern Chinese city of Chengdu. The book paints a detailed picture of the complex ways in which men and women try to buy favors and get ahead in business ventures, often by courting government officials at night clubs and often over drinking and sex. It also describes a milieu beset by anxiety over whether their gains can last.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/world/10sino-OSBURG2/10sino-OSBURG2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 511, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/world/10sino-OSBURG2/10sino-OSBURG2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 511, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/10/