ah-while-everything-else-keeps-going/', 'snippet': 'Celebrating Hanukkah and Christmas has made me aware of how much easier the outside world makes it to protect one tradition over the other.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I spent part of yesterday evening in the basement, as I can only assume anyone might, contemplating such great mysteries as why the box so clearly labeled “Hanukkah” so clearly did not include any menorahs, or dreidels, or in fact anything related to Hanukkah at all except a few boxes of the more depressing brand of candles and whether it was possible that, in mid-December, I still had a big pile of Halloween decorations down there to put away. (It is, and this is the kind of behavior that, one year, led me to use the tail end of the holiday lights still strung on the house to inflate a child’s wading pool in June.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/us/motherlode-menorahs/motherlode-menorahs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/16/us/motherlode-menorahs/motherlode-menorahs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/us/motherlode-menorahs/motherlode-menorahs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/us/motherlode-menorahs/motherlode-menorahs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1078, 'width': 1632, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/us/motherlode-menorahs/motherlode-menorahs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 