ion of North Korea’s leader, the New York premiere was called off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Sony Pictures Entertainment, the F.B.I., theater owners and competing film studios scrambled on Tuesday to deal with a threat of terrorism against movie theaters that show Sony’s “The Interview,” a raunchy comedy about the assassination of the North Korean leader, Kim Jong-un.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/business/Sony/Sony-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/17/business/Sony/Sony-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/business/Sony/Sony-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/business/Sony/Sony-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Quandary for Sony in Terror Threats Over ‘The Interview’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quandary for Sony in Threats Over Film', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Pictures Entertainment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogen, Seth', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name