Mr. Gyllenhaal. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21JPRUTH1/21JPRUTH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21JPRUTH1/21JPRUTH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21JPRUTH1/21JPRUTH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21JPRUTH1/21JPRUTH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21JPRUTH1/21JPRUTH1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21JPRUTH1/21JPRUTH1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21JPRUTH1/21JPRUTH1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After ‘The Affair,’ Ruth Wilson Hits Broadway in ‘Constellations’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Stars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Ruth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Affair (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Showtime', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Constellations (Play)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T13:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d30be6d-428a-55c6-8d19-8893863361b3', 'word_count': 1716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d30be6d-428a-55c6-8d19-8893863361b3'}, {'abstract': 'Market turmoil will test Washington’s efforts to bolster the financial system. | Bond investors skittish over emerging markets. | Venture capital’s feeding frenzy. | Email newsletter theSkimm raises $6.25 million in financing.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/17/morning-agenda-a-test-for-post-crisis-banking-system/', 'snippet': 'Market turmoil will test Washington’s efforts to bolster the financial system. | Bond investors skittish over emerging markets. | Venture capital’s feeding frenzy. | Email newsletter theSkimm raises $6.25 million in financing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The market turmoil this week will test Washington’s efforts over the last five years to bolster the financial system, Peter Eavis reports in DealBook. Investors are stampeding out of risky markets, dumping junk bonds issued by American energy companies that have borrowed heavily to exploit the shale oil boom. A steep slide in the price of oil could now cause some of the companies to default, analysts say. But the most dangerous pain is occurring abroad, particularly in Russia, which is dealing with a currency crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: A Test for Post-Crisis Banking System', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T13:05:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2b7a506-95b6-55ae-8c02-9eaa05e43a90', 'word_count': 2130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2b7a506-95b6-55ae-8c02-9eaa05e43a90'}, {'abstract': 'Fifteen ideas for teaching and learning about 2014, using retrospective videos, photos, articles and lists from The New York Times and around the Web.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/17/looking-back-on-2014-fifteen-ways-to-teach-and-learn-about-the-year-that-was/', 'snippet': 'Fifteen ideas for teaching and learning about 2014, using retrospective videos, photos, articles and lists from The New York Times and around the Web.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What were the biggest events of 2014? How will the year be remembered? What will 2015 be like?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/arts/artsspecial/WILLIAMSOBIT-slide-GQB5-LN2/WILLIAMSOBIT-slide-GQB5-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/11/arts/artsspecial/WILLIAMSOBIT-slide-GQB5-LN2/WILLIAMSOBIT-slide-GQB5-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/arts/artsspecial/WILLIAMSOBIT-slide-GQB5-LN2/WILLIAMSOBIT-slide-GQB5-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 's