ichigan Tech is 13-3-0 and ranked No. 5 in the N.C.A.A.’s Division I, a development that is more than welcome in Copper Country, where professional hockey was born.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/sports/hockey/michigan-tech-huskies-are-off-to-a-milestone-start.html', 'snippet': 'Michigan Tech is 13-3-0 and ranked No. 5 in the N.C.A.A.’s Division I, a development that is more than welcome in Copper Country, where professional hockey was born.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUGHTON, Mich. — Hockey rules this remote part of Michigan’s Upper Peninsula, where it is played by everyone from children to those in their 70s and 80s. All through the long winter it is always game on — in modern arenas, outside (into the wee hours of the night) and in two of the oldest hockey rinks in the world. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/sports/18michtech2/18michtech2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/18/sports/18michtech2/18michtech2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/sports/18michtech2/18michtech2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/sports/18michtech2/18michtech2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/sports/18michtech2/18michtech2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/18/sports/18michtech2/18michtech2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/sports/18michtech2/18michtech2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stirring Passions in Hockey Hotbed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stirring Passions in Hockey Hotbed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pearson, Mel K (1959- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper Peninsula (Mich)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Michigan Technological University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T14:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/115ac2c0-59f4-5078-aa72-145d0fc96f2e', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/115ac2c0-59f4-5078-aa72-145d0fc96f2e'}, {'abstract': 'The inside story of how Yahoo’s C.E.O. lost her way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/magazine/what-happened-when-marissa-mayer-tried-to-be-steve-jobs.html', 'snippet': 'The inside story of how Yahoo’s C.E.O. lost her way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Jackson was sitting in his hotel room on Sea Island, Ga., watching his kids splash around in the pool, when he clicked “publish” on his latest blog post for Forbes.com. Jackson, an influential hedge-fund manager, had become fixated on Yahoo and the efforts of its chief executive, Marissa Mayer, to turn around the enormous yet floundering Internet company. It was July 21, 2014, almost exactly two years to the day since Mayer took over, arriving at Yahoo’s headquarters to an unfurled purple carpet and Shepard Fairey-style “HOPE” posters bearing her face. During those 24 months, Mayer eliminated dozens of products and rebooted others. She acquired 41 start-ups and even hired Katie Couric. But just one week earlier, Mayer announced the company’s lowest quarterly earnings in a decade. Jackson argued in his post that Yahoo no longer made sense as an independent entity. Instead, it might be a nice takeover target for one of the tech industry’s Big Four: Apple, Facebook, Amazon or Google.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21marissamayer1/21marissamayer1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21marissamayer1/21marissamayer1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21marissamayer1/21marissamayer1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21marissamayer1/21marissamayer1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 810, 'width': 1440, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21marissamayer1/21marissamayer1-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21marissamayer1/21marissamayer1-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21marissamayer1/21marissamayer1-thumbLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happened When Marissa Mayer Tried to Be Steve Jobs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Results', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlson, Nicholas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayer, Marissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alibaba Group Holding Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AOL Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T14:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Carlson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carlson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82f6fd06-41c5-529c-beac-98d5fd9aae18', 'word_count': 6980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82f6fd06-41c5-529c-beac-98d5fd9aae18'}, {'abstract': 'Two stars of the movie answer the question: did you know what you were talking about when you had to say astrophysics-y things?', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/17/the-science-and-eye-makeup-of-interstellar/', 'snippet': 'Two stars of the movie answer the question: did you know what you were talking about when you had to say astrophysics-y things?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fervent speculation preceded the release of Christopher Nolan’s “Interstellar,” with at least one outlet dubbing it the year’s “most mysterious film.” Though the film did pick up a Golden Globe nomination (for Hans Zimmer’s score), prognosticators have geared down, wondering if the lengthy film’s recursive time loops and astrophysical acrobatics would woo Oscar voters or repel them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/arts/hathawaybagger/hathawaybagger-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/04/arts/hathawaybagger/hathawaybagger-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/arts/hathawaybagger/hathawaybagger-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/arts/hathawaybagger/hathawaybagger-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/arts/hathawaybagger/hathawaybagger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/