respondents said torture of suspected terrorists could be justified “often” or “sometimes.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following the Senate Intelligence Committee report on torture, a Washington Post/ABC News poll released Tuesday found that a majority of Americans believe torture of suspected terrorists can be justified.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facts & Figures: Americans for Torture', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T15:39:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a14c4d5-0514-59da-9788-78a14ec6e63d', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a14c4d5-0514-59da-9788-78a14ec6e63d'}, {'abstract': 'The last of a group of Democratic lawmakers who have lived in a Washington rowhouse for years finally moved out, taking their comforters and Hendrix records with them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/12/17/first-draft-focus-packing-up-the-alpha-house/', 'snippet': 'The last of a group of Democratic lawmakers who have lived in a Washington rowhouse for years finally moved out, taking their comforters and Hendrix records with them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawmakers Are Roommates No More', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/us/politics/17firstdraft-alpha-house/17firstdraft-alpha-house-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/17/us/politics/17firstdraft-a