 bookish Jewish kid from Chicago, Zemel had a love for Israel inherited from his grandfather, Rabbi Solomon Goldman, a friend of Albert Einstein’s who was president from 1938 to 1940 of the then left-leaning Zionist Organization of America. With the other members of his Jewish education group, the 13-year-old Zemel spent two weeks in Jerusalem, Tel Aviv and Haifa. He lunched in cafeterias with the kibbutzniks he idolized, ate frozen treats on the beach and climbed a lookout tower, peering into Jerusalem’s still forbidden Old City. A year later, Zemel was ecstatic when Israeli forces captured everything he had surveyed and beyond, including the Temple Mount, the West Bank and Gaza, in the Six-Day War with Egypt, Syria and Jordan. Over the decades, as Israel matured and began to wrestle with the occupation, Zemel did, too. He visited Israel again and again, as a college student, a rabbinical student and an assistant rabbi in Minnesota.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21zionists1/21zionists1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21zionists1/21zionists1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21zionists1/21zionists1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21zionists1/21zionists1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1492, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21zionists1/21zionists1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21zionists1/21zionists1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/magazine/21zionists1/21zionists1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Liberal Zionists Count On Hillary Clinton?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Exile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T18:59:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Horowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66c625a6-34af-5053-9006-cb3d0ae2dd9c', 'word_count': 4068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66c625a6-34af-5053-9006-cb3d0ae2dd9c'}, {'abstract': 'The new video from the duo, also comprised of the sound designer Joseph Fraioli, features dreamy footage of New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/17/big-noble-music-video-premiere-interpol-daniel-kessler/', 'snippet': 'The new video from the duo, also comprised of the sound designer Joseph Fraioli, features dreamy footage of New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s really a blending of our two worlds,” says the guitarist Daniel Kessler about Big Noble, his not-so-newfound collaboration with the sound designer Joseph Fraioli. The pair originally met in New York back in 1999; at the time, Kessler was working as a music manager for the electronic label Caipirinha, to which Fraioli’s Datach’i project was signed. Since then, Kessler has written and recorded five albums with Interpol, while Fraioli has expanded his reach to the commercial world, creating soundscapes for clients like Nissan, Nike and VH1.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17symonds-bignoble/17symonds-bignoble-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17symonds-bignoble/17symonds-bignoble-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17symonds-bignoble/17symonds-bignoble-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17symonds-bignoble/17symonds-bignoble-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17symonds-bignoble/17symonds-bignoble-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17symonds-bignoble/17symonds-bignoble-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17symonds-bignoble/17symonds-bignoble-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Atmospheric Music Video from Big Noble, Featuring Interpol’s Daniel Kessler', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interpol (Music Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T19:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aly Comingore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Comingore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5999ed48-058b-58f3-b73a-ab05f4df0f34', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5999ed48-058b-58f3-b73a-ab05f4df0f34'}, {'abstract': 'Defensive tactics can serve legitimate business interests, but many invite criticism that companies are eager to avoid, Reynolds Holding writes in Reuters Breakingviews.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/17/anti-takeover-defense-measures-often-hurt-investors/', 'snippet': 'Defensive tactics can serve legitimate business interests, but many invite criticism that companies are eager to avoid, Reynolds Holding writes in Reuters Breakingviews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Corporate defenses can hurt investors, rain or shine. Anti-takeover measures adopted on so-called clear days – before threats arise – are more likely to weather legal scrutiny. It’s one reason Allergan was able to beat back Valeant Pharmaceutical’s unwanted $52 billion advance. When such protections are put in place in the heat of battle, though, they’re considered unfair surprises. Either way, the outlook is gloomy for shareholders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/18/business/dbpix-allergan1/dbpix-allergan1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/18/business/dbpix-allergan1/dbpix-allergan1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/18/business/dbpix-allergan1/dbpix-allergan1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/18/business/dbpix-allergan1/dbpix-allergan1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/18/business/dbpix-allergan1/dbpix-allergan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/18/business/dbpix-allergan1/dbpix-allergan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/18/business/dbpix-allergan1/dbpix-allergan1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {