chael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a8bd435-db26-5123-833f-c8229c6784ac', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a8bd435-db26-5123-833f-c8229c6784ac'}, {'abstract': 'Francis helped bridge the divide by first sending letters to President Obama and President Raúl Castro of Cuba, and then having the Vatican host a meeting between them in October.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/world/americas/breakthrough-on-cuba-highlights-popes-role-as-diplomatic-broker.html', 'snippet': 'Francis helped bridge the divide by first sending letters to President Obama and President Raúl Castro of Cuba, and then having the Vatican host a meeting between them in October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Pope Francis had quite a 78th birthday. The pontiff began Wednesday with prayers and a birthday celebration with tango dancers near St. Peter’s Square. His day ended with a historic diplomatic breakthrough between Cuba and the United States — and the disclosure that the Argentine pope played a key role as broker.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pope Francis Is Credited With a Crucial Role in U.S.-Cuba Agreement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pope Played a Quiet Role in U.S. Deal With Cuba', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pianigiani, Gaia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value'