fe in classics like “Ferris Bueller’s Day Off,” “Sixteen Candles” and “The Breakfast Club.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a luminous late-summer day, but I was stuck in a police station in the northern Chicago suburb of Des Plaines, a 1970s-era concrete behemoth that had the cool sterility of a hospital. Speed walking ahead of me were two officers, middle-aged men with buzz cuts, Smokey Bear hats and shiny black patent leather belts. They were on the hunt and I was racing to keep up. I had never been in this maze of hallways, linoleum floors and dreary courtyards before, yet the building was as familiar to me as any deeply embossed memory from childhood. Which, in a way, it was. I was raised on John Hughes movies, and this was the setting of one of his most beloved films, “The Breakfast Club," from 1985.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Teen Streets of John Hughes’s Chicago', 'kicker': 'Footsteps', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Walking the Teen Streets of John Hughes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moon, Freda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, John (1950-2009)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Ferris Bueller's Day Off (Movie)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Home Alone (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Pretty in Pink (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sixteen Candles (Movie)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T20:36:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'ori