//article/105d5ed3-83e6-50a4-b3e9-3b1cd3705919'}, {'abstract': 'Political historians said the steps announced on Wednesday were akin to the steps taken to normalize relations with China and Vietnam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/world/americas/cuba-off-the-blacklist-leaves-only-north-korea.html', 'snippet': 'Political historians said the steps announced on Wednesday were akin to the steps taken to normalize relations with China and Vietnam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The normalization of diplomatic relations with Cuba after more than a half-century of enmity would leave only North Korea on America’s Cold War blacklist, and only Iran, Sudan and Syria as countries that are regarded by the United States government as pariah states that sponsor terrorism.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/world/18NORMALIZE/18NORMALIZE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/18/world/18NORMALIZE/18NORMALIZE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/world/18NORMALIZE/18NORMALIZE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/world/18NORMALIZE/18NORMALIZE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/world/18NORMALIZE/18NORMALIZE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'im