reams of emaciated 20-somethings mugging for party flicks. It closed in 2013, well after its popularity petered out. In late November, the two-level space reopened with the same name and address but revamped, by Teddy Perweiler, Oliver Stumm (Cafe Select) and Max Levai (of the Marlborough Chelsea gallery) as a restaurant, bar and club. Still, they’re not looking to exorcise the house-of-ill-repute feeling entirely.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy Ending Reopens on the Lower East Side', 'kicker': 'Boîte', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Happy Ending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Detrick, Ben', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Happy Ending (Manhattan, NY, Bar)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T22:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Detrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Detrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/814e02f6-ca8f-5983-87fb-3be554863f5b', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/814e02f6-ca8f-5983-87fb-3be554863f5b'}, {'abstract': 'Many bond funds have loaded up on high-risk, high-return securities and, in the process, have become ever more opaque about the risks involved.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/17/a-wager-on-emerging-markets-that-seems-poorly-timed/', 'snippet': 'Many bond funds have loaded up on high-risk, high-return securities and, in the process, have become ever more opaque about the risks involved.', 'lead_para