, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derivatives (Financial Instruments)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gross, William H', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gundlach, Jeffrey E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PIMCO (Pacific Investment Management Company)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T22:45:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Landon Thomas Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Landon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13b52a66-ad11-5072-a2ed-d7d9c1c6d04e', 'word_count': 1291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13b52a66-ad11-5072-a2ed-d7d9c1c6d04e'}, {'abstract': 'The Second Stage Theater company is moving ahead on buying the Helen Hayes Theater and hopes to set aside a reserve fund to cover production costs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/theater/second-stage-in-push-for-money-to-buy-helen-hayes.html', 'snippet': 'The Second Stage Theater company is moving ahead on buying the Helen Hayes Theater and hopes to set aside a reserve fund to cover production costs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Off Broadway Second Stage Theater announced in 2008 that it would buy and renovate a Broadway house, the total cost was $35 million. Now, after multiple delays, the sale is finally on a fast track to close in mid-February, but Second Stage executives are rushing to raise money for a much higher goal: $58 million.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/arts/JPSECONDSTAGE/JPSECONDSTAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/18/arts/JPSECONDSTAGE/JPSECONDSTAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/arts/JPSECONDSTAGE/JPSECONDSTAGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/arts/JPSECONDSTAGE/JPSECONDSTAGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1475, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/arts/JPSECONDSTAGE/JPSECONDSTAGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/18/arts/JPSECONDSTAGE/JPSECONDSTAGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/arts/JPSECONDSTAGE/JPSECONDSTAGE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '$58 Million Is Sought for Theater', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '$58 Million Is Sought for Theater', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Second Stage Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hayes, Helen, Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T22:47:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5d90d28-a021-5fe2-a375-4e1790c14046', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5d90d28-a021-5fe2-a375-4e1790c14046'}, {'abstract': 'Germany’s cabinet approved a plan for 100 soldiers to help train Kurdish pesh merga forces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/world/europe/german-soldiers-may-help-train-forces-in-iraq.html', 'snippet': 'Germany’s cabinet approved a plan for 100 soldiers to help train Kurdish pesh merga forces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Germany plans to send about 100 soldiers to northern Iraq to help train Kurdish pesh merga forces fighting Islamic State militants. A final parliamentary vote on the proposal, approved by the German cabinet on Wednesday, is expected next month. The government noted that the deployment to a war zone — unusual but not unprecedented for Germany — would be closely coordinated with Italian, Dutch and Scandinavian forces. But the far-left opposition has objected that the mission is illegal because it is not sanctioned by the United Nations or NATO.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'German Soldiers May Help Train Forces in Iraq', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pesh Merga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T22:48:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44f471f5-9be8-5785-92ff-89ade234b1d3', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44f471f5-9be8-5785-92ff-89ade234b1d3'}, {'abstract': 'In three recent programs at City Center, as the Alvin Ailey American Dance troupe continued its five-week run, a sense of in-this-together companionship animated every piece.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/arts/alvin-ailey-dance-highlights-teamwork-in-recent-performances.html', 'snippet': 'In three recent programs at City Center, as the Alvin Ailey American Dance troupe continued its five-week run, a sense of in-this-together companionship animated every piece.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 2011, when Robert Battle became the artistic director of Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater, his choice of new repertory has been the subject of much scrutiny. This season’s arrivals, while once again introducing welcome variety, are not all felicitous. What’s more consistently striking is the ensemble he’s cultivating: how the company, under his direction, is working together as a whole. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/arts/AILEY/AILEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/18/arts/AILEY/AILEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo