h-now-can-be-yours.html', 'snippet': 'Auctioning off rock mementos from a famed recording studio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Jim Guercio, a music producer, bought Caribou Ranch, outside Boulder, Colo., in the early 1970s, he envisioned it as a place for artists to record without distractions. The 4,000-acre property ultimately became a retreat for rock stars, who stayed in the old guest cabins, ate dinner with their band mates in the mess hall and went on outdoor adventures when not making hits in the hayloft-turned-studio.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/garden/18CURR7-9_COMBO/18CURR7-9_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/18/garden/18CURR7-9_COMBO/18CURR7-9_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/garden/18CURR7-9_COMBO/18CURR7-9_COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/garden/18CURR7-9_COMBO/18CURR7-9_COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/garden/18CURR7-9_COMBO/18CURR7-9_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/18/garden/18CURR7-9_COMBO/18CURR7-9_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/garden/18CURR7-9_COMBO/18CURR7-9_COMBO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Elton Sang and Rode', 'kicker': 'Events', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Elton Sang and Rode', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boulder (Colo)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'John, Elton', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-17T23:54:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0f2a6ae-c3dc-524a-a712-8adf82df50be', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0f2a6ae-c3dc-524a-a712-8adf82df50be'}, {'abstract': 'Tiles in decorative bug patterns by Timorous Beasties.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/garden/if-it-flutters-or-buzzes-surely-its-art-.html', 'snippet': 'Tiles in decorative bug patterns by Timorous Beasties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Simmons, who heads the Scottish design studio Timorous Beasties with Alistair McAuley, describes their mission as making the ugly beautiful. Since 1990, the men have worked iguanas, devil heads and hairy thistles into their products.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption