mal accessories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/style/street-style-in-the-bronx-new-york-city-arthur-avenue.html', 'snippet': '“I feel at home here,” said Bertol Dragani, 25, of Arthur Avenue in the Bronx. He was wearing a mostly monochromatic look, with minimal accessories.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xadAlbanian and Italian flags line Arthur Avenue in the Bronx, a neighborhood that seems frozen in time, where cafes blast traditional folk music and shops selling handmade mozzarella are plentiful. “I feel at home here,” said Bertol Dragani, an architect who was raised in Albania but went to a university in Milan. Wearing a mostly monochromatic look, which included a structured trench coat, Zara shoes and Persol sunglasses, Mr. Dragani came to the area recently to grab a panini and coffee with his friends. This interview has been edited and condensed. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Street Style in the Bronx', 'kicker': 'Intersection', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Non-Ornamental', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Arthur Avenue (Bronx, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBANIA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T00:21:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna Nikas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nikas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/992b45e9-8527-5504-83e9-7ee77d42f975', 'word_count': 