1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Canada, Australia and New Zealand will render vast aid to Great Britain soon in the production of airplanes and the training of pilots, it was announced today with the signing in Ottawa of the Empire air training agreement for the expansion of facilities in the Dominions. Prime Minister Mackenzie King of Canada, in a broadcast from Ottawa, declared that Canada will become one of the greatest air training centers in the world under the $600,000,000 program, which will run until March 31, 1943, but may be prolonged. Canada’s share of the cost will be approximately $350,000,000. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Dec. 19, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/blogs/18iht-old19-1939/18iht-old19-1939-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 418, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/blogs/18iht-old19-1939/18iht-old19-1939-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 418, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/blogs/18iht-old19-1939/18iht-old19-1939-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/18/blogs/18iht-old19-1939/18iht-old19-1939-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/blogs/18iht-old19-1939/18iht-old19-1939-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Empire Air Accord Is Signed', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospectiv