 '_id': 'nyt://article/c1602820-27de-50d8-98c1-ef2e33834fc1', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1602820-27de-50d8-98c1-ef2e33834fc1'}, {'abstract': 'Bond funds have piled into high-risk securities. | The Fed to be patient on raising interest rates. | Ruble crisis tests Russia’s resources. | Big reward for Countrywide whistle-blower.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/morning-agenda-ill-timed-bet-on-emerging-markets/', 'snippet': 'Bond funds have piled into high-risk securities. | The Fed to be patient on raising interest rates. | Ruble crisis tests Russia’s resources. | Big reward for Countrywide whistle-blower.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before William H. Gross left Pimco, the giant asset manager he co-founded, he made a change to his investor prospectus for the firm’s $200 billion flagship Total Return fund, DealBook’s Landon Thomas Jr. writes. He was bullish on the bonds of emerging markets in Mexico and Brazil but was approaching Pimco’s 15 percent limit for the fund’s exposure to emerging markets. His change meant that the fund could now buy short-term Mexican, Brazilian, Russian or Chinese local currency government bonds and not exceed its limit for emerging markets. Perhaps curiously, Pimco deems these securities equivalent to cash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Ill-Timed Bet on Emerging Markets', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T12:52:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae5e2f95-48bc-526a-a319-3677d680b494', 'word_count': 2395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae5e2f95-48bc-526a-a319-3677d680b494'}, {'abstract': 'A dockworker dispute at American ports has led to a shortage of processed potatoes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/business/international/mcdonalds-in-japan-rations-french-fries.html', 'snippet': 'A dockworker dispute at American ports has led to a shortage of processed potatoes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Complete with rationing and emergency airlifts, Japan has entered the great French fry shortage of 2014.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/business/19fries-web1/19fries-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/business/19fries-web1/19fries-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/business/19fries-web1/19fries-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/business/19fries-web1/19fries-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/business/19fries-web1/19fries-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/19/business/19fries-web1/19fries-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/business/19fries-web1/19fries-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'McDonald’s in Japan Is Driven to Ration Fries', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "McDonald's in Japan Is Driven to Ration Fries", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McDonald's Corporation", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Potatoes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T12:54:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Soble', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soble', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/115bdae2-8c03-5ef2-acc3-391bd0b5ec5b', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/115bdae2-8c03-5ef2-acc3-391bd0b5ec5b'}, {'abstract': 'Michiko Kakutani chooses books by Gary Shteyngart, Robert M. Gates, Phil Klay, Lena Dunham, Marilynne Robinson and others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/books/phil-klays-redeployment-gary-shteyngarts-memoir-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Michiko Kakutani chooses books by Gary Shteyngart, Robert M. Gates, Phil Klay, Lena Dunham, Marilynne Robinson and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'REDEPLOYMENT by Phil Klay (the Penguin Press). The gritty, unsparing stories in this debut collection give us a visceral feel for what it was like to be a soldier on the ground in Iraq and what it was like to return home to a country that was mostly oblivious to the fact that America was even at war. A veteran of the Marine Corps, who served in Iraq during the surge, Mr. Klay writes with enormous precision and depth of feeling, the exactitude of his prose containing, and at the same time underscoring, war’s violence and chaos. His 12 stories are told in the first person, but from a variety of points of view (a young artilleryman, a member of Mortuary Affairs, a veteran attending law school). Together, these tales create a choral portrait of the war, and they testify to Mr. Klay’s range as a writer and his understanding of its human costs.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/books/19kakutani/19kakutani-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 364, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/books/19kakutani/19kakutani-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 364}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/books/19kakutani/19kakutani-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/books/19kakutani/19kakutani-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1241, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/books/19kakutani/19kakutani-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/19/books/19kakutani/19kakutani-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/books/19kakutani/19kakutani-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_nam