 episodes? If you are a teacher, do you teach with it? Let us know', 'lead_paragraph': 'What began as an animated sideshow to break up the live-action sketches for Tracey Ullman’s show became its own show in December 1989 and has gone on to become a maypole for American culture, writes David Carr in an article that asked, in 2005, Will ‘The Simpsons’ Ever Age? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Throwback Thursday | 25 Years of ‘The Simpsons’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T13:03:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1608011b-15d7-5468-b52a-e9e5fb00aa51', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1608011b-15d7-5468-b52a-e9e5fb00aa51'}, {'abstract': 'Alimentation Couche-Tard is paying about $860 million in cash, or $36.75 a share, 27 percent above Pantry’s closing price on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/canadian-convenience-store-operator-buys-pantry-in-u-s/', 'snippet': 'Alimentation Couche-Tard is paying about $860 million in cash, or $36.75 a share, 27 percent above Pantry’s closing price on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alimentation Couche-Tard, a Canadian operator of convenience stores, said on Thursday that it had agreed to buy Pantry Inc., which runs a network of stores in the southeastern United States, for about $860 million in cash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/business/dbpix-couche-tard/dbpix-couche-tar