munications Department at The Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/12/18/daily-clip-report-85/', 'snippet': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Clip Report', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T13:25:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c573d48-ad3e-57f4-af2d-ac2d9237a0f5', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c573d48-ad3e-57f4-af2d-ac2d9237a0f5'}, {'abstract': 'Wang Mengshu, one of China’s top railway construction engineers, talks about his idea for a “China-Russia-Alaska-Canada-U.S. high-speed rail.”', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/q-and-a-with-wang-mengshu-on-a-railroad-linking-china-and-the-u-s/', 'snippet': 'Wang Mengshu, one of China’s top railway construction engineers, talks about his idea for a “China-Russia-Alaska-Canada-U.S. high-speed rail.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wang Mengshu, one of China’s top railway construction engineers and a scholar with the Chinese Academy of Engineering specializing in tunnel and underground projects, told The Beijing Times this year about his idea for a “China-Russia-Alaska-Canada-U.S. high-speed rail,” which would start in northeastern China, go through eastern Russia toward the Bering Sea, cross the Bering Strait via a tunnel, arrive in Alaska and eventually traverse Canada to the United States. The tunnel across the Bering Strait alone would be about 125 miles long, Mr. Wang said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Wang Mengshu on a Railroad Linking China and the U.S.', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engineering and Engineers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Speed Rail Projects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bering Sea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bering Strait', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dalian (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T13:36:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mia Li', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Li', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a73baa97-44e4-51ae-a2c3-b6788c13b81c', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a73baa97-44e4-51ae-a2c3-b6788c13b81c'}, {'abstract': 'When a student decides to declare Santa a fraud, there’s little a teacher or parent can do.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/when-a-classmate-takes-on-santa/', 'snippet': 'When a student decides to declare Santa a fraud, there’s little a teacher or parent can do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My oldest child was due on Christmas Day 1998, and since then, December has continued to be the birthplace of innocence and magic in our house. Like many families, we have enthusiastically perpetuated the mythology of the season, an odd mix of Santa Claus, my Latin teacher Saturnalia trivia and many discussions about Herschel’s Hanukkah goblins. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/us/motherlode-ben/motherlode-ben-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/us/motherlode-ben/motherlode-ben-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/us/motherlode-ben/motherlode-ben-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/17/us/motherlode-ben/motherlode-ben-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/us/motherlode-ben/motherlode-ben-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Classmate Takes On Santa', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1,