, 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c53d200-24b7-5dfa-9327-44ba0ed8b847', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c53d200-24b7-5dfa-9327-44ba0ed8b847'}, {'abstract': 'Steven Hall wished to buy a one-bedroom apartment in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/realestate/searching-for-a-one-bedroom-in-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'Steven Hall wished to buy a one-bedroom apartment in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven Hall had been a renter all his life. He grew up in an apartment in Flushing, Queens, and moved to Manhattan in 1985. “I moved around too much to have a rent-stabilized apartment,” he said.\xa0', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/realestate/21HUNT-MAIN/21HUNT-MAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/21/realestate/21HUNT-MAIN/21HUNT-MAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/realestate/21HUNT-MAIN/21HUNT-MAIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/realestate/21HUNT-MAIN/21HUNT-MAIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/1