ecouped its $3.9 million capitalization, becoming the first show of the 2014-15 season to announce that it has turned a profit. The play’s producers disclosed the news on Wednesday, saying in a statement that the show’s hefty ticket sales at the Gerald Schoenfeld Theater “exceeded our expectations.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘It’s Only a Play’ Recoups on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It May Be Only a Play, but It’s Making Money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T16:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26df2bee-d409-5ce2-bab5-c2016ffaadb4', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26df2bee-d409-5ce2-bab5-c2016ffaadb4'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Dalis was a mezzo-soprano who starred at the Metropolitan Opera for two decades before building a second career as the founder and director of Opera San José.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/arts/music/irene-dalis-opera-singer-and-company-founder-dies-at-89-.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Dalis was a mezzo-soprano who starred at the Metropolitan Opera for two decades before building a second career as the founder and director of Opera San José.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Irene Dalis, a versatile and fiery mezzo-soprano who starred at the Metropolitan Opera for two decades before building a second career as the director of Opera San José, an innovative company she founded in her California hometown, died on Dec. 14 in nearby Saratoga, Calif. She was 89.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/dalisobit/dalisobit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/dalisobit/dalisobit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 721}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/dalisobit/dalisobit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 853, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/dalisobit/dalisobit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1705, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/dalisobit/dalisobit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/dalisobit/dalisobit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/dalisobit/dalisobit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Irene Dalis, Opera Singer and Company Founder, Dies at 89 ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Irene Dalis, 89; Traded a Diva’s Life for a Dream', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yardley, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalis, Irene (1925-2014)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T16:11:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/52e92f39-199a-52ac-92b9-33c9b3fb363e', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52e92f39-199a-52ac-92b9-33c9b3fb363e'}, {'abstract': 'The year may be coming to a close, but it’s been an emotional and difficult week at The Times.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/a-tumultuous-year-at-the-times/', 'snippet': 'The year may be coming to a close, but it’s been an emotional and difficult week at The Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My posting here has fallen off this week, but for pretty good reasons. I’ve been focused on two things. The first is on giving the commencement address Friday morning for the City University of New York’s graduate journalism school. It’s a great honor, and I thought it would be good to come up with something slightly more original than “wear sunscreen,” although that’s excellent advice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tumultuous Year at The Times', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T16:12:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edaef013-013b-58e2-b4e7-ad74d9aff971', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edaef013-013b-58e2-b4e7-ad74d9aff971'}, {'abstract': 'An internationally oriented design community, with influences from East and West, is springing up in the capital.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/tbilisi-georgia-fashion-scene-emerges/', 'snippet': 'An internationally oriented design community, with influences from East and West, is springing up in the capital.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’ve always believed that Georgia can be known for its rich culture, its art and now for its fashion – not only for politics, war and conflicts,” says the fashion entrepreneur Sofia Tchkonia, who founded the platforms BENEXT and ARTGeorgia in 2013 to promote young Georgian designers at home and abroad. While an internationally oriented fashion scene has only emerged in Tbilisi, the country’s capital, in recent years, style has long been part of the national identity. During Soviet rule, Tchkonia says, “Georgian women always looked different, even during that hard period when everything was forbidden. My mother told me that their inspiration was movies, especially French and Italian.” These days, Georgian designers are coming into their own with a new sense of creative – and infrastructural – autonomy. And while Georgia’s notable wine culture and the local taste for elegance might lend the impression that Georgia is the Italy of Eurasia, the capital’s experimentalism feels more like Antwerp’s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17tbilisi-perlson/17tbilisi-perlson-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17tbilisi-perlson/17tbilisi-perlson-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17tbilisi-perlson/17tbilisi-perlson-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17tbilisi-perlson/17tbilisi-perlson-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17tbilisi-perlson/17tbilisi-perlson-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17tbilisi-perlson/17tbilisi-perlson-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/t-magazine/17tbilisi-perlson/17tbilisi-perlson-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Tbilisi, Georgia, an Experimental Fashion Scene Emerges', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia (Georgian Republic)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_da