 'Stars and Galaxies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Planets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T16:26:43+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'Jason Drakeford, Jonathan Corum and Dennis Overbye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drakeford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Overbye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/01889e6f-d4cb-572f-a2b1-c752dcbdfea7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/01889e6f-d4cb-572f-a2b1-c752dcbdfea7'}, {'abstract': 'A skating trail along a frozen river in the Canadian city is home to inventive installations called “warming huts.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/travel/in-winnipeg-a-skating-rink-that-doubles-as-a-sculpture-park.html', 'snippet': 'A skating trail along a frozen river in the Canadian city is home to inventive installations called “warming huts.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'At minus 37 degrees Celsius (that’s minus 35 Fahrenheit) on a cloudless February morning, most of Winnipeg, Manitoba, was quiet. But I wasn’t the only one who was defiantly laced into ice skates. Out on the Assiniboine River, commuters, dog walkers, stroller pushers, hockey players and general dawdlers were gliding along a smooth band of ice, steam clouds drifting from behind their scarves with every aerobic side-to-side stride. One couple succumbed to the cold, wrapping themselves in curtainlike wool blankets that were suspended from a bridge like a massive Hudson Bay comforter, which was precisely their purpose.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/travel/21GETAWAY1/21GETAWAY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/21/travel/21GETAWAY1/21GETAWAY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/travel/21GETAWAY1/21GETAWAY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/travel/21GETAWAY1/21GETAWAY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/travel/21GETAWAY1/21GETAWAY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/21/travel/21GETAWAY1/21GETAWAY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/travel/21GETAWAY1/21GETAWAY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Winnipeg, a Skating Rink That Doubles as a Sculpture Park', 'kicker': 'Next Stop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Skating Rink or Sculpture Park?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glusac, Elaine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice Skating', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Winnipeg (Manitoba)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manitoba (Canada)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T16:27:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a1d5f58-65f4-5a67-8b20-3ab05cf7d68d', 'word_count': 1173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a1d5f58-65f4-5a67-8b20-3ab05cf7d68d'}, {'abstract': 'Astronomers have obtained, in the image of the young star HL Tauri, what might be the best view yet of dust in the act of turning into planets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/science/space/a-picture-captures-planets-waiting-to-be-born.html', 'snippet': 'Astronomers have obtained, in the image of the young star HL Tauri, what might be the best view yet of dust in the act of turning into planets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We might be stardust, Joni Mitchell sang of Woodstock in 1969, echoing what was already a half-century of hard-headed astronomical truth. But astronomers have struggled to understand just exactly how stardust goes from being cosmic smog, littering the lanes of the galaxy, to planets and people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Picture Captures Planets Waiting to Be Born', 'kicker': 'Out There', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Planets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stars and Galaxies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T16:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Overbye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Overbye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/257a9bd6-0830-573c-ae60-4f0fe1951bc8', 'word_count': 671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/257a9bd6-0830-573c-ae60-4f0fe1951bc8'}, {'abstract': 'With four carts, a restaurant in the East Village and one on the Upper West Side, Halal Guys patrons can’t get enough of the white sauce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/dining/hungry-city-the-halal-guys.html', 'snippet': 'With four carts, a restaurant in the East Village and one on the Upper West Side, Halal Guys patrons can’t get enough of the white sauce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little over two decades ago, a nameless food cart on the southwestern corner of 53rd Street and Avenue of the Americas started serving platters of lamb and chicken slaughtered in accordance with Islamic law, steeped in Middle Eastern spices and striped with a mysterious and mighty white sauce.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s All About the Sauce', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s All About the Sauce', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mishan, Ligaya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'