ll be housed at the University of California, Berkeley Art Museum and Pacific Film Archive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The death two years ago of the obsessive San Francisco collector and dealer Steven Leiber left a gaping hole in the scholarship of late-20th-century art books and ephemera. But his legacy will live on at the University of California, Berkeley Art Museum and Pacific Film Archive, which has acquired Mr. Leiber’s vast collection of Conceptual art and art materials, as well as his library of reference and artists’ books related to Conceptualism and the Fluxus movement.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Permanent Home for a Collection of Art Ephemera', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ephemera Collection Finds Permanent Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T16:56:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07702710-23d9-5aca-82a5-ed92d1219eff', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07702710-23d9-5aca-82a5-ed92d1219eff'}, {'abstract': 'The true story of a Spanish teacher’s (fulfilled) quest to meet a Beatle is at the heart of an Oscar foreign-language contender.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/john-lennons-spain-sojourn-becomes-a-film-without-lennon/', 'snippet': 'The true story of a Spanish teacher’s (fulfilled) quest to meet a Beatle is at the heart of an Oscar foreign-language contender.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In the fall of 1966, John Lennon took a break from the Beatles and went to southern Spain, where he acted in Richard Lester’s black comedy 