ie directed by Mitchell Leisen, is to be screened as part of the weekend series “Screwball Romance” at the IFC Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Depression-era comedy “Easy Living,” one of the nation’s richest bankers, J. B. Ball (Edward Arnold), is outraged after his wife, Jenny (Mary Nash), buys a sable coat without his knowledge. Rummaging through her closet, he picks out one of her many fur coats and throws it off his penthouse roof. It lands on Mary Smith (Jean Arthur) who is riding on a Fifth Avenue double-decker bus. That’s just the beginning of this riotous satire of inequality and insider trading. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21GUIDE5/21GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 482, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21GUIDE5/21GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 482}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21GUIDE5/21GUIDE5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 823, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21GUIDE5/21GUIDE5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1608, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21GUIDE5/21GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21GUIDE5/21GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 