aragraph': 'GREENBURGH, N.Y. — Lee Stempniak could be the third Rangers forward to contract mumps. He is being tested for the virus, which has been spreading through N.H.L. locker rooms, and he will be isolated from the team for five days.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/sports/SUB-Y-NHL/SUB-Y-NHL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/sports/SUB-Y-NHL/SUB-Y-NHL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 576}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/sports/SUB-Y-NHL/SUB-Y-NHL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 983, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/sports/SUB-Y-NHL/SUB-Y-NHL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1942, 'width': 2023, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/sports/SUB-Y-NHL/SUB-Y-NHL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/19/sports/SUB-Y-NHL/SUB-Y-NHL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/sports/SUB-Y-NHL/SUB-Y-NHL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Forward for Rangers Is Feared to Have Mumps', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Forward for Rangers Is Feared to Have Mumps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kreda, Allan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stempniak, Lee (1983- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mumps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T21:18:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kreda', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kreda', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/395272fe-fe08-5573-9c0f-ef56c23bc805', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/395272fe-fe08-5573-9c0f-ef56c23bc805'}, {'abstract': 'Over three dozen states have at least one insurer offering individual plans outside the government exchanges, but they aren’t eligible for financial help.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/your-money/looking-outside-the-government-box-for-suitable-health-coverage.html', 'snippet': 'Over three dozen states have at least one insurer offering individual plans outside the government exchanges, but they aren’t eligible for financial help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re uninsured and want individual health coverage starting on Jan. 1, you’re mostly out of time, if you want to buy on the government marketplaces. Some individual plans are still available outside the marketplaces, however, with late-December enrollment deadlines, provided you don’t want financial help with your premiums.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Outside the Government Box for Suitable Health Coverage', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T21:22:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b522900-d624-5bb9-a530-a3cef909ad32', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b522900-d624-5bb9-a530-a3cef909ad32'}, {'abstract': 'After three consecutive games of 300 passing yards and two touchdowns, experts have Matt Ryan back in Tier 2 this week against New Orleans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/sports/fantasy-football-week-16-player-tiers.html', 'snippet': 'After three consecutive games of 300 passing yards and two touchdowns, experts have Matt Ryan back in Tier 2 this week against New Orleans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this statistical model, I apply a clustering algorithm called the Gaussian mixture model to an aggregation of expert ranking data provided by Fantasypros.com. The algorithm finds natural tiers and clusters within the data. The charts that result visualize the tiers and help you decide your starting lineup each week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Football: Week 16 Player Tiers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckham, Odell Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Matt (1985- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T21:25:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Boris Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Boris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a76efbf-1670-5aa7-8215-7cf0adc353bc', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a76efbf-1670-5aa7-8215-7cf0adc353bc'}, {'abstract': 'The nation’s largest life insurer now has 30 days to decide whether to contest the Financial Stability Oversight Council’s decision in court.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/metlife-deemed-systemically-important-but-says-its-not/', 'snippet': 'The nation’s largest life insurer now has 30 days to decide whether to contest the Financial Stability Oversight Council’s decision in court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MetLife, the nation’s largest life insurer, said on Thursday that a federal panel had decided that it required the special oversight reserved for financial institutions deemed too big to fail.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/business/Sifi1/Sifi1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/business/Sifi1/Sifi1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/business/Sifi1/Sifi1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im