two siblings and Celtic folklore are at the center of an animated tale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/movies/song-of-the-sea-an-animated-fable-from-tomm-moore.html', 'snippet': 'In “Song of the Sea,” two siblings and Celtic folklore are at the center of an animated tale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After his 2010 success with “The Secret of Kells,” the Irish animator Tomm Moore once again mines Celtic folklore for “Song of the Sea,” a Pied Piper-like fable about the power of music and the magic in the everyday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SONGOFTHESEA/SONGOF-THESEA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SONGOFTHESEA/SONGOF-THESEA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SONGOFTHESEA/SONGOF-THESEA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SONGOFTHESEA/SONGOF-THESEA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1156, 'width': 1966, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SONGOFTHESEA/SONGOF-THESEA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SONGOFTHESEA/SONGOF-THESEA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/