ly supplies Illy but makes most of its money off tourism.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SMALL/19SMALL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 328, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SMALL/19SMALL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 328}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SMALL/19SMALL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SMALL/19SMALL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1120, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SMALL/19SMALL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SMALL/19SMALL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19SMALL/19SMALL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Business Inspiration, From Bean to Cup', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Small Section of the World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chilcott, Lesley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Association of Organized Women Biolley (Asomobi)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Costa Rica', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Small Section of the World (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T21:35:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicolas Rapold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicolas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rapold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f89c8a46-aaa6-5674-9332-7de4cbb94001', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f89c8a46-aaa6-5674-9332-7de4cbb94001'}, {'abstract': 'Reporter Sam Roberts explains how his story about the possibility of quieter jackhammers found its way into the paper.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/12/18/quieter-jackhammers-reporters-notebook/', 'snippet': 'Reporter Sam Roberts explains how his story about the possibility of quieter jackhammers found its way into the paper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Thursday’s paper, the reporter Sam Roberts wrote about electric jackhammers and revised noise rules that may help quiet ear-splitting noise in New York City. Here he explains how the story took shape.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quieter Jackhammers: Reporter’s Notebook', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T21:35:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dde006c-6827-5644-84bf-5435fba78634', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dde006c-6827-5644-84bf-5435fba78634'}, {'abstract': '“Home Movies,” at Postmasters Gallery, is a series of portraits of working-class people struggling in hard times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/arts/design/chris-verene-home-movies.html', 'snippet': '“Home Movies,” at Postmasters Gallery, is a series of portraits of working-class people struggling in hard times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chris Verene has been photographing members of his extended family and circle of friends in his hometown, Galesburg, Ill., regularly for the past 30 years. Along with eight photographs made since 2006, this show presents something new and different: a 30-minute video called “Home Movies.” Made with low-budget cameras, it’s a riveting, sad and sometimes comical series of short, documentary portraits of poor, white working-class people getting by in a time of pervasive economic hardship.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19VERNE-GALLERY6/VERNE-GALLERY6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19VERNE-GALLERY6/VERNE-GALLERY6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 608}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19VERNE-GALLERY6/VERNE-GALLERY6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1010, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19VERNE-GALLERY6/VERNE-GALLERY6-superJumbo.jp