two-day offensive, which involved 8,000 Kurdish fighters, was the largest one to date in the war against the Islamic State.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/world/middleeast/backed-by-us-airstrikes-kurds-regain-ground-from-isis.html', 'snippet': 'The two-day offensive, which involved 8,000 Kurdish fighters, was the largest one to date in the war against the Islamic State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Kurdish forces, backed by a surge of American airstrikes in recent days, recaptured a large swath of territory from Islamic State militants on Thursday, opening a path from the autonomous Kurdish region to Mount Sinjar in the west, near the Syrian border.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backed by U.S. Airstrikes, Kurds Reverse an ISIS Gain ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Backed by U.S. Airstrikes, Kurds Reverse an ISIS Gain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arango, Tim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pesh Merga', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T21:44:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69d80de9-0f9a-543c-81c2-19d65c22959d', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69d80de9-0f9a-543c-81c2-19d65c22959d'}, {'abstract': 'Takeshi Murata’s video “OM Rider,” at Salon 94 Bowery, represents the struggle between the avant-garde and the establishment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/arts/design/takeshi-murata-om-rider.html', 'snippet': 'Takeshi Murata’s video “OM Rider,” at Salon 94 Bowery, represents the struggle between the avant-garde and the establishment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Takeshi Murata’s funny and weird digitally animated video “OM Rider” is projected onto one wall of the dark gallery, which is empty, except for bleacher seating. The 11 ½-minute movie involves two cartoon characters who are archetypal opposites: a restless, punk werewolf in a black T-shirt and cutoff shorts, and a grumpy old man who is bald, but for wispy white hair hanging down below his ears. Nattily dressed in a yellow sport coat, plaid pants and brown-and-white wingtip shoes, he’s a personification of country club conservatism.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19MURATAGALLERY1/MURATA-GALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19MURATAGALLERY1/MURATA-GALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19MURATAGALLERY1/MURATA-GALLERY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19MURATAGALLERY1/MURATA-GALLERY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1279, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'capt