 'nyt://article/9b0e1d1e-6f08-5c4a-b703-ba084792365b'}, {'abstract': 'Urs Fischer has fun with paint on a large scale at Gavin Brown’s Enterprise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/arts/design/urs-fischer.html', 'snippet': 'Urs Fischer has fun with paint on a large scale at Gavin Brown’s Enterprise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Urs Fischer’s latest, seemingly gestural abstract paintings seduce and abandon. Collusions of hand and machine, they begin as luscious paint studies that are fed into a computer and greatly enlarged. They are then printed on aluminum panels as much as 11 feet across with almost unimaginable accuracy, thanks to a labor-intensive process involving multiple silk-screens.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Urs Fischer', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Urs Fischer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fischer, Urs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T22:10:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/93bf1f43-5885-51f8-8b06-889da49e2551', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93bf1f43-5885-51f8-8b06-889da49e2551'}, {'abstract': 'Motherwell took flight when he worked with paper, creating drawings and collages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/arts/design/robert-motherwell-works-on-paper-1951-1991.html', 'snippet': 'Motherwell took flight when he worked with paper, creating drawings and collages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York School artist Robert Motherwell could be ponderous in oil on canvas. But on paper, he was lighter and looser, to judge from the Kasmin Gallery’s career-spanning mini-survey of Mr. Motherwell’s drawings and collages (organized with the artist’s Dedalus Foundation). Working with ink, charcoal, acrylic and assorted labels and wrapping papers, Mr. Motherwell offset strong colors and muscular gestures with the suggestion of chance and accident.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19MOTHERWELLGALLERY2/MOTHERWELL-GALLERY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19MOTHERWELLGALLERY2/MOTHERWELL-GALLERY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 734}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19MOTHERWELLGALLERY2/MOTHERWELL-GALLERY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19MOTHERWELLGALLERY2/MOTHERWELL-GALLERY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1393, 'width': 1139, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19MOTHERWELLGALLERY2/MOTHERWELL-GALLERY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19MOTHERWELLGALLERY2/MOTHERWELL-GALLERY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19MOTHERWELLGALLERY2/MOTHERWELL-GALLERY2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Motherwell: ‘Works on Paper, 1951-1991’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robert Motherwell: ‘Works on Paper, 1951-1991’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Karen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Motherwell, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-18T22:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/78083621-32e3-5eff-99f7-04e3343cfa56', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78083621-32e3-5eff-99f7-04e3343cfa56'}, {'abstract': 'Times critics share what they’ve been listening to lately.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/classical-playlist-beethoven-brahms-and-more/', 'snippet': 'Times critics share what they’ve been listening to lately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEETHOVEN: Piano Concerto No. 5; Piano Sonata No. 32Nelson Freire, pianist; Gewandhausorchester; Riccardo Chailly, conductor(Decca, 478 6771)After recording Brahms’s piano concertos with the rejuvenated Gewandhausorchester, Nelson Freire and Riccardo Chailly embark on a Beethoven cycle with this “Emperor.” Two different styles clash here, but work themselves out. Mr. Freire is almost self-effacing at times, extreme at others: Mr. Chailly and his orchestra are lean and full of bite. The Opus 111 sonata is Mr. Freire at his best, too, in playing full of danger and, ultimately, repose. (David Allen) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/artsbeat-classical/artsbeat-classical-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/artsbeat-classical/artsbeat-classical-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/artsbeat-classical/artsbeat-classical-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/artsbeat-classical/artsbeat-classical-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/artsbeat-classical/artsbeat-classical-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/artsbeat-classical/artsbeat-classical-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/artsbeat-classical/artsbeat-classical-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Classical Playlist: Beethoven, Brahms and More', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chailly, Riccard