cations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T00:53:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/dac626bd-7067-5909-8079-4cb692b6badd', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dac626bd-7067-5909-8079-4cb692b6badd'}, {'abstract': 'Tunisian fighters with the Islamic State group have claimed responsibility in a video for the assassinations of two left-wing politicians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/world/africa/tunisia-isis-fighters-claim-2-killings.html', 'snippet': 'Tunisian fighters with the Islamic State group have claimed responsibility in a video for the assassinations of two left-wing politicians.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Tunisian fighters with the Islamic State have claimed responsibility in a video for the assassinations of the left-wing politicians Chokri Belaid and Mohamed Brahmi last year and have threatened to carry out more assassinations before Tunisia’s presidential runoff on Sunday. Three Tunisians, dressed in black and armed with rifles, speak in the video, exhorting Tunisians to rise up and expand the Islamic State, also known as ISIS or ISIL, across North Africa from Libya to Algeria. The video was released Wednesday on social media. The Interior Ministry on Thursday confirmed that one of the men was Boubakr Hakim, the chief suspect in the two murders. Mr. Hakim says in the video, according to the SITE Monitoring Service, that Tunisians “will not live secured as long as Tunisia is not governed by Islam.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunisia: ISIS Fighters Claim 2 Killings', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tunisia: ISIS Fighters Claim 2 Killings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gall, Carlotta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T00:53:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlotta Gall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlotta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/be71e455-ee8a-5a5d-9153-0b43443aeb32', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be71e455-ee8a-5a5d-9153-0b43443aeb32'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Stephan J. Levitan, a psychoanalyst, writes that “some patients are unable to tolerate its intensity.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/opinion/trauma-in-psychoanalysis.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Stephan J. Levitan, a psychoanalyst, writes that “some patients are unable to tolerate its intensity.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trauma in Psychoanalysis', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trauma in Psychoanalysis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T00:54:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opin