pe': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'DVD', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. Hoberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/adcd6f86-8301-5aa3-be15-95d756fedff1', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adcd6f86-8301-5aa3-be15-95d756fedff1'}, {'abstract': 'Margaret Keane and Amy Adams, who plays her in Tim Burton’s “Big Eyes,” talk about Ms. Keane’s fight for recognition as the artist behind well-known paintings of waifs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/movies/the-artist-margaret-keane-vindicated-in-tim-burtons-film.html', 'snippet': 'Margaret Keane and Amy Adams, who plays her in Tim Burton’s “Big Eyes,” talk about Ms. Keane’s fight for recognition as the artist behind well-known paintings of waifs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — In 1964, Margaret Keane was among the most famous living artists in the country, only no one knew it. Ms. Keane was the painter behind the big-eyed waifs that were gracing rec rooms and lounges all across America, the mother of a legion of adorable, forsaken children. Her canvases were all signed simply “Keane,” and that allowed her husband, Walter Keane, a charlatan and salesman par excellence, to take credit for the work.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21KEANE1/21KEANE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21KEANE1/21KEANE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21KEANE1/21KEANE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21KEANE1/21KEANE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21KEANE1/21KEANE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21KEANE1/21KEANE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21KEANE1/21KEANE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Avenging the Big Lie Behind the Big Eyes ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Avenging the Big Lie Behind the Big Eyes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, Amy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burton, Tim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keane, Margaret', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Big Eyes (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T01:11:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5299d991-85c6-54c0-b9b6-0cbe2b5335ce', 'word_count': 1439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5299d991-85c6-54c0-b9b6-0cbe2b5335ce'}, {'abstract': 'Kailash Satyarthi, who shared the Nobel Peace Prize with Malala Yousafzai this year, turned his life’s setbacks into a mission.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/18/where-does-moral-courage-come-from/', 'snippet': 'Kailash Satyarthi, who shared the Nobel Peace Prize with Malala Yousafzai this year, turned his life’s setbacks into a mission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers of Fixes know that our primary mission each week is to highlight strategies that work to effect social change and improve lives. In her column last week, Tina Rosenberg zeroed in on some of the strategies that successful efforts have in common. They are crucial, but there is also something fundamental that underlies all these efforts: the human ability to imagine that wrongs can be righted, and the belief that change can happen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {