 “How to Murder Your Wife” in 1965, had an award-winning revival in the 1990s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Virna Lisi, who first captivated Italian moviegoers with her smoldering eyes, sulky smile and stunning beauty before sweeping into Hollywood in the 1960s to star opposite such leading men as Frank Sinatra and Tony Curtis, died on Wednesday. She was 78.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/LISI-1-obit/LISI-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 775, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/LISI-1-obit/LISI-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 775}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/LISI-1-obit/LISI-1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 794, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/LISI-1-obit/LISI-1-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1587, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/LISI-1-obit/LISI-1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/LISI-1-obit/LISI-1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/LISI-1-obit/LISI-1-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Virna Lisi, Italian Actress Lured to 