brating 100 years with 17 exhibitions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/arts/design/a-centennial-for-asian-art-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'The Met’s department of Asian art, once tiny, is celebrating 100 years with 17 exhibitions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maxwell K. Hearn remembers when he first arrived at the Metropolitan Museum of Art in 1971. “There were only two spaces for Asian art: the Great Hall Balcony, which housed Chinese ceramics, and an adjacent gallery of Chinese Buddhist art,” he recalled. “Douglas Dillon, then chairman, and Thomas Hoving, the director, surveyed the museum and realized that Asian art was the weakest department. They also recognized that it was too important an area to neglect.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19VOGEL1/VOGEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19VOGEL1/VOGEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19VOGEL1/VOGEL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19VOGEL1/VOGEL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1053, 'width': 1544, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19VOGEL1/VOGEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/19/arts/19VOGEL1/VOGEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnai