ish and exorbitant buildings across China, government officials, planners and architects have been scrambling to figure out what it means for them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the newest dreamscape in a country clotted with them. When it opens in two years on Beijing’s east side, Chaoyang Park Plaza, a ring of glass towers molded like mountains in a classic Chinese landscape painting and designed by the renowned architect Ma Yansong, will feature apartments, offices and shops.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under Xi, China’s Wave of ‘Weird Architecture’ May Have Peaked', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'u2018Weirdu2019 Buildings in China Are Now Under Watch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hadid, Zaha', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koolhaas, Rem', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T09:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cao Li', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Li', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/726fd7bb-7f89-5ede-a6fe-071d47ce2079', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/726fd7bb-7f89-5ede-a6fe-071d47ce2079'}, {'abstract': 'Fosun International raised its bid for the resort operator just hours before the expiration of a Friday deadline set by the French market regulator.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/chinese-investors-raise-their-bid-for-club-med/', 'snipp