, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/16/multimedia/creme-brulee-toast/creme-brulee-toast-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crème Brûlée French Toast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T16:10:24+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'Jenny Woodward', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woodward', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/305c54c5-47aa-5252-a05f-55d9a736d736', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/305c54c5-47aa-5252-a05f-55d9a736d736'}, {'abstract': 'Welcome to Motherlode’s weekly open thread. Do you have thoughts about the news this week, and how it affects families? A question to ask? A rant to share? This is your place. Go.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/your-turn-a-weekend-thread-open-for-comments-39/', 'snippet': 'Welcome to Motherlode’s weekly open thread. Do you have thoughts about the news this week, and how it affects families? A question to ask? A rant to share? This is your place. Go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to Motherlode’s weekly open thread. Do you have thoughts about the news this week, and how it affects families? A question to ask? A rant to share? This is your place. Go.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Turn: A Weekend Thread, Open for Comments', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T16:11:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c7a327a-d2c4-53f3-87b9-2cb576cbfac6', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c7a327a-d2c4-53f3-87b9-2cb576cbfac6'}, {'abstract': 'Let’s be franc about monetary policy.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/switzerland-and-the-inflation-hawks/', 'snippet': 'Let’s be franc about monetary policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I tend to go on a lot about the persistence of inflation paranoia, but it is an amazing thing. A lot of people have been predicting soaring inflation since 2009 if not earlier, and have refused to change their views even though actual events have been nothing like what they predicted — and almost exactly what liquidity-trap theorists predicted, in advance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Switzerland and the Inflation Hawks', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T16:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8bbd523-6f40-5a2e-ae41-37e82cecfd89', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8bbd523-6f40-5a2e-ae41-37e82cecfd89'}, {'abstract': 'The technique differs from other French toast recipes, with their quick dip into eggy milk. This one calls for patience. (Article plus video.)', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/dining/french-toast-recipe-with-a-creme-brulee-twist.html', 'snippet': 'The technique differs from other French toast recipes, with their quick dip into eggy milk. This one calls for patience. (Article plus video.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have to admit that when a friend offered me her recipe for the French toast she learned during her Girl Scout days, I didn’t exactly rush to accept. An unfortunate experience with a campfire stew involving canned vegetables and cream-of-something soup is still etched in my mind. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Girl Scout French Toast: As Good as the Cookies', 'kicker': 'A Good Appetite', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Girl Scout French Toast: As Good as the Cookies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bread', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Girl Scouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T16:15:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c9bff24-4bc8-5a15-aa26-7d2a593d42ec', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c9bff24-4bc8-5a15-aa26-7d2a593d42ec'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama said the reopening of relations with Cuba would give the United States more sway there, and promised to “respond proportionally” to a cyberattack on Sony.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/20/us/politics/obama-cuba-north-korea-news-conference.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama said the reopening of relations with Cuba would give the United States more sway there, and promised to “respond proportionally” to a cyberattack on Sony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama on Friday rejected criticism that he should not have reopened American relations with Cuba because of the nation’s human rights record, saying the historic thaw would give the United States more sway over the Cuban government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/us/19prexy-4/19prexy-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/19/us/19prexy-4/19prexy-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/us/19prexy-4/19prexy-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/us/19prexy-4/19prexy-4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/us/19prexy-4/19prexy-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/19/us/19prexy-4/19prexy-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/19/us/19prexy-4/19prexy-4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Defends Actions on Cuba and Promises So