ganization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96c626b7-a3d1-5243-ad17-19fa18cd9bd1', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96c626b7-a3d1-5243-ad17-19fa18cd9bd1'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DREADFUL: The Short Life and Gay Times of John Horne Burns,  by David Margolick. (Other Press, $17.95.) Burns, the closeted son of a wealthy New England family, rose to fame in 1947 with “The Gallery,” a World War II novel notable for its frank portrayal of gay soldiers in occupied Naples. But he squandered his early promise, succumbed to drink and depression, and was dead six years later at 36. Margolick reconstructs Burns’s largely forgotten story, evoking the glamorous but often dark underbelly of America’s postwar literary scene.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T16:53:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ihsan Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ihsan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3bb0567-38cd-5d16-916c-536f8599a009', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3bb0567-38cd-5d16-916c-536f8599a009'}, {'abstract': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/books/review/editors-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FAMILY FURNISHINGS: Selected Stories, 1995-2014,  by Alice Munro. (Knopf, $30.) Many of the Nobel Prize-winning author’s later stories seem driven by a pure curiosity about other people’s journeys through life.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Editors’ Choice | Recent Books of Particular Interest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T16:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7b41a41-fd15-515f-a28f-32c02d4acc7b', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7b41a41-fd15-515f-a28f-32c02d4acc7b'}, {'abstract': 'Recalling the days when radio and TV reception were so imperfect, and so much better.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/arts/television/recalling-the-imperfect-radio-and-tv-reception-of-the-past.html', 'snippet': 'Recalling the days when radio and TV reception were so imperfect, and so much better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I miss the television snows of yesteryear. And I don’t mean easy nostalgia for the inevitable reruns of “It’s a Wonderful Life” or “A Charlie Brown Christmas.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21STATIC/21STATIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/21/arts/21STATIC/21STATIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewi