/books/review/raphal-jerusalmys-brotherhood-of-book-hunters.html', 'snippet': 'François Villon travels to Jerusalem in this literary mystery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter how often academics kill the author, dedicated readers will resurrect him. The sense that artworks hide meanings only their creators could know nags so continuously at the imagination that a sizable subgenre of literary mystery has grown to satisfy it. If some artists’ lives encouraged this (there are at least three contradictory reports of Caravaggio’s death), others have it thrust upon them: Nothing about Noël Coward justifies his appearance as a detective in “The Noël Coward Murder Mysteries,” for example, any more than Abraham Lincoln ever killed a vampire, so far as we know — but fame has unpredictable penalties.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/books/review/sub-21KOELB/sub-21KOELB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/21/books/review/sub-21KOELB/sub-21KOELB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 807}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/books/review/sub-21KOELB/sub-21KOELB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 762, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/books/review/sub-21KOELB/sub-21KOELB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1427, 'width': 1061, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/books/review/sub-21KOELB/sub-21KOELB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbn