_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a0e91ab-eb38-5ebd-bfd6-734c0e3c7175', 'word_count': 6318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a0e91ab-eb38-5ebd-bfd6-734c0e3c7175'}, {'abstract': 'Given the number of injuries the team has endured, and the drama regarding Coach Jim Harbaugh’s future and Ray McDonald’s legal troubles, it is a testament to the depth of the 49ers’ roster that they still have a shot at a winning season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/20/sports/football/san-diego-chargers-at-san-francisco-49ers-preview.html', 'snippet': 'Given the number of injuries the team has endured, and the drama regarding Coach Jim Harbaugh’s future and Ray McDonald’s legal troubles, it is a testament to the depth of the 49ers’ roster that they still have a shot at a winning season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chargers (8-6) at 49ers (7-7)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'San Diego Chargers at San Francisco 49ers Prediction', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Diego Chargers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T18:52:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/345cf330-2de0-5f6a-b3d5-41c40851fe39', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/345cf330-2de0-5f6a-b3d5-41c40851fe39'}, {'abstract': 'He said 13 St. Louis County municipalities were ignoring a state that sets limits on the revenue derived from traffic fines.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/missouri-a-g-sues-over-issue-at-heart-of-ferguson-riots/', 'snippet': 'He said 13 St. Louis County municipalities were ignoring a state that sets limits on the revenue derived from traffic fines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The upheaval in Ferguson, Mo. following Michael Brown’s death \xa0was partly about the death itself, and partly about economic exploitation at the hands of the law. The discontent that eventually exploded into riots was fueled for years by the sense that municipalities in St. Louis County were systematically looting black peoples’ assets by targeting them for street and traffic stops fines that flow into public coffers. In one county community, for example, public interest lawyers found that 100 percent of all the searches and arrests that originated from traffic stops in 2013 were of African Americans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missouri A.G. Sues Over Issue at Heart of Ferguson Riots', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic and Parking Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T18:53:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'titl