des-details-of-conversation-with-castro/', 'snippet': 'The president said that it was too early to discuss a visit to the United States by Mr. Castro, and said he had no target date to visit Cuba.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama recounted that in his phone call with President Raúl Castro last week he opened with a lengthy preamble and then apologized to Mr. Castro for going on too long. “Don’t worry, Mr. President,” the Cuban leader replied. “You’re still a young man. You still have a chance to break Fidel’s record. He once spoke for seven hours.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Provides Details of Conversation With Castro', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T19:31:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8b925a9-46f0-56f3-a560-1363d73a962f', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8b925a9-46f0-56f3-a560-1363d73a962f'}, {'abstract': 'The price plunge is forcing oil producers everywhere to recalibrate. But the high costs of Britain’s industry make it particularly vulnerable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/20/business/international/sinking-oil-price-is-hard-on-north-sea-producers.html', 'snippet': 'The price plunge is forcing oil producers everywhere to recalibrate. But the high costs of Britain’s industry make it particularly vulnerable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Back in September, when oil was still selling for close to $100 a barrel, North Sea energy reserves were the big prize at stake in Scotland’s referendum on whether to secede from