9b36f', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6ba6e01-5551-5216-bf4e-979ec1e9b36f'}, {'abstract': 'Insurers are hoping that a new competitor to Gilead Sciences’ drugs for the disease will drive down prices, though the new drug’s price is higher than was hoped.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/20/business/abbvie-wins-approval-of-hepatitis-c-treatment.html', 'snippet': 'Insurers are hoping that a new competitor to Gilead Sciences’ drugs for the disease will drive down prices, though the new drug’s price is higher than was hoped.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new treatment for hepatitis C developed by AbbVie won approval from the Food and Drug Administration on Friday, setting the stage for a marketing battle with Gilead Sciences, whose two new drugs for the disease have drawn an outcry about the high cost of medicines.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hepatitis C Treatment Wins Approval, but Price Relief May Be Limited', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hepatitis C Treatment Wins Approval, but Price Relief May Be Limited', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollack, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AbbVie Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gilead Sciences Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hepatitis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Harvoni (Drug)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sovaldi (Drug)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T22:02:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbc82cf5-b737-5768-aaab-f09d4768b13e', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbc82cf5-b737-5768-aaab-f09d4768b13e'}, {'abstract': 'The spate of entertainments this year, in a never-ending loop of galas and parties, brought with them a problem: How to traverse it all?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/fashion/the-year-of-the-never-ending-party.html', 'snippet': 'The spate of entertainments this year, in a never-ending loop of galas and parties, brought with them a problem: How to traverse it all?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The dress was a pale confection, designed by Dolce & Gabbana as if by way of Sylvia Weinstock. Garlanded with cloth flowers, it had a train so long it called not just for an attendant but possibly its own ZIP code. It was worn to this year’s Met Gala by Tabitha Simmons, a comely British shoe designer enlisted that spring evening to provide an engineering solution: a gown-propulsion device.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Year of the Never-Ending Party', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Year of the Never-Ending Party', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T22:02:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/144da918-1f72-5414-a041-cccf24ab9675', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/144da918-1f72-5414-a041-cccf24ab9675'}, {'abstract': 'The president is acting like a man who’s been given the political equivalent of a testosterone boost.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/20/opinion/obama-unbound.html', 'snippet': 'The president is acting like a man who’s been given the political equivalent of a testosterone boost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There may not be a lightness to his step, a lilt in his voice or a bit of jauntiness returned to his manner. The office ages everyone prematurely, and makes spontaneity all but impossible. But President Obama is acting like a man who’s been given the political equivalent of a testosterone boost. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/