 Pharrell Williams; the death of Oscar de la Renta; the popularity of wearable tech and men’s wear; and the role of designers in cultural institutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a funny, mixed-up year in fashion.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/fashion/21COVER/21COVER-articleLarge-v7.png', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/21/fashion/21COVER/21COVER-articleLarge-v7.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/fashion/21COVER/21COVER-jumbo-v7.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/fashion/21COVER/21COVER-superJumbo-v7.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/fashion/21COVER/21COVER-thumbStandard-v8.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/21/fashion/21COVER/21COVER-thumbStandard-v8.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/fashion/21COVER/21COVER-thumbLarge-v8.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '5 Highs (and Lows) From the Year in Fashion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Year in Fashion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alamuddin, Amal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de la Renta, Oscar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dior, Christian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Nyong'o, Lupita", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawrence, Jennifer', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T22:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27752966-8393-5f1c-98fd-cdecbbaf7282', 'word_count': 1994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27752966-8393-5f1c-98fd-cdecbbaf7282'}, {'abstract': 'The new Hugh Jackman play on Broadway, “The River,” has recouped its $3.2 million capitalization.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/20/theater/a-river-of-money-thanks-to-jackman.html', 'snippet': 'The new Hugh Jackman play on Broadway, “The River,” has recouped its $3.2 million capitalization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new Hugh Jackman play on Broadway, “The River,” has recouped its $3.2 million capitalization in just seven weeks, the show’s producers said on Friday. It is a remarkably fast achievement, aided by the show’s unusual ticketing policy. While “The River” is offering dozens of seats at the relatively low prices of $35 and $95 at every performance, the producers are reaping profits by selling many more tickets for more than $275. The show’s average ticket price last week was $154.37, one of the highest on Broadway. While the reviews were mixed for “The River,” a dark tale of a man who brings his girlfriend to a fishing cabin, the box-office power of Mr. Jackman (above) — a Tony winner as well as a movie action hero — is potent enough to reliably sell out performances. Written by Jez Butterworth (“Jerusalem”) and directed by Ian Rickson, “The River” is at the Circle in the Square Theater until Feb. 8.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A River of Money Thanks to Jackman', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A River of Money Thanks to Jackman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackman, Hugh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Butterworth, Jez', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The River (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-19T22:59:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/59956eef-93b8-5d95-bd87-b7f88ff4e201', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59956eef-93b8-5d95-bd87-b7f88ff4e201'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama said Sony should not have backed down. So why doesn’t he host a viewing?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/19/the-white-house-should-screen-the-interview/', 'snippet': 'President Obama said Sony should not have backed down. So why doesn’t he host a viewing?', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama was unusually blunt today when he was asked at his year-end news conference about Sony’s decision to kill the release of “The Interview,” the Seth Rogen/James Franco buddy movie about an attempt on the life of the North Korean dictator, Kim Jong-un.', 'source': 'The New York Times'