led by Gov. Andrew Cuomo of New York, officials in his administration announced that they had decided not to allow hydraulic fracturing, or fracking, anywhere in the state. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cuomo Cop-Out', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cuomo Cop-Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martens, Joseph', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zucker, Howard A', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-20T02:29:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/562c3196-0095-592d-8a03-8dbb6a56639a', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/562c3196-0095-592d-8a03-8dbb6a56639a'}, {'abstract': 'The Centers for Disease Control is advising consumers not to eat commercially produced packaged caramel apples after tying the treats to five deaths and 21 hospitalizations in 10 states.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/20/us/health-warning-given-against-caramel-apples.html', 'snippet': 'The Centers for Disease Control is advising consumers not to eat commercially produced packaged caramel apples after tying the treats to five deaths and 21 hospitalizations in 10 states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention is advising consumers not to eat commercially produced packaged caramel apples after tying the treats to five deaths and 21 hospitalizations in 10 states. The agency said it believes 28 people have been infected with listeriosis after eating the apples. It is working to identify the producer of the apples but in the meantime cautioned consumers not to eat any packaged caramel apples, including those coated in nuts and other toppings. Four people in Minnesota who were infected bought apples at Cub Foods, Kwik Trip and Mike’s Discount Foods, which sold Carnival brand and Kitchen Cravings brand apples. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Warning Given Agains