n Act reform.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/opinion/sunday/freedom-to-see-government-records.html', 'snippet': 'Congress needs to act on Freedom of Information Act reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the disappointments of the lame-duck congressional session was Speaker John Boehner’s refusal to schedule a House vote on a broadly supported Senate bill to strengthen the Freedom of Information Act, the federal law that allows journalists and the public to access federal government records. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Freedom to See Government Records', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Freedom to See Government Records', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Information Act', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-20T19:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f247480c-7ead-5e7c-b677-4901228b0f1c', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f247480c-7ead-5e7c-b677-4901228b0f1c'}, {'abstract': 'Who knew animals could be so helpful in psychotherapy?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/20/the-pets-in-my-practice/', 'snippet': 'Who knew animals could be so helpful in psychotherapy?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been a clinical psychologist for over 30 years. Trained in the psychoanalytic method, I spent most of my career in an office seated behind clients who lay on a couch. Then, three years ago, after several followers of my blog asked if I would be willing to work with them by Skype, I started practicing face-to-face video psychotherapy with clients all over the world. Usually I “meet” them in their homes.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pets in My Practice', 'kicker': 'Couch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Therapy, With Pets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-20T19:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Burgo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burgo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f91ceb07-bbac-5c6c-a983-55071b5587b4', 'word_count': 1075, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f91ceb07-bbac-5c6c-a983-55071b5587b4'}, {'abstract': 'The astronomer on Franklin, Hitchcock and anagrams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/opinion/sunday/pierre-cox.html', 'snippet': 'The astronomer on Franklin, Hitchcock and anagrams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pierre Cox is a French astronomer and director of ALMA, the Atacama Large Millimeter/submillimeter Array, a collection of radio antennas high on a Chilean plateau that gather photons from distant corners of the universe to help an international consortium of scientists fathom how stars formed and life itself began.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/sunday-review/21DOWNLOAD/21DOWNLOAD-arti