 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7837d2ca-0a5e-5a45-a8ce-ca991db2876f', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7837d2ca-0a5e-5a45-a8ce-ca991db2876f'}, {'abstract': 'An inquiry into “a certain secular mentality” and “a certain feminist spirit” seems incongruous in the era of Pope Francis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/opinion/sunday/romes-scrutiny-of-american-nuns.html', 'snippet': 'An inquiry into “a certain secular mentality” and “a certain feminist spirit” seems incongruous in the era of Pope Francis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six years ago, in the midst of the scandal over child abuse by rogue Catholic priests, the Vatican shocked many of the laity by ordering a sweeping investigation into the behavior and fidelity of the 50,000 American nuns who quietly labor in hospitals, prisons and outposts of the nation’s impoverished. The inquiry, ordered by the church under Pope Benedict XVI, seemed a deliberate distraction from the abuse scandal, and was tinged with male chauvinism.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rome’s Scrutiny of American Nuns', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rome’s Scrutiny of American Nuns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuns', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-20T19:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ab71e18-ca10-5c70-988f-fbe386b69c19', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ab71e18-ca10-5c70-988f-fbe386b69c19'}, {'abstract': 'Ebola can be battled back, but conditions in Sierra Leone make it very, very hard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/sunday-review/ebola-should-be-easy-to-treat.html', 'snippet': 'Ebola can be battled back, but conditions in Sierra Leone make it very, very hard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FREETOWN, Sierra Leone — NOT even 30 minutes away from the little house where I watched a girl die from Ebola sat the clinic she had been so desperate to reach. It was a modest compound, of simple rooms lined with iron cots. I didn’t see any blinking computer screens or machines that beeped. It looked more like a high school nurse’s office than an I.C.U.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/sunday-review/21EBOLA/21EBOLA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/21/sunday-review/21EBOLA/21EBOLA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/sunday-review/21EBOLA/21EBOLA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/sunday-review/21EBOLA/21EBOLA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1202, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/21/sunday-review/21EBOLA/21EBOLA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height'