_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eccce417-6d62-5476-a421-0fc19432ce52'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: After intense German shelling near Arras in 1914, the French fight back.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/1914-france-silences-enemy-guns-near-arras/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: After intense German shelling near Arras in 1914, the French fight back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Arras is once more the centre of severe fighting, and that fine city of the north of France, so many of whose artistic or historic monuments are already in ruins, has received further punishment from the pitiless German shells. Having already destroyed the belfry of the famous church, the Germans are now probably bent on leaving not one stone of it upon another. But although the army of “Kultur” may destroy the beauties of helpless French cities, it is having no success when opposing itself to the French troops. In front of Arras the French artillery threw such a rain of shells into the enemy’s lines that no fewer than thirty-six cannon were silenced. Immediately after the infantry advanced, and after a hand-to-hand fight gained several trenches. The cavalry also took a distinguished part, the cuirassiers nailing the German artillerymen at their guns. Not satisfied with working further havoc in Arras, the Germans have also had recourse to another one of their favorite diversions, and have bombarded the hospital in Ypres. Such tactics on the part of the Germans generally indicate that they can make no headway in legitimate fighting. This view is, in fact, frankly expressed by a war correspondent of the “Berliner Tageblatt.” — The New York Herald, European Edition, Dec. 22, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/blogs/22iht-olddec22-ypres/22iht-olddec22-ypres-jumbo.png', 'height': 287, 'width': 487, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/blogs/22iht-olddec22-ypres/22iht-olddec22-ypres-superJumbo.png', 'height': 287, 'width': 487, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/blogs/22iht-olddec22-ypres/22iht-olddec22-ypres-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/22/blogs/22iht-olddec22-ypres/22iht-olddec22-ypres-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/blogs/22iht-olddec22-ypres/22iht-olddec22-ypres-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1914: France Silences Enemy Guns Near Arras', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-21T11:54:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8118e7aa-810a-5cdd-917e-a33a8fa9663d', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8118e7aa-810a-5cdd-917e-a33a8fa9663d'}, {'abstract': 'In an effort to move fast, phone apps like Uber, Lyft and Flywheel may be placing a premium on speed and in the process sacrificing safety.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/distracted-driving-and-the-risks-of-ride-hailing-services-like-uber/', 'snippet': 'In an effort to move fast, phone apps like Uber, Lyft and Flywheel may be placing a premium on speed and in the process sacrificing safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It Can Wait. The buzz phrase, popularized by AT&T in a public service campaign, urges drivers to show restraint with their phones.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/technology/17bits-distracted/17bits-distracted-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/17/technology/17bits-distracted/17bits-distracted-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/technology/17bits-distracted/17bits-distracted-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/technology/17bits-distracted/17bits-distracted-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1475, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/17/technology/17bits-distracted/17bits-distracted-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/17/technology/17bits-distracted/17bits-distracted-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thu