le Earth entries, “The Hobbit: The Battle of the Five Armies” garners $90.6 million in ticket sales to lead box office take', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Hobbit: The Battle of the Five Armies” collected $90.6 million in ticket sales during its first five days in North American theaters, slightly better than the five-day total for last year’s “Hobbit” installment.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Hobbit’ Movie Wins Box Office Skirmish', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Hobbit’ Movie Wins Box Office Skirmish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rentrak Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-21T17:34:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2100f274-4230-5da2-b444-223bf5b07648', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2100f274-4230-5da2-b444-223bf5b07648'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: After failed ninth and 10th rounds of voting, the presidential election became the longest in the 18-year history of the Italian Republic in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/21/1964-tempers-flare-as-italian-parliament-fails-to-elect-new-president/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: After failed ninth and 10th rounds of voting, the presidential election became the longest in the 18-year history of the Italian Republic in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Communists and neo-Fascists nearly came to blows in the Italian parliament today as its two houses failed again — in the ninth and tenth ballots — to elect a new president of the republic. Today’s two votes made the current presidential election the longest in the 18-year-old history of the Italian Republic. The previous record was the nine ballots it took in 1962 to elect Antonio Segni president. Mr. Segni resigned earlier this month after it became clear that he would not be able to perform the functions of the office as a result of a stroke he suffered in August. The voting today was also marked by the appearance, for the first time on the ballot, of Deputy Premier Pietro Nenni’s name. Mr. Nenni, long an outsider in government affairs, is leader of the left-wing Socialists. He joined the government of Premier Aldo Moro last year in its “opening to the left.” Former Premier Giovanni Leone, the official Christian Democrat candidate, polled 299 votes tonight — six less than in the ninth ballot this morning. A total of 482 votes are needed for election. The Social Democrats and Republicans, as well as the neo-Fascist Italian Social Movement, abstained in tonight’s vote. Legislators nearly came to blows in the morning session when Communists and Fascists jeered and shouted at each other. It was the first such outbreak since balloting began Dec. 16. Parliament meets again tomorrow morning for the 11th ballot. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Dec. 22, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/blogs/22iht-olddec22-Italy/22iht-olddec22-Italy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/22/blogs/22iht-olddec22-Italy/22iht-olddec22-Italy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 649}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/blogs/22iht-olddec22-Italy/22iht-olddec22-Italy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 947, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/blogs/22iht-olddec22-Italy/22iht-olddec22-Italy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1400, 'width': 1294, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/blogs/22iht-olddec22-Italy/22iht-olddec22-Italy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/22/blogs/22iht-olddec22-Italy/22iht-olddec22-Italy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/blogs/22iht-olddec22-Italy/22iht-olddec22-Italy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Tempers Flare as Italian Parliament Fails to Elect New President', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-21T17:45:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd38b3c6-ba34-57d0-8b4f-997524706250', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd38b3c6-ba34-57d0-8b4f-997524706250'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama said he would “review” whether to return North Korea to the list, part of a broader government response to a damaging cyberattack on Sony’s Hollywood studio.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/22/us/politics/obama-cuba-north-korea-cyberattack.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama said he would “review” whether to return North Korea to the list, part of a broader government response to a damaging cyberattack on Sony’s Hollywood studio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONOLULU — As the United States moves closer to taking Cuba off the list of state sponsors of terrorism, President Obama said he would “review” whether to return North Korea to the list, part of a broader government response to a damaging cyberattack on Sony’s Hollywood studio.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama to See if North Korea Should Return to Terror List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama to See if North Korea Should Return to Terror List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Pictures Entertainment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Interview (Movie)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-21T18:07:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c378a1a7-4b06-5426-8717-9a14792c220d', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c378a1a7-4b06-5426-8717-9a14792c220d'}, {'abstract': 'The volunteer group, which transports patients and trains medical technicians, is eligible for a $125,000 grant, but it must raise that much before it can receive the money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/22/nyregion/in-brooklyn-an-ambulance-corps-seeks-its-own-emergency-aid.html', 'snippet': 'The volunteer group, which transports patients and trains medical technicians, is eligible for a $125,000 grant, but it must raise that much before it can receive the money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The phone never stops ringing at Brooklyn’s Bedford-Stuyvesant Volunteer Ambulance Corps, and not just for urgent medical help. These days, many of the callers are looking to train as emergency medical technicians with the hope of finding steady work with decent pay.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/nyregion/22SIDEweb/22SIDEweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/22/nyregion/22SIDEweb/22SIDEweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption'