imes', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama, the Least Lame President?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama, the Least Lame President?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ayres, Ian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witt, John Fabian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-21T23:34:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Ayres and John Fabian Witt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ayres', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Fabian', 'lastname': 'Witt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/12aef440-7756-5f71-9f60-a9edeee7cb63', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12aef440-7756-5f71-9f60-a9edeee7cb63'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks, with injuries continuing to sap their strength, fell to 5-25 after an uninspired performance against the Raptors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/22/sports/basketball/knicks-limp-to-another-loss-this-time-in-toronto.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks, with injuries continuing to sap their strength, fell to 5-25 after an uninspired performance against the Raptors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO — It took the Knicks only 37 seconds to concede three offensive rebounds to the Toronto Raptors on Sunday. At the 39-second mark, James Johnson scored the Raptors’ first basket on a two-handed, put-back dunk.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 549, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/22/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 549}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 937, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1874, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/22/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks Sleepwalk Through Loss as Nightmare Continues ', 'kicker': 'Raptors 118, Knicks 108', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knicks Sleepwa