cus: The Year in Political Pictures', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-22T11:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23adc6be-d9b3-5b53-b3a1-0e5c449ac6b1', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23adc6be-d9b3-5b53-b3a1-0e5c449ac6b1'}, {'abstract': 'Companies are expected to spend more money on digital advertising next year than on TV commercials in China, which has 527 million smartphone users.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/22/advertising-on-smartphones-embraced-in-china/', 'snippet': 'Companies are expected to spend more money on digital advertising next year than on TV commercials in China, which has 527 million smartphone users.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Liu Xuelong, a television and documentary producer in Beijing, hasn’t used his television in years. He gets all of his entertainment on his iPhone 6 Plus, where he also taps a plethora of apps to buy plane tickets, pay bills and talk with clients.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'arti