 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85ef5860-0512-509b-9377-3771876d4377', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85ef5860-0512-509b-9377-3771876d4377'}, {'abstract': 'More than 80 percent of managing directors and partners at financial firms in London expect their annual bonuses to increase this year, to an average of about $194,749, according to a survey by the recruitment firm Astbury Marsden.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/22/top-finance-employees-in-london-expect-bonuses-to-be-21-bigger-this-year/', 'snippet': 'More than 80 percent of managing directors and partners at financial firms in London expect their annual bonuses to increase this year, to an average of about $194,749, according to a survey by the recruitment firm Astbury Marsden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Despite recent curbs on bonus payments in Europe, senior employees of financial companies in London expect their bonuses for 2014 to be 21 percent higher than last year, according to the results of a survey by a recruiting firm released on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top Finance Employees in London Expect Bonuses to Be 21% Bigger', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-22T11:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c52aaf5-a280-5b2c-b0bc-0e66e7081c62', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c52aaf5-a280-5b2c-b0bc-0e66e7081c62'}, {'abstract': 'The current wave of problems caused by opioid drugs like OxyContin is the third in United States history. Balancing their risks and benefits has been a delicate task.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/23/upshot/painkiller-abuse-a-cyclical-challenge.html', 'snippet': 'The current wave of problems caused by opioid drugs like OxyContin is the third in United States history. Balancing their risks and benefits has been a delicate task.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as the Food and Drug Administration approves new, powerful opioid-based painkillers, the United States is in the midst of an epidemic of opioid overuse. This is not the first time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/upshot/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/22/upshot/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/upshot/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/upshot/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1450, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/upshot/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/22/upshot/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/22/upshot/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR/22UP-Opioids-slide-W9HR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Painkiller Abuse, a Cyclical Challenge', 'kicker': 'The New Health Care', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain-Relieving Drugs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buprenorphine (Drug)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-22T11:49:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Frakt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frakt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d24f030-6b92-5865-97a8-c020e8587327', 'word_count': 1721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d24f030-6b92-5865-97a8-c020e8587327'}, {'abstract': 'I used our 24-inch printer to print very large blow-ups of these grids, and then spread them out on my conference table. The printouts entirely covered a table 15 feet by 5 feet — a huge mess, but at least I could walk around the table and see all of the details in one place.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/22/is-this-any-way-to-pick-a-company-health-insurance-plan/', 'snippet': 'I used our 24-inch printer to print very large blow-ups of these grids, and then spread them out on my conference table. The printouts entirely covered a table 15 feet by 5 feet — a huge mess, but at least I could walk around the table and see all...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having chosen to continue with my current insurance provider, Independence Blue Cross, and also to continue offering multiple plans for my employees, my next step was to choose which of the company’s 38 plans to offer. Independence’s multiplan option, called “Blue Solutions” allows me to choose any five from a subset of 26 of the company’s 38 plans. Because I had a bad experience with the plan that most of my employees chose last year, a high-deductible bronze plan with low premiums, I wanted to take a look at all 26 plans again and compare their features.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is This Any Way to Pick a Company Health Insurance Plan?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Downs, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paul Downs Cabinetmakers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-22T12:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa4df10a-cec0-5002-bb06-a29c48ab938d', 'word_count': 1451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa4df10a-cec0-5002-bb06-a29c48ab938d'}, {'abstract': 'On Mondays, we publish a Times photo without a caption, headline or other information about its origins. Join the conversation by posting about what you see, and why. A live discussion is offered from 9 a.m. to 2 p.m. Eastern time.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/22/whats-going-on-in-this-picture-dec-22-2014/', 'snippet': 'On Mondays, we publish a Times photo without a caption, headline or other information about its origins. Join the conversation by posting about what you see, and why. A live discussion is offered from 9 a.m. to 2 p.m. Eastern time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated: Dec. 23, 2014', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/learning/VTS12-22-14LN/VTS12-22-14LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 321, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/18/learning/VTS12-22-14LN/VTS12-22-14LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 321}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/learning/VTS12-22-14LN/VTS12-22-14LN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 548, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/18/learning/VTS12-22-14LN/VTS12-22-14LN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1095, 'width': 2048, 'subTy