 fined it 22.8 million euros, or about $27.9 million, and ordered it to dismiss its chief financial officer by 2016 because of improper gains from interest-rate hedging.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dutch Insurer Fined $27.9 Million and Ordered to Dismiss C.F.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'De Nederlandsche Bank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delta Lloyd Group', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-22T12:05:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/825edf8f-44d2-54c6-b5b4-3ed6fdafc5b0', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/825edf8f-44d2-54c6-b5b4-3ed6fdafc5b0'}, {'abstract': 'Jeh Johnson, the Homeland Security secretary, placed flowers at a memorial to the officers; President Obama is under pressure to address growing racial tensions after the fatal shootings of two New York City police officers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/12/22/today-in-politics-62/', 'snippet': 'Jeh Johnson, the Homeland Security secretary, placed flowers at a memorial to the officers; President Obama is under pressure to address growing racial tensions after the fatal shootings of two New York City police officers.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today in Politics', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jeh C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-22T12:12:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38f6850d-db36-5178-891d-8f38cc612cc7', 'word_count': 1629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38f6850d-db36-5178-891d-8f38cc612cc7'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A bridge crashed into the Seine in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/22/1939-pont-st-louis-falls-into-seine/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A bridge crashed into the Seine in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The 200-foot Pont St. Louis, the only connecting link between the Île de la Cité and the Île St. Louis, was knocked down yesterday at 2:05 p.m. by the thump of a 600-ton barge, the Tunisie, while twenty or thirty persons and an automobile were on it. Late last night police set the toll at three dead and seven injured. The bodies of the three persons were recovered early in the evening. Three persons were trapped in the automobile that went to the bottom of the river. In the history of Paris’s many bridges, the Pont St. Louis is believed to have been the most luckless. It had met destruction twice since the original span was built by the order of Marie de Medici in 1614. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Dec. 23, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Pont St. Louis Falls Into Seine', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-22T12:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b273795d-7f3a-56c0-b459-11317f46ed24', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b273795d-7f3a-56c0-b459-11317f46ed24'}, {'abstract': 'New documents raise troubling issues about the government’s actions in the 2008 bailout of A.I.G. | The chairman of Ocwen Financial will step down as part of a legal settlement, according to a report. | Wall Street scored its latest victory against financial regulation. | Why we need an insider trading statute.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/22/morning-agenda-fresh-doubt-over-a-i-g-s-bailout/', 'snippet': 'New documents raise troubling issues about the government’s actions in the 2008 bailout of A.I.G. | The chairman of Ocwen Financial will step down as part of a legal settlement, according to a report. | Wall Street scored its latest victory agains...', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRESH DOUBT OVER A.I.G.’S BAILOUT | Documents produced after a trial over the 2008 bailout of the American International Group raise troubling new issues about the government’s actions in the rescue of the insurance giant, Gretchen Morgenson writes in the Fair Game column in The New York Times. The trove of material stems from a lawsuit brought by Maurice R. Greenberg, the former chief executive of A.I.G., who contends the bailout amounted to an improper seizure of private property under the Fifth Amendment. While Mr. Greenberg is not the most sympathetic figure, his fight has unearthed significant information, Ms. Morgenson writes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Fresh Doubt Over A.I.G.’s Bailout', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-22T12:29:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26a25f3b-a69f-54b7-8f63-744b0502c73a', 'word_count': 1723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26a25f3b-a69f-54b7-8f63-744b0502c73a'}, {'abstract': 'A longtime resident of Brazil’s westernmost Amazon state reflects on forests, martyrs and the future.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/22/a-postcard-from-the-western-amazon-on-peril-and-hope/', 'snippet': 'A longtime resident of Brazil’s westernmost Amazon state reflects on forests, martyrs and the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lou Gold, a fairly frequent guest here, recently sent some fresh reflections about his life in the western Amazon city of Rio Branco, Brazil. Gold is a self-described retired ancient-forest defender. He suggested I post his piece around the December anniversaries of the birth (the 15th) and assassination (the 22nd) of Chico Mendes, Brazil’s most famous rain forest defender, because, as Gold told me, “Even though it’s tough times for the forest, hope for the dream is still alive.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Postcard from the Western Amazon, on Peril and Hope', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Walking', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berry, Wendell', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanh, Thich Nhat', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mendes, Chico', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Global Witness', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAZON JUNGLE', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAZON RIVER BASIN', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brasilia (Brazil)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ecuador', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lima (Peru)', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peru', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-22T12:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c0c10c8-f476-5248-b403-ebc72b349c0b', 'word_count': 1581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c0c10c8-f476-5248-b403-ebc72b349c0b'}, {'abstract': 'The move to oversee a benchmark rates for currencies as well as other rates follows the taking over last year of regulation of the London interbank offered rate, or Libor.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/12/22/british-regulator-to-oversee-7-additional-financial-benchmarks/', 'snippet': 'The move to oversee a benchmark rates for currencies as well as other rates follows the taking over last year of regulation of the London interbank offered rate, or Libor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The Financial Conduct Authority of Britain said on Monday that it would regulate seven additional financial benchmark rates in Britain beginning in April, including an important rate for foreign currency trading, as part of its new power to oversee previously unregulated rates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Regulator to Oversee 7 Additional Financial Benchmarks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libor (London Interbank Offered Rate)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation o