, but we’ve left you with lots to do.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/23/happy-holidays-3/', 'snippet': 'The blog will be on vacation through Jan. 4, but we’ve left you with lots to do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Merry Christmas, happy Hanukkah, joyous Kwanzaa and happy New Year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy Holidays', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-23T11:20:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f8a6d52-4ac1-54b2-a0c9-e3caa0712c76', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f8a6d52-4ac1-54b2-a0c9-e3caa0712c76'}, {'abstract': 'The singer shows she remains a force to be reckoned with by releasing six songs from her coming album in response to an online leak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/arts/music/madonna-6-songs-offers-preview-of-rebel-heart-album.html', 'snippet': 'The singer shows she remains a force to be reckoned with by releasing six songs from her coming album in response to an online leak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In some circles, the six saddest words in the English language may be: “Don’t you know who I am?” Often the answer is an ego-crushing “no.” So when Madonna names a song “Bitch I’m Madonna” — and books Nicki Minaj to add praise — well, no one knows better than she does that celebrity is Darwinian.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/24/arts/music/24madonn