 Nicki', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madonna', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-23T11:24:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3be8eedf-c2b5-50cc-a958-a723d446ba09', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3be8eedf-c2b5-50cc-a958-a723d446ba09'}, {'abstract': 'The weak spot at JPMorgan appears to have been a fairly simple two-step password system that was neglected, leading to a major security breach this summer.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/23/daily-report-simple-flaw-allowed-jp-morgan-computer-breach/', 'snippet': 'The weak spot at JPMorgan appears to have been a fairly simple two-step password system that was neglected, leading to a major security breach this summer.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The computer breach at JPMorgan Chase this summer — the largest intrusion of an American bank to date — might have been thwarted if the bank had installed a simple security fix to an overlooked server in its vast network, said people who have been briefed on internal and outside investigations into the attack, Matthew Goldstein, Nicole Perlroth and Michael Corkery report.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Simple Flaw Allowed JPMorgan Computer Breach', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-23T11:25:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/403eabf4-b3c6-56f8-863d-3f91594bb699', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/403eabf4-b3c6-56f8-863d-3f91594bb699'}, {'abstract': 'The former No. 2 official in the city government and a real estate mogul were given terms of seven and a half years and five years in prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/world/asia/hong-kong-corruption-trial-sentencing.html', 'snippet': 'The former No. 2 official in the city government and a real estate mogul were given terms of seven and a half years and five years in prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The former second-highest ranking official in the Hong Kong government and a property tycoon were sentenced on Tuesday to seven and a half years and five years in prison after their convictions in a high-profile corruption case.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Official and Property Tycoon Are Sentenced in Hong Kong Graft Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Official and Property Tycoon Are Sentenced in Hong Kong Graft Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sun Hung Kai Properties Limited', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hui, Rafael (1948- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kwok, Raymond', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kwok, Thomas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-23T11:48:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b116e1d-3019-503f-aab4-7ec367a40452', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b116e1d-3019-503f-aab4-7ec367a40452'}, {'abstract': 'After five years, this is the final post on You’re the Boss. As a parting gift, we offer some highlights from another year spent in the trenches, where we all continued to make mistakes and learn lessons.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/23/so-long-from-youre-the-boss/', 'snippet': 'After five years, this is the final post on You’re the Boss. As a parting gift, we offer some highlights from another year spent in the trenches, where we all continued to make mistakes and learn lessons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past five years, it’s been my pleasure to edit the You’re the Boss small-business blog, which has afforded me the opportunity to work with a talented array of journalists and business owners. The journalists covered their beats diligently, the owners shared their ups and downs generously, and we all benefited from the comments offered by an exceedingly smart group of readers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So Long, From You’re the Boss', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-23T12:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Loren Feldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Loren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9702c6b3-05e1-507f-8b97-fc89801f1b59', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9702c6b3-05e1-507f-8b97-fc89801f1b59'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio faces a political crisis over the fatal shooting of two police officers by an African-American man.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2014/12/23/today-in-