and the protests.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/23/when-officers-die-and-protests-get-the-blame/', 'snippet': 'Some officials have linked Ismaaiyl Brinsley’s killings of two N.Y.P.D. officers to protests against police violence. But others say this linkage misunderstands Mr. Brinsley and the protests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the days after Ismaaiyl Brinsley’s killings of two New York Police Department officers and the shooting of a Baltimore woman, some in positions of authority\xa0have linked the crimes to protests against police violence.\xa0But others believe this linkage misunderstands both Mr. Brinsley and the protests\xa0—\xa0and that such misunderstanding could have serious consequences.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Officers Die and Protests Get the Blame', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Patrolmen's Benevolent Assn", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sentencing Project', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-23T15:08:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4d0545a-5745-5390-afce-75ac79f21158', 'word_count': 1112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4d0545a-5745-5390-afce-75ac79f21158'}, {'abstract': 'It’s hard to be FDR.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/23/nothing-non-gold-can-stay/', 'snippet': 'It’s hard to be FDR.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Beckworth has a good post pointing out that the Fed has been signaling all along that the big expansion in the monetary base is a temporary measure, to be withdrawn when the economy improves. And he argues that this vitiates the effectiveness of quantitative easing, citing many others with the same view. My only small peeve is that you might not realize from his list that I made this point sixteen years ago, which I think lets me claim dibs. Yes, I’m turning into one of those crotchety old economists who says in response to anything, “It’s trivial, it’s wrong, and I said it decades ago.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nothing Non-Gold Can Stay', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-23T15:19:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e0838a3-d714-5bb8-b501-c489ac197716', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e0838a3-d714-5bb8-b501-c489ac197716'}, {'abstract': 'Officials expressed concerns that Noble Energy, a Ho