.7 million residents, New York now ranks behind California, Texas and Florida, according to new figures released by the United States Census Bureau.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/nyregion/new-york-falls-to-florida-dropping-to-no-4-in-population.html', 'snippet': 'With 19.7 million residents, New York now ranks behind California, Texas and Florida, according to new figures released by the United States Census Bureau.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — We’re No. 4!', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/24/nyregion/NYCENSUS/NYCENUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/24/nyregion/NYCENSUS/NYCENUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/24/nyregion/NYCENSUS/NYCENUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/24/nyregion/NYCENSUS/NYCENUS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/24/nyregion/NYCENSUS/NYCENUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/24/nyregion/NYCENSUS/NYCENUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/24/nyregion/NYCENSUS/NYCENUS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ceding to Florida, New York Falls to No. 4 in Population', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ceding to Florida, New York Falls to No. 4 in Population', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKinley, Jesse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-23T16:09:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f39fd77-9d23-538d-b6b2-f0a836c646b0', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f39fd77-9d23-538d-b6b2-f0a836c646b0'}, {'abstract': 'Botequim is a Brazilian restaurant that takes some searching.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/dining/restaurant-review-botequim-in-the-east-village.html', 'snippet': 'Botequim is a Brazilian restaurant that takes some searching.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Restaurants hide in all kinds of ways. There is the coy, unmarked-door hiding of the neo-speakeasy. There is the romantic hiding of restaurants whose positioning at, say, the end of an alley allows men to seem clever and their dates to seem impressed. There is the snooty hiding of exclusive restaurants that behave like private clubs, an affectation that is going out of style and won’t be missed.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Review: Botequim in the East Village', 'kicker': 'Restaurants', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Samba in the Basement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Botequim (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-23T16:14:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/131d29e2-a52c-5179-aaea-889005f2f46d', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/131d29e2-a52c-5179-aaea-889005f2f46d'}, {'abstract': 'A parliamentary vote to pursue closer ties to the West drew a sharp rebuke from Russia, which called the step counterproductive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/world/europe/ukraine-parliament-nato-vote.html', 'snippet': 'A parliamentary vote to pursue closer ties to the West drew a sharp rebuke from Russia, which called the step counterproductive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — With a Russian-backed separatist insurgency still gripping eastern Ukraine, the Ukrainian Parliament voted on Tuesday to take steps toward joining NATO. It was a pointed rebuke to Russia that immediately drew an angry response.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ukraine Vote Takes Nation a Step Closer to NATO', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ukraine Vote Takes Nation a Step Closer to NATO', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'