pet': 'Companies still need to invest in cyberprotection and detection, says Richard Beales of Reuters Breakingviews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A high-profile hack at JPMorgan \xa0Chase – to say nothing of monstrous breaches at Sony and Home Depot – has made cybersecurity a daily concern for executives at big banks and corporations. One partial protection is to take out insurance. It’s a confusing market, but growing fast. With a United States government campaign on top of all the publicity, coverage may become standard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Need for Bank Cyberinsurance', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Depot Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-23T19:40:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Beales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f1bb55c-3018-5110-bede-133eae3ae747', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f1bb55c-3018-5110-bede-133eae3ae747'}, {'abstract': 'The ticketing system at this spot makes sense; a communal, three-hour meal there feels more like an event than a dinner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/28/travel/restaurant-report-lazy-bear-in-san-francis