um of Women in the Arts will be the first American organization to receive the Simone de Beauvoir Prize for Women’s Freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/arts/design/museum-of-women-gets-freedom-award.html', 'snippet': 'The National Museum of Women in the Arts will be the first American organization to receive the Simone de Beauvoir Prize for Women’s Freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Museum of Women in the Arts, in Washington, will be the first American organization to receive the Simone de Beauvoir Prize for Women’s Freedom, the museum announced. The prize, created in 2008 to commemorate the 100th anniversary of Ms. de Beauvoir’s birth, is awarded annually, with the winner chosen by an international jury. It will be presented to the museum next month. Previous winners include Malala Yousafzai, a co-recipient of the Nobel Peace Prize this year.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum of Women Gets Freedom Award', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Museum of Women Gets Freedom Award', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Museum of Women in the Arts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-23T22:09:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecf8df78-5bd5-55e9-a094-c9e57849fbd6', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecf8df78-5bd5-55e9-a094-c9e57849fbd6'}, {'abstract': 'The Library of Congress said that it would award the 2014 Rebekah Johnson Bobbitt National Prize for Poetry to Patricia Smith.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/books/staten-island-poet-to-receive-bobbitt-prize.html', 'snippet': 'The Library of Congress said that it would award the 2014 Rebekah Johnson Bobbitt National Prize for Poetry to Patricia Smith.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Library of Congress announced that it would award the 2014 Rebekah Johnson Bobbitt National Prize for Poetry to Patricia Smith for her book “Shoulda Been Jimi Savannah.” The $10,000 prize, given for “the most distinguished book of poetry published in the preceding two years,” is donated by the family of Ms. Bobbitt, who was Lyndon B. Johnson’s sister. Ms. Smith, an associate professor at the College of Staten Island, has written six poetry collections; one, “Blood Dazzler” (2008), was a finalist for a National Book Award. Previous winners of the Bobbitt Prize include Charles Wright, W. S. Merwin, Louise Glück and Mark Strand.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Staten Island Poet to Receive Bobbitt Prize', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Staten Island Poet to Receive Bobbitt Prize', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Patricia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Library of Congress', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-23T22:18:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/886fd751-161e-5ff4-a6c3-5b0141e1e090', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/886fd751-161e-5ff4-a6c3-5b0141e1e090'}, {'abstract': 'Get recommendations from New 