, '_id': 'nyt://article/4bacb2ba-20fd-58a3-8508-de00b839f6a0', 'word_count': 37, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bacb2ba-20fd-58a3-8508-de00b839f6a0'}, {'abstract': 'In “Chewing Gum and Chocolate,” Shomei Tomatsu explored the attractions and contradictions of American culture and the military in postwar Japan.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/american-culture-riding-a-mushroom-cloud/', 'snippet': 'In “Chewing Gum and Chocolate,” Shomei Tomatsu explored the attractions and contradictions of American culture and the military in postwar Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Shomei Tomatsu was drawn to ninja and samurai movies as a child in post-World War II Japan, even though teachers forbade students from seeing them. They called them “disreputable.” He found them irresistible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Culture, Riding a Mushroom Cloud', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berger, Maurice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomatsu, Shomei', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APERTURE FOUNDATION', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Okinawa and Other Ryukyu Islands (Japan)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-24T10:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maurice Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maurice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee2d3f38-d63b-5b9d-8083-5b361da51429', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee2d3f38-d63b-5b9d-8083-5b361da51429'}, {'abstract': 'Ava DuVernay’s film “Selma” follows civil rights demonstrators in March 1965 across an Alabama bridge and into a new era for black Americans, with progress made and promises unkept.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/25/arts/in-selma-king-is-just-one-of-the-heroes.html', 'snippet': 'Ava DuVernay’s film “Selma” follows civil rights demonstrators in March 1965 across an Alabama bridge and into a new era for black Americans, with progress made and promises unkept.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the afternoon of March 7, 1965, Alabama state troopers and members of a Dallas County posse, armed with clubs, cattle prods and tear gas, attacked civil rights demonstrators on the Edmund Pettus Bridge in Selma, Ala. The marchers had planned to walk the 50 miles to Montgomery, the state capital, as part of a long-building protest against the denial of basic voting rights to Southern blacks. The procession would have crossed Lowndes County, where not a single African-American voter had been registered in more than 60 years. Efforts to change this had been met with bureaucratic obstruction, intimidation and lethal brutality, including the killing, a week earlier, of Jimmie Lee Jackson, a 26-year-old laborer and protester, by a state trooper.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/SELMA/SELMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/SELMA/SELMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/SELMA/SELMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/SELMA/SELMA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1303, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/SELMA/SELMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/SELMA/SELMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/SELMA/SELMA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A 50-Mile March, Nearly 50 Years Later', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A 50-Mile March, Nearly 50 Years Later', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DuVernay, Ava', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oyelowo, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Selma (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-24T10:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 