t you to 2015.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apps to Ring In the New Year, and for the Resolutions After', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Celebration and the Self-Improvement After', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eaton, Kit', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Secret Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-24T20:15:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f4e90da-7ead-5b49-be65-53ccdef12b6c', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f4e90da-7ead-5b49-be65-53ccdef12b6c'}, {'abstract': 'Three translated novellas set in the shadow of the Nazi occupation of Paris, by the 2014 Nobel Prize winner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/28/books/review/patrick-modianos-suspended-sentences.html', 'snippet': 'Three translated novellas set in the shadow of the Nazi occupation of Paris, by the 2014 Nobel Prize winner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The surest sign that international publishers were caught off guard when the French novelist Patrick Modiano won this year’s Nobel literature prize was that few of his books were available in translation. Many people in France were also surprised, but for a different reason. Unlike most of that country’s intellectuals, Modiano has never sought celebrity. Indeed, this 69-year-old man seems as shy and withdrawn today as he was at 23, when his first novel was published.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/books/review/28RIDING/28riding-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1050, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/28/books/review/28RIDING/28riding-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1050}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/books/review/28RIDING/28riding-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 586, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/books/review/28RIDING/28riding-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2039, 'width': 1165, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/books/review/28RIDING/28RIDING-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/28/books/review/28RIDING/28RIDING-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/books/review/28RIDING/28RIDING-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Patrick Modiano’s ‘Suspended Sentences’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Search of the Irrevocable', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riding, Alan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'majo