rds season to a circus, consider it official: The movers, shakers, rope-walkers and high-fliers of the circus world will be honored next month at Lincoln Center with the first American Circus Awards. The event, called the Celebration of American Circus, is presented by Circus Now, a nonprofit group that supports North American circuses.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oscars, Shmoscars: Presenting the American Circus Awards', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oscars, Shmoscars: Awards for the Circus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petit, Philippe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big Apple Circus', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Circus Now', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Damrosch Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-24T20:41:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02fa2ad9-0208-5111-a8da-e8598ffd806b', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02fa2ad9-0208-5111-a8da-e8598ffd806b'}, {'abstract': 'Good news for the economy, bad news for the bugs.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/recession-recovery-and-gold/', 'snippet': 'Good news for the economy, bad news for the bugs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twas the afternoon before Christmas, and I needed a break from the holiday spirit. Bah humbug.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recession, Recovery, and Gold', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-24T20:41:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc678d58-acf3-5518-a72c-95cdf4721bcd', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc678d58-acf3-5518-a72c-95cdf4721bcd'}, {'abstract': 'DirecTV will run a special Christmas episode of “Black Mirror,” a British anthology series with touches of “The Twilight Zone” and “Alfred Hitchcock Presents.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/25/arts/television/a-black-mirror-christmas-tale-on-directv.html', 'snippet': 'DirecTV will run a special Christmas episode of “Black Mirror,” a British anthology series with touches of “The Twilight Zone” and “Alfred Hitchcock Presents.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'So many movies, television series and books about the future posit postapocalyptic collapse and feral scavengers scuttling across a scorched landscape. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/JPBLACKMIRROR/JPBLACKMIRROR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/JPBLACKMIRROR/JPBLACKMIRROR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/JPBLACKMIRROR/JPBLACKMIRR