{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-24T21:10:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Hawgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hawgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cfc0753-77f9-5446-9c88-7b0fd723b54d', 'word_count': 1651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cfc0753-77f9-5446-9c88-7b0fd723b54d'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Gambler,” Mark Wahlberg takes big risks with money and relationships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/25/movies/the-gambler-stars-mark-wahlberg-indulging-in-a-habit.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Gambler,” Mark Wahlberg takes big risks with money and relationships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “The Gambler,” a movie about a guy who’s a glutton for criminally high stakes and for punishment, a skeletonized Mark Wahlberg wears a mop of greasy hair and an abject look. In some scenes, he looks crushed and lost, like a wadded scrap of paper that fell short of the garbage bin. It soon becomes clear why. His character, Jim Bennett, hit the literary jackpot years ago with a well-received first and only published novel. Now Jim splits his time between teaching college — say hello to Professor Wahlberg — and betting and losing at gaming tables, some in underworld parlors around a Los Angeles that’s been Michael Mann-ed into a smear of throbbing color and would-be existential dread. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/GAMBLER/GAMBLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'h