8-7574-5084-9cda-7596ed939cdd'}, {'abstract': 'Molly Guptill Manning’s “When Books Went to War: The Stories That Helped Us Win World War II” feels like the bibliophile’s equivalent of “It’s a Wonderful Life.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/25/books/when-books-went-to-war-by-molly-guptill-manning.html', 'snippet': 'Molly Guptill Manning’s “When Books Went to War: The Stories That Helped Us Win World War II” feels like the bibliophile’s equivalent of “It’s a Wonderful Life.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heartwarming war stories aren’t easy to come by, especially if they insist on being entirely realistic about the hellishness of military life. But Molly Guptill Manning’s “When Books Went to War” winds up feeling like the bibliophile’s equivalent of “It’s a Wonderful Life.” It tells of enlisted men during World War II whose one and only form of entertainment became reading, and of the enormous home-front effort to supply them with the books they desperately wanted.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/JPBOOK2/JPBOOK2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 841, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/JPBOOK2/JPBOOK2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 841}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/JPBOOK2/JPBOOK2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/arts/JPBOOK2/JPBOOK2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1461, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'imag