throws-softly-conquering-the-winter-blahs.html', 'snippet': 'For one designer, the ideal wrap offers texture, warmth and strong graphic appeal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York rug designer Inigo Elizalde loves pattern — the bolder and more graphic, the better. His collections include punchy motifs inspired by traditional designs from his native Philippines, and vividly colored lines and grids recalling computer malfunctions.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25SHOP5/25SHOP5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 441, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25SHOP5/25SHOP5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 441}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25SHOP5/25SHOP5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25SHOP5/25SHOP5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1506, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25SHOP5/25SHOP5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25SHOP5/25SHOP5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25SHOP5/25SHOP5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Throws: Softly Conquering the Winter Blahs', 'kicker': 'Shopping With Inigo Elizalde', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Such a Winter’s Throw', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKeough, Tim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elizalde, Inigo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wool and Woolen Goods', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-24T23:50:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d85fdaab-0165-5dc1-bcec-d097ab40db32', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d85fdaab-0165-5dc1-bcec-d097ab40db32'}, {'abstract': 'Doug Meyer, a New York interior designer, created a 41-foot-long “drip” wall in the Stripe Café at the Palos Verdes Art Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/25/garden/linear-thinking-at-an-art-center-cafe.html', 'snippet': 'Doug Meyer, a New York interior designer, created a 41-foot-long “drip” wall in the Stripe Café at the Palos Verdes Art Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his renovation of the Palos Verdes Art Center near Los Angeles, which took almost two years, Doug Meyer not only refreshed the spaces of an 83-year-old institution but he also introduced a new one. After Mr. Meyer, a New York interior designer, persuaded his clients to feed their visitors (and the community), the Stripe Café opened last month with a farm-to-table menu by its chef, Brett Hickey. To anchor the colorful décor, the designer created a 41-foot-long “drip” wall that looks like an afternoon’s lark, but in reality took him two weeks to paint. He also made the most of the bump-outs created by three skylights to design installations with some 3,000 vinyl strips in five different colors. “It looks like glass, and plays off the drip stripes,” he said. 5504 West Crestridge Road, Rancho Palos Verdes, Calif. Information: 310-541-2479 or pvartcenter.org.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS1/25CURRENTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 889, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS1/25CURRENTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 889}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS1/25CURRENTS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 692, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS1/25CURRENTS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1383, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS1/25CURRENTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS1/25CURRENTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS1/25CURRENTS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Linear Thinking at an Art Center Cafe', 'kicker': 'Rooms', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rooms: Linear Thinking at an Art Center Cafe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suqi, Rima', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyer, Doug', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palos Verdes Art Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paint', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-24T23:50:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bad517f1-0516-59dc-ad97-6fc59c382a06', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bad517f1-0516-59dc-ad97-6fc59c382a06'}, {'abstract': 'Topped by a 6½-inch-thick marble block, the Terranova table weighs about a quarter of a ton. It could have been much heavier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/25/garden/a-coffee-table-that-stays-put.html', 'snippet': 'Topped by a 6½-inch-thick marble block, the Terranova table weighs about a quarter of a ton. It could have been much heavier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For lovers of marble, there is Terranova, a coffee table topped by a 6½-inch-thick block of the material. But be warned: The stone slab, which is 4 feet long by 2 feet wide, weighs about 450 pounds. Such a massive piece gives the $19,375 table “a whole different vocabulary,” said David Khouri, a partner at Khouri Guzman Bunce Lininger in New York, which designed it. “We’re used to seeing it sliced so thin,” he said, “like sliced bread.” Terranova’s top, which sits on a four-pronged silicon bronze base, came close to being heavier. “It was originally going to weigh 1,100 pounds,” Mr. Khouri said, “so we carved out the underside as much as we could.” Even so, five movers were required to install the table in the company’s showroom. Information: 212-420-7866 or kgblnyc.com.\xad', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS5/25CURRENTS5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS5/25CURRENTS5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS5/25CURRENTS5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS5/25CURRENTS5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1327, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS5/25CURRENTS5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS5/25CURRENTS5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/garden/25CURRENTS5/25CURRENTS5-thumbLarge.jpg', 