astery in Sichuan Province, Tibetan exile and advocacy groups said Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Tibetan monk died Tuesday after setting himself on fire near his monastery in Sichuan Province, Tibetan exile and advocacy groups said Wednesday. It was the third fatal self-immolation in Tibetan parts of China in less than two weeks. The monk, Kalsang Yeshi, 37, took his life in front of a police station that had been set up to monitor activity at his monastery in Dawu County, in Kardze Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture, the organization Free Tibet. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Monk Burns Himself to Death in a Political Protest', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Monk Burns Himself to Death in a Political Protest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immolation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monasteries and Monks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-25T00:40:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6baaf02-0179-5ce0-a924-1cb18ca87973', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6baaf02-0179-5ce0-a924-1cb18ca87973'}, {'abstract': 'Phyllis Atwood’s son, Jamel, has autism, and slight variations in his routine can be jarring. His birthday celebration was part party and part prayer.'