57-b98f-0889a782a5bf'}, {'abstract': 'Since the fatal shootings of two police officers in Brooklyn, some protests against police tactics have become more subdued.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/25/nyregion/video-a-shift-in-protests-after-officers-are-killed.html', 'snippet': 'Since the fatal shootings of two police officers in Brooklyn, some protests against police tactics have become more subdued.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio has led calls for a suspension of demonstrations while the families of two New York police officers prepare to bury the men, who were fatally shot in Brooklyn. Officers Wenjian Liu, 32, and Rafael Ramos, 40, of the 84th Precinct, were killed Saturday in Bedford-Stuyvesant by Ismaaiyl Brinsley, 28, who had proclaimed his intention of targeting the police.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: A Shift in Protests After Officers Are Killed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-25T03:08:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e179dd6-4c2f-5222-8ce0-508dac454e34', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e179dd6-4c2f-5222-8ce0-508dac454e34'}, {'abstract': 'Following a longstanding tradition, Gramercy Park was opened to the public for an hour on Wednesday for Christmas Eve festivities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/25/nyregion/inside-gramercy-parks-gates-one-night-less-silent-than-the-other-364.html', 'snippet': 'Following a longstanding tradition, Gramercy Park was opened to the public for an hour on Wednesday for Christmas Eve festivities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The line of people laced down the block an hour before the opening on Wednesday night, stalwart as rain spat down, growing in size even as the damp descended. Before them lay not a velvet-roped nightclub or a red-carpet awards show, but something far more exclusive: a park.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST/NOCTURNALIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/25/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST/NOCTURNALIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST/NOCTURNALIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST/NOCTURNALIST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/25/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST/NOCTURNALIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/25/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST/NOCTURNALIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': 