explored in a show at the Studio Museum in Harlem; two Japanese groups perform at Carnegie Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miser figures that the truly astute artist is awake to any potential source of inspiration, no matter how humble or ordinary the origin. Bela Bartok borrowed freely from folk melodies, just as Andy Warhol repurposed pictures directly from newsmagazines.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Artistic Inspiration in the Pages of Jet and Ebony', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Artistic Inspiration in the Pages of Jet and Ebony', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Studio Museum in Harlem', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-25T17:23:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. C. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3684df45-cd88-5b8a-bacc-d8924c028606', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3684df45-cd88-5b8a-bacc-d8924c028606'}, {'abstract': 'Local vintners are fighting a project under which tens of millions of gallons of liquefied petroleum gas, and up to two billion cubic feet of natural gas, would be stored in caverns near Seneca Lake.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/26/nyregion/new-york-winemakers-fight-gas-storage-plan-near-seneca-lake.html', 'snippet': 'Local vintners are fighting a project under which tens of millions of gallons of liquefied petroleum gas, and up to two billion cubic feet of natural gas, would be stored in caverns near Seneca Lake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WATKINS GLEN, N.Y. — Over the last two decades, vintners in the Finger Lakes region of New York State have slowly, and 