inces in “Into the Woods,” a highly anticipated adaptation of the 1986 Stephen Sondheim-James Lapine fairy-tale mash-up.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I was raised to be charming, not sincere” is certainly a pathetic way to explain one’s caddish behavior, but when Chris Pine speaks the line as Cinderella’s Prince in the new film adaptation of “Into the Woods,” you almost feel sorry for this deep-as-a-bottle-cap guy. “Oh the poor fella,” you think, “no one ever taught him how to care about anyone but himself.” The Prince, who has surely not suffered rejection before, then gets dumped. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28WOODS1/28WOODS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28WOODS1/28WOODS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28WOODS1/28WOODS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28WOODS1/28WOODS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28WOODS1/28WOODS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28WOODS1/28WOODS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/2