s gained a following.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/26/arts/design/degass-little-dancer-spotlights-a-seminal-sculpture.html', 'snippet': '“Degas’s Little Dancer” is a small show at the National Gallery of Art, but full of reasons Degas gained a following.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The more you return to the art of Degas, the more ambiguous and many-layered it becomes — nowhere more so than in his many depictions of ballet. Mainly he seems to pay painstaking attention to complex aspects of reality and realism. Researchers have documented the accuracy with which he recorded specific costumes and décors in individual ballets. But his work shows that he delighted in using ballet for a multifaceted consideration of many aspects of existence. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vintage Ballerina, Adored Anew ', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vintage Ballerina, Adored Anew', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Gallery of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Degas, Edgar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-25T19:11:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da3575e0-a816-5bd3-8f87-c3bbfc097546', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da3575e0-a816-5bd3-8f87-c3bbfc097546'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: the U.S. Air Force was preparing a reorganization in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/25/1964-u-s-a-f-seeks-new-role/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: the U.S. Air Force was preparing a reorganization in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Air Force is preparing a dramatic reorganization proposal which would, if adopted, give it major responsibility in developing and maintaining Army air elements. While not yet in final form, the proposal is expected to go to the joint chiefs of staff and Defense Secretary Robert S. McNamara within the next few months. It will be in effect a major part of the Air Force’s answer to the Army’s campaign for a large scale expansion of the Army’s integral air arm. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Dec. 26, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: U.S.A.F. Seeks New Role', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Aircraft', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Air Force', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-25T19:12:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1ae6dfd-025b-5cc4-9521-e0c745508615', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1ae6dfd-025b-5cc4-9521-e0c745508615'}, {'abstract': 'As officers were eating, assailants sneaked into the base, killing three soldiers and a civilian in what the African Union called a “reprehensible attack.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/26/world/africa/somalia-shabab-ambush-christmas-at-african-union-base.html', 'snippet': 'As officers were eating, assailants sneaked into the base, killing three soldiers and a civilian in what the African Union called a “reprehensible attack.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOGADISHU, Somalia — A Christmas meal at the African Union peacekeeping base here was ambushed Thursday by Islamist gunmen and suicide bombers, including some dressed as Somali soldiers, turning a festive respite into a bloody battleground.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shabab Fighters Ambush Base of Peacekeepers in Somalia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shabab Fighters Ambush Base of Peacekeepers in Somalia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahim, Mohammed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN UNION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-25T19:39:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mohamed Ibrahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohamed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ibrahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81ca6470-f178-5a2c-8d80-838c04155fa1', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81ca6470-f178-5a2c-8d80-838c04155fa1'}, {'abstract': 'In the opening game of the N.B.A.’s Christmas Day schedule, Washington sent the host Knicks to their sixth straight loss and 26th defeat of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/26/sports/basketball/for-kni