'_id': 'nyt://article/0256637e-dabc-5a9a-b542-4b680de9efbd', 'word_count': 3006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0256637e-dabc-5a9a-b542-4b680de9efbd'}, {'abstract': 'Some factions want to keep pressing for police reform, as two slain officers are mourned in New York City. Others say that might alienate the public.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/26/nyregion/after-killing-of-2-officers-a-reversal-in-attitudes-to-police-of-some-demonstrators-and-officials.html', 'snippet': 'Some factions want to keep pressing for police reform, as two slain officers are mourned in New York City. Others say that might alienate the public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'City Council members took to the streets in New York to block traffic in solidarity with the demonstrators demanding changes in policing. The Council speaker opened a meeting of her fellow Council members with a call to utter the protest mantra, “I can’t breathe,” the final words of a Staten Island man killed by a police chokehold. And last Friday, the mayor sat down with leaders of the demonstrations, heeding their appeal for a face-to-face meeting even as they vowed to continue disrupting the city.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Killing of Police Officers, Protest Movement Is at a Crossroads', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Killing of 2 Officers, a Reversal in Some Attitudes Toward the Police', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, Wenjian (1982-2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramos, Rafael (1974-2014)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice League NYC', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brinsley, Ismaaiyl Abdullah', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diaz, Ruben Jr', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mark-Viverito, Melissa', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-25T23:27:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikita Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stewart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fad3400-051c-5701-a560-4fb817882464', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fad3400-051c-5701-a560-4fb817882464'}, {'abstract': 'Consumers are flocking to smaller S.U.V.s, fueling a boom in vehicles that handle like a car, get the mileage of a midsize sedan, and yet offer features many drivers want.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/26/automobiles/move-over-land-yachts-compact-suvs-are-in-demand.html', 'snippet': 'Consumers are flocking to smaller S.U.V.s, fueling a boom in vehicles that handle like a car, get the mileage of a midsize sedan, and yet offer features many drivers want.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Susan Mahoney has for years owned a string of sport utility vehicles — land yachts that gave her plenty of room and a commanding view, along with a big fuel bill. Bu