k': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-26T12:16:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40323714-d44b-56de-b8d4-0aced4492b8e', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40323714-d44b-56de-b8d4-0aced4492b8e'}, {'abstract': 'An anniversary exhibition in Mexico City, a new production of Verdi’s ‘‘Ballo in Maschera’’ in London and a retrospective of the works of Lynn Hershman Leeson in Karlsruhe, Germany.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/26/whats-on-this-week-around-the-world-3/', 'snippet': 'An anniversary exhibition in Mexico City, a new production of Verdi’s ‘‘Ballo in Maschera’’ in London and a retrospective of the works of Lynn Hershman Leeson in Karlsruhe, Germany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beijing', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On This Week Around the World', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-26T12:42:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher D. Shea', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/645ff626-e6a8-5479-a345-f62a7fd6f870', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/645ff626-e6a8-5479-a345-f62a7fd6f870'}, {'abstract': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/12/26/daily-clip-report-90/', 'snippet': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Clip Report', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-26T13:01:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a6c6f33-bda8-53e7-8e68-f966ce079e31', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a6c6f33-bda8-53e7-8e68-f966ce079e31'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Theaters in London put on Christmas shows in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/26/1914-christmas-shows-in-london/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Theaters in London put on Christmas shows in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Sir Herbert Tree’s production of ‘‘David Copperfield,’’ adapted by Mr. Louis N. Parker, was given its initial performance at His Majesty’s Theatre on Thursday evening [Dec. 24], and it proved a rare Christmas Eve treat. Sir Herbert, in the dual role of Micawber and Daniel Peggotty, was never seen to better advantage, and the difficult task of adapting Dickens for the stage was carried out remarkably well. There was a great ovation at the end, and the audience insisted upon a speech from Sir Herbert, who replied with the modesty of a schoolgirl, but with evident gratitude. Judging from the dress rehearsal of the ‘‘Sleeping Beauty Re-Awakened,’’ at Drury Lane, this pantomime will be a great favorite of the festive season. During one of the intervals, the band played ‘‘Tipperary,’’ and everyone in the audience joined in with such relish that encore after encore followed. At the Lyceum, Miss Louise Beckman will be the hero of ‘‘Jack and the Beanstalk,’’ and Miss Doris Dean will be the pretty princess.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Dec. 26, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1914: Christmas Shows in London', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Copperfield, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-26T13:05:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd91f8b9-a3d1-5356-82c6-1549109d7676', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd91f8b9-a3d1-5356-82c6-1549109d7676'}, {'abstract': 'Leading business schools are breaking from traditional approaches and picking up the digital-age arts of speed and constant experimentation.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/26/daily-report-m-b-a-programs-start-to-follow-silicon-valley-into-the-data-age/', 'snippet': 'Leading business schools are breaking from traditional approaches and picking up the digital-age arts of speed and constant experimentation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greg Pass, the former chief technology officer of Twitter, put the matter succinctly, Steve Lohr reports. The M.B.A., he observed, is “a challenged brand.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/