ttps://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/31/dining/the-2014-restaurant-reviews.html', 'snippet': 'The restaurants Pete Wells reviewed in 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following is an alphabetical list of the restaurants Pete Wells reviewed in 2014. A list of his 10 favorite restaurants of the year can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 2014 Restaurant Reviews', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wells, Pete', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-26T13:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/73bfaa38-f817-545b-95e9-91812ac30ade', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73bfaa38-f817-545b-95e9-91812ac30ade'}, {'abstract': 'Fish cakes break out with chiles and aromatic herbs. (Article plus video.)', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/31/dining/a-recipe-for-spicy-fish-cakes.html', 'snippet': 'Fish cakes break out with chiles and aromatic herbs. (Article plus video.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'The typical fish cake does not call attention to itself. Potato-rich, monochromatic and satisfying, it is the kind of thing you’d make for a homey dinner when the food wasn’t the point.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fish Cakes Conquer Their Shyness', 'kicker': 'A Good Appetite', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fish Cakes Conquer Their Shyness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-26T13:30:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ee1800a-e981-5770-a2d9-bc18f0154fde', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ee1800a-e981-5770-a2d9-bc18f0154fde'}, {'abstract': 'From a hot roast beef sandwich at Bar Primi to sashimi with Japanese chimichurri at Cagen, Pete Wells names his favorite dishes of 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/31/dining/nyc-best-restaurant-dishes-2014.html', 'snippet': 'From a hot roast beef sandwich at Bar Primi to sashimi with Japanese chimichurri at Cagen, Pete Wells names his favorite dishes of 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE HOT ROAST BEEF SANDWICH AT BAR PRIMI Thinly sliced meat with hot pepper sauce and provolone on a sesame roll isn’t meant to be the centerpiece of a formal dinner. Eating it should be a spontaneous act: You’re on the Bowery, you see that there’s no line, and you strike like a Predator drone.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Restaurant Dishes of 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Dishes That Defined the Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-26T13:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e18e462f-3c38-5f61-abd4-ba141b16e65c', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e18e462f-3c38-5f61-abd4-ba141b16e65c'}, {'abstract': 'From Bâtard to Russ & Daughters Cafe, the restaurants that brought a fresh perspective to the dining scene this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/31/dining/nyc-best-new-restaurants-2014.html', 'snippet': 'From Bâtard to Russ & Daughters Cafe, the restaurants that brought a fresh perspective to the dining scene this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the foxhole where I attempt to pin stars on restaurants, the view is limited. Mostly, I can see the establishment I’m writing about that week. I may glance at its competitors, to see if Slugburger Deluxe is performing up to the high standards set by Slugburger 5000 at the Trump Galaxy. But the question I’m trying to answer, above others, is how close Slugburger Deluxe comes to succeeding on its own terms.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 10 Best New Restaurants of 2014', 'kicker': 'Restaurants', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gazing Beyond the Stars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Batard (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Russ & Daughters Cafe (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Simone, The (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cherche Midi (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ivan Ramen (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delaware and Hudson (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Contra (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dirty French (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gato (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bar Bolonat (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-26T13:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/458688c8-b793-51b7-a8d4-b0d8ad95d975', 'word_count': 1984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/458688c8-b793-51b7-a8d4-b0d8ad95d975'}, {'abstract': 'For many, consuming this frugal dish on the first day of the year is said to augur prosperity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/31/dining/a-black-eyed-peas-recipe-for-luck-in-the-new-year.html', 'snippet': 'For many, consuming this frugal dish on the first day of the year is said to augur prosperity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For good fortune in the New Year, a plate of black-eyed peas is considered auspicious, especially in the American South. Believe it or don’t. For many, consuming this frugal dish on the first day of the year is said to augur wealth. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/31/dining/31KITCH1/31KITCH1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 