mall but growing number of universities have adopted a more engaging, demanding form of the standard introductory courses, and research suggests the new style works better.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/27/us/college-science-classes-failure-rates-soar-go-back-to-drawing-board.html', 'snippet': 'A small but growing number of universities have adopted a more engaging, demanding form of the standard introductory courses, and research suggests the new style works better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVIS, Calif. — Hundreds of students fill the seats, but the lecture hall stays quiet enough for everyone to hear each cough and crumpling piece of paper. The instructor speaks from a podium for nearly the entire 80 minutes. Most students take notes. Some scan the Internet. A few doze.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/27/us/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/27/us/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/27/us/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/27/us/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/27/us/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/27/us/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/27/us/DAVIS1/DAVIS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': ' Colleges Reinvent Classes to Keep More Students in Science ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colleges Reinvent Classes to Keep More Students in Science', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Davis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of North Carolina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Colorado', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gates, Bill and Melinda, Foundation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-26T16:44:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dbf5c25-c1ab-51df-a085-7b7585ba7add', 'word_count': 1407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dbf5c25-c1ab-51df-a085-7b7585ba7add'}, {'abstract': 'To help her children become bilingual, a travel writer investigates options from public school programs at home to day camps abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/28/travel/making-language-immersion-fun-for-the-kids.html', 'snippet': 'To help her children become bilingual, a travel writer investigates options from public school programs at home to day camps abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was summer in Tuscany. The rolling hills were adorned with their famous haystacks. The cypress trees were majestically verdant against the golden backdrop. We were in the picturesque Renaissance town Pienza, its spire shooting up into a cloudless sky. I watched as my children boarded a scuolabus with 15 Italian kids they’d never met before. The bus pulled away, heading to a local terra-cotta museum. I looked at the faces of my children — crying, hysterical, their tiny hands banging on the windows. And I was filled with joy.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/travel/28-LANGUAGE/28-LANGUAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 258, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/28/travel/28-LANGUAGE/28-LANGUAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 258}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/travel/28-LANGUAGE/28-LANGUAGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 441, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/travel/28-LANGUAGE/28-LANGUAGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 882, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/travel/28-LANGUAGE/28-LANGUAGE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/28/travel/28-LANGUAGE/28-LANGUAGE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 7