every day if you want to keep in touch with the ongoing economics discussion — links to Martin Feldstein’s latest on macroeconomic policy, and editorializes with one word: “Wow”.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quantitative Levitation', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-26T20:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42fd7e0a-dfb5-5350-85a4-7aa51b1cf67e', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42fd7e0a-dfb5-5350-85a4-7aa51b1cf67e'}, {'abstract': 'Going from a virtual unknown to an awards-season darling can have its rewards, but it can also come with a cautionary tale or two.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/28/fashion/when-the-red-carpet-is-rolled-up.html', 'snippet': 'Going from a virtual unknown to an awards-season darling can have its rewards, but it can also come with a cautionary tale or two.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Every year at this time, a few dozen actors are paraded through Hollywood like livestock before judges at a really fancy state fair.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/fashion/28STEALERSSUB01/28STEALERSSub01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/28/fashion/28STEALERSSUB01/28STEALERSSub01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': No