': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | Garden Hideaway', 'kicker': 'On the Street', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Garden Hideaway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gardner, Isabella Stewart, Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-27T00:22:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1aab7ceb-b388-5241-a1e6-d2e18977afcf', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1aab7ceb-b388-5241-a1e6-d2e18977afcf'}, {'abstract': 'They have lost almost every battle in this Republican stronghold.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/27/opinion/nebraskas-lonely-progressives.html', 'snippet': 'They have lost almost every battle in this Republican stronghold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LINCOLN, Neb. — WHEN I travel to the East or West Coasts, people sometimes ask me, “Why do you live in Nebraska?” Or even, “Have you considered moving?” Outsiders often believe Nebraska is a nondescript state with little to recommend it in culture, politics or landscape. But I reply that Nebraska is my home and that I love its people and its geography. To me there is nothing more beautiful than the muddy Platte River or the vast undulating Sand Hills. Of course, our state can be blistering in the summer, arctic in the winter. It’s a windswept, spare place designed to toughen up its inhabitants. ', 'print_section': 'A', '