: 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a98fd20-fb72-5700-b73a-8d0e8e7fd062', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a98fd20-fb72-5700-b73a-8d0e8e7fd062'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Chris Christie continues to repudiate a court order that could result in tens of thousands of affordable units.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/27/opinion/no-more-delays-on-new-jersey-housing.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Chris Christie continues to repudiate a court order that could result in tens of thousands of affordable units.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last several years, Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey has shown utter contempt for the State Supreme Court’s three-decades-old ruling in the Mount Laurel housing case, which bars wealthy towns from excluding affordable housing and requires them to write zoning laws that permit a reasonable amount of such housing to be built. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No More Delays on New Jersey Housing ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No More Delays on New Jersey Housing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mount Laurel Township (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-27T01:20:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/30046303-70e1-575d-b416-e597ad36984b', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30046303-70e1-575d-b416-e597ad36984b'}, {'abstract': 'Proof that hockey has taken root in Arizona exists in Auston Matthews, a 17-year-old prodigy who was born in Scottsdale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/27/sports/though-ice-is-in-short-supply-arizona-warms-up-to-hockey.html', 'snippet': 'Proof that hockey has taken root in Arizona exists in Auston Matthews, a 17-year-old prodigy who was born in Scottsdale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEMPE, Ariz. — The teenage boys in\xa0pressed black pants and shiny black dress shoes stumbled\xa0out of sedans and sport utility vehicles. They\xa0sleepily tapped at the cars’ liftbacks, which yawned open to reveal bulky equipment bags that the boys slung over their shoulders. It was daybreak on a recent Saturday, and the Phoenix Junior Coyotes and the Arizona Bobcats, 17-member bantam hockey teams, streamed into the Oceanside Ice Arena to renew a rivalry as prickly as the native cactuses.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/27/sports/hockey-yyy/hockey-yyy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/27/sports/hockey-yyy/hockey-yyy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 443}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/27/sports/hockey-yyy/hockey-yyy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/27/sports/hockey-yyy/hockey-yyy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1513, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnai