 "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6188b818-9e88-5f73-926c-29b9904a3805', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6188b818-9e88-5f73-926c-29b9904a3805'}, {'abstract': 'When do we need a regime change?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/27/fiscal-policy-at-the-zero-lower-bound-again/', 'snippet': 'When do we need a regime change?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hmm. For a moment there I thought David Beckworth and I had reached a common understanding of the role and limitations of monetary policy at the zero lower bound. Leave aside Fed purchases of unconventional assets; we agree, I think, that conventional open-market operations are ineffectual in a liquidity trap unless the increase in the monetary base is perceived as permanent. As I explained, that’s why I pushed for a fiscal response in 2009; I didn’t believe that the Fed was ready to make a credible announcement of a regime change, so I didn’t believe monetary policy could get much traction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fiscal Policy at the Zero Lower Bound, Again', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-27T14:12:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f750ce9-2ec8-5273-bd1d-692a47e41bc0', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f750ce9-2ec8-5273-bd1d-692a47e41bc0'}, {'abstract': 'The Affordable Care Act provided a big increase in Medicaid payments for primary care the past two years, but the higher fees expire Thursday, raising questions of whether there will be enough doctors to provide services.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/28/us/obamacare-medicaid-fee-increases-expiring.html', 'snippet': 'The Affordable Care Act provided a big increase in Medicaid payments for primary care the past two years, but the higher fees expire Thursday, raising questions of whether there will be enough doctors to provide services.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Just as millions of people are gaining insurance through Medicaid, the program is poised to make deep cuts in payments to many doctors, prompting some physicians and consumer advocates to warn that the reductions could make it more difficult for Medicaid patients to obtain care.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/us/MEDICAID/MEDICAID-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/28/us/MEDICAID/MEDICAID-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/us/MEDICAID/MEDICAID-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/us/MEDICAID/MEDICAID-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/us/MEDICAID/MEDICAID-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/28/us/MEDICAID/MEDICAID-thumbStandard.jpg',