eater/jonny-donahoes-every-brilliant-thing-diary.html', 'snippet': 'The British comedian, actor and writer Jonny Donahoe shares his reflections about performing his one-man show “Every Brilliant Thing” at the Barrow Street Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last January, the playwright Duncan MacMillan asked if I’d work with him for a few days on a little project, “making something funny about depression.” Two years later, we’re still doing it, now in New York for a four-month run in Greenwich Village. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28JONNY/28JONNY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28JONNY/28JONNY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28JONNY/28JONNY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28JONNY/28JONNY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28JONNY/28JONNY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28JONNY/28JONNY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28JONNY/28JONNY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'That’s Sherlock Bones to You, Mate ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That’s Sherlock Bones to You, Mate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donahoe, Jonny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barrow Street Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Every Brilliant Thing (Play)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-27T21:27:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonny Donahoe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donahoe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca7a1a39-24f7-569d-bbb8-8653021fda19', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca7a1a39-24f7-569d-bbb8-8653021fda19'}, {'abstract': 'It’s nearly New Year’s Eve: time to make a list — and check it twice — of all the museum shows that will close soon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/28/arts/design/end-of-year-must-see-.html', 'snippet': 'It’s nearly New Year’s Eve: time to make a list — and check it twice — of all the museum shows that will close soon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s nearly New Year’s Eve: time to make a list — and check it twice — of all the museum shows that will close soon. One of the best, which ends Sunday, is the midcareer survey of Nicole Eisenman at the Institute of Contemporary Art in Philadelphia. “Dear Nemesis, Nicole Eisenman, 1993-2003,” traces an unusually inspiring evolution.\xa0Organized by the Contemporary Art Museum St. Louis, it shows a immensely talented graphic artist — cartoonist; pointed social commentator, especially about the art world and same-sex love; and all-around pillager of art history — morphing into one of the best painters of the moment. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28GUIDE6/28GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28GUIDE6/28GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 475}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28GUIDE6/28GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28GUIDE6/28GUIDE6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1434, 'width': 1811, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28GUIDE6/28GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28GUIDE6/28GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/28/arts/28GUIDE6/28GUIDE6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'End-of-Year Must-See ', 'kicker': 'Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'End-of-Year Must-See', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eisenman, Nicole', 'rank': 3