pe_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5533467c-5c13-592b-870f-d7af99d4faee', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5533467c-5c13-592b-870f-d7af99d4faee'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/28/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:05 A.M. (Showtime 2) SILVER LININGS PLAYBOOK (2012) Pat Solatano (Bradley Cooper) has returned to the home of his parents (Jacki Weaver and Robert De Niro) after eight months in a mental institution in this film from David O. Russell. Pat wants to tackle the world and reclaim his estranged wife, Nikki, who took out a restraining order against him. Then he meets Tiffany (Jennifer Lawrence, above with Mr. Cooper), who persuades him that she can circumvent the law by passing a letter from him to Nikki, if only he’ll enter a dance contest with her. Soon, she is leading, and he is following. “For all its high-flying zaniness, the movie has the sting of life, and its humor feels dredged up from the same dark, boggy place from which Samuel Beckett extracted his yuks,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times about this best picture Oscar nominee, which also earned nominations for Mr. Cooper, Ms. Weaver and Mr. De Niro, and a win for Ms. Lawrence.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-12-28T06:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brandon K. Thorp', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brandon', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Thorp', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id