'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/962f4659-89ce-51c1-9e10-ba66829094eb'}, {'abstract': 'Ravi Howard uses Nat King Cole as a device for exploring the civil rights movement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/29/arts/in-driving-the-king-ravi-howard-imagines-nat-king-cole.html', 'snippet': 'Ravi Howard uses Nat King Cole as a device for exploring the civil rights movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Driving the King,” Ravi Howard tells a thoroughly convincing story about the singing star Nat King Cole’s best friend. Both are black men named Nat and were boyhood pals in Montgomery, Ala., but Nat King Cole owes Nat Weary an extraordinary debt of gratitude. Weary, a soldier newly home after the end of World War II, was present at the Alabama concert where Cole was attacked onstage in the middle of a performance. He bludgeoned the white assailant with a microphone, saved the singer and served 10 grueling years in prison for his trouble.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/JPBOOK/JPBOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Civil Rights Map, a Crooner and His Driver', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Civil Rights Map, a Crooner and His Driver', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Ravi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cole, Nat King', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Driving the King (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-28T22:50:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3092ed5d-eb61-5fa2-8467-6cc53fef8e77', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3092ed5d-eb61-5fa2-8467-6cc53fef8e77'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Cosby’s team has used an aggressive legal and media strategy to keep accusations of sexual misconduct quiet for years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/29/arts/cosby-teams-strategy-hush-accusers-insult-them-blame-the-media.html', 'snippet': 'Bill Cosby’s team has used an aggressive legal and media strategy to keep accusations of sexual misconduct quiet for years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2005, when Tamara Green told the “Today” show and The Philadelphia Inquirer that Bill Cosby drugged and sexually assaulted her in the early 1970s, one of Mr. Cosby’s lawyers publicly branded the allegations “absolutely false,” while his aides approached another newspaper with “damaging information” about her, according to court documents.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/COSBY/COSBY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/COSBY/COSBY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/COSBY/COSBY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/COSBY/COSBY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1276, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/COSBY/COSBY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/COSBY/COSBY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/29/arts/COSBY/COSBY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cosby Team’s Strategy: Hush Accusers, Insult Them, Blame the Media ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cosby Team’s Strategy: Hush Accusers,