o Father Divine, the preacher who rose to prominence in Depression-era Harlem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Kristin Bedford trekked through the sweltering summer streets of Philadelphia in 2013, looking for remnants of forgotten religions. In college, as a religious studies major, she’d been influenced by Arthur Fauset’s 1944 book “Black Gods of the Metropolis: Negro Cults of the Urban North,” in which he’d chronicled five spinoff religions in African-American communities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Philadelphia, City of Father Divine', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-29T10:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Blaustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blaustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/958183d7-aef3-5b3d-ac1b-6da19c9f1184', 'word_count': 934, 'uri': 'nyt://article/958183d7-aef3-5b3d-ac1b-6da19c9f1184'}, {'abstract': 'Circumstances had changed, and all these documents needed to change, too.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/12/29/the-future-revisited/', 'snippet': 'Circumstances had changed, and all these documents needed to change, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When last I wrote my will, I didn’t have a dog, a point that had begun to nag at me. ', 'source'