ent south at the start of the civil rights movement were stunned to find localities where African-Americans represented an overwhelming majority of the population – but not a single black person could be found on the county voting rolls or in the jury pool. The new movie “Selma,” which focuses on the civil rights campaign in Selma, Alabama that led to the passage of the Voting Rights Act of 1965, vividly illustrates the system of intimidation and misdirection that made this possible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Selma’ and Real-World Voter Intimidation', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winfrey, Oprah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Selma (Ala)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-30T19:11:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75b4d70d-93a0-59ca-8e28-23b36d1ffdce', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75b4d70d-93a0-59ca-8e28-23b36d1ffdce'}, {'abstract': 'The former San Francisco 49ers coach Jim Harbaugh spoke after he signed a deal to return to the University of Michigan to become the next football coach of the Wolverines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/sports/ncaafootball/100000003423747/harbaugh-on-new-role-as-michigan-coach.html', 'snippet': 'The former San Fran