ecent performances of “La Traviata” and “Aida” showcased both the potential pitfalls and the triumphs that await young Americans singing Verdi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/31/arts/music/stephen-costello-and-tamara-wilson-show-opposing-approaches.html', 'snippet': 'The Met’s recent performances of “La Traviata” and “Aida” showcased both the potential pitfalls and the triumphs that await young Americans singing Verdi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Young American opera singers have long faced the same bum rap as some other American products. They’ve been thought to be well tooled but inauthentic, genial but ultimately impersonal. While they’re as well trained as any musicians in the world, their smooth versatility is said to come across as anonymous onstage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/31/arts/verdi1/verdi1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/31/arts/verdi1/verdi1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/31/arts/verdi1/verdi1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/31/arts/verdi1/verdi1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/31/arts/verdi1/verdi1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/31/arts/verdi1/verdi1-thumbStandard.jpg', '