valny, who has been under house arrest for nearly a year, was given a suspended sentence and spared jail time. His younger brother Oleg, however, was sentenced to serve three and a half years. Aleksei Navalny is an anti-corruption activist and outspoken critic of President Vladimir V. Putin, and the verdicts were seen as a cynical strategy to punish him without turning him into an imprisoned martyr. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can the Internet Defeat Putin?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Will the Internet Defeat Putin?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Emily', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navalny, Aleksei A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navalny, Oleg A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-30T23:55:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5e8c1c0-853d-5439-b4b2-a2ef7ccf9f5f', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5e8c1c0-853d-5439-b4b2-a2ef7ccf9f5f'}, {'abstract': 'Can a prison theater workshop prepare men for a life of freedom?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/31/opinion/inmate-improv.html', 'snippet': 'Can a prison theater workshop prepare men for a life of freedom?', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — ONE of the members of our improv workshop, a baby-faced man in his 30s, made up a rule: The last person to arrive has to do a cartwheel. A shaggy-haired man with creaky knees manages a groaning little hop, while another wheels like a shot of light. In this fluorescent-lit classroom at the Macomb Correctional Facility in Michigan, it’s the willingness to take a risk that counts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/31/opinion/31Clark/31Clark-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 994, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/12/31/opinion/31Clark/31Clark-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 994}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/31/opinion/31Clark/31Clark-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 619, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/31/opinion/31Clark/31Clark-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1237, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/12/31/opinion/31Clark/31Clark-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/12/31/opinion/31Clark/31Clark-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': N