ir lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The main street of Maotanchang, a secluded town in the furrowed hills of eastern China’s Anhui province, was nearly deserted. A man dozed on a motorized rickshaw, while two old women with hoes shuffled toward the rice paddies outside town. It was 11:44 on a Sunday morning last spring, and the row of shops selling food, tea and books by the pound stood empty. Even the town’s sacred tree lured no supplicants; beneath its broad limbs, a single bundle of incense smoldered on a pile of ash.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside a Chinese Test-Prep Factory', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cram City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larmer, Brook', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maotanchang (China)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maotanchang (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-12-31T13:59:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brook Larmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Larmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ec5f4dc-dbd1-5013-829b-a98b7d30c3b9', 'word_count': 5256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ec5f4dc-dbd1-5013-829b-a98b7d30c3b9'}, {'abstract': 'Today, six years after its bankruptcy, the Yellowstone Club is thriving.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/201